ia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ce5e77ac-cd08-5682-9f28-34f66b343445', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ce5e77ac-cd08-5682-9f28-34f66b343445'}, {'abstract': 'Jagsheer Singh said the boy was injured in a fall, but a doctor said the infant’s injuries indicated “nonaccidental inflicted trauma” to the head.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/01/nyregion/queens-man-is-charged-with-murdering-4-month-old-son.html', 'snippet': 'Jagsheer Singh said the boy was injured in a fall, but a doctor said the infant’s injuries indicated “nonaccidental inflicted trauma” to the head.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Queens man who was accused of beating his 4-month-old son was rearrested and charged with murder on Wednesday, one week after the infant died from his injuries, the authorities said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Queens Man Is Charged With Murdering 4-Month-Old Son', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-01T04:21:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd986312-b418-5c73-ad91-9d66a6eed2f9', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd986312-b418-5c73-ad91-9d66a6eed2f9'}, {'abstract': 'One of the foremost challenges is finding a way to get the world’s major economies humming enough that deflation is no longer a worry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/upshot/five-surprising-economic-trends-in-2014-and-what-they-mean-for-2015.html', 'snippet': 'One of the foremost challenges is finding a way to get the world’s major economies humming enough that deflation is no longer a worry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a confounding year in global financial markets. Not because it was a disaster for most investors; American stocks and bonds both rose in value. It was confounding because of some major moves that defied expert consensus this time a year ago — not only what was predicted, but what was even thought plausible.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/upshot/01UP-Markets/01UP-Markets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/07/upshot/01UP-Markets/01UP-Markets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/upshot/01UP-Markets/01UP-Markets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/upshot/01UP-Markets/01UP-Markets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/upshot/01UP-Markets/01UP-Markets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/07/upshot/01UP-Markets/01UP-Markets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/upshot/01UP-Markets/01UP-Markets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Five Surprising Economic Trends in 2014, and What They Mean for 2015', 'kicker': 'Global Markets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Market Trends of 2014: What They Mean for 2015', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irwin, Neil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'US Dollar (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deflation (Economics)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-01T05:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Irwin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Irwin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0a69941-5141-5ca5-a608-d1acc16d4ddd', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0a69941-5141-5ca5-a608-d1acc16d4ddd'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/01/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '11 A.M. (HGTV) ROSE PARADE 2015 The new year is once again coming up roses for HGTV, which heralds 2015 from its traditional perch at this 126th annual parade. Louis Zamperini, the Olympic runner turned World War II bombardier of “Unbroken” fame, who died in July, will be honored as the grand marshal as nearly 40 floats inch their way down Colorado Boulevard in Pasadena, Calif. The floats, adorned with more botanical elements than the average florist might go through in year, are based on inspirational stories. The “Property Brothers” — Drew and Jonathan Scott — and Nancy O’Dell will provide play-by-play. (The parade will also be broadcast on ABC, NBC and the Hallmark Channel. The University of Oregon will take on Florida State in the Rose Bowl game at 5 p.m. on ESPN.) The HGTV programming moves into prime time at 8 with a tour of the latest “Dream Home” giveaway: a 3,200-square-foot, three-bedroom Cape Cod-style vacation house on Martha’s Vineyard. The property includes soaring ceilings, patios off each sleeping area, a bike rack and a doggy dream home. The winner also gets furnishings from Ethan Allen, a GMC Acadia Denali and $250,000.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-01T06:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f14978f-0fae-5bc0-bf07-158132e7f6da', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f14978f-0fae-5bc0-bf07-158132e7f6da'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, January 1, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/01/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, January 1, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“They had forgotten. We had to call to remind them. The whole country has forgotten. People don’t realize we still have troops risking their lives out there.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-01T06:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ccfead8-be9b-5525-a62c-97430d4ae3bc', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ccfead8-be9b-5525-a62c-97430d4ae3bc'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Thursday, January 1, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/01/pageoneplus/corrections-january-1-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Thursday, January 1, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 1, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-01T06:26:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c5f3fea-9dc1-5387-a90d-61691b7c602c', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt: