 Mountain.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regrets, Annie Proulx has had a few, starting with “Brokeback Mountain.” That 1997 story about two gay cowboys may have won wide acclaim and been turned into an Oscar-winning movie, but in a 2009 interview with The Paris Review, which drew renewed attention this week, Ms. Proulx said she wished she could take it back.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Proulx Says She Regrets ‘Brokeback Mountain’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proulx Regrets Writing u2018Brokeback Mountainu2019', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Proulx, Annie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-01T17:36:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42dcdb7e-0558-5e29-9b2c-e4de6aed3417', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42dcdb7e-0558-5e29-9b2c-e4de6aed3417'}, {'abstract': 'The blaze began in a ninth-floor kitchen apartment in LeFrak City and killed a married couple and their 37-year-old niece.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/nyregion/3-die-in-queens-fire-on-new-years-eve.html', 'snippet': 'The blaze began in a ninth-floor kitchen apartment in LeFrak City and killed a married couple and their 37-year-old niece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just minutes before the New Year’s Eve ball dropped in Times Square, three members of a family in Queens died in a fire that started in the kitchen of their ninth-floor apartment in the LeFrak City housing complex, officials said on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Time