’s wide embrace. By contrast, if Asian artists showed signs of absorbing Western models, their work was disdained as derivative, inauthentic and evidence that Western Modernism was the only true one, the source that supplied the world.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Indian Modernist With a Global Gaze ', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Indian Modernist With a Global Gaze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaitonde, V S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-01T19:55:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/07f51efe-4244-52e8-a7ae-5d99d6e59993', 'word_count': 1363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07f51efe-4244-52e8-a7ae-5d99d6e59993'}, {'abstract': 'Paramount Pictures will show the film free at Selma’s Walton Theater beginning Jan. 9 as part of the movie’s national release.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/01/selma-to-be-screened-free-in-selma/', 'snippet': 'Paramount Pictures will show the film free at Selma’s Walton Theater beginning Jan. 9 as part of the movie’s national release.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Selma,” Ava DuVernay’s film about the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s 1965 civil rights marches in that small Alabama town, is making the rounds among Oscar voters, who began casting 