st but most salient works in “Jean Dubuffet: Soul of the Underground,” at the Museum of Modern Art, is a sketchbook page covered with tiny contour drawings of footprints. Made during one of Dubuffet’s late-1940s sojourns in El Goléa, a Saharan oasis, it hints at the inspiration he would find under his soles over the next couple of decades. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02DUBUFFET1/DUBUFFET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02DUBUFFET1/DUBUFFET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 458}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02DUBUFFET1/DUBUFFET1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02DUBUFFET1/DUBUFFET1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1562, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02DUBUFFET1/DUBUFFET1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02DUBUFFET1/DUBUFFET1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02DUBUFFET1/DUBUFFET1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Creative Vision, So Down to Earth ', 'kicker': 'Art Review'