nch countryside filled with racist children and bizarre killings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/arts/lil-quinquin-a-new-mystery-by-bruno-dumont.html', 'snippet': 'Bruno Dumont’s “Li’l Quinquin” unfolds in a French countryside filled with racist children and bizarre killings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French filmmaker Bruno Dumont has described his mesmerizing 197-minute murder mystery, “Li’l Quinquin,” as a comedy. The term fits that definition only if you understand that he means the human comedy in all its grotesque and happy-sad variations. As in most of his films, Mr. Dumont assumes the aesthetic and moral stance of a semidetached, some would say pitiless, observer of the human condition. “Li’l Quinquin” is a quasi-epic farce that mostly wears a poker face as it elaborates his continuing obsession with the collision of humankind’s bestial and spiritual impulses. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02QUINQUIN1/02QUINQUIN1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02QUINQUIN1/02QUINQUIN1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02QUINQUIN1/02QUINQUIN1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02QUINQUIN1/02QUINQUIN1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/arts/02QUINQUIN1/02QUINQUIN