ce-chief-on-leave-after-shooting-of-his-wife.html', 'snippet': 'William E. McCollom of Peachtree City was placed on administrative leave after calling in the shooting of his wife, Margaret, who is in critical condition and has not yet been questioned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police chief of an Atlanta suburb shot his wife early on New Year’s Day, telling 911 operators that it was an accident, officials said. The victim, Margaret McCollom, 58, was in critical condition, and the chief, William E. McCollom, was placed on administrative leave.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia Police Chief on Leave After Shooting of His Wife ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Atlanta Suburb’s Police Chief on Leave After Shooting Wife', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dewan, Shaila K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peachtree City (Ga)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCollom, William E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCollom, Margaret', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T01:31:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54f4a6e0-c407-50fc-ad76-8264f174342e', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54f4a6e0-c407-50fc-ad76-8264f174342e'}, {'abstract': 'Even if the Palestinian Authority becomes a member of the court, the cases it plans to bring over the Gaza war last summer would face many hurdles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/world/middleeast/court-membership-wouldnt-guarantee-palestinians-a-war-crimes-case.html', 'snippet': 'Even if the Palestinian Authority becomes a member of the court, the cases it plans to bring over the Gaza war last summer would face many hurdles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The political fallout from the Palestinian move Wednesday to join the International Criminal Court is likely to be swift and profound.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joining International Criminal Court Wouldn’t Guarantee Palestinians a War Crimes Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Membership Wouldn’t Guarantee Palestinians a War Crimes Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T01:39:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1bf4ee8-1ea9-5cd6-ae9a-215829bd6249', 'word_count': 1254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1bf4ee8-1ea9-5cd6-ae9a-215829bd6249'}, {'abstract': 'Russia needs to know that defiance of arms control treaties will come at a cost.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/opinion/a-vital-nuclear-agreement-at-risk.html', 'snippet': 'Russia needs to know that defiance of arms control treaties will come at a cost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s much more to the deeply troubled Russian-American relationship than Ukraine. Under the radar, tensions have also been brewing over compliance with a number of arms control treaties that for decades have been vital to keeping the peace between the two nuclear powers and setting an example for other countries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vital Nuclear Agreement, at Risk', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vital Nuclear Agreement, at Risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMS CONTROL AND LIMITATION AND DISARMAMENT', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Treaties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T01:42:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa42222e-967a-579f-bf68-d6ebcea6b081', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa42222e-967a-579f-bf68-d6ebcea6b081'}, {'abstract': 'The leader of the correction officers’ union has a record of bullying and shielding abusive officers, so federal oversight might be needed to do the job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/opinion/an-enemy-of-reform-in-new-york-jails.html', 'snippet': 'The leader of the correction officers’ union has a record of bullying and shielding abusive officers, so federal oversight might be needed to do the job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department’s decision in December to join a class-action suit against New York City’s Correction Department has prepared the way for reforms proposed by Mayor Bill de Blasio to root out corruption and brutality at the notorious Rikers Island jail complex. Success depends heavily on the cooperation of Norman Seabrook, the president of the politically powerful correction officers’ union and a longtime supporter of the disastrous status quo. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/opinion/02FRI2/02FRI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/02/opinion/02FRI2/02FRI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/opinion/02FRI2/02FRI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/opinion/02FRI2/02FRI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 