gton Capitals defeated the Chicago Blackhawks in the seventh edition of the Winter Classic on a goal by Troy Brouwer with 12.9 seconds remaining.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Under a national spotlight, there was no avoiding the glare.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Battling Sun’s Glare at Ballpark, the Capitals Deliver a Final Bit of Brilliance', 'kicker': 'Capitals 3, Blackhawks 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Battling Sun’s Glare at Ballpark, the Capitals Deliver a Final Bit of Brilliance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothenberg, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Blackhawks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T02:23:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3696bbc3-e6fa-5231-87f2-c259896707ee', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3696bbc3-e6fa-5231-87f2-c259896707ee'}, {'abstract': 'Syrian fighters and activists who once gathered in southern Turkey to plan a revolution are now marooned, their hopes rapidly deflating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/world/europe/vanguard-of-an-uprising-now-on-the-run-weighs-a-bleak-future-.html', 'snippet': 'Syrian fighters and activists who once gathered in southern Turkey to plan a revolution are now marooned, their hopes rapidly deflating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANTAKYA, Turkey — The cigarette smoke in the hotel room grew as thick as the cottony fog outside in this Turkish border town, as Syrian men, night after night, told their war stories. Their memories veered from exhilaration to black humor to terror, but mostly they told of what they had lost: Friends. A fiancée. An arm. A country. None were out of their mid-20s.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/ANTAKYA/ANTAKYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/02/world/ANTAKYA/ANTAKYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/ANTAKYA/ANTAKYA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/ANTAKYA/ANTAKYA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/ANTAKYA/ANTAKYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/02/world/ANTAKYA/ANTAKYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/ANTAKYA/ANTAKYA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vanguard of Syria’s Uprising, Now on the Run From ISIS, Weighs a Bleak Future', 'kicker': 'Antakya Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vanguard of Syrian Uprising, Now on the Run, Weighs a Bleak Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Antakya (Turkey)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T02:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e724beae-3499-56cc-9336-64b1b55b5b0e', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e724beae-3499-56cc-9336-64b1b55b5b0e'}, {'abstract': 'Doctors seeking to stem the Ebola epidemic disagree on whether most patients in West Africa should, or can, be given intravenous hydration, a standard therapy in developed countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/health/ebola-doctors-are-divided-on-iv-therapy-in-africa.html', 'snippet': 'Doctors seeking to stem the Ebola epidemic disagree on whether most patients in West Africa should, or can, be given intravenous hydration, a standard therapy in developed countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Medical experts seeking to stem the Ebola epidemic are sharply divided over whether most patients in West Africa should, or can, be given intravenous hydration, a therapy that is standard in developed countries. Some argue that more aggressive treatment with IV fluids is medically possible and a moral obligation. But others counsel caution, saying that pushing too hard would put overworked doctors and nurses in danger and that the treatment, if given carelessly, could even kill patients.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/africa/A1-sub-Hydrate/A1-sub-Hydrate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/02/world/africa/A1-sub-Hydrate/A1-sub-Hydrate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/africa/A1-sub-Hydrate/A1-sub-Hydrate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/africa/A1-sub-Hydrate/A1-sub-Hydrate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/africa/A1-sub-Hydrate/A1-sub-Hydrate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/02/world/africa/A1-sub-Hydrate/A1-sub-Hydrate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/world/africa/A1-sub-Hydrate/A1-sub-Hydrate-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge