sented here, features Tony Bennett performing “New York State of Mind,” LeAnn Rimes singing “Lullabye (Goodnight, My Angel),” Josh Groban rendering “Always a Woman” and John Mellencamp covering “Allentown.” Then it’s Mr. Joel’s turn with renditions of “Movin’ Out,” “Vienna,” “You May Be Right” and, with Kevin Spacey, “Piano Man.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T05:23:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7ce2de8-ccd2-568e-b397-2dd11c12e16d', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7ce2de8-ccd2-568e-b397-2dd11c12e16d'}, {'abstract': 'Led by the third-string quarterback Cardale Jones, the Buckeyes pulled off an upset in New Orleans in the semifinals of the inaugural College Football Playoff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/sports/ncaafootball/ohio-state-cardale-jones-alabama-sugar-bowl-advances-national-title-game.html', 'snippet': 'Led by the third-string quarterback Cardale Jones, the Buckeyes pulled off an upset in New Orleans in the semifinals of the inaugural College Football Playoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Nick Saban walked slowly down the sideline Thursday night, barely picking up his head as Ohio State running back Ezekiel Elliott sprinted toward the end zone with a trail of Alabama defenders helplessly chasing him.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia'