blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/tim-burton-narrates-a-scene-from-big-eyes/', 'snippet': 'In Anatomy of a Scene, the director Tim Burton discusses his process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this video, the director Tim Burton discusses a sequence from his film “Big Eyes,” based on the life of the artist Margaret Keane (Amy Adams) and her husband, Walter (Christoph Waltz), who takes credit for her artwork. Some of the look of the scene, Mr. Burton said, was inspired by the films of the Italian director Mario Bava. He also discusses the quiet, internal performance given by Ms. Adams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Burton Narrates a Scene From ‘Big Eyes’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Amy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burton, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keane, Margaret', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waltz, Christoph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T15:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e965bada-2dac-5f37-bd7b-81c22fc7fe6f', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e965bada-2dac-5f37-bd7b-81c22fc7fe6f'}, {'abstract': 'The new year promises further attempts at online censorship, as the web increasingly serves as a platform for civil rights efforts.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/02/daily-report-web-freedom-is-seen-as-a-growing-global-issue/', 'snippet': 'The new year promises further attempts at online censorship, as the web increasingly serves as a platform for civil rights efforts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Government censorship of the Internet is a cat-and-mouse game. And despite more aggressive tactics in recent months, the cats have been largely frustrated while the mice wriggle away, Vindu Goel and Andrew E. Kramer report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Web Freedom Is Seen as a Growing Global Issue', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T15:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dd88106-7ca5-51c7-a93c-33069e189ec3', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd88106-7ca5-51c7-a93c-33069e189ec3'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the genesis of four particularly satisfying projects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/03/upshot/letter-from-the-editor-about-writing-what-we-wished-to-read.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the genesis of four particularly satisfying projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of the most satisfying work I’ve done has stemmed from a bit of dissatisfaction I’ve had as a reader: Why haven’t I been able to read that before?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/upshot/03UP-Letter/03UP-Letter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/07/upshot/03UP-Letter/03UP-Letter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo'