 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mrs Bridge (Book)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mr Bridge (Book)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T15:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4064f208-3381-5e4d-b869-94a52f8d9c6d', 'word_count': 1482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4064f208-3381-5e4d-b869-94a52f8d9c6d'}, {'abstract': 'They didn’t know what was wrong with me. What if I never got better?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/04/magazine/brain-freeze.html', 'snippet': 'They didn’t know what was wrong with me. What if I never got better?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was wheeled into a room full of doctors ready to pry and poke, clipboards in hand. I counted more than seven and fewer than 15 — I couldn’t tell, because it was hard to turn my neck. All I could think about was how bad I smelled. God, how I must have smelled. I hadn’t washed myself in juvenile protest of my symptoms, which arrived with no notice and, I convinced myself, would surely depart as quickly. Help me, I thought while trying not to slump in my wheelchair, but please forgive me for reeking.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/magazine/04LIVES/04LIVES-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 328, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/04/magazine/04LIVES/04LIVES-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 328}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 