'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Prevost', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prevost', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b0e2607-3f4e-5849-b7ab-33fba629b5c5', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b0e2607-3f4e-5849-b7ab-33fba629b5c5'}, {'abstract': 'Steven Brill, whose new book is “America’s Bitter Pill,” once reviewed a John Grisham novel for the Book Review.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Steven Brill, whose new book is “America’s Bitter Pill,” once reviewed a John Grisham novel for the Book Review.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grishamstyle: “Thrillers thrive on villains and heroes, and usually these characters are not overly complicated; writers don’t want to confuse or slow the plot.” That was Steven Brill — whose book about the health care system, “America’s Bitter Pill,” is reviewed in next week’s Book Review — writing in 2008, in these pages, about John Grisham’s novel “The Appeal.” Brill is best known as a media mogul and entrepreneur: He founded The American Lawyer magazine in 1979, followed a decade later by Court TV and then by the short-lived magazine Brill’s Content. (“I believe in journalism,” he told the National Press Club in 1998. “I believe deeply in journalism.” Apparently he still does; his latest venture is a partnership with The Times’s former executive editor Jill Abramson to promote articles too long for a magazine and too short for a book.) But Brill also has personal experience with the best-seller list: In 1978 he hit the nonfiction list with his first book, “The Teamsters” — “the whole squalid story meticulously researched,” according to the Book Review back then — while in 2011 he spent a few weeks on the extended list with “Class Warfare,” a look at education in America. Reviewing Grisham’s novel, Brill had some kind words for its political observations, although he didn’t think much of what he called “Grishamstyle”: “At times,” he wrote, “his weakness with words is painful to watch, . . . as if someone new to English decided to mimic ‘The Bonfire of the Vanities.’ ”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/books/review/02list/02list-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 450, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/books/review/02list/02list-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 450, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/books/review/02list/02list-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/02/books/review/02list/02list-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/02/books/review/02list/02list-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-02T15:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66c2b4c6-a9b6-5b4c-a7e5-9ae8d8111396', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66c2b4c6-a9b6-5b4c-a7e5-9ae8d8111396'}, {'abstract': 'Information on sales in New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/01/04/realestate/04-Real-Estate-Matrix-Graphic.html', 'snippet': 'Information on sales in New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Information on sales in New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/realestate/04matrix-image/04matrix-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/04/realestate/04matrix-image/04matrix-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 652}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/realestate/04matrix-image/04matrix-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 943, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/realestate/04matrix-image/04matrix-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1885, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/realestate/04matrix-image/04matrix-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/04/realestate/04matrix-image/04matrix-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth':