pinion/sunday/the-paradox-of-the-free-market-liberal.html', 'snippet': 'Why personality and politics don’t always align.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN American politics, personality is, supposedly, destiny: Having a conservative personality makes us conservative on economic and social policy, and vice versa for liberals. Think of the stereotypes: the free-spending, libertine liberal; the rock-ribbed, free-market conservative. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04GRAYMATTER/04GRAYMATTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 558, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04GRAYMATTER/04GRAYMATTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 558}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04GRAYMATTER/04GRAYMATTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 953, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04GRAYMATTER/04GRAYMATTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1102, 'width': 1184, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04GRAYMATTER/04GRAYMATTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04GRAYMATTER/04GRAYMATTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04GRAYMATTER/04GRAYMATTER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'heigh