 passport. They told Ms. Bruguera, who divides her time between Cuba, New York and France, that she could not leave the country while “resistance and public disorder” charges were pending. Several activists among about 50 government opponents detained Tuesday were also released. The crackdown, condemned by the State Department and 1,000 artists who signed a letter on Friday to President Raúl Castro, was the largest since the diplomatic thaw between the United States and Cuba was announced Dec. 17. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuba: Performance Artist Is Freed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuba: Performance Artist Is Freed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruguera, Tania', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-03T00:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ed0d82f-879b-5ee7-ac5c-90d2e7c6fddf', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ed0d82f-879b-5ee7-ac5c-90d2e7c6fddf'}, {'abstract': 'The Seriously Spoiled spa in Dix Hills, N.Y., is one of an increasing number of spas that cater to children. A birthday party celebration includes hairstyling, manicu