le/887a4342-0ea5-58da-b0d9-55e8774f1444'}, {'abstract': 'State ethics laws are incredibly feeble, and penalties for violations can be little more than a tap on the wrist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/03/opinion/albany-lawmakers-and-their-secret-incomes.html', 'snippet': 'State ethics laws are incredibly feeble, and penalties for violations can be little more than a tap on the wrist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has taken far too long, but federal authorities are finally asking the right questions about how New York’s part-time lawmakers make money apart from their legislative salaries. The Times reported Tuesday that investigators are examining “substantial” secret payments from a small law firm to one of New York’s most powerful politicians, Speaker Sheldon Silver of the Assembly. So far, there has been no real explanation from Mr. Silver. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/03/opinion/03SAT3/03SAT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/03/opinion/03SAT3/03SAT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/03/opinion/03SAT3/03SAT3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/03/opinion/03SAT3/03SAT3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/03/opinion/03SAT3/03SAT3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_