reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6937f6f-e444-527b-ae6d-c8b68b15aaba', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6937f6f-e444-527b-ae6d-c8b68b15aaba'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t just do what you should be doing. Reflect on the person you can be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/04/opinion/sunday/resolving-to-create-a-new-you.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t just do what you should be doing. Reflect on the person you can be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE annual ritual of the New Year’s resolution — I’ll lose 10 pounds, get my finances in order, be more patient with my family, feel more grateful — misses the point. We try to steel our wills to do what we already know we should be doing. Kick-in-the-pants reminders, however stern, are missed opportunities for genuine self-renewal. (Not to mention that the shelf life of any motivational juice we generate in January tends to expire in February.) ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04CHANG/04CHANG-articleLarge-v3.gif', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04CHANG/04CHANG-articleLarge-v3.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04CHANG/04CHANG-jumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04CHANG/04CHANG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 941, 'width': 1169, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 