n tied) for most grand slams in a season — six — and those were the only ones he ever hit. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sports/DOG-mattingly/DOG-mattingly-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/04/sports/DOG-mattingly/DOG-mattingly-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 832}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sports/DOG-mattingly/DOG-mattingly-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sports/DOG-mattingly/DOG-mattingly-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1478, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sports/DOG-mattingly/DOG-mattingly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/04/sports/DOG-mattingly/DOG-mattingly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sports/DOG-mattingly/DOG-mattingly-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the Case for Don Mattingly on His Last Chance for Cooperstown', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making the Case for Mattingly on His Last Chance for Cooperstown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Bruce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mattingly, Don', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-03T20:13:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83ddc044-61bc-5973-a16b-cc78cb30b185', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83ddc044-61bc-5973-a16b-cc78cb30b185'}, {'abstract': 'I gave up Big Macs and started exercising. But I was neglecting my inner life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/04/opinion/sunday/healthy-body-unhealthy-mind.html', 'snippet': 'I gave up Big Macs and started exercising. But I was neglecting my inner life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANY of my friends were shocked some years ago when I cut down on my junk-food intake. Even my wise old physician was a little put out. He had more or less given me the green light to the “golden arches” a few years before when, one afternoon, following my annual checkup, he’d asked me what I consumed every day. “A Big Mac, medium fries and Coke for lunch,” I answered, “and frozen pizza from the convenience store for dinner.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/sunday-review/04JUNKFOOD/04JUNKFOOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'heig