Alan Gilbert has championed the music of the Danish composer Carl Nielsen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/04/arts/emotions-flip-from-note-to-note.html', 'snippet': 'Almost from the outset of his tenure as music director of the New York Philharmonic, Alan Gilbert has championed the music of the Danish composer Carl Nielsen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost from the outset of his tenure as music director of the New York Philharmonic, Alan Gilbert has championed the music of the Danish composer Carl Nielsen. This week he conducts performances of Nielsen’s Clarinet Concerto with the orchestra’s new principal clarinetist, Anthony McGill, taking on the solo part that flips through emotions ranging from sardonic humor to deep melancholy. The program also includes Ravel’s “Valses nobles et sentimentales” and selections from Tchaikovsky’s “Swan Lake.” (Thursday, Friday and Saturday, Avery Fisher Hall, Lincoln Center, nyphil.org.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE8/04GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE8/04GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE8/04GUIDE8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE8/04GUIDE8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE8/0