 'John Huston made his 1946 documentary, “Let There Be Light,” about soldiers with “neuropsychiatric disorders” — what we now call post-traumatic stress disorder — for the Army.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Huston made his 1946 documentary, “Let There Be Light,” about soldiers with “neuropsychiatric disorders” — what we now call post-traumatic stress disorder — for the Army. But the Army banned the film for 35 years. What did it fear? Presumably the power of the soldiers’ pain and of Huston’s movie, which follows a group of soldiers from admission to a hospital through treatment (talk therapy, hypnosis) and rehabilitation to release. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1526, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/04GUIDE7/04GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': 