', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T13:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan H. Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb9660a9-0a58-5e2e-8bcd-8fbd92b16b90', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb9660a9-0a58-5e2e-8bcd-8fbd92b16b90'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Britain announced it would take control of British and colonial shipping in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/04/1940-british-shipping-to-be-operated-by-government/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Britain announced it would take control of British and colonial shipping in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The government will take over full control of British and colonial shipping beginning February 1 to obtain more tonnage for national use, the Ministry of Shipping announced tonight [Jan. 4]. All ships of United Kingdom and colonial registry, with the exception of vessels of Indian and Burman registry, will be taken over when they discharge their first cargo in Great Britain after that date. The scheme, identical to the one employed successfully during the World War, will make it possible to operate ships more efficiently and economically because of the community of interests of the British Dominions, it was explained. Such a control system, it was stated, will result in a regular execution of the shipping program for the efficient conduct of the war. The companies will continue to manage and operate their ships as though carrying on their own business but will receive instructions as to the cargoes to be carried and the routes to be followed. They will maintain their organizations in Britain and abroad but will keep an account of costs for the Ministry. Operating profits and losses are to be treated as on government account. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 5, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: British Shipping to Be Operated by Government', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T14:21:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d86a1cb-934e-5b61-9186-ce69c7543fa3', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d86a1cb-934e-5b61-9186-ce69c7543fa3'}, {'abstract': 'The snub by many uniformed officers watching the funeral of Officer Wenjian Liu in Brooklyn showed a willingness by the rank and file to disregard their leadership.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/nyregion/police-officers-gather-for-the-funeral-of-wenjian-liu-killed-in-an-ambush.html', 'snippet': 'The snub by many uniformed officers watching the funeral of Officer Wenjian Liu in Brooklyn showed a willingness by the rank and file to disregard their leadership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second time in just over a week, a river of pressed blue uniforms filled the streets of a New York City neighborhood on Sunday as law enforcement officers from across the country paid respects to a slain colleague. And for the second time, hundreds of those officers made a silent show of protest against Mayor Bill de Blasio.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Silent Protest of Mayor de Blasio as Officer Liu Is Laid to Rest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Silent Protest as 2nd Officer Is Laid to Rest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, Wenjian (1982-2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Semple, Kirk', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramos, Rafael (1974-2014)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T15:04:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman and Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}