0-524a-ae35-732ed1c01241', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/9afe98a7-a410-524a-ae35-732ed1c01241'}, {'abstract': 'Many came from countries that have never had a cardinal, like Myanmar, Tonga and the Cape Verde islands, and were reflective of the Roman Catholic Church’s growth in Asia and Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/world/europe/pope-francis-names-new-cardinals.html', 'snippet': 'Many came from countries that have never had a cardinal, like Myanmar, Tonga and the Cape Verde islands, and were reflective of the Roman Catholic Church’s growth in Asia and Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VERBANIA, Italy — Pope Francis named 15 new cardinals from 14 countries on Sunday, continuing his efforts to diversify the church hierarchy and extend the global reach of the church.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/blogs/05FRANCIS/05FRANCIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/04/blogs/05FRANCIS/05FRANCIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/blogs/05FRANCIS/05FRANCIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/blogs/05FRANCIS/05FRANCIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1468, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/blogs/05FRANCIS/05FRANCIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/04/blogs/05FRANCIS/05FRANCIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/blogs/05FRANCIS/05FRANCIS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pope Names 15 New Cardinals Reflective of Diversity of the Faithful', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pope Names 15 New Cardinals Reflective of Diversity of the Faithful', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cardinals (Roman Catholic Prelates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T17:05:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a73f34c-df49-549b-a74e-826e01e72db1', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a73f34c-df49-549b-a74e-826e01e72db1'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/04/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13, 49) DOWNTON ABBEY The times are a-changin’ at Downton as Season 5 of this soapy “Masterpiece” drama picks up in 1924. Upstairs, Lord Grantham stews about the first Labour Government under Prime Minister Ramsay MacDonald and what he perceives as its anti-aristocracy stance. Downstairs, the servants think that someone in charge might finally understand the concept of hard work. Lady Edith, meanwhile, turns to the tenant farmer Mr. Drewe and his unsuspecting wife to secret away Marigold, her illegitimate daughter with her married lover, Michael Gregson, still missing in Germany. Lady Mary finds herself inundated by dashing suitors. And when the committee in charge of creating a World War I memorial comes knocking, it isn’t Lord Grantham they want, but rather Mr. Carson, the butler. In “The Manners of Downton Abbey,” at 10:15, Alastair Bruce, an expert on royal ceremony and custom who serves as the show’s historical adviser, discusses the code of conduct that governed Britain in the early 20th century and how he goes about tutoring the actors in speaking, sitting, dressing and keeping an appropriately stiff upper lip. Hugh Bonneville, Elizabeth McGovern, Michelle Dockery (above, with Allen Leech), Laura Carmichael, Brendan Coyle, Joanne Froggatt and Lily James chime in.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T17:28:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/febfd3d7-908e-55f7-9e73-b742494e259f', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/febfd3d7-908e-55f7-9e73-b742494e259f'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: T.S. Eliot dies in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/04/1965-t-s-eliot-76-dies/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: T.S. Eliot dies in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — T. S. Eliot, 76, American-born poet, critic and dramatist, died at his London home tonight [Jan. 4]. Thomas Stearns Eliot’s best known poems include ‘‘The Waste Land’’, ‘‘The Love Song of J. Arthur Prufrock,’’ and ‘‘Four Quartets,’’ and his plays: ‘‘The Cocktail Party’’ and ‘‘Murder in the Cathedral.’’ Born in St. Louis. Mo., of a Colonial Boston family, he was a naturalized British subject and held the highest civilian honors of both Britain and the United States. He was given the U.S. Presidential Medal of Freedom last September, and received the Order of Merit in Britain; as well as the Nobel Prize for Literature in 1948. France also made him an Officer of the Legion of Honor. Mr. Eliot was acknowledged as one of the most important creators of poetic style in the 20th century. He found in the cultural tradition of Europe a source of renewal for English poetry. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 5, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: T. S. Eliot, 76, Dies', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eliot, Thomas Stearns', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T18:12:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e46ada3-6a03-553c-8e2e-9992aca6d8c4', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e46ada3-6a03-553c-8e2e-9992aca6d8c4'}, {'abstract': '“The Hobbit: The Battle of the Five Armies” (Warner Bros.) continued to lead the North American box office, taking in an estimated $21.9 million, for a three-week total of $220.8 million.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/04/the-hobbit-the-battle-of-five-armies-reigns-at-the-box-office/', 'snippet': '“The Hobbit: The Battle of the Five Armies” (Warner Bros.) continued to lead the North American box office, taking in an estimated $21.9 million, for a three-week total of $220.8 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As expected, “The Hobbit: The Battle of the Five Armies” (Warner Bros.) continued to lead the North American box office, taking in an estimated $21.9 million, for a three-week total of $220.8 million. But the two films hot on its tail – Rob Marshall’s “Into the Woods” and Angelina Jolie’s “Unbroken” – were the reason Hollywood started the year smiling: Each release is a prime example of a type of film that supposedly can no longer succeed in theaters. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/hobbit-arts/hobbit-arts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/hobbit-arts/hobbit-arts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/hobbit-arts/hobbit-arts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/04/arts/hobbit-arts/hobbit-arts-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1