 Linklater’s “Boyhood” by just one vote for best picture.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/04/national-society-of-film-critics-chooses-goodbye-to-language-as-best-film/', 'snippet': 'The movie by Jean-Luc Godard edged out Richard Linklater’s “Boyhood” by just one vote for best picture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jean-Luc Godard’s 3-D film “Goodbye to Language” took top honors from the National Society of Film Critics on Saturday, edging out Richard Linklater’s “Boyhood” by just one vote for best picture.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Society of Film Critics Chooses ‘Goodbye to Language’ as Best Film', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Squeaker, a 3-D Film Tops u2018Boyhoodu2019 for Honor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Goodbye to Language (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Society of Film Critics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Film Critics Circle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T18:39:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbfef4f2-260c-5625-97cc-5682aba90ce7', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbfef4f2-260c-5625-97cc-5682aba90ce7'}, {'abstract': 'Olympic stadiums can engender more passion than almost any other buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/01/04/arts/design/20150105-STADIUMS.html', 'snippet': 'Olympic stadiums can e