in': 'Pricey Arenas, With a Patriotic Furor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadid, Zaha', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T19:37:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/fa6da623-f706-5360-9f69-97fe7d73b851', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/fa6da623-f706-5360-9f69-97fe7d73b851'}, {'abstract': 'The debate over an Olympic stadium to be built for the 2020 Summer Games illustrates how the structures have become potent symbols of architectural prowess and economic pride.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/arts/design/olympic-stadium-in-tokyo-is-dogged-by-controversy.html', 'snippet': 'The debate over an Olympic stadium to be built for the 2020 Summer Games illustrates how the structures have become potent symbols of architectural prowess and economic pride.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The Olympic stadium designed by the Pritzker-winning architect Zaha Hadid, to be built here for the 2020 Summer Games, looks to some like a pleasingly sleek, contoured spaceship. But many others deplore it, with one prominent Japanese architect saying it reminded him of a turtle. Another likened the $1.37 billion building, already projected to be the most expensive Olympic stadium in recent history, to another kind of animal.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Pride at a Steep Price ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'National Pride at a Steep Price', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qin, Amy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2020)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadid, Zaha', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T19:38:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Qin and Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01b21b39-3487-5380-b9b4-c9de83849950', 'word_count': 1198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01b21b39-3487-5380-b9b4-c9de83849950'}, {'abstract': 'Hourly employees across New York City are hoping to see their protests for better hours and wages bear fruit in 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/nyregion/new-jobs-and-pay-raises-give-some-workers-reasons-to-be-hopeful-about-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Hourly employees across New York City are hoping to see their protests for better hours and wages bear fruit in 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news came in a text: All employees at Zara clothing stores would receive raises in the first month of the new year. Valery Jourdan, a sales associate at Zara, directed a dubious eye at her cellphone. Really? Really?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '