aid Iranians were entitled to have major issues put to a nationwide vote, according to the country’s Constitution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/world/middleeast/irans-president-proposes-direct-referendums-as-a-way-to-bypass-rivals.html', 'snippet': 'President Hassan Rouhani said Iranians were entitled to have major issues put to a nationwide vote, according to the country’s Constitution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iran’s president said Sunday that he might invoke a powerful but neglected tool in his fight with hard-liners, suggesting the possibility of organizing direct referendums that would bypass the institutions the conservatives control and give more of a voice to Iranian voters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Leader Suggests Direct Votes on Issues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Leader Suggests Direct Votes on Issues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-04T21:45:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e1956de-e44d-56bf-8fe3-55a6c536ba40', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://arti