st of the worst.” They were those who were too poor, mentally ill or disabled to avoid it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/opinion/shifting-politics-on-the-death-penalty.html', 'snippet': 'The people executed in recent years were not the “worst of the worst.” They were those who were too poor, mentally ill or disabled to avoid it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In January 1992, Bill Clinton, then the governor of Arkansas, left the presidential campaign trail to fly home for the execution of a man named Ricky Ray Rector. Mr. Clinton’s decision not to grant clemency to Mr. Rector, who had been sentenced to death for killing a police officer, was widely seen as an attempt to fend off the familiar charge that Democrats were soft on crime.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shifting Politics on the Death Penalty', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shifting Politics on the Death Penalty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Malley, Martin J", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-05T02:13:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e239adc-d46b-555d-a