st at home, until symptoms start resolving, before gradually returning to school and physical activity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Limiting Rest Is Found to Help Young Concussion Patients', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Limiting Rest Is Found to Help Young Concussion Patients', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saint Louis, Catherine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pediatrics (Journal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Children's Hospital of Wisconsin", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Danny G', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-05T05:03:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbc7b1dd-b2ff-5dc6-a35d-4288bdccead6', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbc7b1dd-b2ff-5dc6-a35d-4288bdccead6'}, {'abstract': 'Member of the American Historical Association agreed not to consider two resolutions that would have condemned what was characterized as Israel’s violations of academic freedom for Palestinians and others.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/scholars-effort-to-condemn-israel-fails/', 'snippet': 'Member of the American Historical Association agreed not to consider two resolutions that would have condemned what was characterized as Israel’s violations of academic freedom for Palestinians and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The movement among some scholars to condemn Israel hit a bump on Sunday night, when members of the American Historical Association, the nation’s largest organization for professional historians, agreed not to vote on two resolutions condemning what was characterized as Israel’s violations of academic freedom for Palestinians and others.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scholars’ Effort to Condemn Israel Fails', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Historical Group Sidesteps Israel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACADEMIC FREEDOM', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN HISTORICAL ASSN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boycott, Divestment and Sanctions (BDS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Historians Against the War', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-05T05:07:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c98b4168-cca2-5526-9efe-b49748ece896', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c98b4168-cca2-5526-9efe-b49748ece896'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Monday, January 5, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/pageoneplus/corrections-january-5-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Monday, January 5, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 5, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-05T05:17:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f490bbc-1e4b-5744-8374-a67cc7cbfd04', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f490bbc-1e4b-5744-8374-a67cc7cbfd04'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:30 A.M. (Showtime) THE DIVING BELL AND THE BUTTERFLY (2007) Jean-Dominique Bauby, a 43-year-old French magazine editor and something of a playboy, had a stroke in 1995 that left him with a condition in which he retained vision, hearing and a functioning mind but was almost completely paralyzed. He told his story in a book that he dictated to an assistant by blinking. In this film from the artist Julian Schnabel, Mr. Bauby is played by Mathieu Amalric, above at right with Max von Sydow; Emmanuelle Seigner is Céline, the longtime partner he has recently left and the mother of his three children; and Marie-Josée Croze is a speech therapist who teaches him to use his left eyelid to communicate. “The phrase ‘triumph of the human spirit’ hovers over ‘The Diving Bell and the Butterfly,’ along with a swarm of other empty, uplifting clichés,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “But Mr. Schnabel and the screenwriter, Ronald Harwood, have other themes in mind” — among them, limitation, constraint and incarceration — Mr. Scott said. (Both men were nominated for Oscars.) “Their common subject, however, is freedom, the self-willed liberation of a difficult, defiant individual,” he added, noting that Mr. Schnabel demonstrated this with “imaginative freedom in every frame and sequence, dispensing with narrative and expository conventions in favor of a wild, intuitive honesty.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-05T05:21:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/093c54db-ac3e-5045-8e63-e2d295f6b3db', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/093c54db-ac3e-5045-8e63-e2d295f6b3db'}, {'abstract': 'Chen Shui-bian, the former president of Taiwan who was sentenced to 20 years in prison, suffers from a series of medical conditions including depression, brain atrophy and Parkinsonism.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/05/taiwan-approves-medical-parole-for-imprisoned-ex-leader/', 'snippet': 'Chen Shui-bian, the former president of Taiwan who was sentenced to 20 years in prison, suffers from a series of medical conditions including depression, brain atrophy and Parkinsonism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chen Shui-bian, the imprisoned former president of Taiwan, was released on medical parole on Monday, after Justice Ministry officials accepted the recommendation of a panel of medical experts that his failing health could be better treated at home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0,