, 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/749e18fd-afba-58a7-821d-9cd5aa933546', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/749e18fd-afba-58a7-821d-9cd5aa933546'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Myerson, the only Jewish Miss America, was one of a select group of American figures to parlay pop culture celebrity into positions of influence in government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/06/nyregion/bess-myerson-miss-america-and-new-york-official-tarnished-in-scandal-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Myerson, the only Jewish Miss America, was one of a select group of American figures to parlay pop culture celebrity into positions of influence in government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bess Myerson, a New York favorite daughter who basked in the public eye for decades — as Miss America in 1945, as a television personality, as a force in public affairs and finally as a player in a shattering municipal scandal — died on Dec. 14 at her home in Santa Monica, Calif. She was 90.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bess Myerson, New Yorker of Beauty, Wit, Service and Scandal, Dies at 90', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bess Myerson, 90, Dies; New Yorker of Beauty, Wit, Service and Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nemy, Enid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miss America Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty Contests', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Myerson, Bess', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-05T17:07:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Enid Nemy and William McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Enid', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nemy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/eab0d2f7-346c-59b7-ad2c-0adfbc591e8d', 'word_count': 2778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eab0d2f7-346c-59b7-ad2c-0adfbc591e8d'}, {'abstract': 'As people spend more time using apps, their Internet has taken a step backward, becoming more isolated — more like the web before search engines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/06/technology/tech-companies-look-to-break-down-walls-between-apps.html', 'snippet': 'As people spend more time using apps, their Internet has taken a step backward, becoming more isolated — more like the web before search engines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Navigating the Internet used to mean painstakingly typing the exact address you wanted into your computer. The web browser and the search engine simplified that, giving us the Internet we take for granted today.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/technology/06appsearch-web3/06appsearch-web3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/06/technology/06appsearch-web3/06appsearch-web3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '