including the Tuesday night shows “MasterChef Junior” and “Child Genius.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a child chef is eliminated on “MasterChef Junior,” two things happen. First, the unbearable: The child cries. This is almost always the case: Competitors range in age from 8 to 13, and by and large don’t have the backbone to endure being told they didn’t succeed. It’s agonizing, of course, or maybe heartening, if you’re the sort of person who appreciates emotional transparency.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/arts/SUB-KIDTV/SUB-KIDTV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/06/arts/SUB-KIDTV/SUB-KIDTV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/arts/SUB-KIDTV/SUB-KIDTV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/arts/SUB-KIDTV/SUB-KIDTV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/arts/SUB-KIDTV/SUB-KIDTV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/06/arts/SUB-KIDTV/SUB-KIDTV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/arts/SUB-KIDTV/SUB-KIDTV-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'cr