8d4'}, {'abstract': 'Since 1993, Robert Heller’s advanced photography students have documented life in LaFollette, Tenn., an old coal town that has seen better days.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/06/telling-stories-in-a-tennessee-coal-town/', 'snippet': 'Since 1993, Robert Heller’s advanced photography students have documented life in LaFollette, Tenn., an old coal town that has seen better days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Heller felt out of place when he first arrived in Knoxville to teach photography at the University of Tennessee in 1986. Mr. Heller — who had been raised on Long Island, N.Y., by second-generation Russian-Jewish immigrant parents — had never been to Tennessee and didn’t know much about the state other than it is a center of country and bluegrass music (so much so that it has at least five official state songs, including “Tennessee Waltz” and “Rocky Top”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Telling Stories in a Tennessee Coal Town', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heller, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Tennessee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'LaFollette (Tenn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-06T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/963943f2-515e-592e-9db8-75f3504844a9', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/963943f2-515e-592e-9db8-75f3504844a9'}, {'abstract': 'The servi