nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/01/06/jeb-bushs-mission-statement-in-translation/', 'snippet': 'First Draft reads between the lines of the mission statement for Jeb Bush’s new PAC, “Right to Rise.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which First Draft reads between the lines of the mission statement for Jeb Bush’s new PAC, Right to Rise.We believe passionately that the Right to Rise — to move up the income ladder based on merit, hard work and earned success — is the central moral promise of American economic life.Besides paying homage to Paul Ryan, who coined the phrase “right to rise,” Mr. Bush is playing to the G.O.P.’s linguistic foundation, with words like “earned” and “merit” to telegraph a message of personal responsibility, rather than government help.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeb Bush’s Mission Statement, in Translation', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Right to Rise Policy Solutions Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-06T15:43:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad4355fe-55a1-5251-8c42-e19ced025f22', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad4355fe-55a1-5251-8c42-e19ced025f22'}, {'abstract': 'Masayoshi Takayama’s restaurant in the basement of Larry Gagosian’s Upper East Sid