T17:56:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c4942c5-2c8f-5a2c-be18-76d828c3695f', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c4942c5-2c8f-5a2c-be18-76d828c3695f'}, {'abstract': 'I could lose a finger or two and still count on one hand the number of kids I’ve had more than a passing conversation with in my life. What if I can’t connect with children, even those that share my biological imprint?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/06/the-child-averse-sperm-donor/', 'snippet': 'I could lose a finger or two and still count on one hand the number of kids I’ve had more than a passing conversation with in my life. What if I can’t connect with children, even those that share my biological imprint?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I hadn’t even fastened my seatbelt before the woman next to me tapped me on my shoulder. “I just have to show you something!” she exclaimed. Just my luck, I thought. Not only was I stuck in the middle seat on a five-hour red-eye, but now I also had to deal with Chatty Cathy here the whole flight home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/us/motherlode-david-bjorn/motherlode-david-bjorn-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/06/us/motherlode-david-bjorn/motherlode-david-bjorn-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/us/motherlode-david-bjorn/motherlode-david-bjorn-jumbo.jpg',