onomics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keynes, John Maynard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-06T18:42:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b85faec-e041-5d1c-bdbe-b96ca10c0f50', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b85faec-e041-5d1c-bdbe-b96ca10c0f50'}, {'abstract': 'Industry forecasters predict Mexico, Canada and Britain as top choices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/travel/where-will-americans-travel-in-2015-.html', 'snippet': 'Industry forecasters predict Mexico, Canada and Britain as top choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans today are taking less vacation time than at any point in nearly 40 years, according to an October report for the U.S. Travel Association by Oxford Economics. So where and how will we be spending our precious leisure time in 2015?', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/travel/11GETAWAY/11GETAWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/travel/11GETAWAY/11GETAWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 741}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/travel/11GETAWAY/11GETAWAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption'