an', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenhill & Company Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-06T22:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/443a583f-5dc9-5e84-863f-02b11f9da8bf', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/443a583f-5dc9-5e84-863f-02b11f9da8bf'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo said his father would have asked the city to come together and stop the negative energy.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/06/a-message-to-new-york-city-from-mario-cuomo-through-his-son/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo said his father would have asked the city to come together and stop the negative energy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo gave one of the more poignant speeches of his career\xa0Tuesday at the Church of St. Ignatius Loyola in Manhattan, a eulogy for his father, former Gov. Mario Cuomo. It was full of humanity, wit and self-deprecation — qualities not always on display with this intensely political governor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Message to New York City From Mario Cuomo, Through His Son', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Mario M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-06T22:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Randolph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Randolph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/528a195c-9715-5e32-a9f0-07f945d5d964', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/528a195c-9715-5e32-a9f0-07f945d5d964'}, {'abstract': 'In “Hindsight,” a new series on VH1, Laura Ramsey plays a woman who wakes up in 1995 with a sure sense of how to fix her life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/arts/television/hindsight-is-a-new-vh1-series.html', 'snippet': 'In “Hindsight,” a new series on VH1, Laura Ramsey plays a woman who wakes up in 1995 with a sure sense of how to fix her life.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Hindsight,” a clever, affecting and sly new show about bad choices begetting worse ones, begins somewhere near the intersection of romance and horror. On the eve of her second wedding, to a onetime childhood friend turned midlife paramour, Becca (Laura Ramsey) blacks out in a New York elevator and wakes up back in 1995, on the eve of her first wedding, to a set of oily abdominals named Sean (Craig Horner). Sean has an appealing Australian accent, and looks like an extra from “Singles”: He is, of course, a tortured artist. The new guy is, of course, neither of those things.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cred