gay-views.html', 'snippet': 'Kelvin Cochran wrote and gave workers copies of his book, in which he wrote that homosexuality was among “vile, vulgar and inappropriate” activities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Mayor Kasim Reed announced Tuesday that he had fired the chief of the city’s Fire Rescue Department, Kelvin Cochran, after Mr. Cochran gave workers a religious book he wrote containing passages that condemn homosexuality.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Atlanta Ousts Fire Chief Who Has Antigay Views', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Atlanta Ousts Fire Chief Who Has Antigay Views', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cochran, Kelvin J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Kasim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T01:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Fausset', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fausset', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64f60a82-57fa-5ab7-be9f-09490348ee17', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64f60a82-57fa-5ab7-be9f-09490348ee17'}, {'abstract': 'Federal land officials on Tuesday announced new restrictions on rope-swinging from giant natural rock arches in the desert canyonlands outside Moab.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/us/utah-rope-swinging-on-rock-arches-is-banned-.html', 'snippet': 'Federal land officials on Tuesday announced new restrictions on rope-swinging from giant natural rock arches in the desert canyonlands outside Moab.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal land officials on Tuesday announced new restrictions on the daredevil pursuit of rope-swinging from giant natural rock arches in the desert canyonlands outside the tourist destination of Moab. The Bureau of Land Management placed a two-year ban on activities including zip-lining, rope-swinging and rappelling. The move came after a handful of serious accidents and dozens of complaints from hikers and tourists, who said that the screams and whoops of swinging adrenaline junkies were ruining a tranquil natural setting.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Utah: Rope-Swinging on Rock Arches Is Banned', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Rockies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Utah: Rope-Swinging on Rock Arches Is Banned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Land Management', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Lands', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moab (Utah)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T01:23:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a36ae6d-9362-554b-8392-4c661dd3b69a', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a36ae6d-9362-554b-8392-4c661dd3b69a'}, {'abstract': 'The appointment comes as Brazil is seeking to assert leadership in global talks and as scientists are questioning the nation’s commitment to reducing deforestation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/world/americas/climatologists-balk-as-brazil-picks-skeptic-for-key-post.html', 'snippet': 'The appointment comes as Brazil is seeking to assert leadership in global talks and as scientists are questioning the nation’s commitment to reducing deforestation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — Calling Aldo Rebelo a climate-change skeptic would be putting it mildly. In his days as a fiery legislator in the Communist Party of Brazil, he railed against those who say human activity is warming the globe and called the international environmental movement “nothing less, in its geopolitical essence, than the bridgehead of imperialism.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climatologists Balk as Brazil Picks Skeptic for Key Post', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Climatologists Balk as Brazil Picks Skeptic for Key Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rousseff, Dilma', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rebelo, Aldo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T01:24:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dfb97fd-c7a6-5702-aa56-8ec90931014d', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dfb97fd-c7a6-5702-aa56-8ec90931014d'}, {'abstract': 'A judge in St. Louis granted a 45-day extension to an order barring the police from using tear gas unless they provide a warning, give peaceful demonstrators time to leave and try to minimize the impact of the tear gas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/us/missouri-tear-gas-restrictions-extended.html', 'snippet': 'A judge in St. Louis granted a 45-day extension to an order barring the police from using tear gas unless they provide a warning, give peaceful demonstrators time to leave and try to minimize the impact of the tear gas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge in St. Louis granted a 45-day extension to an order she issued in December that bars the police from using tear gas unless they provide a warning, give peaceful demonstrators time to leave and try to minimize the impact of the tear gas. Judge Carol. E. Jackson of the United States District Court for the Eastern District of Missouri took the action Tuesday after lawyers for protesters and law enforcement said they needed more time to negotiate policy changes regarding the gas. The issue arose during unrest after the shooting in August of an unarmed black teenager by a white police officer in Ferguson. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri: Tear Gas Restrictions Extended ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missouri: Tear Gas Restrictions Extended', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yokley, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank':