 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1136a336-46f7-5e15-a867-96e4400cb46d', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1136a336-46f7-5e15-a867-96e4400cb46d'}, {'abstract': 'For the final number in her first opera, which opens tomorrow in New York, the iconic singer handpicked a dramatic number from the designer’s fall 2014 collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/t-magazine/courtney-love-zac-posen-kansas-city-choir-boy.html', 'snippet': 'For the final number in her first opera, which opens tomorrow in New York, the iconic singer handpicked a dramatic number from the designer’s fall 2014 collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the fashion designer Zac Posen first met Courtney Love in the summer of 1997, he realized that “with her, nothing is what it seems.” That couldn’t ring any truer today, as the grunge music icon prepares to star in “Kansas City Choir Boy” a provocative new opera love story about a singer and her musician boyfriend which was written by Todd Almond and opens tomorrow. And for her dramatic finale on stage, she’ll be wearing an equally spectacular number that she handpicked from Posen’s fall 2014 collection: a voluminous ball gown in black taffeta jacquard and duchesse satin (the performance space is so small that the gown balloons out over much of the floor). It’s a far cry from the baby-doll and slip dresses that make up the singer’s personal wardrobe. “I thought it was really important to do something that felt transformative for her,” Posen explains. “The first dress I had designed and draped didn’t feel right, and it just wasn’t surprising enough.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07posen-bobb/07posen-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07posen-bobb/07posen-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07posen-bobb/07posen-bobb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07posen-bobb/07posen-bobb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07posen-bobb/07posen-bobb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07posen-bobb/07posen-bobb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07posen-bobb/07posen-bobb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Courtney Love Wears (and Serenades) Zac Posen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Bobb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bobb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material':