: 'organizations', 'value': 'Export-Import Bank of China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nairobi (Kenya)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tanzania', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T12:11:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bree Feng', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bree', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feng', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8ef7008-1f1d-5e3f-bfec-33e1262be409', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8ef7008-1f1d-5e3f-bfec-33e1262be409'}, {'abstract': 'The bond market may be sounding an economic warning. | Why McDonald’s isn’t Shake Shack and shouldn’t be. | Coach adds celebrity cachet with acquisition of Stuart Weitzman. | Bitcoin exchange Bitstamp suspends services after breach.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/morning-agenda-bond-prices-flash-warning/', 'snippet': 'The bond market may be sounding an economic warning. | Why McDonald’s isn’t Shake Shack and shouldn’t be. | Coach adds celebrity cachet with acquisition of Stuart Weitzman. | Bitcoin exchange Bitstamp suspends services after breach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite signs that the United States economy is accelerating, a huge bond market with a strong track record for predicting economic problems may be sounding a warning, DealBook’s Peter Eavis reports. As they do in times of stress, investors are seeking the safety of government bonds. In turn, the prices of government bonds are rallying, pushing their yields to lows. The yield on the 10-year Treasury note, for instance, fell to 1.94 percent on Tuesday. In Europe, yields are even lower.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Bond Prices Flash Warning', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T12:40:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12e17c9b-27c4-5a21-b5c1-a6965c542a89', 'word_count': 2072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12e17c9b-27c4-5a21-b5c1-a6965c542a89'}, {'abstract': 'Pvt. Richard Halvey’s death in North Africa in 1943 was a loss his family never got over, but his great-niece, Kiley Bense, has sought him out through family stories and a scrapbook containing some ephemera of his short life, including his letters home.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/a-young-private-killed-in-world-war-ii-still-leaps-off-the-page/', 'snippet': 'Pvt. Richard Halvey’s death in North Africa in 1943 was a loss his family never got over, but his great-niece, Kiley Bense, has sought him out through family stories and a scrapbook containing some ephemera of his short life, including his letters...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pvt. Richard Halvey scribbled his last letter home in the passenger seat of an Army radio vehicle rumbling somewhere through North Africa in February 1943. He wrote on the desk built into the front of the car while his friend Ryan drove, passing across chocolate bars and sticks of gum. He complained about his warts (“I even have an idea they are bringing friends”). He asked after his driver’s license and his brother, Bob. He spoke of regret that he had to shave his mustache without taking a photo first (“Beards aren’t permitted in this company and mustache was starting to strain coffee etc so rather than have it dry cleaned I decided to dispense with it”). The last letter addressed to my grandmother, Patricia, his sister, was just a quick note about a $30 money order, later carefully pressed flat; his mistake in dating the top delicately corrected in Pat’s spindly hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/us/atwar-bense-gram/atwar-bense-gram-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 473, 'width': 342, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/us/atwar-bense-gram/atwar-bense-gram-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 473, 'width': 342, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/us/atwar-bense-gram/atwar-bense-gram-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/06/us/atwar-bense-gram/atwar-bense-gram-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/us/atwar-bense-gram/atwar-bense-gram-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Young Private, Killed in World War II, Still Leaps Off the Page', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cemeteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARLINGTON (VA)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T13:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kiley Bense', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kiley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bense', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/483044a0-4798-580c-afe2-3afe57755d08', 'word_count': 1329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/483044a0-4798-580c-afe2-3afe57755d08'}, {'abstract': 'High expectations and expensive initial investment seems to put some new brands in trouble before they have the chance to really start.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/christopher-burchs-retail-brand-c-wonder-closes/', 'snippet': 'High expectations and expensive initial investment seems to put some new brands in trouble before they have the chance to really start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news on Tuesday that C. Wonder, the accessibly priced, bright-’n’-busy women’s lifestyle brand started by J. Christopher Burch in 2011, had ceased operations, closing its stores, firing employees and starting to “evaluat