gue, Miss Elizabeth Reid Rogers, whose engagement to Prince Christian of Hesse has just been announced, is passing the winter in Berlin. The prince is a German submarine officer, now at Kiel, but has received a few days’ leave and will visit his fiancée. Miss Rogers is the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Richard R. Rogers, of Washington, D.C. Miss Rogers, who made her début in Washington three years ago, first met the prince in Cairo. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Jan. 8, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/blogs/08-retrospective-Christian/08-retrospective-Christian-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/08/blogs/08-retrospective-Christian/08-retrospective-Christian-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 527}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/blogs/08-retrospective-Christian/08-retrospective-Christian-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/blogs/08-retrospective-Christian/08-retrospective-Christian-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/blogs/08-retrospective-Christian/08-retrospective-Christian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/08/blogs/08-retrospective-Christian/08-retrospective-Christian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', '