a-d529-5fbf-8703-13b89ea9de17', 'word_count': 1152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e577648a-d529-5fbf-8703-13b89ea9de17'}, {'abstract': 'Zephyr Teachout reviews Steven Brill’s new book, a guide to the maze of issues in American health care and health care reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/books/review/americas-bitter-pill-by-steven-brill.html', 'snippet': 'Zephyr Teachout reviews Steven Brill’s new book, a guide to the maze of issues in American health care and health care reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Brill is not easily intimidated. The founder of Court TV and Brill’s Content, among many other ventures, Brill likes to dive deeply and quickly into complicated national policy issues — public education, health care — that he, by his own admission, knows relatively little about when he begins. This is his great appeal and can be a great frustration. It makes him vulnerable to the charisma of his sources, as was apparent in his 2011 book, “Class Warfare,” in which he seemed dazzled by individuals involved in privatizing public education, while he largely ignored the existing research.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/books/review/11BKSCOVER/0111-bks-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/books/review/11BKSCOVER/0111-bks-Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/books/review/11BKSCOVER/0111-bks-Cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/books/review/11BKSCOVER/0111-bks-Cover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/books/review/11BKSCOVER/0111-bks-Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/books/review/11BKSCOVER/0111-bks-Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/books/review/11BKSCOVER/0111-bks-Cover-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘America’s Bitter Pill,’ by Steven Brill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Ails Us', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teachout, Zephyr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brill, Steven T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "America's Bitter Pill: Money, Politics, Backroom Deals, and the Fight to Fix Our Broken Healthcare System (Book)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T15:48:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zephyr Teachout', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zephyr', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Teachout', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed2cd16d-7594-56b2-99af-798ce54e848a', 'word_count': 1728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed2cd16d-7594-56b2-99af-798ce54e848a'}, {'abstract': 'This year an increased number of less sanguine musicians have found their way into the Oscar conversation, the Carpetbagger reports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/movies/awardsseason/subversive-and-smart-scores-raise-the-volume-in-oscar-talk.html', 'snippet': 'This year an increased number of less sanguine musicians have found their way into the Oscar conversation, the Carpetbagger reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The musical tastes of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences have rarely been synonymous with cutting edge. For every Oscar doled out to the likes of Eminem and Three 6 Mafia, who in the last dozen years became the first rap and hip-hop acts to win best song, umpteen more have landed in the hands of such syrupy crooners as Phil Collins, or, God bless him, the inarguably talented, sardonically chipper Randy Newman. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/bagger/bagger-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/bagger/bagger-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/bagger/bagger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/bagger/bagger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1341, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':