d933aec1-82c6-5f28-a1a9-829b09989d66'}, {'abstract': 'The Library of Congress is putting photographs by Camilo José Vergara online, and will update the archive as he continues his time-lapse studies of sites in certain cities.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/bringing-time-lapse-photo-studies-into-real-time-online/', 'snippet': 'The Library of Congress is putting photographs by Camilo José Vergara online, and will update the archive as he continues his time-lapse studies of sites in certain cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Camilo José Vergara, the Chilean-born photographer who has documented the street culture and the changing face of America’s inner cities for 40 years, agreed to place his entire photographic archive with the Library of Congress in 2013, and now more than 400 images have been digitized and put on the library’s website. This is the first step toward making more than 10,000 works available to the public.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing Time-Lapse Photo Studies Into Real Time, Online', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vergara, Camilo Jose', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Library of Congress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T17:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/303e9e28-fe23-5dff-a5c7-0a0453e81c43', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/303e9e28-fe23-5dff-a5c7-0a0453e81c43'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker and othe