btype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/science/08antibiotic2/08antibiotic-1420668278562-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Antibiotic Stirs Hope Against Resistant Bacteria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Antibiotic Stirs Hope Against Resistant Bacteria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grady, Denise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soil', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NovoBiotic Pharmaceuticals LLC', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Northeastern University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Kim (Biologist)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T18:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a3bd177-ea49-5b5e-bec2-0ec11e0f13e7', 'word_count': 1140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a3bd177-ea49-5b5e-bec2-0ec11e0f13e7'}, {'abstract': 'For a new multimedia show at Marianne Boesky Gallery, the perennially tongue-in-cheek provocateur reimagined his X-rated 1972 cult classic with a cast of children.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/john-waters-kids-pink-flamingos/', 'snippet': 'For a new multimedia show at Marianne Boesky Gallery, the perennially tongue-in-cheek provocateur reimagined his X-rated 1972 cult classic with a cast of children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1972, John Waters raised eyebrows with the X-rated film “Pink Flamingos,” the story of Divine, played by the drag queen of the same name, a criminal hiding under the moniker Babs Johnson in a pink trailer with two plastic flamingos at the front. Waters filled it with the types of raunchy, lewd acts that turned his movies into cult favorites. More than four decades later, Waters has reinvented “Pink Flamingos” as video art for his new exhibition “Beverly Hills John,” on view at Marianne Boesky Gallery’s Chelsea location through February 14. “I’ve become my own worst enemy and rewrote the script so that it’s G-rated,” explains Waters, who hired a cast full of children — most, he says, were friends’ kids — to do a costumed table reading that was filmed over the course of one day. The 72-minute video, titled “Kiddie Flamingos,” pokes fun at the original; an exclusive preview runs here. “I see it as a new kind of perversity not to ever make an X-rated thing again,” he said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-johnwaters/07symonds-johnwaters-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-johnwaters/07symonds-johnwaters-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-johnwaters/07symonds-johnwaters-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-johnwaters/07symonds-johnwaters-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-johnwaters/07symonds-johnwaters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-johnwaters/07symonds-johnwaters-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-johnwaters/07symonds-johnwaters-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Director John Waters, a Kiddie-Friendly “Pink Flamingos”', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, John (1946- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boesky, Marianne, Gallery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Pink Flamingos (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T18:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Binlot', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Binlot', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_m