', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cdcb769-09ef-5494-b75f-48a3b9df0e49', 'word_count': 1143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cdcb769-09ef-5494-b75f-48a3b9df0e49'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Vogel’s archive will join those of other playwrights, including Eugene O’Neill and Thornton Wilder, in the Yale Collection of American Literature.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/yale-library-acquires-paula-vogel-archive/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Vogel’s archive will join those of other playwrights, including Eugene O’Neill and Thornton Wilder, in the Yale Collection of American Literature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Beinecke Rare Book and Manuscript Library at Yale has acquired the literary archive of Paula Vogel, whose play “How I Learned to Drive” won the Pulitzer Prize for drama in 1998. Ms. Vogel, who has taught at the Yale School of Drama since 2008 and is a playwright in residence at Yale Repertory Theater, is the first female playwright to be included in the library’s Yale Collection of American Literature, a repository that includes the papers of Eugene O’Neill, Thornton Wilder. A. R. Gurney and John Guare.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/theater/07vogel/07vogel-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 859, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/07/theater/07vogel/07vogel-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 859}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/theater/07vogel/07vogel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1009, 'width': 705, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/theater/07vogel/07vogel-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1009, 'width': 705, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 