u Poirier. That term has lately has been tossed around in art circles as frequently as the very same names being put up at auction. But Poirier may, in fact, have an informed perspective on the matter. After all, he wrote the book (or rather, the catalogue) on Soto, the late Venezuelan-born midcentury artist who pioneered the practice known as kinetic art. Poirier, an art history lecturer at the Sorbonne, curated “Dynamo: A Century of Light and Movement in Art 1913–2013″ last year at the Galeries Nationales du Grand Palais, which he says “tried to demonstrate, with 143 artists’ contribution, that Soto’s context and influence goes much beyond the South American historical and geographic borders within which he is regularly considered.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Retrospective of Jesús Rafael Soto Debuts on Both Sides of the Atlantic', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arsham, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soto, Jesus Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galerie Perrotin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T21:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cc9a750-4c60-54ed-b13e-3590d4b07bb4', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cc9a750-4c60-54ed-b13e-3590d4b07bb4'}, {'abstract': 'On Charlie Hebdo, and why offenses that provoke violence are the ones most worth defending.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/07/the-blasphemy-we-need/', 'snippet': 'On Charlie Hebdo, and why offenses that provoke violence are the ones most worth defending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of the vicious murders at the offices of the satirical French newspaper Charlie Hebdo today, let me offer three tentative premises about blasphemy in a free society.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Blasphemy We Need', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Earnest, Josh', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitchens, Christopher', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANTI-DEFAMATION LEAGUE', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic League', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-07T21:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f48d0fcb-b3e8-5f77-8c75-1303d568481a', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f48d0fcb-b3e8-5f77-8c75-1303d568481a'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of routing their attacks through decoy servers, the hackers sent them directly from web addresses in North Korea, the F.B.I. said. But some skeptics still wanted to see the agency’s evidence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/business/chief-says-fbi-has-no-doubt-that-north-korea-attacked-sony.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of routing their attacks through decoy servers, the hackers sent them directly from web addresses in North Korea, the F.B.I. said. But some skeptics still wanted to see the agency’s evidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The F.B.I.’s director, James B. Comey, said on Wednesday that the United States had concluded that North Korea was behind the destructive attacks on Sony Pictures partly because the hackers failed to mask their location when they broke into the company’s servers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/business/08cyber-web/08cyber-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/08/business/08cyber-web/08cyber-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/business/08cyber-web/08cyber-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/business/08cyber-web/08cyber-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/business/08cyber-web/08cyber-web-thumbStan