'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randall Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randall', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3340eb03-171e-51e0-8dab-d5c80854ce77', 'word_count': 1296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3340eb03-171e-51e0-8dab-d5c80854ce77'}, {'abstract': 'The living green roof and new populations of insects, birds and bats are testament to the success of the eco-friendly renovation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/opinion/more-life-at-the-javits-center.html', 'snippet': 'The living green roof and new populations of insects, birds and bats are testament to the success of the eco-friendly renovation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the complaints about the Jacob K. Javits Convention Center over the years — it’s too small, too outdated, too gloomy — it never reported a bat invasion until its ambitious eco-friendly renovation was completed. The center now features a 6.75-acre living green roof, bird protective glass and a new population of insects that bats can’t resist. Five species of bats have unexpectedly been attracted to this new urban habitat on the West Side along with a flurry of bird species like foraging American kestrels, according to delighted watchers at the New York City Audubon Society.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Life at the Javits Center', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Life at the Javits Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Javits, Jacob K, Convention Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Epstein Global', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FXFowle Architects', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design (LEED)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T01:40:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b93c39ad-af9c-57f7-8eed-18b881c95068', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b93c39ad-af9c-57f7-8eed-18b881c95068'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge on Wednesday struck down a state law barring sale of foie gras, ending a ban of the fatty duck liver that had lasted more than two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/us/california-ban-on-foie-gras-is-ended-.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge on Wednesday struck down a state law barring sale of foie gras, ending a ban of the fatty duck liver that had lasted more than two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge on Wednesday struck down a state law barring sale of foie gras, ending a ban of the fatty duck liver that had lasted more than two years. Animal rights groups have long condemned foie gras, which has traditionally been produced by force-feeding ducks and geese, as inhumane. Many chefs across the state, who had lamented the loss of a favored ingredient, were elated by the ruling. “The person who buys our foie gras called us from the courthouse crying with happiness,” said Jon Shook, one of the chef-owners of Animal in Los Angeles. The judge ruled the ban unconstitutional because it attempted to override existing federal law regulating poultry products. The state can appeal the decision, and animal rights groups warned that restaurants that serve it could face protests. “Foie gras is French for ‘fatty liver,’ and ‘fathead’ is the American word for the shameless chefs who actually need a law to make them stop serving the swollen, near-bursting organ of a cruelly force-fed bird,” Ingrid E. Newkirk, the president of People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals, said in an email. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Ban on Foie Gras Is Ended', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Ban on Foie Gras Is Ended', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foie Gras', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T01:40:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff0f97cf-4abc-5852-ba51-6181f6f53019', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff0f97cf-4abc-5852-ba51-6181f6f53019'}, {'abstract': 'An encouraging and realistic agreement by student and school leaders to crack down on binge drinking and partying abuses is worthy of being copied elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/opinion/spring-rush-at-the-university-of-virginia.html', 'snippet': 'An encouraging and realistic agreement by student and school leaders to crack down on binge drinking and partying abuses is worthy of being copied elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before it was discredited, a coed’s sensational story alleging gang rape at the University of Virginia prompted the university’s president, Teresa Sullivan, to suspend fraternity and sorority activities on campus so that underlying problems of frat-house excesses could be addressed. The result, announced Tuesday, is an encouraging and realistic agreement by student and university leaders to crack down on the sort of binge drinking and partying abuses that have given frat-house behavior a notorious reputation on campuses across the nation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Rush at the University of Virginia', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spring Rush at the University of Virginia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fraternities and Sororities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T01:42:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/73c8a709-c2e0-585c-bf19-06306efb4580', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73c8a709-c2e0-585c-bf19-06306efb4580'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Popkin, the former president of Hadassah, the Jewish National Fund and the World Zionist Congress, assisted immigrants and environmental projects in Israel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/nyregion/ruth-popkin-president-of-hadassah-who-worked-to-resettle-refugees-in-israel-dies-at-101.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Popkin, the former president of Hadassah, the Jewish National Fund and the World Zionist Congress, assisted immigrants and environmental projects in Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ruth Popkin, who emerged from a secular background to lead two major Jewish organizations, Hadassah and the Jewish National Fund, in work that benefited Israelis and refugees in the 1980s and ’90s, died on Jan. 2 at her home in Manhattan. She was 101.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/nyregion/POPKIN-obit/POPKIN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 903, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/08/nyregion/POPKIN-obit/POPKIN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 903}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/nyregion/POPKIN-obit/POPKIN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/nyregion/POPKIN-obit/POPKIN-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1361, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/nyregion/POPKIN-obit/POPKIN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/08/nyregion/POPKIN-obit/POPKIN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/nyregion/POPKIN-obit/POPKIN-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruth Popkin Dies at 101; Hadassah Leader Worked to Resettle Refugees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ruth Popkin, 101, President of Hadassah; Worked to Resettle Refugees in Israel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Popkin, Ruth (1913-2015)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hadassah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zionism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T01:42:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f66ca77-da49-5a08-bb34-8a3b0c52eba6', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f66ca77-da49-5a08-bb34-8a3b0c52eba6'}, {'abstract': 'Authorities in El Paso on Wednesday released the names of two men who died in a shooting at a Department of Veterans Affairs mental health clinic at Fort Bliss on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/us/texas-fort-bliss-shooter-and-victim-identified.html', 'snippet': 'Authorities in El Paso on Wednesday released the names of two men who died in a shooting at a Department of Veterans Affairs mental health clinic at Fort Bliss on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Authorities in El Paso\xa0on Wednesday\xa0released the names of two men who died in a shooting at a Department of Veterans Affairs mental health clinic at Fort Bliss on Tuesday. An Army veteran, Jerrry Serrato, 48, killed a psychologist, Timothy Fjordbak, 63, before shooting himself, the authorities said. Mr. Serrato worked at the clinic in 2013 as a scheduling clerk. At the time, according to an F.B.I. spokesman, he made verbal threats to Mr. Fjordbak at a local supermarket. The F.B.I. spokesman, who said Mr. Fjordbak did not recognize Mr. Serrato, paraphrased the threat as, “I know what you did and I will take care of it.” The agency has not established that the two men had a professional relationship. The clinic will remain closed Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Fort Bliss Shooter and Victim Identified', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Shooter and Victim Identified', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Philipps, Dave', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serrato, Jerry (1966-2015)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fjordbak, Timothy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Bliss (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'El Paso (Tex)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T01:44:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Philipps', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Philipps', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d2bee18-1778-59e0-93b0-1c875bb3de13', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d2bee18-1778-59e0-93b0-1c875bb3de13'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans and the coal industry were quick to criticize the move, which is meant to pre-empt states that refuse to submit plans of their own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/us/politics/for-states-that-dont-file-carbon-cutting-plans-epa-will-impose-model-rule-.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans and the coal industry were quick to criticize the move, which is meant to pre-empt states that refuse to submit plans of their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Environmental Protection Agency will force states to comply with a federal “model rule” to cut their carbon emissions if the states do not submit customized plans under the Obama administration’s new climate change regulations, a senior official said Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For States That Don’t File Carbon-Cutting Plans, E.P.A. Will Impose ‘Model Rule’ ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For States That Don’t File Carbon-Cutting Plans, E.P.A. Will Impose ‘Model Rule’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCabe, Janet G', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Coalition for Clean Coal Electricity', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T01:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Coral Davenport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Coral', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davenport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f60d0d05-abb0-57dc-9580-c91a72637272', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f60d0d05-abb0-57dc-9580-c91a72637272'}, {'abstract': 'Jeremy Wilcox cannot go anywhere in Wisconsin without being recognized as the guy with the nine-inch-long beard pulled by Aaron Rodgers during Green Bay’s regular-season finale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/sports/football/aaron-rodgers-pulls-a-packers-fans-beard-and-transforms-him-into-a-wisconsin-celebrity.html', 'snippet': 'Jeremy Wilcox cannot go anywhere in Wisconsin without being recognized as the guy with the nine-inch-long beard pulled by Aaron Rodgers during Green Bay’s regular-season finale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREEN BAY, Wis. — The man with the most famous red beard in Wisconsin was three bites into his chicken sandwich Tuesday night when someone approached his table at Kroll’s West, a bar and restaurant across the street from Lambeau Field, with a small placard and a Sharpie. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/sports/PACKERS1/PACKERS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 308, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/08/sports/PACKERS1/PACKERS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 308}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/sports/PACKERS1/PAC