nadequate-effort/', 'snippet': 'In which Jacob Stulberg makes me feel inadequate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY PUZZLE — All together now: Deb probably had trouble with this one because it was a rebus. Even more so, because, technically, it was a double rebus, with two rebus entries in each theme entry. And because, if we as a group could take an educated guess, Deb has never heard of a measurement called a GILL. Also, Deb was not warned that there would be math that required that she cleave her brain in two. So she tanked on this one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inadequate Effort', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T03:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7695878e-df79-549d-8c32-5ccaf2c187c6', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7695878e-df79-549d-8c32-5ccaf2c187c6'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Israel composed and sold hundreds of letters that she said had been written by Dorothy Parker, Noël Coward, Lillian Hellman and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/arts/lee-israel-a-writer-proudest-of-her-literary-forgeries-dies-at-75.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Israel composed and sold hundreds of letters that she said had been written by Dorothy Parker, Noël Coward, Lillian Hellman and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a rented storage locker on Manhattan’s Upper West Side, the writer Lee Israel kept a cache of antique typewriters: Remingtons and Royals, Adlers and Olympias. Each was tenderly curated, hung with a tag whose carefully lettered names — Edna, Dorothy, Noël, Eugene O’Neill, Hellman, Bogart, Louise Brooks — hinted at the felonious intimacy for which the machines were used.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/LEEISRAEL-obit/LEEISRAEL-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/LEEISRAEL-obit/LEEISRAEL-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/LEEISRAEL-obit/LEEISRAEL-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/LEEISRAEL-obit/LEEISRAEL-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/LEEISRAEL-obit/LEEISRAEL-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/LEEISRAEL-obit/LEEISRAEL-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/arts/LEEISRAEL-obit/LEEISRAEL-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lee Israel, a Writer Proudest of Her Literary Forgeries, Dies at 75', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lee Israel, 75, a Writer Proudes