 recently reopened restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': '“‘Craveable’ is something that’s really important to me because that’s why I go back to certain restaurants for maybe a singular dish,” explains Angela Dimayuga, executive chef of Mission Chinese Food New York, in the above video. In October 2013, much to the dismay of Manhattan’s foodie set, the original Lower East Side location of Danny Bowien’s buzzy downtown joint was shut down by the city’s health department for sanitary violations. But as New Yorkers recently toasted the end of 2014, they celebrated, too, the much-anticipated reopening of Mission Chinese Food.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making a Meal With Mission Chinese Food’s (Really Cool) Executive Chef', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TLiving', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alainna Lexie Beddie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alainna', 'middlename': 'Lexie', 'lastname': 'Beddie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a0c4b28-2e1a-5845-b0b9-37475d8cf1e8', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a0c4b28-2e1a-5845-b0b9-37475d8cf1e8'}, {'abstract': 'The Los Angeles-based artist’s new show at Marlborough Chelsea, “Space Jam,” combines commentary on other artists’ practices with basketball iconography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/t-magazine/the-artist-devin-troy-strother-turns-to-michael-jordan-and-joan-miro.html', 'snippet': 'The Los Angeles-based artist’s new show at Marlborough Chelsea, “Space Jam,” combines commentary on other artists’ practices with basketball iconography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the gallery Marlborough Chelsea called the Los Angeles-based artist Devin Troy Strother in September to ask whether he’d like to do a show with them this winter, he initially misunderstood the request: he thought they were asking him to have new work ready by December 2015. When he called back, he learned he had only a few months to conceive of an entire exhibition. For inspiration, he turned to the movie that was still queued up on his computer: the 1996 Michael Jordan vehicle “Space Jam.” The play on words proved too good to resist. “My initial thought was the idea of ‘Space Jam’ — I had to fill this huge space in a short amount of time and work very quickly,” Strother says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Artist Devin Troy Strother Turns to Michael Jordan — and Joan Miró', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandria Symonds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Symonds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccc49c57-5fb7-580e-9f25-67b8ba85ad72', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccc49c57-5fb7-580e-9f25-67b8ba85ad72'}, {'abstract': 'Designers are once again exploring such motifs as gabardine twill, cargo pockets and olive-drab hues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/t-magazine/military-inspired-looks-from-the-resort-collections.html', 'snippet': 'Designers are once again exploring such motifs as gabardine twill, cargo pockets and olive-drab hues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Military style has been a recurring theme in fashion ever since Burberry invented the trench coat. And for the resort 2015 season, designers once again explored such motifs as gabardine twill, cargo pockets and olive-drab hues. Valentino, for instance showed embroidered cargo pants and a camouflage dress, while Michael Kors incorporated such covetable items as a knee-length green trench coat that doubles as a utility cape. Since the big designers always seem to revisit the theme, it’s safe to say that this small army of styles — available in stores now — will always be on-trend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/t-magazine/08market-koh/08market-koh-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/08/t-magazine/08market-koh/08market-koh-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/t-magazine/08market-koh/08market-koh-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/t-magazine/08market-koh/08market-koh-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/t-magazine/08market-koh/08market-koh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/08/t-magazine/08market-koh/08market-koh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/t-magazine/08market-koh/08market-koh-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Military-Inspired Looks From the Resort Collections', 'kicker': 'Market Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TCulture', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Angela Koh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Angela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e010e85f-6abf-53de-82f1-1deba72897ba', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e010e85f-6abf-53de-82f1-1deba72897ba'}, {'abstract': 'In part because of wage stagnation, even smaller rises in health care costs are less affordable, a study by the Commonwealth Fund said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/business/health-premiums-rise-more-slowly-but-workers-shoulder-more-of-cost.html', 'snippet': 'In part because of wage stagnation, even smaller rises in health care costs are less affordable, a study by the Commonwealth Fund said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Charlotte Alger, 25, was working at a Home Depot just outside Boston last year, she said she earned $10.75 an hour working on the sales floor in the woodworking department. She chose one of the more comprehensive health insurance plans offered, but it came with a whopping $3,000 deductible.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/08/business/08HEALTH/08HEALTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/08/business/08HEALTH/08HEALTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/0