w-to-regain-his-form-at-the-plate.html', 'snippet': 'Drew, who has agreed to a one-year, $5 million deal, hit far below his career average last year after missing spring training and the first two months of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the final week of the 2014 regular season, when almost every microphone and camera lens at Yankees games was pointed in Derek Jeter’s direction, Stephen Drew was quietly finishing his worst year in the major leagues. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09yankees1/09yankees1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09yankees1/09yankees1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09yankees1/09yankees1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09yankees1/09yankees1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09yankees1/09yankees1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09yankees1/09yankees1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09yankees1/09yankees1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Are Banking on Stephen Drew to Regain His Form at the Plate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Counting on Drew to Rediscover His Swing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drew, Stephen (1983- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T14:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdc24750-ed19-5717-a6bb-bf4c9ab3ae42', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdc24750-ed19-5717-a6bb-bf4c9ab3ae42'}, {'abstract': 'For their sophomore album’s title single, “Pour It On,” the band approached the filmmaker Richard Heslop, who offered up a video starring the performance artist Rachel Gomme.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/new-build-pour-it-on-video/', 'snippet': 'For their sophomore album’s title single, “Pour It On,” the band approached the filmmaker Richard Heslop, who offered up a video starring the performance artist Rachel Gomme.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We had no real desire to release a video for this song unless we found something we really liked,” says the British synthesizer artist and programmer Felix Martin of “Pour It On,” the new single from his band New Build. It was serendipity, then, when the band received an entrancing, unreleased video by the filmmaker Richard Heslop, known for his work with the Smiths and the Cure, which fit perfectly with the atmospheric track. “I had seen a show reel of his work, and I really liked his approach to editing, as well as the way he worked with sound footage and different kinds of textures,” Martin says. The band approached Heslop, who offered up the footage that would eventually become the video for “Pour It On.” It stars the British performance artist Rachel Gomme, who walks the beach while continuously filling her dress up with stones as a personal test of endurance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-newbuild/07symonds-newbuild-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-newbuild/07symonds-newbuild-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-newbuild/07symonds-newbuild-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-newbuild/07symonds-newbuild-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-newbuild/07symonds-newbuild-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-newbuild/07symonds-newbuild-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/07/t-magazine/07symonds-newbuild/07symonds-newbuild-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artistic Video from the Hot Chip Spinoff New Build', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Felix', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hot Chip (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T14:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ilana Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ilana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9d6b6a1-b347-5e95-b634-351b9d550ac6', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9d6b6a1-b347-5e95-b634-351b9d550ac6'}, {'abstract': 'Unexpected musical names are coming up this awards season, including Patti Smith, who said she felt a responsibility when it came to composing a ballad for “Noah.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/singing-oscars-tune/', 'snippet': 'Unexpected musical names are coming up this awards season, including Patti Smith, who said she felt a responsibility when it came to composing a ballad for “Noah.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For even the most established musician, composing for film can be terrifying. As Patti Smith, the “godmother of punk” who wrote the lullaby “Mercy Is” for “Noah,” told the Bagger: “There’s nothing worse than when you’re watching a movie and one of the characters takes you out and you no longer believe the atmosphere. The same thing can happen with the wrong piece of music, so I felt a responsibility.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singing Oscar’s Tune', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T14:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4d5e3f5-a4e7-59ad-8e6c-f4d43e2e5ef9', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4d5e3f5-a4e7-59ad-8e6c-f4d43e2e5ef9'}, {'abstract': 'Muve, a subscription service for prepaid mobile phones, will be discontinued in February and customers will be moved to Deezer, the company said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/business/media/deezer-a-french-streaming-service-to-buy-muve-music.html', 'snippet': 'Muve, a subscription service for prepaid mobile phones, will be discontinued in February and customers will be moved to Deezer, the company said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the race to sign up subscribers for digital music, the French streaming service Deezer has had success around the world but is little known in the United States, where it faces more established competitors like Spotify, Rhapsody and Google Play.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Streaming Service Acquires Toehold in the U.S. ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'French Streaming Service Acquires Toehold in the U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deezer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value':