New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c7d56873-cea0-5f1e-8a7d-39cb00061bd1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c7d56873-cea0-5f1e-8a7d-39cb00061bd1'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives:1915 Heavy Flooding Forces Wedding Party to Travel in Punts.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/1915-wedding-party-travels-in-punts/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives:1915 Heavy Flooding Forces Wedding Party to Travel in Punts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As a result of the floods there was a romantic military wedding at Bray yesterday.The bride, bridegroom and the guests had to travel part of the way to the church in punts. The bridegroom was Captain Forbes Adams, of the Indian army, who only arrived here last night straight from the trenches on a week’s leave. The bride was Miss Pitman, the second daughter of Mr. F. Pitman, the well-known Cambridge ‘‘Blue.’’ Every arrangement had been made by Mr. Pitman to enable the wedding party to get to and from the church, for his house, Bray Mead, is completely surrounded by water. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Jan. 8, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-floods/09-iht-retrospective-floods-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-floods/09-iht-retrospective-floods-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-floods/09-iht-retrospective-floods-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo',