 Institute has helped the gritty Tenderloin neighborhood define its cultural assets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Ira Watkins paints his pictures in a faded Dodge van with velveteen seats parked beside a center for seniors in the Tenderloin, a seamy part of town frequently associated with displaced loners, drug addicts in squalid alleyways and other manifestations of human misery.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Wealth Changes the Tenderloin, a Move to Preserve Artistic ‘Gems’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Wealth Changes the Tenderloin, a Move to Preserve Artistic ‘Gems’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Patricia Leigh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gentrification', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wildflowers Institute', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T16:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Leigh Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02551179-ee2c-583e-b040-be89bccc029b', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02551179-ee2c-583e-b040-be89bccc029b'}, {'abstract': 'Graham W. J. Beal, who led the museum through an unprecedented threat to its world-class collection during Detroit’s federal bankruptcy, will retire in June.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/detr