int_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honda Fined for Violations of Safety Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honda Is Fined for Violations of Safety Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T17:54:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8df5c23-1372-579c-be8b-511baed2f714', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8df5c23-1372-579c-be8b-511baed2f714'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: 1965: Elizabeth Taylor Decides Not To Renounce Her U.S. Citizenship.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/1965-actress-still-a-u-s-citizen/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: 1965: Elizabeth Taylor Decides Not To Renounce Her U.S. Citizenship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Elizabeth Taylor tried to renounce her U.S. citizenship but failed because she could not bring herself to disavow ‘‘all allegiance and fidelity’’ to the United States, the State Department said today. The London-born film star reportedly said the United States had been good to her and that she did not want to imply that she bore it ill will by using such language. Miss Taylor’s New York spokesman said she decided to renounce her citizenship because she wanted to have the same citizenship as her husband, British actor Richard Burton. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 8, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-taylor/09-iht-retrospective-taylor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-taylor/09-iht-retrospective-taylor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 625}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-taylor/09-iht-retrospective-taylor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 978, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-taylor/09-iht-retrospective-taylor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 978, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-taylor/09-iht-retrospective-taylor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-taylor/09-iht-retrospective-taylor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/blogs/09-iht-retrospective-taylor/09-iht-retrospective-taylor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Actress Still a U.S. Citizen', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burton, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Elizabeth (1932-2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T17:55:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e72c5469-b173-5e90-bf61-c6cf0c5f7b31', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e72c5469-b173-5e90-bf61-c6cf0c5f7b31'}, {'abstract': 'Like last year when the Israeli and Palestinian entries followed similar plots, this year’s Oscar entries from Estonia and Georgia tell nearly the same story, though in very different ways.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/a-foreign-film-coincidence-two-years-in-a-row/', 'snippet': 'Like last year when the Israeli and Palestinian entries followed similar plots, this year’s Oscar entries from Estonia and Georgia tell nearly the same story, though in very different ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In last year’s competition for the Oscar for best foreign-language film, something seemingly odd, the apparent product of coincidence, happened: the Israeli and Palestinian submissions dealt with the same story. Both Yuval Adler’s “Bethlehem” and Hany Abu-Assad’s “Omar,” which eventually received a nomination, focused on the relationship between a young Palestinian informer and his control agent in Israeli intelligence, and the two movies even ended the same way, with the mole turning on his handler.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Foreign Film Coincidence, Two Years in a Row', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Estonia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T18:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cf9d87f-2c26-5eb2-aaff-84a5fbeb5f89', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cf9d87f-2c26-5eb2-aaff-84a5fbeb5f89'}, {'abstract': 'The election had to be decided by the Legislature after the front-runner, Gov. Peter Shumlin, a Democrat, failed to win 50 percent of the vote in November.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/us/vermont-legislature-gives-governor-a-third-term.html', 'snippet': 'The election had to be decided by the Legislature after the front-runner, Gov. Peter Shumlin, a Democrat, failed to win 50 percent of the vote in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTPELIER, Vt. — November came and went, and even until Thursday, Vermonters did not know who would be inaugurated as governor. They seemed to take this uncertainty in stride, much as they ignored the record-breaking low temperature of minus 20 degrees that encased the gray granite statehouse here in a brittle air.', 'print_section': 'A', 'p