://article/ae70162e-0541-54e7-b898-4a0b0a2bc4ea'}, {'abstract': 'Based on a short story by the science-fiction writer Robert A. Heinlein, “Predestination” tracks the journeys of a Temporal Agent assigned to right wrongs before they happen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/movies/predestination-starring-ethan-hawke.html', 'snippet': 'Based on a short story by the science-fiction writer Robert A. Heinlein, “Predestination” tracks the journeys of a Temporal Agent assigned to right wrongs before they happen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jumping across time and space is tough, thankless business in “Predestination,” a slab of science-fiction speculation draped in old-fashioned detective story crepe. The story centers on a temporal agent, a futuristic enforcer (he tries to right wrongs before they happen) nicely played by Ethan Hawke with a hungry, hangdog look that suggests that his character has spent long nights howling in the wasteland, often without either a scrap or a prayer. Whether slinking through 1985 or another vintage year (usually while chasing down a bomber), the temporal agent looks like a classic lone wolf. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/09PREDESTINATION1/PREDESTINATION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/09PREDESTINATION1/PREDESTINATION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/09PREDESTINATION1/PREDESTINATION1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/09PREDESTINATI