abstract': 'Michael Bloomberg, who recently returned to running the company, said in a note to staff that the departure of Laurie Hays, a senior executive editor, was amicable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/business/media/laurie-hays-to-leave-bloomberg-news.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Bloomberg, who recently returned to running the company, said in a note to staff that the departure of Laurie Hays, a senior executive editor, was amicable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laurie Hays, a senior executive editor at Bloomberg News, is leaving the company, people with knowledge of the matter said on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High-Ranking Editor to Leave Bloomberg News', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bloomberg News', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T23:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63906a16-cf7b-5282-ad19-e4ec83ddd39a', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63906a16-cf7b-5282-ad19-e4ec83ddd39a'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Olympic Committee on Thursday chose Boston as the American bid city for the 2024 Summer Games, over Los Angeles, San Francisco and Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/sports/olympics/boston-to-be-us-bid-city-for-2024-olympics.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Olympic Committee on Thursday chose Boston as the American bid city for the 2024 Summer Games, over Los Angeles, San Francisco and Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boston, which stages a celebrated marathon and has a rich history of professional championships in basketball, football, baseball and hockey, will now swing for the fences in international sport as it seeks to host the 2024 Summer Olympics.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09olympics-boston/09olympics-boston-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09olympics-boston/09olympics-boston-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09olympics-boston/09olympics-boston-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09olympics-boston/09olympics-boston-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09olympics-boston/09olympics-boston-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09olympics-boston/09olympics-boston-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/sports/09olympics-boston/09olympics-boston-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S.O.C. Chooses Boston as Candidate for 2024 Summer Olympics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boston Is Awarded a Shot at Winning a New Set of Rings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2024)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Olympic Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T23:33:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca927592-c8c8-5918-8f14-d11fe14a9d1f', 'word_count': 1176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca927592-c8c8-5918-8f14-d11fe14a9d1f'}, {'abstract': 'In “Dark Summer,” a teenager becomes the victim of his online obsession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/movies/dark-summer-focuses-on-a-hacker-under-house-arrest.html', 'snippet': 'In “Dark Summer,” a teenager becomes the victim of his online obsession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is something profoundly draining and suffocatingly incestuous about watching a film that’s dedicated to watching a computer screen. It’s as if directors hoped to lure audiences away from their hand-held and desktop devices by focusing on characters who are glued to their own. All they’re likely to end up with, however, are movies that hardly ever move.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Captive, and Not Just to the Internet', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Captive, and Not Just to the Internet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solet, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilchrist, Keir', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dark Summer (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-08T23:37:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/23c77d68-fdfc-55f7-8438-c7727cd4bc86', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23c77d68-fdfc-55f7-8438-c7727cd4bc86'}, {'abstract': 'They cost the country billions, but they don’t save lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/opinion/skip-your-annual-physical.html', 'snippet': 'They cost the country billions, but they don’t save lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE all make resolutions and promises to live healthier and better lives, to make the world a better place. Not having my annual physical is one small way I can help reduce health care costs — and save myself time, worry and a worthless exam. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/opinion/09Emanuel/09Emanuel-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 