, 'value': "It's All So Quiet (Movie)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T00:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9c8079e-38f8-5db6-b60a-8b2e19160ead', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9c8079e-38f8-5db6-b60a-8b2e19160ead'}, {'abstract': 'JK Youn’s “Ode to My Father” has an obsessive hero seeking relatives lost in the Korean War.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/movies/jk-youns-ode-to-my-father-features-a-korean-odyssey.html', 'snippet': 'JK Youn’s “Ode to My Father” has an obsessive hero seeking relatives lost in the Korean War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Little more than an archipelago of historical set pieces linked by a syrupy causeway of sentiment, JK Youn’s “Ode to My Father” may have slain them in South Korea, but its packaged pain and bullet-point structure are likely to leave Western audiences cold.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Searching for Family Along a River of Tears', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Searching for Family Along a River of Tears', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Youn, JK', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T00:06:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b99563a3-d18d-5a42-84b9-671bae4ae3a8', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b99563a3-d18d-5a42-84b9-671bae4ae3a8'}, {'abstract': 'The Super Bowl has become more accessible, to more teams, in recent years, as our dynasty index and accessibility index show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/upshot/nfl-dynasties-on-the-decline.html', 'snippet': 'The Super Bowl has become more accessible, to more teams, in recent years, as our dynasty index and accessibility index show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the Broncos and the Seahawks — last year’s Super Bowl contestants — hosting playoffs games this weekend, the N.F.L. may seem like a closed club, with the same few teams winning every year. Actually, that has never been less true than now.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Dynasties, on the Decline', 'kicker': 'Postseason Chase', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dynasties a Thing of the Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowenstein, Roger', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T00:09:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Lowenstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a2a5e89-2db6-5a52-a4b7-48c448716f58', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a2a5e89-2db6-5a52-a4b7-48c448716f58'}, {'abstract': 'In Christopher Denham’s “Preservation,” a hunting party finds itself pursued.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/movies/preservation-christopher-denhams-new-thriller.html', 'snippet': 'In Christopher Denham’s “Preservation,” a hunting party finds itself pursued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A young money manager, his bored wife and his brother, a war veteran, head into the woods to hunt deer in “Preservation,” and as the venerable movie trailer cliché has it, the hunters become the hunted. That’s assured from the opening sequence, which patiently tails their truck at a respectful stalker-cam distance down winding country roads.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/09PRESERVATION/PRESERVATION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/09PRESERVATION/PRESERVATION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/09PRESERVATION/PRESERVATION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/09PRESERVATION/PRESERVATION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/09PRESERVATION/PRESERVATION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wid