 are witnessing something scripted for a grade school playground. In the stubborn showdown between the police and Mayor Bill de Blasio — turned backs, forgiven infractions — many citizens can only watch with sentiments that flow from bemusement to revulsion, if not a mixture of both.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/09SLOWDOWN1Y/09SLOWDOWN1Y-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/09SLOWDOWN1Y/09SLOWDOWN1Y-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/09SLOWDOWN1Y/09SLOWDOWN1Y-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/09SLOWDOWN1Y/09SLOWDOWN1Y-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/09SLOWDOWN1Y/09SLOWDOWN1Y-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/09SLOWDOWN1Y/09SLOWDOWN1Y-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/09SLOWDOWN1Y/09SLOWDOWN1Y-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'De Blasio and Police Both Blamed for a Feud That Few Like ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'De Blasio and Police Both Blamed for a Feud That Few Like', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kleinfield, N R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, Wenjian (1982-2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramos, Rafael (1974-2014)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T01:05:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By N. R. Kleinfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'N.', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Kleinfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ac5892c-65e2-5d9a-bfd2-52989e8e3bd8', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ac5892c-65e2-5d9a-bfd2-52989e8e3bd8'}, {'abstract': 'Leaders in the Republican Party seem to be wrong on everything that counts, but no amount of contrary evidence will get them to change their minds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/opinion/paul-krugman-voodoo-time-machine.html', 'snippet': 'Leaders in the Republican Party seem to be wrong on everything that counts, but no amount of contrary evidence will get them to change their minds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of us in the econ biz were wondering how the new leaders of Congress would respond to the sharp increase in American economic growth that, we now know, began last spring. After years of insisting that President Obama is responsible for a we