 those takeout containers are truly noxious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Score another victory for the sustainable city. New York is broadly banning expanded polystyrene, the all but unavoidable, near-everlasting plastic foam used in drink cups, food trays, packing peanuts and many, many other things. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Welcome Ban on Forever Foam', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Welcome Ban on Forever Foam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T01:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c1a4c25-c022-5cbb-ae4b-d01dc28a6c54', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c1a4c25-c022-5cbb-ae4b-d01dc28a6c54'}, {'abstract': 'The smuggling of firearms by a Delta baggage handler should shock anyone who has spent time in an airport security line.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/opinion/gun-running-in-the-jet-age.html', 'snippet': 'The smuggling of firearms by a Delta baggage handler should shock anyone who has spent time in an airport security line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone who has spent time waiting shoeless on an airport check-in line — in fact, anyone who flies — should pay serious attention to the recent revelation that an airline baggage handler was allegedly able to smuggle 153 firearms in an accomplice’s carry-on bag on 17 Delta flights from Atlanta to New York during a seven-month period. The reason, shocking in its simplicity, is that most back-room airport workers are not required to pass through metal detectors on the way to the job. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gun-Running in the Jet Age', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gun-Running in the Jet Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T01:39:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b6bb8ad-872f-5c70-a5c1-fc8fb42fba99', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b6bb8ad-872f-5c70-a5c1-fc8fb42fba99'}, {'abstract': 'A company that buys consumer debt is expected to vacate 4,500 court judgments over concerns that its debt collection lawsuits were riddled with errors and fabrications.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/08/debt-buyer-faces-fine-and-loss-of-thousands-of-court-judgments/', 'snippet': 'A company that buys consumer debt is expected to vacate 4,500 court judgments over concerns that its debt collection lawsuits were riddled with errors and fabrications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In courtrooms across New York State, lawsuits poured in by the hundreds as if manufactured on an assembly line. Some included generic testimony, others relied on bogus affidavits, churned out so rapidly that they were seldom viewed for accuracy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/business/DEBT/DEBT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/business/DEBT/DEBT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/business/DEBT/DEBT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/business/DEBT/DEBT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1228, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/business/DEBT/DEBT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/09/business/DEBT/DEBT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/business/DEBT/DEBT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Debt Buyer Faces Fine and Loss of Thousands of Court Judgments', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Debt Buyer Faces Fine in Doubtful Lawsuits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debt Collection', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Encore Capital Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T01:43:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ad146e4-391e-5343-a140-90349772b295', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ad146e4-391e-5343-a140-90349772b295'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Vickers, the sergeant-at-arms of Canada’s House of Commons, rose from relative obscurity when his role in ending an attack on Parliament was revealed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/world/americas/kevin-vickers-from-sergeant-at-arms-to-canadian-ambassador-.html', 'snippet': 'Kevin Vickers, the sergeant-at-arms of Canada’s House of Commons, rose from relative obscurity when his role in ending an attack on Parliament was revealed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin Vickers, the sergeant-at-arms of Canada’s House of Commons who became a national hero in October after an armed attack on Parliament, was appointed the ambassador to Ireland on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cr