int_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ty Hensley, a Top Yankees Prospect, Is Left With Broken Jaw After Altercation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yanks Prospect Is Left With Broken Jaw After Altercation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hensley, Ty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T02:43:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb69eab7-32fd-5369-8e67-55cf11ca404e', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb69eab7-32fd-5369-8e67-55cf11ca404e'}, {'abstract': 'Former President Alberto Fujimori on Thursday was convicted of using public money to influence newspaper coverage during his 2000 re-election campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/world/americas/peru-jailed-ex-president-is-convicted-of-corruption.html', 'snippet': 'Former President Alberto Fujimori on Thursday was convicted of using public money to influence newspaper coverage during his 2000 re-election campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Former President Alberto Fujimori on Thursday was convicted of using public money to influence newspaper coverage during his 2000 re-election campaign. Mr. Fujimori is already serving a 25-year sentence, handed down in 2009, for ordering the killings of 25 people during a war with leftist guerrillas. On Thursday, he was sentenced to eight years to be served concurrently with his earlier sentence so it will not add to his time in jail. Mr. Fujimori, who was president from 1990 to 2000, was also ordered to pay restitution of about $1 million. Local news media reported that evidence showed that a representative of Mr. Fujimori paid newspapers up to $3,000 for articles smearing his opponents. The verdict could affect the political prospects of his daughter, Keiko Fujimori, a probable candidate for president next year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peru: Jailed Ex-President Is Convicted of Corruption', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peru: Jailed Ex-President Is Convicted of Corruption', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peru', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fujimori, Alberto K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T02:46:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/09ea76f1-1331-5537-8413-23554304052f', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09ea76f1-1331-5537-8413-23554304052f'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for Richard J. Combs, the former Eutawville, S.C., police chief, say he fired his weapon because his life was in jeopardy as he was fighting Bernard Bailey, an unarmed black man, in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/us/south-carolina-former-police-chiefs-defense-begins.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for Richard J. Combs, the former Eutawville, S.C., police chief, say he fired his weapon because his life was in jeopardy as he was fighting Bernard Bailey, an unarmed black man, in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prosecutors on Thursday rested their case in the murder trial of a former police chief accused of killing Bernard Bailey, an unarmed black man, in 2011. Lawyers for Richard J. Combs, the former Eutawville, S.C., police chief, immediately began their defense before the jury in Orangeburg County. Prosecutors say Mr. Combs was reckless when he tried to serve an arrest warrant on Mr. Bailey, but Mr. Combs’s lawyers say the chief fired his weapon because his life was in jeopardy when the two men fought. Jurors on Thursday heard from six witnesses, including Brittany Dantzler, a former Eutawville official who saw the shooting and said she thought Mr. Combs was at risk of being “run over” by Mr. Bailey’s truck. Mr. Combs is expected to testify as soon as Friday. The United States Department of Justice investigated the shooting but did not file any charges. Last year, the town agreed to a $400,000 settlement in a lawsuit related to the shooting. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Carolina: Former Police Chief’s Defense Begins ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Carolina: Former Police Chief’s Defense Begins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blinder, Alan S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bailey, Bernard (1956-2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Combs, Richard J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': '