cee0247238', 'word_count': 2524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a8ff7f4-e603-50d5-baa0-34cee0247238'}, {'abstract': 'In his first year as New York City’s mayor, Mr. de Blasio has taken steps to close the economic gap between the rich and poor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/nyregion/outside-the-spotlight-bill-de-blasio-wages-a-war-on-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'In his first year as New York City’s mayor, Mr. de Blasio has taken steps to close the economic gap between the rich and poor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, just days into his tenure as New York City’s 109th mayor, Bill de Blasio fell under criticism for his approach to eating pizza, one that depended on cutlery. That this minor peculiarity became a matter of mass media interest — Jon Stewart, Time magazine, The Guardian all weighed in obsessively — only confirmed Mr. de Blasio’s status as a national celebrity. He had been elected by a wide margin, promising to rectify the imbalances of an ever more economically divided city. On the right were predictions that Mr. de Blasio’s progressive commitments would return the city to the anarchy of the 1970s; elsewhere was the concern that we were now to be led by someone dull and dismissible. And yet we haven’t ended up in an era of another Abe Beame.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/nyregion/11BIG/11BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/nyregion/11BIG/11BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/nyregion/11BIG/11BIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption