{'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/71589078-108f-5e3d-a21c-40fb6de2d31e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/71589078-108f-5e3d-a21c-40fb6de2d31e'}, {'abstract': 'Wayne R. Kubs, 38, a top ranking civil-service veteran, is the second person to file suit against the town of Rutherford, alleging that he was bypassed for a police opening because of favoritism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/nyregion/a-new-jersey-town-faces-scrutiny-on-police-hiring.html', 'snippet': 'Wayne R. Kubs, 38, a top ranking civil-service veteran, is the second person to file suit against the town of Rutherford, alleging that he was bypassed for a police opening because of favoritism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Wayne R. Kubs, a former Navy corpsman who spent years deployed in the Middle East, applied to the police force in his hometown in New Jersey, he thought his chances were good. He had grown up in Rutherford, a working-class borough of 18,000 people and about eight miles from Manhattan. He was a volunteer firefighter and a tactical paramedic for the largest hospital in the state, sometimes part of a SWAT team.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/RUTHERFORDweb3/RUTHERFORDweb3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/RUTHERFORDweb3/RUTHERFORDweb3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/nyregion/RUTHERFORDweb3/RUTHERFORDweb3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ