e': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3a43f56-344c-56f9-b534-6d2552689cff', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3a43f56-344c-56f9-b534-6d2552689cff'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from The International Herald Tribune archives: 1915: Anger Over The Death of Garibaldi’s Grandson.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/1915-anger-over-garibaldis-death/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from The International Herald Tribune archives: 1915: Anger Over The Death of Garibaldi’s Grandson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Feeling against the Austrians, and against the Germans who are supporting them, is growing daily more intense, and it now seems that the nation has been fired to a hatred ripe for action, the death of Lieutenant Bruno Garibaldi having supplied the necessary spark. The death of Costante Garibaldi added fuel to the fire. All Rome mourns Garibaldi’s grandson ‘‘tué à l’ennemi,’’ as the simple but eloquent inscription on Bruno’s coffin read. As I telegraphed to you yesterday [Jan. 8], no funeral ever drew so vast a crowd, and General Ricciotti Garibaldi’s heartfelt words over his son’s grave, foreshadowing Italy’s speedy avenging of the lieutenant’s death, stirred the blood of the whole nation. There was, at the beginning of the European war, a great outburst on the part of the Italian people. War against Austria appeared inevitable, as a consequence of the aggressive action against Servia, which action, in case it proved successful, would have profoundly affected the Balkanic equilibrium. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Jan. 10, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/blogs/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/10/blogs/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/blogs/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/blogs/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1192, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/blogs/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/10/blogs/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/blogs/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno/10-retrospective-garibaldi-bruno-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Anger Over Garibaldi’s Death', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocation