bject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T16:44:52+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/6ba87d72-caf2-50d8-a4e8-a4239484b5cf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/6ba87d72-caf2-50d8-a4e8-a4239484b5cf'}, {'abstract': 'On the eve of the fall 2015 shows, T spoke to five designers about their favorite pubs for the traditional British meal.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/london-mens-wear-designers-on-where-to-savor-a-sunday-roast/', 'snippet': 'On the eve of the fall 2015 shows, T spoke to five designers about their favorite pubs for the traditional British meal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With another round of London’s men’s collections\xa0kicking off today, weary showgoers shuttling around town will need sustenance. Though the U.K.’s gastronomic tradition can’t match those of the other men’s wear capitals, Italy and France, one particular meal is inarguably owned by the Brits. The Sunday roast, a weekend meal with friends and family, can be enjoyed at home or at one of the countless pubs dotted around the capital. Choose between lamb, chicken or beef (or the veggie options) and you’ll be served generously with roasted potatoes, cooked vegetables, gravy and an oversized Yorkshire pudding.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09roast-hellqvist-1/09roast-hellqvist-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09roast-hellqvist-1/09roast-hellqvist-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',