ty’s management after the lane-closing affair that entangled Gov. Chris Christie and several of his allies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/10/nyregion/christies-top-appointee-at-port-authority-is-leaving.html', 'snippet': 'The departure of Deborah Gramiccioni will be the start of the restructuring of the authority’s management after the lane-closing affair that entangled Gov. Chris Christie and several of his allies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year after her predecessor resigned over his role in the shutting of traffic lanes leading to the George Washington Bridge, Gov. Chris Christie’s top executive appointee at the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey is stepping down.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/nyregion/10PORTweb/10PORTweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/10/nyregion/10PORTweb/10PORTweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/nyregion/10PORTweb/10PORTweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/nyregion/10PORTweb/10PORTweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/nyregion/10PORTweb/10PORTweb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/10/nyregion/10PORTweb/10PORTweb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/nyregion/10PORTweb/10PORTweb-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Port Agency’s Reorganization to Start With Exit of Executive Christie Picked', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Port Agency’s Reorganization to Start With Exit of Executive Christie Picked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGeehan, Patrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gramiccioni, Deborah L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'George Washington Bridge', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T16:59:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78de2f00-2fa5-5217-8e57-6d40790d2d83', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78de2f00-2fa5-5217-8e57-6d40790d2d83'}, {'abstract': 'The Oscar-shortlisted documentary “Art and Craft” examines the case of Mark Landis, who copied everything from Picassos to “Peanuts” panels and then donated them to museums.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/the-art-forger-who-wasnt-in-it-for-money/', 'snippet': 'The Oscar-shortlisted documentary “Art and Craft” examines the case of Mark Landis, who copied everything from Picassos to “Peanuts” panels and then donated them to museums.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Even in the shadowy world of art forgery, Mark Landis seemed an aberration. From the 1980s on, he copied all kinds of paintings and drawings, from Picassos and Monets to panels from “Peanuts” and illustrations from “The Cat in the Hat.” But instead of selling his counterfeits, he assumed the role of a philanthropist, sometimes disguising himself as a priest, and donated his fake masterpieces to unsuspecting museums.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/artcraft/artcraft-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/artcraft/artcraft-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/artcraft/artcraft-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/artcraft/artcraft-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/artcraft/artcraft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/artcraft/artcraft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/arts/artcraft/artcraft-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Art Forger Who Wasn’t in It for Money', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forgery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Becker, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cullman, Sam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grausman, Jennifer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landis, Mark A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T17:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3f5b40e-05b4-5289-98cc-49c0c03d18c6', 'word_count': 1318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3f5b40e-05b4-5289-98cc-49c0c03d18c6'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Housing Administration’s plan to lower its annual insurance premiums could make buying a first home possible for a quarter-million more borrowers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/realestate/fha-loans-more-affordable.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Housing Administration’s plan to lower its annual insurance premiums could make buying a first home possible for a quarter-million more borrowers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An announcement by the Obama administration that the Federal Housing Administration would lower its annual insurance premiums by 0.5 percentage point could make it possible for a quarter-