in-america.html', 'snippet': 'Also, some surprising conclusions about tips for taxi drivers, the problem of female poverty, a dynamic flu map and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If this is not proof of American exceptionalism, I am not sure what is. When Pew Research Center’s Global Attitudes survey asked people around the world how their day was going, it found that people in poor countries were often more likely than those in rich ones to report having a good day. But in America, where the pursuit of happiness ranks with life and liberty, the data shows we are pretty happy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/upshot/10UP-Stuff/10UP-Stuff-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 490, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/14/upshot/10UP-Stuff/10UP-Stuff-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 490}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/upshot/10UP-Stuff/10UP-Stuff-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/upshot/10UP-Stuff/10UP-Stuff-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1672, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/upshot/10UP-Stuff/10UP-Stuff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/14/upshot/10UP-Stuff/10UP-Stuff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/upshot/10UP-Stuff/1