g', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The “Punk Ballerina” Karole Armitage Brings Together Lacroix, Gaultier, Koons and More', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T17:59:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/4921c043-766a-5ada-9170-6a753ad4ebba', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/4921c043-766a-5ada-9170-6a753ad4ebba'}, {'abstract': 'The 26-year-old created a voyeuristic look at the new line, which features a cool merging of activewear with unconventional tailoring and knitwear.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/09/sebastiaan-pieter-debuts-his-fallwinter-2015-mens-collection-in-an-eerie-new-video/', 'snippet': 'The 26-year-old created a voyeuristic look at the new line, which features a cool merging of activewear with unconventional tailoring and knitwear.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I wanted to make a video to place the clothes, the Pieter guy, more in a ‘reality’ context,” says Sebastiaan Pieter, the 26-year-old Dutch designer who will present the fall/winter 2015 collection of his nascent line, Pieter, on Saturday in London. Collaborating with Max Pearmain, the stylist and editor of fashion magazine Arena Homme Plus, as well as the art director Jonathan Baron, Pieter created a voyeuristic look at the new collection, which features a cool merging of activewear with unconventional tailoring and knitwear: athletic tights layered under knit tops with slashed openings (inspired by Lucio Fontana paintings) and unstructured outerwear made from fabrics typically used for uniforms of the Royal Guard. Filmed in a bleak office environment with expansive views of London’s Financial District and composed of grainy time-stamped clips mimicking security footage, the video, which will run on loop during the presentation, “grounds the clothes,” says the young designer (albeit rather eerily). For this new season, as with his previous two collections, Pieter, who worked both in publishing (Fantastic Man) and design (for Jil Sander under Raf Simons) before launching his own line in early 2014, explores the loosening and blurring of men’s sartorial norms through more feminine cuts and roomier silhouettes. “There’s a dark twisted way of sexuality,” Pieter says, “that I’m always thinking about.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sebastiaan Pieter Debuts His Fall/Winter 2015 Men’s Collection in an Eerie New Video', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pieter, Sebastiaan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T18:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a03704bb-98f3-5b4f-b2ed-b6ea8e9633ef', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a03704bb-98f3-5b4f-b2ed-b6ea8e9633ef'}, {'abstract': 'Mostafa Kamel Mostafa, 56, a former imam in North London, had been convicted of 11 terrorism-related charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/10/nyregion/british-cleric-sentenced-to-life-in-prison-in-terror-case.html', 'snippet': 'Mostafa Kamel Mo