t of late 1960s and 1970s SoCal fashion. There’s the orange crochet minidress worn by one character, the Rudi Gernreich-style bikini on another, the wacky purple suit of a square dentist trying to be hip. The movie, out today with an all-star cast (Joaquin Phoenix, Josh Brolin, Benicio Del Toro, Owen Wilson, Reese Witherspoon and the promising newcomer Katherine Waterston), follows the sandal-wearing gumshoe Larry “Doc” Sportello (Phoenix) around Los Angeles as clues pile up in a shaggy-dog mystery. But Phoenix’s character is more hippie fashion plate than noir tough guy in his green army coat, navy turtleneck, jean jacket and slew of vintage flannel shirts. And it’s all thanks to Mark Bridges, the film’s costume designer, who has worked with Anderson since before “Boogie Nights.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09vice-kurutz-1/09vice-kurutz-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09vice-kurutz-1/09vice-kurutz-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09vice-kurutz-1/09vice-kurutz-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09vice-kurutz-1/09vice-kurutz-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09vice-kurutz-1/09vice-kurutz-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thu