alue': 'Companhio Hiato (Theater Company)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T20:40:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cad71ff-bcaa-5091-bacd-d7614592cd3c', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cad71ff-bcaa-5091-bacd-d7614592cd3c'}, {'abstract': 'For many Israelis, any terrorism by Islamic extremists bolsters the view that their conflict with the Palestinians is part of a larger clash of civilizations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/10/world/europe/israelis-link-terrorism-in-france-to-their-own-struggles.html', 'snippet': 'For many Israelis, any terrorism by Islamic extremists bolsters the view that their conflict with the Palestinians is part of a larger clash of civilizations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Like leaders around the world, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel was quick to condemn the attack that killed 12 people in Paris on Wednesday at the offices of a satirical newspaper, Charlie Hebdo. The next day, Mr. Netanyahu sent a letter of condolence and outrage to the French president and declared after a meeting with Norway’s foreign minister, “Israel is being attacked by the very same forces that attack Europe.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/world/10ISRAEL/10ISRAEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/10/world/10ISRAEL/10ISRAEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/world/10ISRAEL/10ISRAEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/world/10ISRAEL/10ISRAEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1464, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/world/10ISRAEL/10ISRAEL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/10/world/10ISRAEL/10ISRAEL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/world/10ISRAEL/10ISRAEL-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israelis Link Attacks to Their Own Struggles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israelis Link Attacks to Their Own Struggles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T20:42:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/097eafe6-4ab9-58a0-967d-e6e4aacf7979', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/097eafe6-4ab9-58a0-967d-e6e4aacf7979'}, {'abstract': '“The Scarlet Ibis,” a new chamber opera, is based on a James Hurst short story published in The Atlantic in 1960.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/10/arts/music/the-scarlet-ibis-blends-opera-with-puppetry.html', 'snippet': '“The Scarlet Ibis,” a new chamber opera, is based on a James Hurst short story published in The Atlantic in 1960.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tools that contemporary composers, conductors and directors are using to expand the spectacle of music can sometimes seem like unnecessary embellishments, whether video projections, acrobatics or reflecting pools of water. So the great achievement of “The Scarlet Ibis” — an outstanding new chamber opera by the composer Stefan Weisman and the librettist David Cote that opened the Prototype festival at Here on Thursday night — is not only that it’s a moving, intense and dignified creation, but also that it adds puppetry to opera’s basic elements in a completely organic way.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/arts/IBIS/IBIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/10/arts/IBIS/IBIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '