garage. But the company that powers the bike-sharing programs in New York, London, Chicago and a dozen other cities started much differently: It began with a municipal parking authority, wound through bankruptcy court and got another shot at corporate viability off the Madagascar coast during the annual hatching of the green sea turtles.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-BIKE/11-BIKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-BIKE/11-BIKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-BIKE/11-BIKE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-BIKE/11-BIKE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1477, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-BIKE/11-BIKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-BIKE/11-BIKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-BIKE/11-BIKE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Uphill Push to Save a Bike-Share Pioneer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Uphill Push to Save a Bike-Share Pioneer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodi, Bruno', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PBSC Urban Solutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bixi (Societe de Velo en Libre-Service)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citi Bike', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montreal (Quebec)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T21:03:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1de4ec4f-f84b-51d4-b3bf-40884b0d9fd0', 'word_count': 1923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1de4ec4f-f84b-51d4-b3bf-40884b0d9fd0'}, {'abstract': 'Oil sketches are the Twitter of 18th-century painting. The Morgan Library & Museum will focus on the history of the practice in “Exploring France: Oil Sketches From the Thaw Collection.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/arts/design/exploring-france-oil-sketches-from-the-thaw-collection-at-the-morgan.html', 'snippet': 'Oil sketches are the Twitter of 18th-century painting. The Morgan Library & Museum will focus on the history of the practice in “Exploring France: Oil Sketches From the Thaw Collection.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oil sketches are the Twitter of 18th-century painting, dashed off sometimes in mere minutes to capture a fleeting idea or a quality of light that would be gone forever with the next cloud bank. Their power is not only in their immediacy but also in how they prefigure outdoor painters who elevated landscape as a genre. Starting Tuesday, the Morgan Library & Museum will focus on the history of the practice in “Exploring France: Oil Sketches From the Thaw Collection.” The collector Eugene V. Thaw and his wife, Clare, benefactors of the Morgan and the Metropolitan Museum of Art, have donated 135 oil sketches to the two institutions, in addition to giving hundreds of old master and 19th-century drawings to the Morgan. Mr. Thaw has described the sketches as “the most wonderful, fresh, free pieces on paper” — work that mattered to him because it mattered to the artists, who considered them much more than disposable studies: “They traded them amongst each other, and they preserved them.” (Through Oct. 4, 225 Madison Avenue, at 36th Street, 212-685-0008, themorgan.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE5/11GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE5/11GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE5/11GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE5/11GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1190, 'width': 1795, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE5/11GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE5/11GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE5/11GUIDE5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scenes of France, Sketched in Oil', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scenes of France, Sketched in Oil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T21:03:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b643b748-86ee-5097-8b63-b6134d893d40', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b643b748-86ee-5097-8b63-b6134d893d40'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick Stewart stars in the film version of Stephen Belber’s play “Match,” stepping into the role that earned Frank Langella a Tony nomination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/movies/patrick-stewart-stars-in-match.html', 'snippet': 'Patrick Stewart stars in the film version of Stephen Belber’s play “Match,” stepping into the role that earned Frank Langella a Tony nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the film version of “Match,” Stephen Belber’s play about choices, regrets and long-hidden secrets, Patrick Stewart takes on the role brought to Broadway by Frank Langella in 2004. The movie, adapted and directed by Mr. Belber, opens on Wednesday at the IFC Center (323 Avenue of the Americas, at Third Street, Greenwich Village). Mr. Stewart plays Tobias Powell, a dance teacher and former performer whose long career is supposedly the reason Lisa (Carla Gugino) and her husband, Mike (Matthew Lillard), have come to interview him. But that is just a pretense; they are really interested in a piece of his past he has long buried. It’s a three-hander that’s also a showcase for the actor playing Tobias. What does Mr. Stewart have to live up to?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 536, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1548, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncovering Secrets', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uncovering Secrets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Patrick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T21:05:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb561da7-e168-5570-8731-79fb7c75775d', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb561da7-e168-5570-8731-79fb7c75775d'}, {'abstract': 'A fully renovated townhouse in the West Village that was converted back to a single residence from 10 apartments was the sale of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/realestate/west-village-townhouse-for-21-million.html', 'snippet': 'A fully renovated townhouse in the West Village that was converted back to a single residence from 10 apartments was the sale of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A meticulously renovated townhouse in the West Village, with ample outdoor space that includes a two-tiered patio and a paved roof deck offering a wide range of cityscape and river views, sold for $21,000,000 and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/realestate/11TICKET/11TICKET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/realestate/11TICKET/11TICKET-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 761}}, {'rank'