ino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d78a7bc-c5f1-50d7-b2af-d3cb448a26f3', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d78a7bc-c5f1-50d7-b2af-d3cb448a26f3'}, {'abstract': 'Michelle Ellsworth’s “Preparation for the Obsolescence of the Y Chromosome” is one of 23 productions presented by American Realness, an 11-day festival of contemporary performance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/arts/dance/american-realness-festival-at-abrons-arts-center.html', 'snippet': 'Michelle Ellsworth’s “Preparation for the Obsolescence of the Y Chromosome” is one of 23 productions presented by American Realness, an 11-day festival of contemporary performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are we on our way to becoming a single-sex species? In “Preparation for the Obsolescence of the Y Chromosome,” the choreographer Michelle Ellsworth considers the possibility, building on her body of jubilantly absurd yet pragmatically minded work. (Her past projects include an online inventory of pseudospiritual paraphernalia and a video archive of motivational talks.) “Preparation,” which draws inspiration from the folklorist Alan Lomax and recent genetic research, digests cultural lore through gestural choreography, a “male gaze simulator” and other witty devices.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11SILOGUIDE4/11SILOGUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11SILOGUIDE4/11SILOGUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 597}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/11SILOGUIDE4/11SILOGUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'he