 beer-fueled experimental happening stages its 66th iteration, which will include an interpretation of Chekhov and a Whitney Houston mash-up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'High rents and branded, well, everything may loom over the arts in New York City — but some grassroots culture organizations still manage to tough out the mean streets of the metropolis without compromising their homespun ethics. On Jan. 10, the whirlwind, ball-of-wax performance showcase Catch stages its 66th iteration — a feat for a sui generis arts project. The secret to its fancy-free success for over a decade? “Beer,” deadpans Caleb Hammons, one-third of Catch’s advisory team. As it says on the flyer, “$20 gets you in and gets you drinking.” As Hammons explains, “It signals that it’s okay to enjoy yourself.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09catchcoil-baumgardner-1/09catchcoil-baumgardner-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09catchcoil-baumgardner-1/09catchcoil-baumgardner-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09catchcoil-baumgardner-1/09catchcoil-baumgardner-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09catchcoil-baumgardner-1/09catchcoil-baumgardner-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/09/t-magazine/09catchcoil-baumgardner-1/09catchcoil-baumgardne