 costume jewelry, Broadway Silk Store, in Astoria, Queens, has been an anchor in the neighborhood since the Depression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is it a coincidence that Broadway Silk Store, a Queens purveyor of fabric and costume jewelry, sits across the street from the Greater Astoria Historical Society? The store has been an anchor in the neighborhood since the Depression. It is two blocks from Kaufman Astoria Studios and has furnished costuming for an array of productions over its 80-year history, including “Sesame Street,” “Men in Black 3” and “The Good Wife.” And as with other multigenerational, family-owned institutions, it has an oral history so rich that it can be hard to distinguish fact from fiction. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Elmo’s People Shop: Broadway Silk Store in Astoria', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Elmo’s People Shop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Astoria (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Broadway Silk Store (Queens, NY, Retail Store)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-09T23:12:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Adkins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02e05c50-4bb7-59b7-8c44-0a237068c302', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02e05c50-4bb7-59b7-8c44-0a237068c302'}, {'abstract': 'As New York City’s first lady has found out, public figures have to consider what they wear as a piece of communication.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/fashion/the-fury-over-chirlane-mccrays-trousers.html', 'snippet': 'As New York City’s first lady has found out, public figures have to consider what they wear as a piece of communication.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The firestorm of social media accusation and response that blew up around the question of what New York City’s first lady, Chirlane McCray, did, or did not, wear to the slain police officer Wenjian Liu’s funeral last Sunday may seem a silly distraction in the greater, more urgent story of fraying relations between City Hall and the police force, but it is also a powerful reminder of the power clothes have, for both good and ill.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/fashion/11RUNWAY_COMBO/11RUNWAY_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/fashion/11RUNWAY_COMBO/11RUNWAY_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 843}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/fashion/11RUNWAY_COMBO/11RUNWAY_COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 729, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/fashion/11RUNWAY_COMBO/11RUNWAY_COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1458, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/fashion/11RUNWAY_COMBO/11RUNWAY_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/fashion/11RUNWAY_COMBO/11RUNWAY_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailw