returning to work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An obstetrician/gynecologist in Hobbs whose medical license was suspended over accusations that he had sex with patients, drank on the job and was unavailable as his patients went into labor has been ordered to undergo evaluation for sex addiction as a condition of returning to work. The doctor, Christopher S. Driskill, one of the few obstetrician-gynecologists in Hobbs and president-elect of the New Mexico Medical Society, had his license suspended in November by state medical officials. In December, he reached a settlement with state Medical Board prosecutors to restore his license. The settlement was approved Thursday by the board, which required that he “submit to a comprehensive inpatient evaluation” within the next three months by the Sexual Recovery Institute in Los Angeles. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Mexico: Deal Would Restore Doctor’s License', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Mexico: Deal Would Restore Doctor’s License', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rojas, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Driskill, Christopher S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hobbs (NM)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T00:29:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': '