'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/4362f0d7-8dfd-59fd-aa27-a5c134a3f0a0', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4362f0d7-8dfd-59fd-aa27-a5c134a3f0a0'}, {'abstract': 'Specialty license plates are a new frontier in debates over freedom of speech.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/10/opinion/a-license-to-say-anything.html', 'snippet': 'Specialty license plates are a new frontier in debates over freedom of speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SPECIALTY license plates — which bear the logo of a college or a sports team, or a slogan like “Save Our Seas” or “Stop Child Abuse” — bring in lots of money for state governments, as well as the schools, nonprofit groups, professional organizations and other entities that sponsor them. But these vehicular tags have also become a new frontier in debates over freedom of speech.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/opinion/10Brettschneider/10Brettschneider-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 463, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/10/opinion/10Brettschneider/10Brettschneider-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 463}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/opinion/10Brettschneider/10Brettschneider-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/opinion/10Brettschneider/10Brettschneider-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 1803, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/opinio