, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gospel Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T04:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/12fdf65a-c3cd-5960-b545-a445686f7b93', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12fdf65a-c3cd-5960-b545-a445686f7b93'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition in Purchase, N.Y. features the work of the commercial photographer who was born Mike Meyer, changed his name to Mike Disfarmer and shot postcard-size portraits in Heber Springs, Ark.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/nyregion/faces-of-a-small-southern-town-becoming-disfarmer-at-the-neuberger-museum-of-art.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition in Purchase, N.Y. features the work of the commercial photographer who was born Mike Meyer, changed his name to Mike Disfarmer and shot postcard-size portraits in Heber Springs, Ark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A visitor could spend hours studying the faces on display in “Becoming Disfarmer,” an exhibition of photographic portraits at the Neuberger Museum of Art. Couples, families, men dressed in military uniforms, pretty young women in lipstick and barrettes: They peer out from the walls and up from the glass cases. Some of the faces are freckled, others weathered and lined. A few smile, but most are grave. All stare intently into the camera’s lens. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/nyregion/11ARTSWE2/11ARTSWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'