region/big-city-book-club.html', 'snippet': 'The Big City Book Club returns for 2015, and we’re getting things rolling with Bernard Malamud’s classic New York novel “The Assistant.” Join us for the online discussion of the novel on Thursday, Feb. 12, at 6:30 p.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Big City Book Club returns for 2015, and we’re getting things rolling with Bernard Malamud’s classic New York novel “The Assistant.” Set in Brooklyn in the 1950s, the novel has it all: the clash of immigrant cultures, the threats of modernization to old shopkeeping ways, crime and illicit love. Join us for the online discussion of the novel on Thursday, Feb. 12, at 6:30 p.m. on The New York Times’s City Room blog.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big City Book Club', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big City Book Club', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malamud, Bernard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Assistant (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T04:56:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dbdad81-0b35-5504-b5cd-15943ccb1d7b', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dbdad81-0b35-5504-b5cd-15943ccb1d7b'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Hathout, who helped found the Islamic Center of Southern California, called on American Muslims to embrace their dual identity, and preached interfaith comity and understanding in the aftermath of the Sept. 11 attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/us/maher-hathout-a-powerful-voice-for-american-muslims-dies-at-79-.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Hathout, who helped found the Islamic Center of Southern California, called on American Muslims to embrace their dual identity, and preached interfaith comity and understanding in the aftermath of the Sept. 11 attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Maher Hathout, an Egyptian-born cardiologist who became an influential American Muslim leader, preaching interfaith comity and helping to sustain the Muslim faithful in the United States against the backlash after the Sept. 11 attacks, died on Jan. 3 in Duarte, Calif. He was 79.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/us/obitMaherHathout/obitMaherHathout-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/10/us/obitMaherHathout/obitMaherHathout-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/us/obitMaherHathout/obitMaherHathout-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/us/obitMaherHathout/obitMaherHathout-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1384, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/us/obitMaherHathout/obitMaherHathout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/10/us/obitMaherHathout/obitMaherHathout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/us/obitMaherHathout/obitMaherHathout-