 pores over old family documents and finds an “Aryan declaration” written by his deceased father — a discovery that upends his concept of his history. His mother, Rivka (Jeanne Moreau), a Jewish woman living an elegant life, evades Victor’s questions. “Rivka’s embrace of that life can look like a form of denial, but as Ms. Moreau’s performance unfolds, the character’s courage and resilience emerge more pointedly into view,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times about this meditation on memory, identity and reconciliation from the Israeli director Amos Gitai based on a book by Jérôme Clément. She “gives a master class in how to be regal without vanity and how to use the hard-won charisma of a movie star to illuminate the dignity of an ordinary person.” The film “contains no great revelations or surprises, but rather is suffused with a quiet glow of sympathy and enlightenment,” he added.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T06:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8406dae6-502c-5a60-bea4-aeeb4cbc310a', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8406dae6-502c-5a60-bea4-aeeb4cbc310a'}, {'abstract': 'Tommy Caldwell and Kevin Jorgeson are trying to free-climb the 3,000-foot Dawn Wall, a vertical sheet of mostly smooth granite that many believe is the most difficult climb in the 