pg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-WORKSPACE-1/11-WORKSPACE-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1022, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-WORKSPACE-1/11-WORKSPACE-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1626, 'width': 1629, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-WORKSPACE-1/11-WORKSPACE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-WORKSPACE-1/11-WORKSPACE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/business/11-WORKSPACE-1/11-WORKSPACE-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Staying Up to Speed ', 'kicker': 'Workspace', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Staying Up to Speed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harley-Davidson Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kumbier, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T14:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Patricia R. Olsen', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/40a0fde0-a3c2-5f0a-a9a4-9b0cff5368ad', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40a0fde0-a3c2-5f0a-a9a4-9b0cff5368ad'}, {'abstract': 'No, mainstream economics didn’t justify austerity.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/10/orthodoxy-heterodoxy-and-ideology/', 'snippet': 'No, mainstream economics didn’t justify austerity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many economists responded badly to the economic crisis. And there’s a lot wrong with mainstream economic analysis. But how closely are these two assertions related? Not as much as you might think. So I’m very much in accord with Simon Wren-Lewis on the remarkable unhelpfulness of recent heterodox assaults on the field. Not that there’s anything wrong with being heterodox in general; but a lot of what we’ve been seeing misidentifies the problem, and if anything gives aid and comfort to the wrong people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Orthodoxy, Heterodoxy, and Ideology', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T15:04:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c0e1813-4ab4-5637-82e3-ce754bbf5f59', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c0e1813-4ab4-5637-82e3-ce754bbf5f59'}, {'abstract': 'New legislation, promoted as making only technical changes in a financial regulation law, could end up gutting some of its provisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/business/kicking-dodd-frank-in-the-teeth.html', 'snippet': 'New legislation, promoted as making only technical changes in a financial regulation law, could end up gutting some of its provisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 114th Congress has been at work for less than a week, but a goal for many of its members is already evident: a further rollback of regulations put in place to keep markets and Main Street safe from reckless Wall Street practices.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kicking Dodd-Frank in the Teeth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kicking Dodd-Frank in the Teeth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgenson, Gretchen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Financial Services Committee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzpatrick, Michael G', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T15:09:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Morgenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morgenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95362a6b-0c27-5844-b2be-247aa1f60bbc', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95362a6b-0c27-5844-b2be-247aa1f60bbc'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from The International Herald Tribune archives: A monsignor is called upon to investigate the life of Joan of Arc as cardinals discuss her canonization.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/10/1890-canonization-of-jeanne-darc/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from The International Herald Tribune archives: A monsignor is called upon to investigate the life of Joan of Arc as cardinals discuss her canonization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cause for the canonization of Jeanne d’Arc will, as soon as the documents relating to her life are ready, be discussed by the Cardinals belonging to the Sacred Congregation of Rites. Every minute particular relating to her life is being looked into with the greatest care by Mgr. Caprara, a learned advocate, who is employed by the Vatican always in matters concerning beatifications and canonizations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/blogs/06iht-jeanne-darc/06iht-jeanne-darc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 508, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/blogs/06iht-jeanne-darc/06iht-jeanne-darc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 508, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/06/blogs/06iht-jeanne-darc/06iht-jeanne-darc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/06/blogs/06iht-jeanne-darc/06iht-jeanne-darc-thumbStandard.j