mage', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/sunday-review/11COUCH/11COUCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/sunday-review/11COUCH/11COUCH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/sunday-review/11COUCH/11COUCH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Grief Right', 'kicker': 'Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting Grief Right', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T18:16:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By Patrick O'Malley", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Malley", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9814ba95-e2e7-55ae-96bf-fec599ece9ec', 'word_count': 1397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9814ba95-e2e7-55ae-96bf-fec599ece9ec'}, {'abstract': 'An agreement would carry risks, but a bigger risk would be squandering this moment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/opinion/sunday/saving-the-nuclear-deal-with-iran.html', 'snippet': 'An agreement would carry risks, but a bigger risk would be squandering this moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twice recently, Iran’s president, Hassan Rouhani, has acted boldly in support of his biggest political gamble, pursuit of a nuclear agreement with the major powers. In a speech last Sunday on Iran’s troubled economy, he argued that Iran will never enjoy sustained growth if it is isolated from the rest of the world. Three weeks earlier, he made clear that he would confront Iran’s hard-liners in his efforts to clinch a deal in which Iran would agree never to produce a nuclear weapon in return for the lifting of crippling international sanctions.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun1/11sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun1/11sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun1/11sat1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun1/11sat1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1157, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun1/11sat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun1/11sat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun1/11sat1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving the Nuclear Deal With Iran', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving the Nuclear Deal With Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T18:18:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6543415f-bb04-52f4-81a2-d7de06438344', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6543415f-bb04-52f4-81a2-d7de06438344'}, {'abstract': 'Now that drivers have seen the cost of fuel fall so much and so quickly, a modest increase would hardly be noticeable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/opinion/sunday/raise-the-gas-tax-to-fix-americas-roads.html', 'snippet': 'Now that drivers have seen the cost of fuel fall so much and so quickly, a modest increase would hardly be noticeable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gasoline prices have fallen more than 40 percent since the end of June thanks to the collapse of global oil prices. That makes this the perfect time for Congress to overcome its longstanding terror of offending the nation’s motorists and raise the tax on gasoline and diesel fuel. The results could only be beneficial: for the nation’s roads, bridges and transit systems, which badly need repair; for the budget; and, to the extent that higher taxes encourage greater fuel efficiency, for the climate.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun2/11sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun2/11sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun2/11sun2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun2/11sun2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun2/11sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun2/11sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/opinion/11sun2/11sun2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Raise the Gas Tax to Fix America’s Roads', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Raise the Gas Tax to Fix America’s Roads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gasoline Tax (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Highway Trust Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T18:19:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ddef6ac-d12f-5e8f-8e95-ddc31d6a795b', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ddef6ac-d12f-5e8f-8e95-ddc31d6a795b'}, {'abstract': 'The open-carry debate in Texas is the latest barometer of America’s firearm culture, as it veers somewhere between eerie and lethal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/opinion/sunday/gun-rights-from-holsters-to-bras.html', 'snippet': 'The open-carry debate in Texas is the latest barometer of America’s firearm culture, as it veers somewhere between eerie and lethal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the clichés about pistol-packing Texas, the state is one of the few that has not yet succumbed to the gun lobby’s big push to let citizens carry handguns at the hip wherever they go. That may be about to change as the State Legislature convenes next week with open carry a top priority of the Republican majority and with Governor-elect Greg Abbott pledging to sign it into law. The result could produce a far from reassuring civic tableau if even a modest number of the 800,000 Texans who have concealed-carry licenses choose to strap their weapons on in public.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gun Rights, From Holsters to Bras', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gun Rights, From Holsters to Bras', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Open Carry Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Come and Take It Texas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T18:20:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/91e31b73-5c1e-5a83-881d-98dd6d6a2f48', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91e31b73-5c1e-5a83-881d-98dd6d6a2f48'}, {'abstract': 'Angels have won Most Valuable Player and Cy Young awards, but none have entered the Hall of Fame as members of the franchise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/sports/baseball/angels-have-yet-to-send-a-player-to-the-baseball-hall-of-fame.html', 'snippet': 'Angels have won Most Valuable Player and Cy Young awards, but none have entered the Hall of Fame as members of the franchise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Mead was 12 years old when his family moved from Virginia to California. The family drove, arriving at its new home in Highland ahead of its furniture. Mead, who had brought a transistor radio, sat on the floor of his family’s new kitchen, turned the dial and found an Angels game. He was hooked on a team not much younger than he was. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/sports/kepner/kepner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/10/sports/kepner/kepner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/sports/kepner/kepner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/sports/kepner/kepner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/sports/kepner/kepner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/10/sports/kepner/kepner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/sports/kepner/kepner-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Team Has Golden Moments but Lacks a Halo in Bronze', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Team Has Golden Moments but Lacks a Halo in Bronze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trout, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-10T18:24:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21661e76-0d4c-53ba-abc5-74e462840822', 'word_count': 1165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21661e76-0d4c-53ba-abc5-74e462840822'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Rauner, a Republican businessman who has never held elective office, has called for tax cuts in a state that received the worst credit rating in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/11/us/politics/in-illinois-bruce-rauners-campaign-promises-are-about-to-meet-budget-realities.html', 'snippet': 'Bruce Rauner, a Republican businessman who has never held elective office, has called for tax cuts in a state that received the worst credit rating in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — As Bruce Rauner swept out the Democratic governor of this Democratic-leaning state, he made one absolute pledge: He would shake up Illinois. Mr. Rauner, a multimillionaire who has never held elective office, said the state needed, at long last, to put its finances in order. He has said the state ought to lower income taxes, reduce regulations on businesses and devote more money to education.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1407, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/us/ILLINOIS/ILLINOIS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Illinois, New Governor’s Campaign Promises Are About to Meet Budget Realities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Illinois, New Governor’s Campaign Promises Are About to Meet Budget Realities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauner, Bruce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'val