m/2015/01/11/taken-3-tops-box-office/', 'snippet': 'Liam Neeson’s franchise of vengeance raked in $40 million in its opening weekend, one of the best results on record for January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The weekend box office provided a primer on why Hollywood spends more time pumping out sequels than it does attempting to make meaty, well-reviewed original movies. “Taken 3,” starring Liam Neeson and receiving a paltry 12 percent positive score on the review-aggregation site RottenTomatoes, was a huge No. 1 at North American multiplexes, taking in an estimated $40.4 million – one of the best opening results on record for January. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/arts/ARTS1/ARTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/12/arts/ARTS1/ARTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/arts/ARTS1/ARTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/arts/ARTS1/ARTS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1317, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/arts/ARTS1/ARTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/12/arts/ARTS1/ARTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/arts/ARTS1/ARTS1-thumbLarge.jpg