subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18886ab4-4cc5-5d96-8c1c-f24bcd7358ba', 'word_count': 1009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18886ab4-4cc5-5d96-8c1c-f24bcd7358ba'}, {'abstract': 'The nation’s president is “pro-Western,” with ample supplies of oil and gas. He is also hugely corrupt and authoritarian.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/opinion/the-two-faces-of-azerbaijans-mr-aliyev.html', 'snippet': 'The nation’s president is “pro-Western,” with ample supplies of oil and gas. He is also hugely corrupt and authoritarian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Ilham Aliyev of Azerbaijan does a masterful political Jekyll and Hyde. A cable from the American ambassador to Baku released on WikiLeaks described him as a Michael Corleone-Sonny Corleone figure — referring, respectively, to the coolly calculating and the impetuously violent brothers of the “Godfather” mafia family. Mr. Aliyev is “pro-Western” in many of the ways the West admires: He is suave, well dressed and well spoken in English; he is ready to send his country’s ample supplies of oil and gas to Europe and to Israel; his Islam is moderate and modern; and he hosts lavish international events like the Eurovision Song Contest in 2012 and the European Games to be held next June.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Two Faces of Azerbaijan’s Mr. Aliyev', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Two Faces of Azerbaijan’s Mr. Aliyev', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aliyev, Ilham H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Azerbaijan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio Free Europe-Radio Liberty', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T02:23:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a67a836-c374-5db3-a644-2b68a9f190b6', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a67a836-c374-5db3-a644-2b68a9f190b6'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Santorum sharply criticized potential rivals for the Republican presidential nomination, indicating he intends to reclaim conservative primary voters ahead of a new White House bid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/us/politics/rick-santorum-criticizes-rand-paul-and-ted-cruz-as-bomb-throwers.html', 'snippet': 'Rick Santorum sharply criticized potential rivals for the Republican presidential nomination, indicating he intends to reclaim conservative primary voters ahead of a new White House bid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Rick Santorum sharply criticized a group of potential rivals for the Republican presidential nomination in an interview that indicated he intends to reclaim conservative primary voters ahead of another White House bid in 2016.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/us/SANTORUM/SANTORUM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/12/us/SANTORUM/SANTORUM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype