rk in a neighborhood that has produced some of Europe’s most militant jihadists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — They jogged together or did calisthenics along the hilly lawns and tulip-dotted gardens of Buttes-Chaumont, the public park in northeastern Paris built more than a century ago under Emperor Napoleon III. Or they met in nearby apartments with a janitor turned self-proclaimed imam, a man deemed too radical by one local mosque because of his call for waging jihad in Iraq.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jihadism Born in a Paris Park and Fueled in the Prison Yard', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jihadism Born in a Paris Park and Fueled in the Prison Yard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kouachi, Cherif (1982-2015)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coulibaly, Amedy (1982-2015)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Parc des Buttes Chaumont (Paris, France)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T02:47:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e6e2f52-a008-566c-bb7b-f5ecfe70d65b', 'word_count': 2110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e6e2f52-a008-566c-bb