ded the visit in part to answer criticism that the U.S. had sent only an ambassador to a rally in Paris that drew leaders from 40 countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/world/europe/kerry-paris-terrorist-attacks.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry added the visit in part to answer criticism that the U.S. had sent only an ambassador to a rally in Paris that drew leaders from 40 countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AHMEDABAD, India — Secretary of State John Kerry announced on Monday that he would fly to Paris at the end of the week in a gesture of support for the French government’s struggle against terrorism.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Says He’ll Fly to France to Show U.S. Solidarity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kerry Says He’ll Fly to France to Show U.S. Solidarity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T07:26:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03c6c1a0-9959-57ec-816b-f2c2051fab18', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03c6c1a0-9959-57ec-816b-f2c2051fab18'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities said that they would bolster security to protect potential targets of terrorism, putting in place one of the country’s biggest peacetime security operations.', 'w