itant groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — The United States plans to provide $250 million in emergency aid to help resettle and sustain civilians displaced by the Pakistani military’s campaign against militant groups, senior American officials said Monday night after the first day of a visit by Secretary of State John Kerry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/world/KERRY/KERRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/13/world/KERRY/KERRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/world/KERRY/KERRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/world/KERRY/KERRY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1424, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/world/KERRY/KERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/13/world/KERRY/KERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/world/KERRY/KERRY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Vows Aid for Displaced Pakistanis ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kerry Vows Aid for Displaced Pakistanis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haqqani Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-e-Taiba', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tehrik-e-Taliban', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T12:19:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/494e5ba1-5f92-5503-b944-1bf35edb22b5', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/494e5ba1-5f92-5503-b944-1bf35edb22b5'}, {'abstract': 'Shire agrees to buy NPS Pharmaceuticals for $5.2 billion. | Banks brace for a jolt as the price of oil falls. | Kicking Dodd-Frank in the teeth. | David A. O’Neil, a federal prosecutor, is joining the law firm Debevoise & Plimpton.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/morning-agenda-shires-deal-for-nps/', 'snippet': 'Shire agrees to buy NPS Pharmaceuticals for $5.2 billion. | Banks brace for a jolt as the price of oil falls. | Kicking Dodd-Frank in the teeth. | David A. O’Neil, a federal prosecutor, is joining the law firm Debevoise & Plimpton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Irish drug maker Shire has agreed to acquire NPS Pharmaceuticals for $5.2 billion, the first big corporate acquisition of the year, DealBook’s David Gelles reports. Shire, based in Dublin, said on Sunday that it would pay $46 a share for NPS, which is based in New Jersey and specializes in drugs for gastrointestinal disorders. That represents a 51 percent increase over NPS’s share price on Dec. 16, before rumors of the deal first surfaced. Shire will pay for NPS using all cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Shire’s Deal for NPS', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T12:31:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2495051b-9a99-5eff-a0dd-2b360047634b', 'word_count': 2045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2495051b-9a99-5eff-a0dd-2b360047634b'}, {'abstract': 'The latest men’s collection from Burberry at London Fashion Week.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/burberry-live-stream-london-fashion-week-mens-fall-2015-collection/', 'snippet': 'The latest men’s collection from Burberry at London Fashion Week.', 'lead_paragraph': '[Watch the live stream.]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/t-magazine/12burberry/12burberry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/12/t-magazine/12burberry/12burberry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,