d the question of how to get past handlers and other hurdles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Access and How to Get It: Congressional Reporter’s Notebook', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitol Building (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T16:29:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c72fd67f-a0bb-5100-a044-62fa550416be', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c72fd67f-a0bb-5100-a044-62fa550416be'}, {'abstract': 'From Amal Clooney’s opera gloves to Felicity Jones’s demure Dior, the stars turned it out at last night’s event.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/golden-globes-2015-best-dressed-list/', 'snippet': 'From Amal Clooney’s opera gloves to Felicity Jones’s demure Dior, the stars turned it out at last night’s event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From old-Hollywood glamour to red-carpet rebels, the stars turned it out at last night’s Golden Globe Awards. Several trends emerged on the red carpet, such as silver-embellished gowns that shined like disco balls, worn by Julianne Moore and Dakota Johnson, and suiting and separates, as seen on Emma Stone and Lorde. Only a brave few took risks, but they did so successfully: Last year’s award winner Lupita Nyong’o stood out in one of the night’s only prints; the most anticipated guest of the evening, Amal Clooney, sported white opera gloves; and the nominee Felicity Jones wore demure, high-necked Dior, proving amidst all the cleavage and cutouts that being covered up can make just as much of an impression. Last but not least, there were the ladies who wore true fashion and wore it well: Claire Danes in Valentino, a pregnant Keira Knightley in Chanel and Sienna Miller in Miu Miu. All in all, it was an exciting kick-off to 2015’s awards season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 10 Best Dressed on the Golden Globe Awards Red Carpet', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Danes, Claire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Dakota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Felicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knightley, Keira', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Sienna', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Julianne', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Nyong'o, Lupita", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stone, Emma', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miu Miu (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Valentino Fashion Group SpA', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T16:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ce69870-acc8-5817-9065-6131afa1b4cb', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ce69870-acc8-5817-9065-6131afa1b4cb'}, {'abstract': 'Female stars were paid less than their male counterparts.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/the-sony-hack-and-the-gender-pay-gap/', 'snippet': 'Female stars were paid less than their male counterparts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s rare to see such clear evidence of women making less pay for equal work. Among other unflattering details revealed by the Sony Pictures Entertainment hack (presumably sponsored by North Korea in retaliation for the film The Interview) was that Chris Hemsworth had secured higher compensation than his co-star Charlize Theron for the upcoming movie “The Huntsman.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/opinion/1122015charlize/1122015charlize-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/12/opinion/1122015charlize/1122015charlize-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/opinion/1122015charlize/1122015charlize-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/opinion/1122015charlize/1122015charlize-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, '