26', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd92688-b2aa-5bcf-b54d-61812d376726'}, {'abstract': 'A twist on the classic coin-scale problem by math educator Daniel Finkel.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/finkel/', 'snippet': 'A twist on the classic coin-scale problem by math educator Daniel Finkel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our puzzle this week was proposed by regular contributor Daniel Finkel, part of the Seattle-based Math for Love duo committed to revitalizing grade- and high-school math education. “I think I’ve just concocted a novel coin-balance problem,” he wrote in a recent email. “To the best of my knowledge, it is totally original.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daniel Finkel and the Balance Problem', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'FINKEL, DANIEL', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T17:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c409a71-92cc-54e1-a9aa-e1de50a79cf3', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c409a71-92cc-54e1-a9aa-e1de50a79cf3'}, {'abstract': '“Tales of the Grim Sleeper,” shortlisted for the Oscar for documentary feature, argues that hundreds of women may have died.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/a-killing-spree-ignored-for-decades/', 'snippet': '“Tales of the Grim Sleeper,” shortlisted for the Oscar for documentary feature, argues that hundreds of women may have died.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Nobody knows how many women may have been killed during a spree in Los Angeles that began in the 1980s and ended with the arrest in 2010 of Lonnie Franklin Jr. He has been charged in 10 cases, but in “Tales of the Grim Sleeper,” one of 15 films shortlisted for the Oscar for best documentary feature, the British director Nick Broomfield argues that a more realistic count would have to be in the hundreds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Killing Spree Ignored for Decades', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broomfield, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Lonnie D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T17:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9714412-6965-5dc7-92ce-6c4a39392398', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9714412-6965-5dc7-92ce-6c4a39392398'}, {'abstract': 'The company, which a Chinese tycoon bought from Ford in 2010, said it would ship 1,500 to 2,000 S60 Inscriptions to America this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/business/international/volvo-to-export-sedan-made-in-china-to-the-us.html', 'snippet': 'The company, which a Chinese tycoon bought from Ford in 2010, said it would ship 1,500 to 2,000 S60 Inscriptio