ny-on-moving-under-sand.html', 'snippet': 'A study showed that the long, slender shape of a snake was able to move more efficiently than that of a lizard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some subsurface animals burrow and dig tunnels. Others, in sandy environments like the deserts of Arizona or the Sahara, wiggle along under the surface in a way that looks like swimming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Skinny on Moving Under Sand', 'kicker': 'ScienceTake', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldman, Daniel I', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T17:24:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f1756fb-e411-53d9-944a-d09371e7fb69', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f1756fb-e411-53d9-944a-d09371e7fb69'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to events celebrating the anniversary of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s birth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/travel/martin-luther-kings-birthday-atlanta-memphis-boston.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to events celebrating the anniversary of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s birth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Atlanta, where the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. was born and raised, his holiday, coming up on Jan. 19, feels both somber and celebratory, said Kim Severson, a domestic correspondent for The New York Times based there. “You definitely feel like it’s a special day when you’re in Atlanta, probably more so than in other cities.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 