g', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/13/business/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/business/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/business/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/business/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/13/business/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/business/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill/FIRSTDRAFT12mccaskill-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'McCaskill Says She Won’t Leave Senate to Run for Governor', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T17:53:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a1e5003-327f-5311-b43e-5b6d821ebc13', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a1e5003-327f-5311-b43e-5b6d821ebc13'}, {'abstract': 'Strangers like to tell me what I’m doing wrong as a parent, or at least give me hard, critical looks, all the time. But there’s a big part of our story they often don’t know.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/harsh-critics-in-public-spaces-judging-only-what-they-see/', 'snippet': 'Strangers like to tell me what I’m doing wrong as a parent, or at least give me hard, critical looks, all the time. But there’s a big part of our story they often don’t know.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last time it happened was in the grocery store. A scowling woman closed in on me and my son, Nico, in the produce section. Glaring, she waved at my son’s face and said, “His nose!” And then she mimed wiping with furious gestures. I sighed and pulled a tissue from my pocket. She harrumphed slightly and walked away. I offered Nico the tissue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/us/motherlode-grocery-store/motherlode-grocery-store-jumbo.png', 'height': 278, 'width': 429, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/us/motherlode-grocery-store/motherlode-grocery-store-superJumbo.png', 'height': 278, 'width': 429, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/us/motherlode-grocery-store/motherlode-grocery-store-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/12/us/motherlode-grocery-store/motherlode-grocery-store-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/us/motherlode-grocery-store/motherlode-grocery-store-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Harsh Critics in Public Spaces, Judging Only What They See', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Down Syndrome', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T17:56:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Perry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e15f5643-a8bb-5713-b926-f6fbca2e0f16', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e15f5643-a8bb-5713-b926-f6fbca2e0f16'}, {'abstract': 'Since a police chokehold contributed to a Staten Island man’s death in July, the tactic and its 20-year-old prohibition in New York City have come under intense review.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/nyregion/police-keep-using-chokeholds-despite-bans-and-scrutiny.html', 'snippet': 'Since a police chokehold contributed to a Staten Island man’s death in July, the tactic and its 20-year-old prohibition in New York City have come under intense review.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before pepper spray, Tasers, expandable batons and portable radios, New York police officers facing resistance from a criminal suspect had another option: the chokehold. By 1993, though, the New York Police Department had joined departments in other large cities by banning the chokehold with an order that amounted to, in the words of former Chief of Department John F. Timoney: “Stay the hell away from the neck.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Scrutiny, Police Chokeholds Persist in New York City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Scrutiny, Police Chokeholds Persist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Civilian Complaint Review Board', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pantaleo, Daniel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bratton, William J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baez, Anthony Ramon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T18:04:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mat