orations by Stephen Sondheim and Harold Prince.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/arts/music/david-louds-a-good-thing-going-honors-sondheim-and-prince.html', 'snippet': 'David Loud conducts an erudite survey of collaborations by Stephen Sondheim and Harold Prince.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When David Loud auditioned for the ill-fated original Broadway production of the 1981 Stephen Sondheim-George Furth musical, “Merrily We Roll Along,” he was just a college student. After many callbacks, he joined the cast of a production that closed after only 16 performances, thus ending the string of remarkable collaborations between Mr. Sondheim and the director and producer Harold Prince; they reunited in 2003 for “Bounce.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/LYRICISTS/LYRICISTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/LYRICISTS/LYRICISTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/LYRICISTS/LYRICISTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/LYRICISTS/LYRICISTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1475, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/LYRICISTS/LYRICISTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/LYRICISTS/LYRICISTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumb