lue': 'Sandy, Keith P (1975- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perez, Dominique W (1981- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBUQUERQUE (NM)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T22:10:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas and Joseph J. Kolb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Kolb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1662fd97-14a5-583d-abe1-cb1933d7e735', 'word_count': 850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1662fd97-14a5-583d-abe1-cb1933d7e735'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/walkabout-new-scrutiny-for-u-s-visa-waiver-program/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'High Alert\xa0 Sen. Dianne Feinstein criticized the nascent visa-waiver program, which helps travelers from 38 countries to enter the United States visa-free for fewer than 90 days. The program may come under new scrutiny, following increasing terrorist threats and the latest attacks in Paris. (Skift)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout: New Scrutiny for U.S. Visa-Waiver Program', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T22:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64b70279-ef45-58fe-9af9-781d8bf53580', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64b70279-ef45-58fe-9af9-781d8bf53580'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Pierce’s “Hall of Small Mammals” includes short stories about a cloned mammoth, a corpse that may be a biological weapon, marriage and the multiverse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/books/hall-of-small-mammals-by-thomas-pierce.html', 'snippet': 'Thomas Pierce’s “Hall of Small Mammals” includes short stories about a cloned mammoth, a corpse that may be a biological weapon, marriage and the multiverse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Thomas Pierce’s first book, “Hall of Small Mammals,” makes him sought after on the interview circuit, he will be asked the same thing over and over: “Where do your ideas come from?” Usually, that’s a silly question, but it’s unavoidable for a writer whose short-story collection opens with “Shirley Temple Three,” about a man’s bringing a waist-high, supposedly extinct Bread Island Dwarf Mammoth home to his mother. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/bookpierce/bookpierce-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 908, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/bookpierce/bookpierce-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 908}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/bookpierce/bookpierce-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 677, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/bookpierce/bookpierce-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1354, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/bookpierce/bookpierce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/bookpierce/bookpierce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/bookpierce/bookpierce-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mawmaw, The Dwarf Mammoth and M&Ms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mawmaw, the Dwarf Mammoth and M&Ms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierce, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hall of Small Mammals (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-12T22:19:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a6286c3-3c6e-5cc4-bd7d-8146e5aadb35', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a6286c3-3c6e-5cc4-bd7d-8146e5aadb35'}, {'abstract': '“Klansville U.S.A.,” a documentary about the third wave of Ku Klux Klan activity, which came in the 1960s in response to the civil-rights movement, debuts on PBS on Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/arts/television/klansville-usa-explores-the-ku-klux-klan-of-the-60s.html', 'snippet': '“Klansville U.S.A.,” a documentary about the third wave of Ku Klux Klan activity, which came in the 1960s in response to the civil-rights movement, debuts on PBS on Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Klansville U.S.A.” is a documentary about the Ku Klux Klan, but it’s short on images of terrorists on horseback and bodies hanging from trees. It more often resembles home movies of a Sunday outing: picnics, dancing, cooking a pig. And much of it looks like the civil rights rallies and marches that were taking place at the same time, except for the white robes and the occasional 60-foot burning cross.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/KLANSVILLE/KLANSVILLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/KLANSVILLE/KLANSVILLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/KLANSVILLE/KLANSVILLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/KLANSVILLE/KLANSVILLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2038, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/KLANSVILLE/KLANSVILLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/KLANSVILLE/KLANSVILLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'r