: 'nyt://article/a6d15eef-53ed-58b9-a402-b135f5f62b44', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6d15eef-53ed-58b9-a402-b135f5f62b44'}, {'abstract': 'The Temple of Dendur at the Metropolitan Museum can be a risky setting for a classical Indian dance, but not in the case of two performers from the Nrityagram ensemble on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/arts/dance/nrityagram-dancers-at-the-temple-of-dendur-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'The Temple of Dendur at the Metropolitan Museum can be a risky setting for a classical Indian dance, but not in the case of two performers from the Nrityagram ensemble on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In India, ancient temples teem with sculptures of dancing figures, testifying to the spiritual origins and importance of dance. To see a performance of a classical Indian dance in such a setting must be revelatory, an experience impossible for an Indian dance troupe to reproduce for North American audiences. But New York got the next-best thing on Saturday, as the Nrityagram Dance Ensemble performed in the Temple of Dendur at the Metropolitan Museum of Art. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/DENDUR/DENDUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/DENDUR/DENDUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 479}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/DENDUR/DENDUR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/arts/DENDUR/DENDUR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1634, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'c