agraph': 'West Virginia joined 25 other states several years ago to help develop a set of standards for teaching science across the United States. Among other topics, the standards acknowledge the overwhelming scientific consensus that climate change is real and has been profoundly affected by human activity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'West Virginia Revisits Science Standards', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'West Virginia Revisits Science Standards', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-13T01:23:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40639f0b-87f5-5177-b5be-841447b3230e', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40639f0b-87f5-5177-b5be-841447b3230e'}, {'abstract': 'Yorkville Endoscopy, the Manhattan clinic where Joan Rivers went into cardiac arrest while being treated for a voice problem, will lose those benefits effective on Jan. 31, the letter said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/01/13/nyregion/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services.html', 'snippet': 'Yorkville Endoscopy, the Manhattan clinic where Joan Rivers went into cardiac arrest while being treated for a voice problem, will lose those benefits effective on Jan. 31, the letter said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yorkville Endoscopy, the Manhattan clinic where Joan Rivers went into cardiac arrest while being treated for a voice problem, will lose those benefits effective on Jan. 31, the letter said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/nyregion/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter-jumbo.gif', 'height': 235, 'width': 180, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/nyregion/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 235, 'width': 180, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/nyregion/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/12/nyregion/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/12/nyregion/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter/document-centers-for-medicare-and-medicaid-services-letter-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter From the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services Ending Federal Benefits to Yorkville Endoscopy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yorkville Endoscopy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivers, Joan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-13T01:31:00+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/9e24ceac-bc43-5d7b-961c-05eb5a6378fd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/9e24ceac-bc43-5d7b-961c-05eb5a6378fd'}, {'abstract': 'Deaths from drug overdoses rose by 6 percent in 2013 from 2012, the federal government said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/us/after-stabilizing-overdose-deaths-rose-in-2013-.html', 'snippet': 'Deaths from drug overdoses rose by 6 percent in 2013 from 2012, the federal government said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deaths from drug overdoses rose by 6 percent in 2013 from 2012, the federal government said Monday, reversing progress made in 2012, when the national rate, which had long been increasing, appeared to have stabilized. The 2013 increase was driven in part by a 39 percent jump in heroin deaths, the third consecutive year of increases for that drug. Deaths from opioid pain relievers — the biggest cause of drug overdose deaths — were up by about 1 percent in 2013. In 2012, such deaths declined by 5 percent, the first drop since the late 1990s. That decline helped level out drug overdose deaths overall, for an increase of less than 1 percent from 2011 to 2012. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Stabilizing, Overdose Deaths Rose in 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Stabilizing, Overdose Deaths Rose in 2013', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-13T01:31:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/535ab220-76ac-534c-ac7e-53b3fe4db7be', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/535ab220-76ac-534c-ac7e-53b3fe4db7be'}, {'abstract': 'The injection of venture capital money into the cannabis industry will put pressure on some emerging fault lines.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/12/ethical-questions-of-investing-in-pot/', 'snippet': 'The injection of venture capital money into the cannabis industry will put pressure on some emerging fault lines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, the venture capital firm run by Peter Thiel — a co-founder of PayPal and an early investor in Facebook, SpaceX and Spotify — invested millions of dollars in a marijuana company.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/business/13SORKIN1/13SORKIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/13/business/13SORKIN1/13SORKIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'capt