//artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/in-performance-joey-slotnick-and-cj-wilson-of-dying-for-it/', 'snippet': 'A scene from Moira Buffini’s dark comedy adapted from Nikolai Erdman’s 1928 play “The Suicide.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s video features the actors Joey Slotnick and C.J. Wilson in a scene from the dark comedy “Dying for It,” an adaptation by the playwright Moira Buffini of Nikolai Erdman’s 1928 play “The Suicide.” Set in Moscow in 1929 over a decade after the Russian revolution, the play tells the story of Semyon Semyonovich (played by Mr. Slotnik), who cannot find a job or any meaning in his life and decides to end it all. In this scene, Semyon discovers that his friend Alexander (Mr. Wilson) is exploiting his proposed suicide for money. The show, directed by Neil Pepe for the Atlantic Theater Company, is at the Linda Gross Theater through Jan. 18. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Joey Slotnick and C.J. Wilson of ‘Dying for It’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slotnick, Joey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, C J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-13T13:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ea17e86-bdfe-5222-ba97-ead72bb8bc02', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ea17e86-bdfe-5222-ba97-ead72bb8bc02'}, {'abstract': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email i