'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gluten', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juices', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quinoa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-13T14:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Neilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/886fc932-4e73-57fb-ad68-e1395acc2190', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/886fc932-4e73-57fb-ad68-e1395acc2190'}, {'abstract': 'The country is still wrestling with its wartime past and there have been calls for a boycott of the film.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/angelina-jolie-on-how-japan-may-view-unbroken/', 'snippet': 'The country is still wrestling with its wartime past and there have been calls for a boycott of the film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ll know early Thursday whether Angelina Jolie’s “Unbroken,” which, after months of anticipatory hoopla, was toasted by the American Film Institute but received no Golden Globes love, will land one of the Academy’s best picture nominations. Another place where “Unbroken’s” reception remains unknown is Japan, where the book on which the film is based has not been translated and the country’s wartime past is the subject of debate. Though the film has yet to open there, there have been reports of outrage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/angelinapost/angelinapost-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/angelinapost/angelinapost-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 847}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/angelinapost/angelinapost-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/angelinapost/angelinapost-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1450, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/angelinapost/angelinapost-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/angelinapost/angelinapost-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/arts/angelinapost/angelinapost-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Angelina Jolie on How Japan May View ‘Unbroken’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolie, Angelina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miyavi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-13T14:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1dbc5b6-0b91-5e6e-a37d-e6f53f789492', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1dbc5b6-0b91-5e6e-a37d-e6f53f789492'}, {'abstract': 'Yay tax cuts, never mind positive effects of spending.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/selective-voodoo/', 'snippet': 'Yay tax cuts, never mind positive effects of spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'House Republicans have passed a measure demanding that the Congressional Budget Office use “dynamic scoring” in its revenue projections — taking into account the supposed positive growth effects of tax cuts. It remains to be seen how much damage this rule will actually cause. The reality is that there is no evidence for the large effects that are central to right-wing ideology, so the question is whether CBO will be forced to accept supply-side fantasies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Selective Voodoo', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-13T14:19:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/474e9958-f241-5743-91e3-d4f62e8e88f2', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/474e9958-f241-5743-91e3-d4f62e8e88f2'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s effort comes in the wake of a series of high-profile computer breaches, the most recent involving the military’s Central Command.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/us/obama-to-announce-new-cyberattack-protections.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s effort comes in the wake of a series of high-profile computer breaches, the most recent involving the military’s Central Command.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama on Tuesday called on Congress to pass broad legislation to bolster cybersecurity across the United States government and private industry, working to capitalize on concern about recent high-profile computer breaches to counter an escalating threat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Calls for New Laws to Bolster Cybersecurity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Calls for New Laws to Bolster Cybersecurity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Julie Hirschfeld', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-13T14:21:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Hirschfeld Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'Hirschfeld', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d88da62-9bdf-534d-8ff7-c96d751860bf', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d88da62-9bdf-534d-8ff7-c96d751860bf'}, {'abstract': 'Ryanair said it would be prepared to consider an offer between 2.50 and 2.70 euros a share from the parent of British Airways.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/13/ryanair-expects-revised-i-a-g