n civil rights leader’s Bible and Nobel Prize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers for Bernice King, the daughter of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr., squared off Tuesday against lawyers for Dr. King’s estate in an effort to resolve the disputed ownership of the slain civil rights leader’s Bible and Nobel Prize. But a Fulton County Superior Court judge declined to side with either party, raising the possibility of a February trial. Ms. King contends that the items do not belong to the Estate of Martin Luther King Jr. Inc. The estate’s three directors are Ms. King and her two brothers, Dexter King and Martin Luther King III. The brothers voted earlier to sell the items. Ms. King objects to a sale.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: Fight Over King Legacy Is Closer to Trial', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: Fight Over King Legacy Is Closer to Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wills and Estates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Bernice Albertine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T00:52:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Fausset', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fausset', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3242fbc-6387-50c0-958d-b61300881d68', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3242fbc-6387-50c0-958d-b61300881d68'}, {'abstract': 'Tom A