'_id': 'nyt://article/a5451e29-4f2a-544a-aafd-0a7f5302e071', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5451e29-4f2a-544a-aafd-0a7f5302e071'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/arts/television/whats-on-tv-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:20 P.M. (Starz Cinema) HELLO I MUST BE GOING (2012) A divorced 30-something (Melanie Lynskey, above, now starring in HBO’s “Togetherness”) finds a haven from her adult problems in the suburban Connecticut home of her critical mother (Blythe Danner) and indulgent father (John Rubinstein) in this comedy written by Sarah Koskoff and directed by Todd Louiso. She also discovers sex and romance with a 19-year-old — the stepson (Christopher Abbott) of a potential client her father is desperate to impress — who has allowed his doting mother (Julie White) to believe he is gay. “Needless to say, there are complications, some farcical, some belonging more to the realm of therapeutic melodrama,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “This is ultimately a tale of affirmation, self-acceptance and second chances, and its lessons, while not unwelcome, are a bit too forced and neatly packaged to make it fully satisfying. But when Ms. Lynskey and Mr. Abbott are together, there are inklings of a wilder, riskier, less predictable movie — one you may wish the characters could escape into, even though you know they never will.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T05:29:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fbc9030-b444-5b9c-902c-7e6fc627b155', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fbc9030-b444-5b9c-902c-7e6fc627b155'}, {'abstract': 'While still at the apex of a stellar medical career, Dr. Graboys was found to have Parkinson’s disease. He detailed the stages of his illness in his autobiography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/health/thomas-graboys-doctor-who-recounted-struggle-with-parkinsons-is-dead-at-70.html', 'snippet': 'While still at the apex of a stellar medical career, Dr. Graboys was found to have Parkinson’s disease. He detailed the stages of his illness in his autobiography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he was just 5 years old, Thomas Graboys declared that he intended to become a doctor. As a young physician, he visited a nephew serving in the Peace Corps in Mauritania and remained for two months, treating dozens of patients a day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/arts/GRABOYS-obit/GRABOYS-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/14/arts/GRABOYS-obit/GRABOYS-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 573}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/arts/GRABOYS-obit/GRABOYS-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 979, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/arts/GRABOYS-obit/GRABOYS-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1958, 'widt