'_id': 'nyt://article/a54f3193-4779-5ed6-b215-30ef03075c0f', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a54f3193-4779-5ed6-b215-30ef03075c0f'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s plan to expand free access to two-year schools deserves Congress’s support.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/opinion/tom-hanks-on-his-two-years-at-chabot-college.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s plan to expand free access to two-year schools deserves Congress’s support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 1974, I graduated from Skyline High School in Oakland, Calif., an underachieving student with lousy SAT scores. Allowed to send my results to three colleges, I chose M.I.T. and Villanova, knowing such fine schools would never accept a student like me but hoping they’d toss some car stickers my way for taking a shot. I couldn’t afford tuition for college anyway. I sent my final set of stats to Chabot, a community college in nearby Hayward, Calif., which, because it accepted everyone and was free, would be my alma mater.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/opinion/14Hanks/14Hanks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 269, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/14/opinion/14Hanks/14Hanks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 269}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/opinion/14Hanks/14Hanks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/opinion/14Hanks/14Hanks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cr