nation as “systemically important.” | The Bitcoin industry is wrestling with a price slump.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/morning-agenda-profit-falls-at-jpmorgan-2/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan reports an unexpected drop in fourth-quarter profit. | MetLife sues to fight its designation as “systemically important.” | The Bitcoin industry is wrestling with a price slump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase kicked off fourth-quarter earnings season, reporting an unexpected drop in profit, DealBook’s Nathaniel Popper writes. The bank said its earnings fell 7 percent, to $4.9 billion, or $1.19 a share, from the $5.6 billion, or $1.30 a share, in the period a year earlier. The most recent results fell short of the $1.31 a share expected by analysts surveyed by Thomson Reuters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Profit Falls at JPMorgan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T12:52:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8006c13f-4368-5446-87db-f940fb04e673', 'word_count': 1818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8006c13f-4368-5446-87db-f940fb04e673'}, {'abstract': 'Studies raise interesting questions about those snug-fitting socks, shorts, tights or shirts that are reputed to improve performance during exercise and speed recovery afterward.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/can-compression-clothing-enhance-your-workout/', 'snippet': 'Studies raise interesting questions about those snug-fitting socks, shorts, tights or shirts that are reputed to improve performance during exercise and speed recovery afterward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, many people who exercise have begun wearing compression clothes. These snug-fitting socks, shorts, tights or shirts, which squeeze muscles as tightly as sausage casings, are reputed to improve performance during exercise and speed recovery afterward.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/health/14well_physed/14well_physed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/14/health/14well_physed/14well_physed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/health/14well_physed/14well_physed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/health/14well_physed/14well_physed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/health/14well_physed/14well_physed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/14/health/14well_physed/14well_physed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/health/14well_physed/14well_physed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Compression Clothing Enhance Your Workout?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T13:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4afaed0b-3138-5684-92f9-1d2a5f1cee15', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4afaed0b-3138-5684-92f9-1d2a5f1cee15'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of readers voiced their dissent to the executive editor’s decision, but The Times held its course.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/with-new-charlie-hebdo-cover-news-value-should-have-prevailed/', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of readers voiced their dissent to the executive editor’s decision, but The Times held its course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers responded passionately, and in large numbers, to my post last week about The Times’s decision not to publish the now-famous Charlie Hebdo cartoons of the Prophet Muhammad. (In fact, I’ve never had more comments on a post or column.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With New Charlie Hebdo Cover, News Value Should Have Prevailed', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baquet, Dean', 'rank': 4, 'major': '