t': 'Markets around the world dropped, and copper took the brunt of a sell-off, dropping more than 5 percent. The yield on the 30-year Treasury bond hit a record low.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/business/daily-stock-market-activity.html', 'snippet': 'Markets around the world dropped, and copper took the brunt of a sell-off, dropping more than 5 percent. The yield on the 30-year Treasury bond hit a record low.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The market showed signs of profound unease on Wednesday, notching losses for the fourth consecutive day amid signs that the sell-off in crude oil was on the verge of turning into a broader rout in commodities.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Closes Lower as Bond Yields and Commodity Prices Fall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Losses Mount on Fear Oil Sell-Off Will Drag Down Other Commodities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolly, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Stanley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T14:45:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly and Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9536201-d749-58c6-aa4e-1f92bbc2b551', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9536201-d749-58c6-aa4e-1f92bbc2b551'}, {'abstract': 'This time is different. No, really.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/convergence-in-two-global-economies/', 'snippet': 'This time is different. No, really.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m heading off for an India/Hong Kong/China tour in a few hours, which gives me a reason to stop thinking about deflation in the West for a bit and think about long-run growth issues instead. And one point I mean to make is that the world has changed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Convergence in Two Global Economies', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T14:46:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/977c7a0a-5105-559a-bb52-a8088038c09f', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/977c7a0a-5105-559a-bb52-a8088038c09f'}, {'abstract': 'Less than 12 hours after a warning alarm roused two astronauts from their sleep, everything was back to normal, NASA said, and there were strong indications that the problem was a faulty computer card rather than an actual leak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/science/space/international-space-station-ammonia-leak.html', 'snippet': 'Less than 12 hours after a warning alarm roused two astronauts from their sleep, everything was back to normal, NASA said, and there were strong indications that the problem was a faulty computer card rather than an actual leak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'International Space Station crew members evacuated to the Russian side of the station twice on Wednesday because of worries of a possible ammonia leak, but less than 12 hours after a warning alarm roused them from their sleep, everything was back to normal, NASA said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/us/SPACE/SPACE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/15/us/SPACE/SPACE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/us/SPACE/SPACE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/us/SPACE/SPACE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/us/SPACE/SPACE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/15/us/SPACE/SPACE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/us/SPACE/SPACE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Space Station Crew Temporarily Moves to Russian Side Over Fears of Ammonia Leak', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leak Fears Prompt Space Station Shuffling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Space Station', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson Space Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T14:49:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c9613ad-753d-59b7-b078-39f7e12a5ffd', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c9613ad-753d-59b7-b078-39f7e12a5ffd'}, {'abstract': 'Ariane de Rothschild will serve as chairwoman of the private bank’s executive committee, succeeding Christophe de Backer after he steps down as chief executive at the end of the month.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/edmond-de-rothschild-group-names-chairmans-wife-as-c-e-o/', 'snippet': 'Ariane de Rothschild will serve as chairwoman of the private bank’s executive committee, succeeding Christophe de Backer after he steps down as chief executive at the end of the month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The Edmond de Rothschild Group, a private Swiss bank, said on Wednesday that it had named the wife of its chairman to serve as chief executive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edmond de Rothschild Group Names Chairman’s Wife as C.E.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Backer, Christophe Raoul Fernand (1962- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Rothschild, Ariane (1965- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Rothschild, Benjamin (1963- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Edmond de Rothschild Group', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T14:49:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3072c84e-a14f-54ce-b313-3bb74a9b7dfe', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3072c84e-a14f-54ce-b313-3bb74a9b7dfe'}, {'abstract': 'A new picture book from the cartoonist Roz Chast supplies a laugh for every hour of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/books/review/roz-chasts-around-the-clock.html', 'snippet': 'A new picture book from the cartoonist Roz Chast supplies a laugh for every hour of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After reading aloud to my children virtually every night for over a decade — my daughter just turned 12, and my sons are 9 and 4 — I have, of course, many book recommendations, but I also have some strategic suggestions. The first is, if you can’t picture yourself reading a particular book nightly for, oh, two straight months, don’t even bring it into the house. Small children have a huge appetite for repetition, and you never know what will catch their interest. So be wary. I recently brought home “Hello Kitty Goes to Camp,” which comes with postcards to send home, thinking it would be an opportunity for “ironic” bonding with my frighteningly culturally sophisticated preteenage daughter. She didn’t bite. Then the 4-year-old found it and, fascinated by his sister’s two recent sleepaway camp disappearances, has demanded to hear it for many, many nights now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/14childrens-1/14childrens-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/14childrens-1/14childrens-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/14childrens-1/14childrens-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/14childrens-1/14childrens-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/14childrens-1/14childrens-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/14childrens-1/14childrens-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/14childrens-1/14childrens-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crazy All the Time', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 