: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/style/how-to-use-snapchat-as-well-as-a-14-year-old.html', 'snippet': 'A primer on how to tell stories through Snapchat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Snapchat Stories are pretty confusing to figure out on your own, so here’s a handy guide to get you started. Remember: don’t worry about making your Stories pretty or perfect; they’ll disappear in 24 hours.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1067}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1152, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE/15SUBDISRUPTSIDE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Use Snapchat Like a 14-Year-Old', 'kicker': 'Disruptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Using Snapchat as a Storybook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Snapchat Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Instant Messaging', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T16:18:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efc0b00c-9fdd-5994-9028-493f61268774', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efc0b00c-9fdd-5994-9028-493f61268774'}, {'abstract': 'One of the favored fabrics of the ’70s found its way onto the runways this week, but these weren’t the thrifty sort of cords one might expect.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/london-mens-collection-fall-2015-corduroy-gets-a-luxurious-reboot/', 'snippet': 'One of the favored fabrics of the ’70s found its way onto the runways this week, but these weren’t the thrifty sort of cords one might expect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s clear that ’70s nostalgia is the trend of the moment, with designers of both women’s and men’s fashion lately taking cues from the decade in their collections. So it comes as no surprise that one of the favored fabrics of the era, corduroy, found its way into the men’s shows in London this week. These weren’t the thrifty sort of cords one might expect, however. The new designer Alex Mullins, who debuted his collection in a fluorescent-lit room filled with empty cardboard boxes, featured Me Decade-inspired knits and denim as well as corduroy. One look referenced the classic professorial type (think Donald Sutherland in the 1978 comedy “Animal House”), but its slightly odd proportions — cropped and flared trousers with a fitted jacket — made the suit more eccentric than dowdy. J.W. Anderson incorporated the durable ridged fabric — in a very ’70s powder blue, to boot — into a short zipped jacket with a contrasting black collar. Styled with a pair of leather trousers on a model with slick hair, the jacket looked sharp, urbane and dangerously cool. And at Burberry Prorsum, the British fashion house’s traditional trench was fabricated in a larger-scaled corduroy, giving the coat a bit more heft and the retro cloth a much more modern vibe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/t-magazine/13london-trend-corduroy/13london-trend-corduroy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/13/t-magazine/13london-trend-corduroy/13london-trend-corduroy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/t-magazine/13london-trend-corduroy/13london-trend-corduroy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/t-magazine/13london-trend-corduroy/13london-trend-corduroy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/t-magazine/13london-trend-corduroy/13london-trend-corduroy-thumbStandard-v2.j