01/14/a-promotion-for-lydia-davis-in-french-order-of-arts-and-letters/', 'snippet': 'The writer and translator Lydia Davis, already a chevalier in the French Order of Arts and Letters, is being named an officer in the order.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lydia Davis, the writer and translator acclaimed for her elegant English versions of Marcel Proust’s “Swann’s Way” and Gustave Flaubert’s “Madame Bovary,” and Kent Jones, the director of the New York Film Festival at Lincoln Center, will be honored by the French Ministry of Culture and Communication for their contributions to the arts. Ms. Davis will be named an officer, and Mr. Jones a chevalier, of the Order of Arts and Letters on Thursday at the Cultural Services of the French Embassy in Manhattan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Promotion for Lydia Davis in French Order of Arts and Letters', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Translation and Interpreters', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Lydia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Kent', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T17:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role'