': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/subamazon/subamazon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1551, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/subamazon/subamazon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/subamazon/subamazon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/subamazon/subamazon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Comes Out Swinging', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amazon Comes Out Swinging', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Down Dog (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Man in the High Castle (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T22:14:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b1b14da-fa05-5b45-a7a4-94e452199c6b', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b1b14da-fa05-5b45-a7a4-94e452199c6b'}, {'abstract': 'Cheyenne Jackson was open and upbeat as he sang standards and contemporary material at Café Carlyle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/arts/music/cheyenne-jackson-at-cafe-carlyle.html', 'snippet': 'Cheyenne Jackson was open and upbeat as he sang standards and contemporary material at Café Carlyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Cheyenne Jackson closed his eyes and crooned “Falling Slowly” with an unwavering intensity on Tuesday evening at Café Carlyle, this great ballad from “Once” never sounded more profound and mysterious. For a moment, Mr. Jackson, who was joined on harmony vocal by his excellent musical director, Willy Beaman, transcended his wholesome image of a handsome, genial all-American boy from northeast Washington State who once played Elvis Presley on Broadway and went deep.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/CHEYENNE/CHEYENNE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/CHEYENNE/CHEYENNE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/CHEYENNE/CHEYENNE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/CHEYENNE/CHEYENNE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/CHEYENNE/CHEYENNE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/CHEYENNE/CHEYENNE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/CHEYENNE/CHEYENNE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Crooner and a Belter All in One', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Crooner and a Belter All in One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Cheyenne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe Carlyle (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T22:23:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/670b4791-b9d1-55f4-ad31-bcf77e833ae1', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/670b4791-b9d1-55f4-ad31-bcf77e833ae1'}, {'abstract': 'The painter Tal R’s “Alstadt Girl” series features a variety of women in states of repose — some of whom Tal R stops on the street to ask to pose.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/14/tal-r-paints-nudes-that-allude-to-matisse-bonnard-and-balthus/', 'snippet': 'The painter Tal R’s “Alstadt Girl” series features a variety of women in states of repose — some of whom Tal R stops on the street to ask to pose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever been stopped on the street and been asked to pose nude for a painting? “There are people you look at that you want to draw,” says Tal R, the figurative painter whose mysterious last initial hides as much as the whispers of his aspirated English. The Israeli-born artist — the R stands for Rosenzweig — specializes in florid canvases, especially his new series “Altstadt Girl”: naked women in all states of repose, vivid in red. One is a 16-year-old whose mother granted permission for her to model: “She was smoking in this beautiful arrogant way that you do when you are young because you own the world,” the artist says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evocative Nudes That Allude to Matisse, Bonnard and Balthus', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nudism and Nudity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balthus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matisse, Henri', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-14T22:25:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4317d610-2f6d-59ab-8bd6-3da5b944f9fe', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4317d610-2f6d-59ab-8bd6-3da5b944f9fe'}, {'abstract': 'In “Fear the Darkness,” Becky Masterman’s second novel, the investigator Brigid Quinn returns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/arts/becky-mastermans-fear-the-darkness-with-brigid-quinn.html', 'snippet': 'In “Fear the Darkness,” Becky Masterman’s second novel, the investigator Brigid Quinn returns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Becky Masterman’s first book, “Rage Against the Dying” (2013), introduced a highly original heroine for a detective series. She was Brigid Quinn, an ex-F.B.I. agent old enough to be mistaken for a fragile granny by a sexual predator, who spied her out hiking one day and tried to shove her into his van. Boy, was that sexual predator ever sorry. At 59, Brigid had a white ponytail and a walking stick — but she also had 40 years’ worth of vigorous conditioning and a wicked way of fighting. That walking stick came equipped with a razor blade. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 766}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 803, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1847, 'width': 1447, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/BOOKMASTERMAN/BOOKMASTERMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/arts/BOOKM