ll Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strom, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pork', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T01:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12bafb68-c183-5475-8b63-5f8c34c8b3dd', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12bafb68-c183-5475-8b63-5f8c34c8b3dd'}, {'abstract': 'Dover Street Market to close for three days for a full-on “seasonal changeover” and sales this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/fashion/shopping-sales-and-events-in-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': 'Dover Street Market to close for three days for a full-on “seasonal changeover” and sales this week.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xadIt’s normal this time of year for stores to be making room for new merchandise, but leave it to Dover Street Market to close for three days for a full-on “seasonal changeover.” Reopening Saturday, the luxury emporium will debut several dedicated shop-in-shops and exclusive collections. On the third floor, look out for the first permanent United States retail space for Idea Books, the London distributor of rare art and fashion books and magazines — “4 x 4” by Richard Prince ($195) and Visionaire No. 20: Comme des Garçons ($1,750) may entice — and a new home for Miu Miu. In the DSM Showroom for emerging designers on the fourth floor, you’ll find an oversize V-neck mesh top ($1,530) and a neoprene and space-mesh skirt with bow ($930) designed by Andrea Jiapei Li, a recent graduate from the M.F.A. program at Parsons the New School of Design; and a conceptual taffeta party frock ($2,675) from the Central Saint Martins alumna Molly Goddard. At 160 Lexington Avenue. \xad', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/14SCOUT/14SCOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/14SCOUT/14SCOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/14SCOUT/14SCOUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/14SCOUT/14SCOUT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/14SCOUT/14SCOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/14SCOUT/14SCOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/fashion/14SCOUT/14SCOUT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping Sales and Events in New York City', 'kicker': 'Scouting Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T01:08:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f432a29-2e4a-52c1-9986-e901cb1b9d07', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f432a29-2e4a-52c1-9986-e901cb1b9d07'}, {'abstract': 'Five teenage boys patrolled the Long Island Expressway on Wednesday, looking for $178,000 in cash that supposedly fell out of the back of an armored truck the day before.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/nyregion/fistfuls-of-cash-spilled-on-expressway-swirl-in-young-imaginations-only.html', 'snippet': 'Five teenage boys patrolled the Long Island Expressway on Wednesday, looking for $178,000 in cash that supposedly fell out of the back of an armored truck the day before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five teenage boys in Corona, Queens, awoke on Wednesday to the sort of question that can shape a young man’s future, dividing life into two sections: the part before that morning, and the part that followed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/15/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'widt