ness for felines.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s worth reading all of this 1872 editiorial (PDF), headlined “Cats and Craziness,” to follow the author’s full argument that “lunatics” often have an “excessive fondness for cats.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Throwback Thursday | Cat People and Dog People', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T12:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33e190ba-8846-523a-89d2-8ecbb4543936', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33e190ba-8846-523a-89d2-8ecbb4543936'}, {'abstract': 'A sharp dissent held that the drug combination being used in Oklahoma risked causing severe, unconstitutional suffering. But the other five justices voted without comment to deny the appeal for a stay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/us/oklahoma-execution-charles-warner-lethal-injection.html', 'snippet': 'A sharp dissent held that the drug combination being used in Oklahoma risked causing severe, unconstitutional suffering. But the other five justices voted without comment to deny the appeal for a stay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'McALESTER, Okla. — With a renovated death chamber, new training and a higher dose of drugs, Oklahoma on Thursday carried out its first execution since April, when the slipshod, prolonged killing of Clayton D. Lockett led the state to suspend lethal injections and change its procedures. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, '