on_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/0d46b6f7-f768-53a2-aa6e-5bee7dabc19e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/0d46b6f7-f768-53a2-aa6e-5bee7dabc19e'}, {'abstract': 'The original football superagent tries to pull off a fourth-quarter comeback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/magazine/show-leigh-steinberg-the-money-again-.html', 'snippet': 'The original football superagent tries to pull off a fourth-quarter comeback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leigh Steinberg stepped onto the football field at Southern Methodist University under a cloudy Texas sky. At events he hosts — like his gigantic annual Super Bowl bash — Steinberg, a sports agent, is accustomed to parading around like a presidential candidate, working the crowd with a boyish smile and a pinstripe suit. On the Dallas campus last March, in his sweatshirt and baggy bluejeans, Steinberg looked more like a guy at the local horse track. He riffled through a booklet of notes and popped a stick of Nicorette into his mouth. His client, the quarterback Garrett Gilbert, was the one who had to put on a show in front of more than 30 N.F.L. scouts, but Steinberg’s own prospects were also being tested.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18steinberg1/18steinberg1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 463, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18steinberg1/18steinberg1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 463}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18steinberg1/18steinberg1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18steinberg1/18steinberg1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1581, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18steinberg1/18steinberg1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18steinberg1/18steinberg1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18steinberg1/18steinberg1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Show Leigh Steinberg the Money (Again)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Show Him the Money (Again)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinberg, Leigh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vlahos, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGENTS (BUSINESS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T14:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Vlahos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlahos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d499c3b8-a172-556c-b49f-8b2ffa5d3dc7', 'word_count': 3485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d499c3b8-a172-556c-b49f-8b2ffa5d3dc7'}, {'abstract': 'The workers who patrol Oahu’s North Shore battle a force far greater than anything that technology can overcome: In 2013, they handled more than 1,000 ocean rescues and major medical cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/sports/oahu-lifeguards-face-a-challenge-as-relentless-as-the-waves.html', 'snippet': 'The workers who patrol Oahu’s North Shore battle a force far greater than anything that technology can overcome: In 2013, they handled more than 1,000 ocean rescues and major medical cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HALEIWA, Hawaii — Dusk masked the approaching waves at Banzai Pipeline on the North Shore of Oahu as they climbed to 15 feet before pounding the shallow, jagged reef below. Adrift in the rapid current and foamy sea was a photographer, exhausted from battling the relentless waves and fighting for his life.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surf Is Fierce, but So Are They ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surf Is Fierce, but So Are They', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surfing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corasaniti, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lifeguards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oahu (Hawaii)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lerner, Adam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fletcher, Nathan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T14:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb5cdce6-ba16-5281-9626-da30b5e186cd', 'word_count': 1334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb5cdce6-ba16-5281-9626-da30b5e186cd'}, {'abstract': 'With his lease expiring, Joseph Nawy searched for a one-bedroom apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/realestate/an-upper-east-side-apartment-in-a-hurry.html', 'snippet': 'With his lease expiring, Joseph Nawy searched for a one-bedroom apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph Nawy grew up on Manhattan’s Upper West Side. After his marriage, he lived first in Queens and then in New Jersey. When his two sons were grown, he and his wife moved to Tennessee for work. Shortly thereafter, his wife died.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/realestate/18HUNT-MAIN/18HUNT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/realestate/18HUNT-MAIN/18HUNT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/realestate/18HUNT-MAIN/18HUNT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/realestate/18HUNT-MAIN/18HUNT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/realestate/18HUNT-MAIN/18HUNT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/realestate/18HUNT-MAIN/18HUNT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/realestate/18HUNT-MAIN/18HUNT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Upper East Side Apartment in a Hurry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Buyer Up Against a Ticking Clock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Joyce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T14:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/691fda06-1577-5f7e-beee-fedad1d769eb', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/691fda06-1577-5f7e-beee-fedad1d769eb'}, {'abstract': 'To find the perfect brand, leave no word unturned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/magazine/the-weird-science-of-naming-new-products.html', 'snippet': 'To find the perfect brand, leave no word unturned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The announcement came in November with two names attached: one famous, one not, or at least not yet. The famous name was Paul McCartney. Anyone who wanted to try a virtual-reality experience starring the former Beatle — replicating the sensation of standing center stage with him as he sang “Live and Let Die” to 70,000 screaming fans — had only to download a special video file, put the file into an app for their Android phone and slip the phone into a cardboard headset designed by Google. The not-yet-famous name was of the virtual-reality production process that created this experience. Reviewers said it was “mind-\xadblowingly cool” and an “exciting preview of the future,” but it was also so novel that it had been hard to think of a word to label it. Its inventors had wanted a name that would lodge in the public consciousness the same way Dolby and Imax and Blu-ray had. A name that could become a verb as well as a noun. An iconic name. A name for the ages.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18naming1-copy/18naming1-copy-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18naming1-copy/18naming1-copy-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18naming1-copy/18naming1-copy-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18naming1-copy/18naming1-copy-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18naming1-copy/18naming1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18naming1-copy/18naming1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/magazine/18naming1-copy/18naming1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Weird Science of Naming New Products', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Call It What It Is', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabler, Neal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Organizational', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jaunt Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interbrand', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shore, Anthony (1967- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T14:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neal Gabler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca8d144c-e2bd-59a2-ad04-fc94f46aefc2', 'word_count': 4840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca8d144c-e2bd-59a2-ad04-fc94f46aefc2'}, {'abstract': 'Creative chefs are giving visitors another reason to go to West Waterford.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/travel/in-southeast-ireland-a-culinary-and-coastal-destination.html', 'snippet': 'Creative chefs are giving visitors another reason to go to West Waterford.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The West Waterford region on Ireland’s southeast coast is a favorite among the Irish for its idyllic beaches, picturesque villages and sprawling green fields blanketed with sheep. Now the area, an hour’s drive east from Cork, is fast becoming known for its epicurean culture, which includes new high-quality restaurants and food purveyors.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/travel/18HU2-copy/18HU2-copy-articleLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/travel/18HU2-copy/18HU2-copy-articleLarge-v7.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/travel/18HU2-copy/18HU2-copy-jumbo-v7.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/travel/18HU2-copy/18HU2-copy-superJumbo-v7.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/travel/18HU2-copy/18HU2-copy-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/travel/18HU2-copy/18HU2-copy-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/travel/18HU2-copy/18HU2-copy-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Southeast Ireland, a Culinary and Coastal Destination', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Scenery’s Great but What’s for Dinner?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Waterford (Ireland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T14:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/888138ef-f853-59ab-ab5f-9915afa40fe7', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/888138ef-f853-59ab-ab5f-9915afa40fe7'}, {'abstract': 'The Festival on the Niger, in Ségou, Mali, does much to cheer and calm a country recently torn by jihadists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/travel/along-the-niger-river-the-beat-of-the-sahel.html', 'snippet': 'The Festival on the Niger, in Ségou, Mali, does much to cheer and calm a country recently torn by jihadists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Down by the Niger River last February, a Tuareg street performer was warming up the crowd. The evening concert at the Festival on the Niger was about to begin, and the promenade inside the concert grounds was filled with early arrivals. Dozens had gathered in a circle around the elderly nomad, who was draped in a blue robe and a black veil. Robe flying, the toothless dervish hurled himself to the ground, flipped and twirled with the loose-limbed dexterity of a teenager. Two Tuareg women, seated cross-legged on the ground, served as his musical backups: One beat a calabash with a plastic sandal, the other played a tapered wood-and-goatskin drum known as a tendé.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/travel/18MALI1/18MALI1-arti