'main': 'Plant Love House', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Elmhurst (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Plant Love House (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T16:53:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/aa9732ac-8da2-5b93-b0cc-ef84db7d1fec', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/aa9732ac-8da2-5b93-b0cc-ef84db7d1fec'}, {'abstract': 'At Plant Love House in Elmhurst, Queens, a mother and her daughters offer Thai street food with house rules that will have you grinning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/dining/hungry-city-plant-love-house-in-elmhurst-queens.html', 'snippet': 'At Plant Love House in Elmhurst, Queens, a mother and her daughters offer Thai street food with house rules that will have you grinning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s only at the end that the blood is tipped in, just before the bowl of num tok — an opaque, nearly black Thai noodle soup — is brought to the table. This is time enough for the blood to disperse in the broth and lose its drawn-sword tang. What I tasted was more elliptical: salt, minerals, a distinctly animal sweetness. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answering the Call of Friends ', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Answer to the Call of Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'E