ply into the history, culture...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | For more than half a century, the United States has feuded — sometimes to the edge of war — with the island nation of Cuba. Now that mutual hostility could be coming to an end with last month’s announcement that the two countries will resume diplomatic relations. How will life change for people in both countries?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thawing Relations: Teaching About Cuba and the U.S.', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Raul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T19:38:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Marshall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marshall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46688a3f-8843-5cc2-aab4-b8ab0891dc60', 'word_count': 1436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46688a3f-8843-5cc2-aab4-b8ab0891dc60'}, {'abstract': 'The service, which has a catalog of more than 30 million songs for $2 a month, is beating its Western rivals into the populous country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/business/media/rdio-a-streaming-music-service-to-open-in-india.html', 'snippet': 'The service, which has a catalog of more than 30 million songs for $2 a month, is beating its Western rivals into the populous country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The streaming music wars have arrived in India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rdio, a Streaming Music Service, to Open in India', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spotify', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rdio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T19:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cde8a78a-561e-5b3d-93d4-0af3ebf12a52', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cde8a78a-561e-5b3d-93d4-0af3ebf12a52'}, {'abstract': 'In response to her selection, Ms. Ernst, the first woman elected to federal office from Iowa, said: “It’s a long way from Red Oak, Iowa, to Washington, D.C. But now that I am here, I am excited to get to work in order to craft and implement real solutions as we chart a new path forward for our great nation.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/01/15/senator-ernst-of-iowa-to-deliver-state-of-the-union-response/', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'In response to her selection, Ms. Ernst, the first woman elected to federal office from Iowa, said: “It’s a long way from Red Oak, Iowa, to Washington, D.C. But now that I am here, I am excited to get to work in order to craft and implement real solutions as we chart a new path forward for our great nation.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Ernst, of Iowa, to Deliver State of the Union Response', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T19:45:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a223a87a-2139-542c-a8af-001b7984cf4b', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a223a87a-2139-542c-a8af-001b7984cf4b'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations hopes to negotiate a cease-fire around the northern city and restart a process “with a clear political horizon.” But diplomats see little sign of a breakthrough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/world/middleeast/un-to-resume-cease-fire-talks-with-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations hopes to negotiate a cease-fire around the northern city and restart a process “with a clear political horizon.” But diplomats see little sign of a breakthrough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The United Nations will resume talks with the Syrian government next week in the hope of achieving a cease-fire around Aleppo, the largest city in the north, the special envoy for Syria said Thursday. But the specifics remained hazy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. to Renew Syria Talks, Seeking Aleppo Cease-Fire ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. to Renew Syria Talks, Seeking Aleppo Cease-Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Mistura, Staffan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T19:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c31f8ea-1b18-5cd5-83fd-8e117303a2ae', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c31f8ea-1b18-5cd5-83fd-8e117303a2ae'}, {'abstract': 'Some Oscar counterprogramming.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/the-year-in-movies/', 'snippet': 'Some Oscar counterprogramming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, Frank Bruni and I steered\xa0our latest movies-and-politics dialogue\xa0into the open water between the Golden Globes and the Oscar nominations, wrangling a little over some of the holiday releases, particularly “American Sniper,” which neither of us loved but whose politics (or lack of politics) I was more inclined to defend, while finding a little bit more common ground in the great-“Selma”-and-historical-accuracy debate. That common ground was mildly critical of the way “Selma” so explicitly black-hats Lyndon Johnson, but now that the Oscar nominations are out and neither the\xa0movie’s director nor its star earned a nomination I wish I’d muted my criticism even more, because if accuracy\xa0issues peeled off any support from the film it’s a pretty terrible to reason to have Ana DuVernay and David Oyelowo lose out to\xa0— well, basically anyone associated “Foxcatcher,” “The Theory of Everything,” and “The Imitation Game,” all of which are based-on-true-story movies that are just as vulnerable as “Selma” to historical-inaccuracy critiques, and none of which (despite various strengths) feature directing or acting that equals the work that DuVernay and Oyelowo turned in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year in Movies', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, WES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruni, Frank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandor, J C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oyelowo, David', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swinton, Tilda', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zweig, Stefan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T19:57:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fff6bd42-7a9a-5112-a686-9eecdb65ff51', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fff6bd42-7a9a-5112-a686-9eecdb65ff51'}, {'abstract': 'A federal study found that there was no reliable way to get at the communications of terrorism suspects without sweeping up records of every call in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/us/politics/report-finds-no-alternative-to-bulk-collection-of-phone-data.html', 'snippet': 'A federal study found that there was no reliable way to get at the communications of terrorism suspects without sweeping up records of every call in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A federal study released on Thursday concluded that there was no effective alternative to the government’s “bulk collection” of basic information about every telephone call made in the United States, a practice that civil rights advocates call overly intrusive.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Finds No Substitute for Mass Data Collection', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Finds No Substitute for Mass Data Collection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T20:03:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/421c115e-c167-5a34-b128-743cfd324ed0', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/421c115e-c167-5a34-b128-743cfd324ed0'}, {'abstract': 'Rachel Rossin’s “n=7/The Wake in Heat of Collapse,” an interactive installation, will be open to the public Friday at Signal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/nyregion/a-virtual-reality-installation-in-bushwick.html', 'snippet': 'Rachel Rossin’s “n=7/The Wake in Heat of Collapse,” an interactive installation, will be open to the public Friday at Signal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miser, giving in to nostalgia, recently began playing a Nintendo 64 game in which he has 72 hours to defeat a masked menace before the moon falls on a fictional land. But the apocalypse is more like a reset button; “game over” is shorthand for “let’s try that again.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' Rachel Rossin’s Virtual-Reality Installation in Bushwick', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rachel Rossin’s Virtual-Reality Installation in Bushwick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juilliard415', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rossin, Rachel (1987- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T20:05:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Barone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/851856ff-8208-5d94-8850-e7012d06c4d1', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/851856ff-8208-5d94-8850-e7012d06c4d1'}, {'abstract': 'A profile of Woody Allen and reviews in The New York Times from the early 1960s capture the rapport he forged with audiences in his early stand-up comedy routines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/nyregion/woody-allens-early-stand-up-years.html', 'snippet': 'A profile of Woody Allen and reviews in The New York Times from the early 1960s capture the rapport he forged with audiences in his early stand-up comedy routines.', 'lead_paragraph': '53 YEARS AGO', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times',