one}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b76dede-484d-5f8c-aa91-65b439ab2b4d', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b76dede-484d-5f8c-aa91-65b439ab2b4d'}, {'abstract': 'Learn about how we’ve been unit testing a RequireJS application at The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/how-to-unit-test-a-requirejs-application/', 'snippet': 'Learn about how we’ve been unit testing a RequireJS application at The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adding unit tests to an existing application can be a challenge. If the application wasn’t developed with testing in mind, getting your source code into shape so that your components are isolated and testable is like adding a new character to a story after the book is already written. Significant refactoring must be done to decouple and test your code.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Unit Test a RequireJS Application', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T20:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Wilhelm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilhelm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/103c3419-0bf1-5895-a6f6-8360958aa6dd', 'word_count': 2654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/103c3419-0bf1-5895-a6f6-8360958aa6dd'}, {'abstract': 'In Willy Decker’s production of Verdi’s “La Traviata” at the Metropolitan Opera, the soprano Sonya Yoncheva plays a Violetta full of vitality and sensuality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/arts/music/sonya-yoncheva-stars-in-verdis-la-traviata.html', 'snippet': 'In Willy Decker’s production of Verdi’s “La Traviata” at the Metropolitan Opera, the soprano Sonya Yoncheva plays a Violetta full of vitality and sensuality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Willy Decker’s production of Verdi’s “La Traviata,” a painted backdrop of jewel-tone flowers looms over the second act. As Violetta’s hopes and prospects dim, the blooms’ color seems to slowly leach away, leaving an ashen field of gray.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/TRAVIATA/TRAVIATA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/TRAVIATA/TRAVIATA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 759}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/TRAVIATA/TRAVIATA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 809, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/TRAVIATA/TRAVIATA-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1924, 'width': 1520, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/TRAVIATA/TRAVIATA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/TRAVIATA/TRAVIATA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/TRAVIATA/TRAVIATA-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Irrepressible Passion, Laced With Sadness', 'kicker': 'Opera Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Irrepressible Passion, Laced With Sadness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Decker, Willy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoncheva, Sonya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'La Traviata (Opera)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T20:44:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ef82d6c-49b2-5efe-9ae4-0aeabbb629bb', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ef82d6c-49b2-5efe-9ae4-0aeabbb629bb'}, {'abstract': 'The French conceptual artist Pierre Huyghe has been asked to create an installation for the roof of the Met.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/arts/design/coming-to-the-mets-rooftop-a-pierre-huyghe-installation.html', 'snippet': 'The French conceptual artist Pierre Huyghe has been asked to create an installation for the roof of the Met.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French conceptual artist Pierre Huyghe often plunges viewers into his own, fantastical universe. It can take a surprising number of forms. His creations can include film, performance, sculpture, magic, biology, even nature like insects. So when Sheena Wagstaff, the chairwoman of the Metropolitan Museum’s modern and contemporary art department, and Ian Alteveer, a Met associate curator, saw the beguiling environment Mr. Huyghe created at Documenta 13 in 2012 and the retrospective first at the Pompidou Center in Paris and now on view at the Los Angeles County Museum of Art, they asked him to create a site-specific installation for the roof of the Met next spring. “His work is so captivating, and the way he thinks about the layers of a site, taking into account history, environment and science is so compelling, we thought he’d create something particularly interesting,” Mr. Alteveer said.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16VOGEL/VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16VOGEL/VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16VOGEL/VOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16VOGEL/VOGEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1322, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16VOGEL/VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16VOGEL/VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16VOGEL/VOGEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline'