ge of what promised to be a massive, violence-threatened march in Alabama, led by the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr., to demand free-and-clear voting rights for African-Americans. On short notice, the editor, Stephen Somerstein, grabbed five cameras, climbed on a bus and headed south.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Long March Into History ', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Long March Into History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Somerstein, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New-York Historical Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T23:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/757ca17b-db81-54be-b622-9c714e17bdc9', 'word_count': 1374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/757ca17b-db81-54be-b622-9c714e17bdc9'}, {'abstract': 'Tommy Caldwell and Kevin Jorgeson spoke after their 19-day climb of the Dawn Wall on El Capitan in Yosemite National Park, Calif.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000003452717/yosemite-climbers-talk-about-ascent.html', 'snippet':