e9-5a23-9438-852e30f28b10'}, {'abstract': 'Loris Gréaud’s “The Unplayed Notes Museum,” modeled on a natural history museum, will occupy the entire 26,000-foot exhibition space at the Dallas Contemporary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/15/unplayed-notes-dallas-contemporary-loris-greaud/', 'snippet': 'Loris Gréaud’s “The Unplayed Notes Museum,” modeled on a natural history museum, will occupy the entire 26,000-foot exhibition space at the Dallas Contemporary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Loris Gréaud is one of the biggest names in the Parisian art world, but chances are you’ve never heard of him; the 35-year-old artist has rarely shown his work in the United States. Beginning his career with delicate projects probing the nature of the universe through collaborations with specialists in other fields — scientists, writers, engineers and sound designers, to name a few — by 2008 he had already pulled off an institutional coup, filling the entire Palais du Tokyo with a solo show, for the first time ever. Then, five years later in summer 2013, the Pompidou and the Louvre joined forces to present joint exhibitions by Gréaud, another first.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mysterious New Show in Dallas from a Young French Heavyweight', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greaud, Loris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-15T23:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None,