on': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bombardier Plans Layoffs and $1.4 Billion Write-Down', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bombardier to Cut Jobs as It Halts Work on Plane', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bombardier Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T00:42:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e64bf53-7ea4-5e81-98c3-92b4938d1bb7', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e64bf53-7ea4-5e81-98c3-92b4938d1bb7'}, {'abstract': 'Philippe Dauman, a lawyer, received $37.2 million in 2013 in salary, stock and options.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/business/media/viacom-chiefs-contract-extended-until-2018.html', 'snippet': 'Philippe Dauman, a lawyer, received $37.2 million in 2013 in salary, stock and options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Viacom, the media group that includes MTV, Comedy Central and Nickelodeon as well as the Paramount film studio, has extended the contract of its chief executive and president, Philippe Dauman, until 2018, the company said Thursday. His contract was set to expire in 2016. Mr. Dauman, 60, a lawyer and deal maker, became chief in 2006, beating out rivals from the creative side of the company to install himself as the leading candidate to succeed the executive chairman and founder, Sumner M. Redstone, 91. Mr. Redstone said Mr. Dauman had “been an extraordinary C.E.O.” and “his strategic vision and creative leadership have delivered consistently outstanding operational and financial results.” Mr. Dauman received $37.2 million in 2013 in salary, stock and options. In the quarter that ended last September, ratings for Viacom’s networks dropped 15 percent, though Mr. Dauman pointed out that ratings failed to take account of other platforms. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Viacom Chief’s Contract Extended Until 2018 ', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Viacom Chief’s Contract Extended Until 2018', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Viacom Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dauman, Philippe P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T00:44:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e86e8a0-3f0d-51df-8d2d-00243af29f15', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e86e8a0-3f0d-51df-8d2d-00243af29f15'}, {'abstract': 'In Uberto Pasolini’s “Still Life,” Eddie Marsan plays a Londoner who arranges for the burial of dead people whose bodies have not been claimed by relatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/movies/uberto-pasolinis-still-life-starring-eddie-marsan.html', 'snippet': 'In Uberto Pasolini’s “Still Life,” Eddie Marsan plays a Londoner who arranges for the burial of dead people whose bodies have not been claimed by relatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Uberto Pasolini’s “Still Life,” the wonderful British character actor Eddie Marsan, barely moving his features, his watery eyes glistening slightly, infuses a remarkable depth of empathy into his character, John May, a dignified, solitary 44-year-old South Londoner. John works in a local council office where his job is to find the next of kin to recently deceased people in his borough whose bodies no one has claimed. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16STILL-ALT/STILL-ALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16STILL-ALT/STILL-ALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16STILL-ALT/STILL-ALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16STILL-ALT/STILL-ALT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16STILL-ALT/STILL-ALT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16STILL-ALT/STILL-ALT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16STILL-ALT/STILL-ALT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Designated Mourner, Flirting Warily With Joy', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Designated Mourner, Flirting Warily With Joy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pasolini, Uberto', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Still Life (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T00:45:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eed38704-623d-5cba-989d-aca6cf39608a', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eed38704-623d-5cba-989d-aca6cf39608a'}, {'abstract': 'Denis Côté’s semi-documentary “Joy of Man’s Desiring” captures the humanity of factory workers as they encounter frustrations and the occasional moment of satisfaction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/movies/joy-of-mans-desiring-about-working-in-a-factory.html', 'snippet': 'Denis Côté’s semi-documentary “Joy of Man’s Desiring” captures the humanity of factory workers as they encounter frustrations and the occasional moment of satisfaction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Factories are a byword for drudgery, but they have a certain inherent drama: the mesmerizing and menacing machines, the vivid subjection of people to their labor, the fact that something (usually) is created at the end of the line. In the ruminative semi-fictional film “Joy of Man’s Desiring,” the Canadian director Denis Côté watches men and women on the factory floor with a documentary eye, before trickling in details and dialogue that seem to express the workers’ humanity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16JOY/16JOY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16JOY/16JOY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 321}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16JOY/16JOY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16JOY/16JOY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1094, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16JOY/16JOY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16JOY/16JOY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/arts/16JOY/16JOY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Contrapuntal Hum of a Worker’s Hive ', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contrapuntal Hum of a Worker’s Hive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cote, Denis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T00:45:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline