e New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A 3-D Printed Car, Ready for the Road ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A 3-D Printed Car, Ready for the Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kessler, Aaron M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '3-D Printers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Cars (Compact, Subcompact and Microcars)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Local Motors Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T01:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron M. Kessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/563622a3-98e6-5db7-9459-e0b7c08e1107', 'word_count': 1009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/563622a3-98e6-5db7-9459-e0b7c08e1107'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations high commissioner for human rights, Prince Zeid Ra’ad Zeid al-Hussein of Jordan, publicly appealed to Saudi Arabia on Thursday to halt the flogging of a blogger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/world/middleeast/saudi-arabia-un-denounces-flogging-of-blogger.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations high commissioner for human rights, Prince Zeid Ra’ad Zeid al-Hussein of Jordan, publicly appealed to Saudi Arabia on Thursday to halt the flogging of a blogger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United Nations high commissioner for human rights, Prince Zeid Ra’ad Zeid al-Hussein of Jordan, publicly appealed to Saudi Arabia on Thursday to halt the flogging of a blogger sentenced to 1,000 blows, 10 years’ imprisonment and a large fine for creating a website that contained criticism of the country’s religious establishment. The first 50 blows were given to the blogger, Raif Badawi, last Friday. Prince Zeid made the appeal on the eve of the second in a series of floggings, which are to be administered every Friday until all 1,000 blows with a cane have been completed. “Flogging is, in my view, at the very least, a form of cruel and inhuman punishment,” Prince Zeid said in a statement on his office’s website. He reminded the Saudis that the United Nations considers flogging a form of torture. As of Thursday evening, there was no indication that the authorities planned to halt the punishment, which has been widely condemned around the world.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 529, 'width': 504, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 529, 'width': 504, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/16/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Saudi Arabia: U.N. Denounces Flogging of Blogger', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saudi Arabia: U.N. Denounces Caning of Blogger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Badawi, Raif', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Zeid Ra'ad Zeid Al Hussein", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T01:06:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d41f495-2fd4-5610-a155-51593e506fe8', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d41f495-2fd4-5610-a155-51593e506fe8'}, {'abstract': 'Construction of the 96-story condominium building, arguably New York City’s tallest, was briefly halted after the piece fell from a hoist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/nyregion/guardrail-falls-81-stories-at-park-ave-tower-work-site.html', 'snippet': 'Construction of the 96-story condominium building, arguably New York City’s tallest, was briefly halted after the piece fell from a hoist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Construction work was briefly halted at 432 Park Avenue in Midtown Manhattan this week after a section of guardrail fell from a hoist near the top of the building, wh