'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bf22ed1-9c3a-5fb8-b085-47a887ece62a', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bf22ed1-9c3a-5fb8-b085-47a887ece62a'}, {'abstract': 'Three winning regions would each be awarded $500 million to boost their economies if the New York Legislature approves the proposal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/nyregion/cuomo-wants-1-5-billion-contest-for-upstate-revitalization-grants.html', 'snippet': 'Three winning regions would each be awarded $500 million to boost their economies if the New York Legislature approves the proposal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — In his first four years in office, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo has proffered all kinds of solutions for problems in upstate New York, including casinos, tax-free districts and municipal consolidation. But on Thursday, the governor seemed to embrace a more direct, Darwinian approach: cash, in the form of competition for $1.5 billion in grants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Wants $1.5 Billion Contest for Upstate Revitalization Grants  ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Plans Competition Over Grants for Upstate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKinley, Jesse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Empire State Development Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T03:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname':