', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reading The Times With Naomi Klein', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T13:59:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Lehman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lehman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/680af4d9-75e9-502f-8bf5-651f64303da3', 'word_count': 1482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/680af4d9-75e9-502f-8bf5-651f64303da3'}, {'abstract': 'As the fall 2015 men’s shows kick off, one insider offers up tips for visitors to the city.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/milan-guide-morgan-collett-saturdays-surf/', 'snippet': 'As the fall 2015 men’s shows kick off, one insider offers up tips for visitors to the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fall/winter 2015 men’s wear shows kick off in Milan tomorrow, and men of style from all continents are currently descending on the city. Among them is Morgan Collett, the co-founder of\xa0Saturdays Surf NYC — a versatile line that appeals to Rockaway beach bums and Milanese peacocks alike. “I have been hearing that more and more Italians enjoy surfing, which is fantastic,” he says. “Our brand has so much influence from the fashion industry and the many cultures that exist in New York that I think Italians can appreciate our collection as part of a larger lifestyle.” Collett has come to town twice annually for the past several years for sales appointments, and in that time has come to rely on a few standbys for shelter, sustenance and inspiration. Here, he shares his list of local hangouts — some chilled-out, others classic, all worth a visit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'capt