Yael Averbuch, the hard work of soccer training rarely takes time off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roughly 150 players from the nine National Women’s Soccer League teams currently find themselves in the off-season. Some have headed overseas on loan deals to clubs in Europe, Japan or Australia, but the vast majority stay rooted to a home base for the six months between N.W.S.L. seasons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Art of Off-Season Training', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Averbuch, Yael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National Women's Soccer League (US)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T16:09:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yael Averbuch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Averbuch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90a50f52-003a-5bb9-b2c1-866ac88fb5dd', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90a50f52-003a-5bb9-b2c1-866ac88fb5dd'}, {'abstract': 'Clashes between the police and protesters in Karachi left four people, two of them journalists, with gunshot wounds as protests erupted across Pakistan against the French satirical newspaper.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/world/asia/4-shot-during-protest-against-charlie-hebdo-in-pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'Clashes between the police and protesters in Karachi left four people, two of them journalists, with gunshot wounds as protests erupted across Pakistan against the French satirical newspaper.', 'lead_p