d-5022-a294-f52e24727d9f', 'word_count': 1636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed2f0c91-a75d-5022-a294-f52e24727d9f'}, {'abstract': 'An early novel by José Saramago looks in on the humble residents of a Lisbon apartment building.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/books/review/jose-saramagos-skylight.html', 'snippet': 'An early novel by José Saramago looks in on the humble residents of a Lisbon apartment building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From outside a cobbler’s airy window, a little corner of Lisbon unfurls. Voyeurism is inescapable in José Saramago’s “new” novel, “Skylight,” which peeks in on a shabby apartment building in the 1940s and takes its epigraph from the Portuguese writer Raul Brandão: “In all souls, as in all houses, beyond the facade lies a hidden interior.” The interior at issue in this book is all the heartbreak and tepid dreams of the building’s humble residents, who are stuck in “the inquisitorial silence of the past observing us and the ironic silence of the future that awaits us.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'José Saramago’s ‘Skylight’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'High Windows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saramago, Jose', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costa, Margaret Jull', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Skylight (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T19:21:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Broida', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Broida', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dad477a-4216-57b6-8489-bb5186c9f3ab', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dad477a-4216-57b6-8489-bb5186c9f3ab'}, {'abstract': 'The London offshoot of the Sundance Film Festival has been canceled for this year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/sundance-london-festival-canceled/', 'snippet': 'The London offshoot of the Sundance Film Festival has been canceled for this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Sundance London, an offshoot of the Sundance Film Festival in Park City, Utah, will not return in 2015, the website ScreenDaily reported Friday. The London edition has been held at the O2 Center, more usually home to large-scale pop concerts, since 2012 when Robert Redford, the chairman of the Sundance Festival, said that he hoped it would help “build a picture of our country that is broadly reflective of the diversity of voices not always seen in our cultural exports.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sundance London Festival Canceled', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redford, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sundance Institute', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T19:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fecd4755-3fd9-5bc9-bb70-3de6e8da9cf5', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fecd4755-3fd9-5bc9-bb70-3de6e8da9cf5'}, {'abstract': 'A comment attributed incorrectly to Pope Francis has led to renewed interest in a longstanding theological discussion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/us/fascination-persists-over-pets-and-the-afterlife.html', 'snippet': 'A comment attributed incorrectly to Pope Francis has led to renewed interest in a longstanding theological discussion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In December, Pope Francis got the attention of pet owners everywhere when he was quoted as saying, “Paradise is open to all of God’s creatures.” Alas, media outlets, including The New York Times, confused the remarks and the circumstances under which they were made. The pope had actually made a broader comment about heaven during an event in November. The quotation itself was reportedly taken from remarks made years ago by Pope Paul VI.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/us/17beliefs/17beliefs-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/17/us/17beliefs/17beliefs-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/us/17beliefs/17beliefs-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/us/17beliefs/17beliefs-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1426, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/us/17beliefs/17beliefs-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType'