eloved-overseas-comes-to-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'Jeff Mills, who has been both canonized in Eminem lyrics and knighted Chevalier des Arts et des Lettres by the the French ministry of culture, makes a rare appearance in Williamsburg this Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Half an hour into Jeff Mills’s futuristic black-and-white film “Man From Tomorrow” there is a long, unfocused shot of people dancing in a dark space. The skin from their bodies catches the light at different angles, creating shimmering gray blurs that look like particles under a microscope or energy vibrating out in the cosmos. “That part of the film referenced the idea of what happens when a D.J. has been in that scenario for many, many years,” explains Mills, 51, who began D.J.ing on Detroit radio in the 1980s. After several prolific decades as a producer, label boss and artist, he has become the intellectual Jupiter in the techno solar system and certainly the only person to be both canonized in Eminem lyrics and knighted Chevalier des Arts et des Lettres by the the French ministry of culture. “You develop a certain type of alternative view of the audience as a collective, as a composite,” he says. “In most cases, I’m looking at the audience as a wave, or like when you go to the sea and you’re looking at the different levels of the water.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/t-magazine/16mills-zeke-1/16mills-zeke-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/16/t-magazine/16mills-zeke-1/16mills-zeke-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/16/t-magazine/16mills-zeke-1/16mills-zeke-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 