e': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordy, Berry Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Motown Records', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T21:25:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ead65225-fc76-5ba1-8c32-9d27a752c8bb', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ead65225-fc76-5ba1-8c32-9d27a752c8bb'}, {'abstract': 'Joel Sachs, a professor at Juilliard, has been readying a weeklong survey of the post-1945 Japanese repertory for the school’s annual Focus! festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/arts/music/joel-sachs-directs-the-new-juilliard-ensemble-and-the-focus-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Joel Sachs, a professor at Juilliard, has been readying a weeklong survey of the post-1945 Japanese repertory for the school’s annual Focus! festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alfred Schnittke’s String Trio, written in 1985, swerves from clamorous dissonance to almost unbearably poignant lyricism and back again. On a recent afternoon, three students at the Juilliard School were starting its slow second movement in a practice room high above 66th Street. Joel Sachs, a professor at the school, sat across the room on a slouchy yellow couch, following along with a score. After a few seconds, he stopped the music.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18SACHS1/18SACHS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18SACHS1/18SACHS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18SACHS1/18SACHS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18SACHS1/18SACHS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18SACHS1/18SACHS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18SACHS1/18SACHS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18SACHS1/18SACHS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Heralding New Music and Nurturing It ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heralding New Music and Nurturing It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Joel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juilliard School', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Focus Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Juilliard Ensemble', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T21:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22454e11-6bb3-5be0-8f4a-c4ec468b5b6b', 'word_count': 1555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22454e11-6bb3-5be0-8f4a-c4ec468b5b6b'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet’s new season will feature five ballerinas in top form.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/arts/dance/city-ballets-fab-five-2015-edition.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet’s new season will feature five ballerinas in top form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The word “ballerina” simply means, in Italian, a female dancer. But in the Anglo-Saxon dance world, it means quite specifically a female practitioner of ballet — and not just any female practitioner, but one who has reached the summit of her art, who exemplifies the essential attributes of classical dance. (France and Italy still don’t use the word in this sense, although the Paris Opera Ballet gives us “étoiles” or stars.) What those attributes must be has probably changed from era to era. Today we value, indeed expect, absolute technical mastery from a top ballerina, and we want musicality, dramatic power, charm, assertiveness and radiance, too.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18BALLET3/18BALLET3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18BALLET3/18BALLET3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18BALLET3/18BALLET3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1022, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18BALLET3/18BALLET3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2043, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18BALLET3/18BALLET3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18BALLET3/18BALLET3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18BALLET3/18BALLET3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'City Ballet’s Fab Five (2015 Edition)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Ballet’s Fab Five (2015 Edition)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sulcas, Roslyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mearns, Sara', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peck, Tiler', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reichlen, Teresa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hyltin, Sterling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouder, Ashley', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T21:36:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fae3e5a7-9a7e-5106-baa5-f8bea420ec60', 'word_count': 1377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fae3e5a7-9a7e-5106-baa5-f8bea420ec60'}, {'abstract': 'It’s about listening, empathy and having more women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/opinion/sunday/why-some-teams-are-smarter-than-others.html', 'snippet': 'It’s about listening, empathy and having more women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ENDLESS meetings that do little but waste everyone’s time. Dysfunctional committees that take two steps back for every one forward. Project teams that engage in wishful groupthinking rather than honest analysis. Everyone who is part of an organization — a company, a nonprofit, a condo board — has experienced these and other pathologies that can occur when human beings try to work together in groups.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18gray/18gray-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 589, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18gray/18gray-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 589}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18gray/18gray-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18gray/18gray-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2011, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbna