er-opens-at-city-center.html', 'snippet': '“A Beautiful Day in November on the Banks of the Greatest of the Great Lakes,” a comedy by Kate Benson, transforms a Thanksgiving dinner into a competitive sport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The holidays and all the fraught togetherness they can bring are now in the rearview mirror. But if you’re still smarting over that unkind word from a brother-in-law, or a passive-aggressive takedown from Mom or Dad, some solace may be found by attending a performance of “A Beautiful Day in November on the Banks of the Greatest of the Great Lakes,” a quirky comedy by Kate Benson that cleverly transforms an extended family’s Thanksgiving dinner into a fiercely fought competitive sport. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/beautiful/beautiful-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/beautiful/beautiful-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/beautiful/beautiful-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/beautiful/beautiful-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1260, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/beautiful/beautiful-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/beautiful/beautiful-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/beautiful/beautiful-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dinner Is Also a Sport ', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dinner Is Also a Sport', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benson, Kate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Center Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Beautiful Day in November on the Banks of the Greatest of the Great Lakes (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T22:32:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/96cbd070-d5f6-520e-bdad-15ac2e308888', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96cbd070-d5f6-520e-bdad-15ac2e308888'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic, led by Alan Gilbert, performed Verdi’s powerful Requiem with the New York Choral Artists and a quartet of soloists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/arts/music/new-york-philharmonic-performs-verdis-requiem.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic, led by Alan Gilbert, performed Verdi’s powerful Requiem with the New York Choral Artists and a quartet of soloists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Critics of Avery Fisher Hall and its acoustics usually agree that it is too big. But on Thursday evening, during the galvanic Dies Irae (Day of Wrath) in the New York Philharmonic’s performance of Verdi’s Requiem, it suddenly felt as if the hall were too small to contain such an explosion of sound. As the massed forces of the excellent New York Choral Artists invoked the Day of Judgment, shrieking piccolos pierced through the orchestral texture, and ear-shattering offbeats on the bass drum answered thundering orchestra chords. Trumpeters had been stationed on both sides of the second balcony, and the metallic bite of their salvos seemed to cut into the listener from all directions.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/philharmonic/philharmonic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 850, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/philharmonic/philharmonic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 850}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/philharmonic/philharmonic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 723, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/philharmonic/philharmonic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1446, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/philharmonic/philharmonic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/philharmonic/philharmonic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/arts/philharmonic/philha