aching standards to reflect his doubts about climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friday’s news that 2014 was the Earth’s hottest year on record could not have been timelier for West Virginia, where a dissident member of the Board of Education recently altered new teaching standards to reflect his personal doubts about climate change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Warmest Year on Record, West Virginia Feels the Heat', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T22:48:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/055d860c-20cd-5987-9c24-0943b282af91', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/055d860c-20cd-5987-9c24-0943b282af91'}, {'abstract': 'Alison Chase, a founder of Pilobolus and Momix, presented four pieces in her company’s New York debut at the Miller Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/arts/dance/alison-chases-troupe-has-new-york-debut-at-miller-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Alison Chase, a founder of Pilobolus and Momix, presented four pieces in her company’s New York debut at the Miller Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pilobolus, the mix of acrobatics, dance and dreamlike theater that became famous under the name of a fungus, first germinated in a 1970s Dartmouth College dance class taught by Alison Chase. Ms. Chase joined the troupe, and though, in 1980, she helped found the offshoot Momix, she stuck with Pilobolus until an acrimonious parting in 2005. Four years later, she started another company, Alison Chase/Performance, and at the Miller Theater this weekend, this latest venture had its New York debut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Branching Out, but Never Far From Its Roots', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Branching Out, but Never Far From Its Roots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chase, Alison', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-16T22:48:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/523e25c5-74f4-54a8-b22f-85f86421849c', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/523e25c5-74f4-54a8-b22f-85f86421849c'}, {'abstract': 'The Mariinsky Ballet presented “Swan Lake” to open its two-week season at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/arts/dance/mariinskys-swan-lake-at-brooklyn-academy-of-music.html', 'snippet': 'The Mariinsky Ballet presented “Swan Lake” to open its two-week season at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How can a production as visually beautiful and stylish as the Mariinsky Ballet’s “Swan Lake” be so unmoving? The exquisitely medieval look of this staging, which this St. Petersburg company presented on Thursday to open its two-week season at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, is marvelously right, and other balletic felicities abound. But four central problems remain. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'