heart of the case.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jury Selection for Tsarnaev Trial in Boston Sees Emotions Come to Fore', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emotions Come to Fore in Boston Jury Selection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boston Marathon Bombings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsarnaev, Dzhokhar A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Toole, George A Jr", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T01:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/305b99f0-621b-5ef3-ab76-3b171e4a29f1', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/305b99f0-621b-5ef3-ab76-3b171e4a29f1'}, {'abstract': 'A mother acquires much-needed furnishings with the help of the Neediest Cases Fund.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/opinion/creating-a-cozy-home-for-her-children.html', 'snippet': 'A mother acquires much-needed furnishings with the help of the Neediest Cases Fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the time she was 3 years old until she turned 21, Krystle Jackson lived in 13 different foster homes. So she was distraught when her own young children, Kayla and Isaiah, landed in foster care in 2012 when her daughter was seriously hurt while Ms. Jackson was at a job-training class. She fought hard to get her children back, working with New Alternatives for Children’s foster care program to meet the necessary requirements. She attended parenting class, kept appointments with the children twice a week and participated in therapy. In early 2014, she was reunited with Kayla and Isaiah. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Creating a Cozy Home for Her Children', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Creating a Cozy Home for Her Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foster Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federation of Protestant Welfare Agencies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T01:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a27669bc-6812-5502-8d77-7b9aaf4a4a91', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a27669bc-6812-5502-8d77-7b9aaf4a4a91'}, {'abstract': 'Consumers replaced worn-out models and analysts said they expected a modest upward trend again this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/business/international/car-market-shows-signs-of-revival-for-europe.html', 'snippet': 'Consumers replaced worn-out models and analysts said they expected a modest upward trend again this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European auto market grew last year for the first time since before the global financial crisis began, industry data showed on Friday, as consumers replaced worn-out models and analysts said they expected a modest upward trend again this year. New passenger car registrations, a proxy for sales, rose 5.7 percent in the European Union last year, reaching about 12.6 million vehicles, the European Automobile Manufacturer’s Association reported from Brussels. It was the first annual expansion since 2007, when the market peaked at nearly 16 million new passenger cars. Spain led the major national markets in 2014, with government trade-in incentives helping to lift sales by more than 18 percent. Germany, Europe’s largest auto market, grew 2.9 percent. Still, the industry is not out of danger. The stagnant economy in most of Europe, as well as crushing unemployment in countries like Greece and Spain, will continue to weigh on the market. LMC Automotive, a market research firm, estimates that European sales will gain just 1.1 percent in 2015. Carlos Da Silva, who follows Europe’s car market at IHS Automotive, said in a research note that the 2014 recovery was welcome news, but that Europe was not yet “a fully cured patient.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Car Market Shows Signs of Revival for Europe', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Car Market Shows Signs of Revival for Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolly, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "European Automobile Manufacturers' Assn", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T01:21:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': N