', 'snippet': 'While most accounts of American health workers have focused on the ones returning, Lindsey Hallen, an emergency room nurse in Manhattan, is heading to West Africa to fight an epidemic that has killed more than 8,000 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lindsey Hallen is in the bug spray aisle at REI, the outdoor equipment emporium in SoHo, looking for exactly the right mosquito repellent to take to West Africa’s Ebola zone, when her phone rings. Three ascending tones, the personal anthem of an emergency room nurse, captured in a ringtone called “Summit.” ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nurse Decides to Get Hands-On in the Ebola Zone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heading to the Ebola Zone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hallen, Lindsey E (1983- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Partners in Health', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T01:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'ti