diculed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'USA PATRIOT Act', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T02:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Apuzzo and Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Apuzzo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d6a3b5b-ab84-570a-bf46-d6906870716e', 'word_count': 1080, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d6a3b5b-ab84-570a-bf46-d6906870716e'}, {'abstract': 'California Chrome, Bayern and Main Sequence are the finalists for Saturday’s honor, which some critics say has become too much of a popularity contest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/sports/california-chrome-is-finalist-for-horse-of-the-year-award.html', 'snippet': 'California Chrome, Bayern and Main Sequence are the finalists for Saturday’s honor, which some critics say has become too much of a popularity contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HALLANDALE BEACH, Fla. — California Chrome, the winner of last year’s Kentucky Derby and Preakness Stakes, was not the same scintillating performer in the second half of the season that he was in the first. Bayern won a controversial Breeders’ Cup Classic and faltered in other key races. Main Sequence had a perfect record in four races, but all of them came on grass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/sports/17racing-01/17racing-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/17/sports/17racing-01/17racing-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/sports/17racing-01/17racing-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/sports/17racing-01/17racing-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1487, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/sports/17racing-01/17racing-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/17/sports/17racing-01/17racing-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/sports/17racing-01/17racing-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Eclipse Awards Set to Be Announced, Horse of the Year Honor Raises Questions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chrome Is Finalist for Honor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'California Chrome (Race Horse)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T02:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8be3416d-b6a8-599a-9dcd-40884decf8cc', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8be3416d-b6a8-599a-9dcd-40884decf8cc'}, {'abstract': 'A brain twisting Saturday puzzle by Josh Knapp.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/16/istanbul-is-apparently-on-it/', 'snippet': 'A brain twisting Saturday puzzle by Josh Knapp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY PUZZLE — Usually, fill-in-the-blank clues are an easy way to get a toehold in a crossword puzzle. That’s why you don’t see too many of them in the tougher, late-week puzzles. You’re supposed to struggle. You’re supposed to think.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Istanbul is Apparently on It', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T03:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93062694-74d6-51d5-a680-22f009b0cd76', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93062694-74d6-51d5-a680-22f009b0cd76'}, {'abstract': 'Allah-ade Jenkins, who served over 21 years in prison for attempted armed robbery, has had difficulty finding employment. But he has established two clothing labels that draw inspiration from his African-American heritage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/nyregion/a-tailor-looks-beyond-his-criminal-past-by-connecting-with-his-roots.html', 'snippet': 'Allah-ade Jenkins, who served over 21 years in prison for attempted armed robbery, has had difficulty finding employment. But he has established two clothing labels that draw inspiration from his African-American heritage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Allah-ade Jenkins grew up under rolls of fabric and thread, with the constant rhythmic thump of sewing machines above him. His parents were both master tailors, and he spent his first years wandering the floors of their shop in Harlem. He always loved the machines, he said, and one day, when his mother was away, he climbed up on one.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/nyregion/17NEEDIESTJENKINS/17NEEDIESTJENKINS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/17/nyregion/17NEEDIESTJENKINS/17NEEDIESTJENKINS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/nyregion/17NEEDIESTJENKINS/17NEEDIESTJENKINS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/nyregion/17NEEDIESTJENKINS/17NEEDIESTJENKINS-superJumbo.jpg', '