'Around this time of year, when the holidays are over and the nighttime temperature descends to nostril-numbing levels, many heat-seeking residents of Carroll Gardens, Brooklyn, spend their evenings at the Black Mountain Wine House at 415 Union Street. The quiet saloon, just blocks from busy Smith Street, exudes a rustic warmth: A fireplace crackles in the corner; agricultural bric-a-brac hangs from the walls. The only thing to dispel the impression that you’ve just walked into a farmhouse in Vermont is the aproned chef slicing and sautéing in the open-window kitchen. On Tuesday nights, Black Mountain offers a fondue special ($16), increasing its cold-weather allure, and this past Tuesday, in the after-work chill, the place was full of whispering couples, book-reading singles and three women: a mother, her daughter and her daughter-in-law, taking in a meal before the theater.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/nyregion/18TABLE/18TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/nyregion/18TABLE/18TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/nyregion/18TABLE/18TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/nyregion/18TABLE/18TABLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/nyregion/18TABLE/18TABLE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'w