er', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe4d4bcd-4553-5791-a22c-4472708b2d0e', 'word_count': 1259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe4d4bcd-4553-5791-a22c-4472708b2d0e'}, {'abstract': 'A third Romney run is a bad idea, but it’s hard to see what harm it can do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/opinion/sunday/ross-douthat-mitt-the-insurgent.html', 'snippet': 'A third Romney run is a bad idea, but it’s hard to see what harm it can do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE idea of yet a third Mitt Romney campaign for the presidency, once the idle dream of a few Romney bundlers and now apparently something embraced by the Man From Bain Capital himself, has been greeted by most Republicans with a mixture of horror, exhaustion and embarrassment. The polite ones sound like a girl before the senior prom who can’t believe that the stumblebum date who ruined her last school dance is in line first to ask her again: No, please, not this time. The rest sound like the characters in the third act of a horror movie, confronting a shambling revenant that just keeps coming: How do we kill this thing? ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/douthat-circular/douthat-circular-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/douthat-circular/douthat-circular-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/douthat-circular/douthat-circular-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/douthat-circular/douthat-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/douthat-circular/douthat-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/douthat-circular/douthat-circular-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/douthat-circular/douthat-circular-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1871, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitt the Insurgent', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mitt the Insurgent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douthat, Ross G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T19:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/17d7ff2d-767e-5e53-9079-b56dd039ca21', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17d7ff2d-767e-5e53-9079-b56dd039ca21'}, {'abstract': 'What astrobiology can tell us about the fate of the planet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/opinion/sunday/is-a-climate-disaster-inevitable.html', 'snippet': 'What astrobiology can tell us about the fate of the planet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OUR galaxy, the Milky Way, is home to almost 300 billion stars, and over the last decade, astronomers have made a startling discovery — almost all those stars have planets. The fact that nearly every pinprick of light you see in the night sky hosts a family of worlds raises a powerful but simple question: “Where is everybody?” Hundreds of billions of planets translate into a lot of chances for evolving intelligent, technologically sophisticated species. So why don’t we see evidence for E.T.s everywhere? ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18frank/18frank-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 310, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18frank/18frank-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 310}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18frank/18frank-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 529, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18frank/18frank-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1058, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18frank/18frank-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18frank/18frank-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/sunday-review/18frank/18frank-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is a Climate Disaster Inevitable?', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is a Climate Disaster Inevitable?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frank, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extraterrestrial Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stars and Galaxies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Planets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T19:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bafcaf8b-1252-5d87-aa53-701dd3707f63', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bafcaf8b-1252-5d87-aa53-701dd3707f63'}, {'abstract': 'I was a veteran who needed therapy. What I got was another kind of battle.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/17/after-ptsd-more-trauma/', 'snippet': 'I was a veteran who needed therapy. What I got was another kind of battle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Going in for therapy at a Veterans Affairs hospital is a lot like arriving at a large airport in a foreign country. You pass through a maze of confusing signage. Your documents are scrutinized. There are long lines you must stand in and a series of bureaucratic rituals that must be endured before anything resembling a human encounter occurs.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11