aterial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/557f0b4b-4273-5077-9ff0-7f82038f15ca', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/557f0b4b-4273-5077-9ff0-7f82038f15ca'}, {'abstract': 'A few years ago, a gathering of members of Guyana’s two main ethnic groups — descendants of African slaves and indentured laborers from India — would have been unusual, but a new third party has changed that dynamic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/world/a-multiethnic-movement-emerges-in-guyana-to-counter-politics-as-usual.html', 'snippet': 'A few years ago, a gathering of members of Guyana’s two main ethnic groups — descendants of African slaves and indentured laborers from India — would have been unusual, but a new third party has changed that dynamic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GEORGETOWN, Guyana — Swaying to the rhythms of Afro-Guyanese reggae, the protesters, descendants of African slaves and indentured laborers from India, gathered on the streets of Georgetown in a show of unity against the country’s president.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Multiethnic Movement Emerges in Guyana to Counter Politics-as-Usual', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Multiethnic Movement Emerges in Guyana to Counter Politics-as-Usual', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Girish', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guyana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T22:23:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Girish Gupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Girish', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea213706-91ee-592e-9cc6-dbc08a087a83', 'word_count': 1095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea213706-91ee-592e-9cc6-dbc08a087a83'}, {'abstract': 'The New-York Historical Society is about to present images of the civil rights march to Montgomery captured by someone who was actually there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/arts/design/54-miles-and-5-cameras.html', 'snippet': 'The New-York Historical Society is about to present images of the civil rights march to Montgomery captured by someone who was actually there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as the film “Selma” has recreated the civil rights march to Montgomery for moviegoers, the New-York Historical Society is about to present images of the event captured by someone who was actually there. The exhibition, “Freedom Journey 1965,” features photographs by Stephen Somerstein, who traveled to Alabama to document the march as a student in City College of New York’s night school, where he was picture editor of his student newspaper. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE1/18GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE1/18GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE1/18GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE1/18GUI