ean government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAKARTA, Indonesia — When the political outsider Joko Widodo was sworn in as president of Indonesia, promising “people-centric politics” and a common touch, supporters hoped for miracles while opponents confidently predicted he would be destroyed politically within a year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/INDONESIA/INDONESIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/world/INDONESIA/INDONESIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/INDONESIA/INDONESIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/INDONESIA/INDONESIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1441, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/INDONESIA/INDONESIA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/world/INDONESIA/INDONESIA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/INDONESIA/INDONESIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Indonesians, President’s Political Outsider Status Loses Its Luster', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Indonesians, President’s Political Outsider Status Loses Its Luster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cochrane, Joe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joko Widodo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AirAsia Flight 8501', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Budi Gunawan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T22:25:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Cochrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cochrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/d54a8728-e9ba-5bdc-bae0-42b7ef1b3a1b', 'word_count': 1237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d54a8728-e9ba-5bdc-bae0-42b7ef1b3a1b'}, {'abstract': 'This winter the dazzling young Russian pianist Daniil Trifonov has been almost in residence in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/arts/music/a-young-star-and-a-master.html', 'snippet': 'This winter the dazzling young Russian pianist Daniil Trifonov has been almost in residence in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This winter the dazzling young Russian pianist Daniil Trifonov has been almost in residence in New York. Mr. Trifonov, who won both the Arthur Rubinstein Competition in Tel Aviv and the Tchaikovsky Competition in Moscow in 2011, played an acclaimed solo recital at Carnegie Hall in December. He then appeared with the New York Philharmonic at Avery Fisher Hall, exciting audiences in Rachmaninoff’s First Piano Concerto. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE8/18GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 572, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE8/18GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 572}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE8/18GUIDE8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 976, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE8/18GUIDE8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1429, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE8/18GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE8/18GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE8/18GUIDE8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Young Star And a Master', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical: A Young Star and a Master', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T22:26:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f8a099f-dd54-5a74-990e-c1250df56ba2', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f8a099f-dd54-5a74-990e-c1250df56ba2'}, {'abstract': 'Every live theater event convenes an impromptu community in which artist and audience create a shared experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/arts/dance/everyone-here-is-part-of-the-act.html', 'snippet': 'Every live theater event convenes an impromptu community in which artist and audience create a shared experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every live theater event convenes an impromptu community in which artist and audience create a shared experience. The choreographer Moriah Evans examines this in much of her work, including “Social Dance 1-8: Index,” a new piece commissioned by the Issue Project Room. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Everyone Here Is Part of the Act', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance: Everyone Here Is Part of the Act', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T22:27:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Schaefer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaefer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/238b6598-74da-5811-983e-7bc500af6d0f', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/238b6598-74da-5811-983e-7bc500af6d0f'}, {'abstract': 'The unsettling work of the Swedish filmmaker Ruben Ostlund, whose 2014 movie “Force Majeure” was one the year’s most acclaimed films, has been described as “Michael Haneke lite.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/movies/unearthing-fear-and-mistrust.html', 'snippet': 'The unsettling work of the Swedish filmmaker Ruben Ostlund, whose 2014 movie “Force Majeure” was one the year’s most acclaimed films, has been described as “Michael Haneke lite.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The unsettling work of the Swedish filmmaker Ruben Ostlund, whose 2014 movie “Force Majeure” was one the year’s most acclaimed films, has been described as “Michael Haneke lite.” Like Mr. Haneke, Mr. Ostlund digs under the surface sheen of affluent bourgeois life to discern deep currents of fear and mistrust. His previous two features, “Play” (2011) and “Involuntary” (2008), both running through Thursday at the Elinor Bunin Munroe Film Center in Lincoln Center, are calculated to make you squirm. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE10/18GUIDE10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE10/18GUIDE10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 880}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE10/18GUIDE10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 699, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE10/18GUIDE10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1731, 'width': 1180, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE10/18GUIDE10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE10/18GUIDE10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE10/18GUIDE10-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unearthing Fear and Mistrust', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film: Unearthing Fear and Mistrust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T22:28:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4add5102-cb9e-5868-8514-8696c7f0b824', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4add5102-cb9e-5868-8514-8696c7f0b824'}, {'abstract': 'For Sufjan Stevens, America is an expanse of history, myth, memory, fantasy, ideals and quirks, reflected in music that might be gently homespun, orchestral, jazz-tinged or electronic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/arts/music/rodeo-rockabilly-and-ample-mixing.html', 'snippet': 'For Sufjan Stevens, America is an expanse of history, myth, memory, fantasy, ideals and quirks, reflected in music that might be gently homespun, orchestral, jazz-tinged or electronic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Sufjan Stevens, America is an expanse of history, myth, memory, fantasy, ideals and quirks, reflected in music that might be gently homespun, orchestral, jazz-tinged or electronic. “Round-Up” takes on an institution that is a sport and a cultural touchstone: rodeo. It’s a live score for slow-motion footage from the Pendleton Round-Up; Mr. Stevens plays electronics with the ensemble Yarn/Wire. Maybe he’ll be glancing over his shoulder at Aaron Copland’s “Rodeo.” (Tuesday through Jan. 25 at 7:30 p.m., BAM Harvey Theater, bam.org)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE11/18GUIDE11-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 575, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE11/18GUIDE11-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 575, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE11/18GUIDE11-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE11/18GUIDE11-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/arts/18GUIDE11/18GUIDE11-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rodeo, Rockabilly And Ample Mixing', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop: Rodeo, Rockabilly and Ample Mixing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-17T22:31:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'by