 a star witness for an unprecedented United Nations’ investigation of abuses by the North’s rulers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/asia/19DEFECTOR/19DEFECTOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/18/world/asia/19DEFECTOR/19DEFECTOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/asia/19DEFECTOR/19DEFECTOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/asia/19DEFECTOR/19DEFECTOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1415, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/asia/19DEFECTOR/19DEFECTOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/18/world/asia/19DEFECTOR/19DEFECTOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/18/world/asia/19DEFECTOR/19DEFECTOR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prominent North Korean Defector Recants Parts of His Story of Captivity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prominent North Korean Defector Recants Parts of His Story of Captivity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shin Dong-hyuk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Escape from Camp 14: One Man's Remarkable Odyssey from North Korea to Freedom in the West (Book)", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-18T14:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf76ec6c-4876-5a65-8627-9a98f082252e', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf76ec6c-4876-5a65-8627-9a98f082252e'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The author John Ruskin is rumored to have suffered a breakdown in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/1890-is-john-ruskin-insane/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The author John Ruskin is rumored to have suffered a breakdown in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mental condition of Mr. John Ruskin, the great leader in English critical literature, is causing much sorrow among his friends. There has been a great deal of whispered talk in the upper art circles of London for months past concerning Mr. Ruskin’s state and the peculiar circumstances by which he is environed. There has been no public comment on the matter, because of the general desire, among his most intimate friends, Mr. Swinburne, Mr. Burne Jones and others, to have nothing said about it. Now, however, the removal of his publisher from Orpington to London, and the change in the sale of Mr. Buskin’s books from the no discount system, which he instituted, to the ordinary methods prevailing in the book trade, with other circumstances, make further secrecy impossible. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/blogs/13iht-old19-ruskin/13iht-old19-ruskin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 420, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/blogs/13iht-old19-ruskin/13iht-old19-ruskin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 420, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/blogs/13iht-old19-ruskin/13iht-old19-ruskin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/13/blogs/13iht-old19-ruskin/13iht-old19-ruskin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/13/blogs/13iht-old19-ruskin/13iht-old19-ruskin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1890: Is John Ruskin Insane?', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'},