 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stones', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taschen Books', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bailey, David', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbijn, Anton', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jagger, Mick', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Brian (1942-69)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Terry", 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Keith', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watts, Charlie', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyman, Bill', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-18T18:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/875f47e9-6113-56ae-b83a-923d0b9f0d87', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/875f47e9-6113-56ae-b83a-923d0b9f0d87'}, {'abstract': 'Le terrorisme islamiste est le cancer de l’islam contre lequel les musulmans doivent eux-mêmes lutter à nos côtés.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/opinion/marine-le-pen-la-france-a-ete-attaquee-par-le-fondamentalisme-islamiste.html', 'snippet': 'Le terrorisme islamiste est le cancer de l’islam contre lequel les musulmans doivent eux-mêmes lutter à nos côtés.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — « Mal nommer les choses, c’est ajouter au malheur du monde. » Qu’Albert Camus l’ait prononcée ou non, cette phrase décrit étonnamment bien la situation dans laquelle se trouve l’actuel gouvernement de la France. En effet, le nom des choses, c’est ce que Laurent Fabius, ministre français des Affaires étrangères, n’ose même plus prononcer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bien nommer la menace', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-18T19:34:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marine Le Pen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marine', 'middlename': 'Le', 'lastname': 'Pen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc2ee187-8fc3-5de6-9003-c110a3c706fc', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc2ee187-8fc3-5de6-9003-c110a3c706fc'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The French are seeking their own Walt Disney in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/1940-french-are-seeking-a-walt-disney-artists-asked-to-submit-work/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The French are seeking their own Walt Disney in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'French motion-picture producers, pointing to the artistic triumphs and box-office successes of Walt Disney, have been casting about lately for Gallic talent to give Walt a little competition, and, incidentally, to capture some of the money flowing so copiously into the coffers of the creators of animated screen cartoons. Determined to find native counterparts of Mickey Mouse and Popeye, the Frenchmen have sent out an invitation to all artists, cartoonists and designers to submit their most fanciful brainchildren for study and possible adaptation. The invitation has been answered by scores of good, and — no doubt — bad and indifferent artists. At the Centrale de Coordination des Métiers, 5 Rue de Logelbach, one can see the results of the response in the form of drawings, silhouettes, cutouts and marionettes. Sergent Badu, ‘‘Poilu de l’Avant,’’ is the only war character. Should the war last, he might prove the most popular of the lot. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 19, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/blogs/15iht-old19/15iht-old19-jumbo.png', 'height': 795, 'width': 581, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/blogs/15iht-old19/15iht-old19-superJumbo.png', 'height': 795, 'width': 581, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/blogs/15iht-old19/15iht-old19-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/15/blogs/15iht-old19/15iht-old19-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/blogs/15iht-old19/15iht-old19-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1940: French Are Seeking a Walt Disney, Artists Asked to Submit Work', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'sub