d Box Office', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eastwood, Clint', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Bradley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'American Sniper (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-18T22:51:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff504a51-99ae-5abb-b969-ae2f316215a2', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff504a51-99ae-5abb-b969-ae2f316215a2'}, {'abstract': 'Solve Jean O’Conor’s cool puzzle with me.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/like-alpine-peaks/', 'snippet': 'Solve Jean O’Conor’s cool puzzle with me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY PUZZLE — A timely grid for Jean O’Conor, even if there is no white stuff on the ground here right now. It’s cold enough, so I’m calling this a seasonal puzzle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like Alpine Peaks', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-18T23:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40122a22-031c-51d0-b301-9e5720f068e0', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40122a22-031c-51d0-b301-9e5720f068e0'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Bubble,” a 1960s sci-fi film, a couple’s plane makes an emergency landing in a strange town.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/movies/the-bubble-arch-obolers-1966-sci-fi-film.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Bubble,” a 1960s sci-fi film, a couple’s plane makes an emergency landing in a strange town.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Originally premiering in 1966, Arch Oboler’s 3-D science-fiction puzzler, “The Bubble,” gets a New York theatrical run to show off its Space-Vision technology in an extraordinary restoration. Mr. Oboler, a titan from radio days, predicted in 1967 “that in 20 years there will be no flat movies.” He was a little off, but not for lack of trying: This film thrusts not only a tray of beers but a cancan dancer’s high-kick at the audience.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/BUBBLE/BUBBLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/BUBBLE/BUBBLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 570}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/BUBBLE/BUBBLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/BUBBLE/BUBBLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1831, 'width': 1927, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/BUBBLE/BUBBLE-th