rmory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/arts/music/argento-at-the-armory-with-das-lied.html', 'snippet': 'The Argento Chamber Ensemble presented the second concert in its “Mahler as New York Contemporary” series at the Park Avenue Armory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gustav Mahler, maker of gigantic symphonies, may seem an odd preoccupation for a chamber group. But preoccupation he is, this season, for the adventurous Argento Chamber Ensemble, which presented the second concert in its series Mahler as New York Contemporary on Thursday evening in the Board of Officers Room at the Park Avenue Armory.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/SUB-ARGENTO/SUB-ARGENTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/SUB-ARGENTO/SUB-ARGENTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/SUB-ARGENTO/SUB-ARGENTO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/SUB-ARGENTO/SUB-ARGENTO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1301, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/SUB-ARGENTO/SUB-ARGENTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/SUB-ARGENTO/SUB-ARGENTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/arts/SUB-ARGENTO/SUB-ARGENTO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If Mahler Were Writing Now', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If Mahler Were Writing Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahler, Gustav', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Argento Chamber Ensemble', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-18T23:56:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/14481708-7c6a-5cbe-949a-51bfaafdd3cc', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14481708-7c6a-5cbe-949a-51bfaafdd3cc'}, {'abstract': 'A British judge ruled last week that Sotheby’s had not been negligent in the case of a painting that the auction house sold for much less than it was worth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/arts/design/a-win-for-sothebys-in-dispute-over-painting.html', 'snippet': 'A British judge ruled last week that Sotheby’s had not been negligent in the case of a painting that the auction house sold for much less than it was worth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A British judge ruled last week that Sotheby’s had not been negligent in the case of a painting that the auction house sold in 2006 for 42,000 pounds (about $63,600), only to be declared worth £10 million a year later, the Financial Times reported. Lancelot Thwaytes sued Sotheby’s for £11 million (about $16.7 million) in damages, claiming that the auctioneers had insufficiently researched his painting “The Cardsharps.” The auction house described the work, below, which depicts two hustlers trying to cheat another man in a card game, as a 17th-century copy of the original by the Italian master Caravaggio. The painting was purchased by a friend of the British collector Denis Mahon, who died in 2011 and who, after further analysis, declared it an authentic Caravaggio and valued the painting at £10 million. The Financial Times reported that Judge Vivien Rose dismissed Mr. Thwaytes’s claim, saying in her ruling that the auctioneers had examined the painting thoroughly, and reasonably concluded that the painting was not of high enough quality to be a Caravaggio. The disputed painting is currently on loan to the Museum of the Order of St John in London.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Win for Sotheby’s in Dispute Over Painting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Win for Sotheby’s in Dispute Over Painting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caravaggio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-18T23:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/35b091e1-ae05-5b2a-9a57-f0cf791b6d52', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35b091e1-ae05-5b2a-9a57-f0cf791b6d52'}, {'abstract': 'It wasn’t cuddly or strokable, but I had no choice in the matter: We were going to be sharing our apartment with a turtle.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/18/good-eggs/', 'snippet': 'It wasn’t cuddly or strokable, but I had no choice in the matter: We were going to be sharing our apartment with a turtle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I left our Manhattan apartment for a short trip, everything was more or less normal. But when I returned, I saw the turtle tank — it had come in while I was away. Along with the tank came a turtle — a mature red-eared slider. My wife had bought the tank while I was in another city. Maybe she’d waited until I was traveling so I wouldn’t stop her.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19menagerie/19menagerie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19menagerie/19menagerie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19menagerie/19menagerie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19menagerie/19menagerie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19menagerie/19menagerie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType':