rd', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/20/sports/20yemen/20yemen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/sports/20yemen/20yemen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gun Battles in Capital Shake Yemen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gun Battles in Capital Shake Yemen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almosawa, Shuaib', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadi, Abdu Rabbu Mansour', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houthis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sana (Yemen)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Mubarak, Ahmed Awad', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-19T08:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shuaib Almosawa and Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shuaib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Almosawa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ff7e125-0dab-5299-8d60-5ae26952826c', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ff7e125-0dab-5299-8d60-5ae26952826c'}, {'abstract': 'Even elected members of the judiciary are not lawmakers or political leaders, and they should not be put in the position of asking donors for money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/opinion/judges-with-hat-in-hand.html', 'snippet': 'Even elected members of the judiciary are not lawmakers or political leaders, and they should not be put in the position of asking donors for money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Florida judiciary is no stranger to misconduct and corruption. During one tawdry stretch in the early 1970s, three of the state’s supreme court justices resigned over corruption scandals. One was caught on a gambling junket in Las Vegas that had been paid for by a greyhound track owner with a case pending before the court. Two others stepped down after trying to tamper with cases involving campaign supporters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judges, With Hat in Hand', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judges, With Hat in Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supreme Courts (State)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-19T08:27:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc7b5aa-a547-5873-b641-90d15da16908', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc7b5aa-a547-5873-b641-90d15da16908'}, {'abstract': 'The first federal effort to regulate the gas directly will put a dent in harmful emissions. But only a dent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/opinion/a-modest-move-on-methane.html', 'snippet': 'The first federal effort to regulate the gas directly will put a dent in harmful emissions. But only a dent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is much to like in the Obama administration’s proposal, announced last Wednesday, to reduce harmful methane emissions from oil and gas drilling. The proposal — which calls for detailed rules to be unveiled in early summer — is the first federal effort to directly regulate methane, the main component of natural gas and a major contributor to climate change. The regulations will apply to all new oil and gas wells, and be national in scope, thus setting minimum standards for what is now a patchwork quilt of state laws. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon3/20tue3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon3/20tue3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon3/20tue3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon3/20tue3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon3/20tue3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon3/20tue3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon3/20tue3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Modest Move on Methane ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Modest Move on Methane', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-19T08:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e5c6c80-64c4-58bb-b23c-9a008f5943aa', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e5c6c80-64c4-58bb-b23c-9a008f5943aa'}, {'abstract': 'Professed values must become a reality for the country’s many youths who feel marginalized.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/opinion/paris-attacks-lay-bare-longtime-muslim-exclusion.html', 'snippet': 'Professed values must become a reality for the country’s many youths who feel marginalized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recent terrorist attacks in Paris prompted millions to take to the streets to show national solidarity and to pay tribute to the 17 people murdered. The attacks have also inspired a lot of soul-searching, as the French struggle to understand how three men, born and raised in France, could have trained the murderous intent of Al Qaeda and the Islamic State on their own countrymen. And the attacks have revealed a larger, existential threat to France: that its social compact may be torn apart by sectarian polarization.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon2/19mon2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon2/19mon2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon2/19mon2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon2/19mon2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon2/19mon2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon2/19mon2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/19/opinion/19mon2/19mon2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Inclusive French Republic', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Inclusive French Republic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coulibaly, Amedy (1982-2015)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kouachi, Cherif (1982-2015)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kouachi, Said (1980-2015)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-19T08:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed3bf255-731c-5127-b752-20b3ae9e4e15', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed3bf255-731c-5127-b752-20b3ae9e4e15'}, {'abstract': 'What’s good for the US Chamber of Commerce is probably bad for America.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/suspicious-nonsense-on-trade-agreements/', 'snippet': 'What’s good for the US Chamber of Commerce is probably bad for America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am in general a free trader; there is, I’d argue, a tendency on the part of some people with whom I agree on many issues to demonize trade agreements, to make them responsible for evils that have other causes. And my take on both of the trade agreements currently under negotiation — Pacific and Atlantic — is that there’s much less there than meets the eye.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspicious Nonsense on Trade Agreements', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-19T08:55:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df6c627d-84a0-534d-9298-4676964ee65f', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df6c627d-84a0-534d-9298-4676964ee65f'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement of David Duffy’s planned departure comes a week after the Irish government said it had hired Goldman Sachs to advise it on potential capital restructuring.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/allied-irish-banks-c-e-o-resigns-after-three-years/', 'snippet': 'The announcement of David Duffy’s planned departure comes a week after the Irish government said it had hired Goldman Sachs to advise it on potential capital restructuring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The chief executive of Allied Irish Banks, a nationalized lender, is leaving for a similar position at Clydesdale Bank, the Scottish arm of National Australia Bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Allied Irish Banks’ Chief to Depart for Clydesdale Bank', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-19T09:07:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42edc389-48c6-5803-ac0a-7dddfd5e2953', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42edc389-48c6-5803-ac0a-7dddfd5e2953'}, {'abstract': 'Brazil and the Netherlands withdrew their ambassadors to Indonesia after a Brazilian and a Dutch citizen convicted of drug offenses were executed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/world/asia/indonesias-execution-of-foreigners-prompts-diplomatic-storm.html', 'snippet': 'Brazil and the Netherlands withdrew their ambassadors to Indonesia after a Brazilian and a Dutch citizen convicted of drug offenses were executed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Indonesia’s weekend executions of two foreigners convicted on drug charges have prompted an indignant diplomatic reaction, as Brazil and the Netherlands withdrew their ambassadors and Australia said it would not rule out such a move.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indonesia’s Execution of Foreigners Prompts Diplomatic Storm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value':