emails-to-reporters.html', 'snippet': 'There is no explanation of why, in 2008, the vast collection of messages was sucked into the global system of electronic surveillance created and maintained by British and American spies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In November 2008, British spies captured email messages addressed to reporters and photographers with at least a dozen international news organizations, many United Nations officials, workers at far-flung oil companies and tens of thousands of other people, according to a newly disclosed classified document.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Spies Seized Emails to Reporters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Spies Seized Emails to Reporters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glanz, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reuters Group PLC', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'na