015/01/20/business/international/china-gdp-growth-rate-slowest-since-1990.html', 'snippet': 'The country’s gross domestic product grew by 7.4 percent in 2014, adding to fears of a broader economic slowdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China grew at its slowest rate in 24 years in 2014, according to data released by the National Bureau of Statistics on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Economy Expands at Slowest Rate in Quarter-Century', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T02:41:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/441ee183-ec28-542f-b7ee-457ea5ea8e9d', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/441ee183-ec28-542f-b7ee-457ea5ea8e9d'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/nyregion/winning-lottery-numbers-for-jan-19-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan. 19, 2015', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Lottery Numbers for Jan. 19, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T02:49:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/568c629c-9fa4-5166-a547-9fbafb365f54', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/568c629c-9fa4-5166-a547-9fbafb365f54'}, {'abstract': 'Canadian soldiers exchanged fire with Islamic State fighters in Iraq over the past week, a commander said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/world/americas/canada-troops-clash-with-isis-in-iraq.html', 'snippet': 'Canadian soldiers exchanged fire with Islamic State fighters in Iraq over the past week, a commander said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Canadian soldiers exchanged fire with Islamic State fighters in Iraq over the past week, a commander said Monday. The officer, Brig. Gen. Michael Rouleau, the commander of Canadian special operations forces, said his troops were advising Iraqi officers “at the front lines” when the soldiers came under machine-gun and mortar fire. “That resulted in the immediate requirement to return fire,” he said. Canadian snipers, he said, then “neutralized” the fighters of the Islamic State group, also known as ISIS or ISIL. He did not say how many Canadians were involved nor did he say how many attackers were killed. As many as 69 Canadians are providing training and advice to Iraqis. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Troops Clash With ISIS in Iraq', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Troops Clash With ISIS in Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T02:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/52a15449-89db-55fd-81dc-1c686ff66376', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52a15449-89db-55fd-81dc-1c686ff66376'}, {'abstract': 'The deaths were among serious cases of H7N9 avian flu in humans confirmed by China, the World Health Organization reported Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/world/asia/china-who-reports-3-deaths-among-bird-flu-cases-in-humans.html', 'snippet': 'The deaths were among serious cases of H7N9 avian flu in humans confirmed by China, the World Health Organization reported Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' China has confirmed 15 serious cases of H7N9 avian flu in humans, the World Health Organization reported Monday. All the people first reported symptoms in December; three have died, the rest are in critical condition. Their ages range from 20 to 78, with most over 50. All but one had a known history of exposure to live poultry. Human infections with this bird flu strain were first noticed in March 2013. Since then, there have been more than 450 cases, with the numbers spiking in winter and vanishing in summer. Thus far, the H7N9 strain has not been known to move easily between humans, although there have been some family clusters. There has been no known spread to health care workers. China has tried to fight outbreaks by shutting live poultry markets for cleaning, but legal and illegal markets continue to operate, the W.H.O. has said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: W.H.O. Reports 3 Deaths Among Bird Flu Cases in Humans', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: W.H.O. Reports 3 Deaths Among Bird Flu Cases in Humans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T02:50:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4ad66fd-82e3-5c93-9aa3-5e90713731fe', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4ad66fd-82e3-5c93-9aa3-5e90713731fe'}, {'abstract': 'The former police official was convicted of crimes against humanity and homicide in the 1980 siege of the Spanish Embassy that ended in a fire, killing 37 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/world/americas/guatemala-former-police-official-is-convicted-in-1980-embassy-siege.html', 'snippet': 'The former police official was convicted of crimes against humanity and homicide in the 1980 siege of the Spanish Embassy that ended in a fire, killing 37 people.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A court on Monday convicted a former police official of crimes against humanity and homicide in the 1980 siege of the Spanish Embassy that ended in a fire, killing 37 people, including diplomats, Guatemalan politicians and student and rural activists. Among the dead was the father of the Nobel Peace laureate Rigoberta Menchú; he was a member of an indigenous group that seized the embassy to protest the military’s brutal campaign against Indian villages as part of its battle against leftist rebels. The three-judge tribunal ruled that the official, Pedro García Arredondo, 70, the leader of a special police investigative unit, cut off negotiations, ordered officers to attack the embassy and prevented anyone from leaving after the fire broke out. The cause of the fire has never been determined. Mr. García was sentenced to 90 years in prison for his actions in the embassy fire and the killing of two students at a subsequent mass funeral. He is already serving a 70-year prison sentence for his role in the 1981 disappearance of a student leader. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guatemala: Former Police Official Is Convicted in 1980 Embassy Siege', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guatemala: Former Police Official Is Convicted in 1980 Embassy Siege', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia Arredondo, Pedro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala City (Guatemala)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T02:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/71b34ce5-9183-5100-b867-d4d6352c3d83', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71b34ce5-9183-5100-b867-d4d6352c3d83'}, {'abstract': 'Susan Gelfand humors us.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/19/comfort-in-action/', 'snippet': 'Susan Gelfand humors us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial New Puzzle Website Alert! Fred Piscop, author of the Split Decisions® variety puzzles, has recently launched a website where he will occasionally post new ones. You can check out these fun puzzles here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comfort in Action', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T03:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64f05119-9463-5298-b221-cb3a3608796e', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64f05119-9463-5298-b221-cb3a3608796e'}, {'ab