news-they-dont-need-a-league-of-their-own/', 'snippet': 'What sets the Central Illinois Xpress apart from other teams in its league?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Team’s Mission: Beat the Boys (and Maybe Make Them Cry),” Scott Cacciola writes about the Central Illinois Xpress, a basketball team that stands out in its fifth-grade league. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | They Don’t Need a League of Their Own', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T09:06:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25aefb72-aa8a-5280-9756-740173b4b4dd', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25aefb72-aa8a-5280-9756-740173b4b4dd'}, {'abstract': 'How do you think you would react if you had to quickly evacuate your home?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/what-would-you-grab-in-a-fire/', 'snippet': 'How do you think you would react if you had to quickly evacuate your home?', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who have only a moment or two to safely grab their possessions before fleeing a fire often say they reached for sentimental items like photographs or things that once belonged to departed loved ones or things that would be costly or otherwise difficult to replace. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/15/opinion/0115PRIVATELIVES-LN/0115PRIVATELIVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'x