or Martin J. Walsh, who is not in favor of holding a referendum on Boston’s hosting the 2024 Summer Olympics, said Tuesday that he would not try to block one.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston Mayor Says He Won’t Try to Block Referendum on Hosting 2024 Olympics ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boston Mayor Says He Won’t Try to Block Referendum on Hosting 2024 Olympics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2024)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Olympic Committee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walsh, Martin J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WBUR', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T11:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9650b84-464f-5177-8085-4c4752fd2504', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9650b84-464f-5177-8085-4c4752fd2504'}, {'abstract': 'What to do with the most offensive word in English? The Internet has an answer: Make it disappear.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/as-i-lay-lying-the-web-fixes-faulkner/', 'snippet': 'What to do with the most offensive word in English? The Internet has an answer: Make it disappear.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The past is never dead,” William Faulkner wrote, rather famously. “It’s not even past.” But that was before the Internet, which can shed the past so smoothly that we don’t even notice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/business/bits-faulkner/bits-faulkner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/17/business/bits-faulkner/bits-faulkner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/business/bits-faulkner/bits-faulkner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/business/bits-faulkner/bits-faulkner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1459, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/business/bits-faulkner/bits-faulkner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/17/business/bits-faulkner/bits-faulkner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/17/business/bits-faulkner/bits-faulkner-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As I Lay Lying: The Web Fixes Faulkner', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Faulkner, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RapGenius.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T11:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be1ffeb0-cc3a-5be5-86ca-b6268aa8d622', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be1ffeb0-cc3a-5be5-86ca-b6268aa8d622'}, {'abstract': 'The next president has to take on Boko Haram.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/opinion/the-boko-haram-factor.html', 'snippet': 'The next president has to take on Boko Haram.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAGOS, Nigeria — Here in Nigeria’s commercial hub, it is tempting to regard Boko Haram, the Islamist terrorist group that for more than five years has waged war in the country’s far northeast, as a distant tragedy. We are, of course, aware of the fallout: the thousands of deaths, the hundreds of thousands of displaced persons, the destroyed infrastructure — schools, churches, mosques, homes, police stations — that will take years, and millions of dollars, to rebuild. But in southern Nigeria, it is easy to feel removed from the crisis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/opinion/21ogunlesi/21ogunlesi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/opinion/21ogunlesi/21ogunlesi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/opinion/21ogunlesi/21ogunlesi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/opinion/21ogunlesi/21ogunlesi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/opinion/21ogunlesi/21ogunlesi-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/21/opinion/21ogunlesi/21ogunlesi-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/opinion/21ogunlesi/21ogunlesi-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nigeria’s Army of Psychopaths', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nigeria’s Army of Psychopaths', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ogunlesi, Tolu', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jonathan, Goodluck', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T11:05:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tolu Ogunlesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tolu', 'middl