1-9da9-5d6b-81a5-ba50d7f497b8'}, {'abstract': 'Chilina Kennedy will succeed Jessie Mueller, who won a Tony Award in the role of Carole King.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/stratford-festival-mainstay-will-be-new-star-of-beautiful-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Chilina Kennedy will succeed Jessie Mueller, who won a Tony Award in the role of Carole King.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chilina Kennedy, who previously starred on Broadway in “Jesus Christ Superstar,” will take over the title role of “Beautiful: The Carole King Musical” on March 7. Ms. Kennedy has big shoes to fill: she is replacing Jessie Mueller, who won a Tony Award in June for her performance as the seminal singer-songwriter. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stratford Festival Mainstay Will Be New Star of ‘Beautiful’ on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Next Carole King, at Least on Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Chilina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Carole', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Jessie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T18:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew R. Chow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Chow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d0d18f0-854c-51f2-a866-21dd033c6659', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d0d18f0-854c-51f2-a866-21dd033c6659'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama should abandon the $10.10 benchmark in favor of a bolder goal that is in keeping with economic and political realities — and with his promise to restore the middle class.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/the-state-of-the-union-and-the-minimum-wage/', 'snippet': 'President Obama should abandon the $10.10 benchmark in favor of a bolder goal that is in keeping with economic and political realities — and with his promise to restore the middle class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his State of the Union speech on tonight, President Obama is expected to again call on Congress to raise the federal minimum wage. His case is unassailable. The minimum was last updated eight years ago, when lawmakers passed a plan to raise it in steps to $7.25 in 2009. That level was too low even back then. And with each passing year, its inadequacy becomes more apparent. The economic underclass is growing, the economy is becoming more unequal and taxpayers are being forced to subsidize low-wage employers by providing public aid to underpaid workers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/opinion/1202015sotu/1202015sotu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/20/opinion/1202015sotu/1202015sotu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/opinion/1202015sotu/1202015sotu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/opinion/1202015sotu/1202015sotu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1275, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/opini