a cocktail and ends with dessert. At tableside trolleys inside the many dining rooms, bananas still go up in flames every few minutes. The stucco facade on Royal Street in the French Quarter is still pink, although the paint manufacturer prefers to call it Tomato Cream Sauce. (The trim color is Mayonnaise.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brennan’s in New Orleans Walks the Tightrope of Tradition', 'kicker': 'Critic on the Road', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walking the Tightrope of Tradition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Brennan's (New Orleans, La, Restaurant)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T18:56:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f36acf7-9fd0-5931-b993-abadd2e1ff1d', 'word_count': 1463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f36acf7-9fd0-5931-b993-abadd2e1ff1d'}, {'abstract': 'Job growth is up, and the deficit is down. But incomes are not doing so well, and neither is the climate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/upshot/better-but-still-troubled-our-take-on-the-state-of-the-union.html', 'snippet': 'Job growth is up, and the deficit is down. But incomes are not doing so well, and neither is the climate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama isn’t going to offer an objective overview of the country when he delivers his sixth annual address to Congress on Tuesday night. No president does so in a State of the Union. He will instead emphasize the positive, mostly elide the negative and take a few wry digs at the other political party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-State-1/21UP-State-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-State-1/21UP-State-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-State-1/21UP-State-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-State-1/21UP-State-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Better but Still Troubled: Our Take on the State of the Union', 'kicker': 'Overview', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_dat