etic, spectacle-driven reimagining of the Robin Hood story, is selling well for its current Toronto production, but two New York group sales agents said that seats for the Broadway run haven’t been snatched up in droves. The two sales agents spoke on condition of anonymity to describe confidential sales information.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Heart of Robin Hood’ Delays Plans for Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T19:45:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3617785-f1f8-51b3-9821-b6e5a4ab9f8b', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3617785-f1f8-51b3-9821-b6e5a4ab9f8b'}, {'abstract': 'The Upshot is offering its own take on the state of the union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/01/20/from-the-upshot-the-state-of-the-union/', 'snippet': 'The Upshot is offering its own take on the state of the union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Better but Still Troubled: Our Take on the State of the Union', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From The Upshot: The State of the Union', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T19:49:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4220b20c-c31a-5c19-96d6-75582338c39f', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4220b20c-c31a-5c19-96d6-75582338c39f'}, {'abstract': 'If dwarf planets are considered actual planets, the mnemonic device for remembering their order will need to be rewritten. We are taking suggestions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/science/a-new-planet-mnemonic-pluto-dwarf-planets.html', 'snippet': 'If dwarf planets are considered actual planets, the mnemonic device for remembering their order will need to be rewritten. We are taking suggestions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Pluto was demoted from planethood, the trusty mnemonic “My Very Educated Mother Just Served Us Nine Pizzas” lost its main dish. Teachers and students across the world came up with adjustments. “My Very Educated Mother Just Served Us Noodles” was an easy tweak. Others revamped the mnemonic entirely — “Mean Very Evil Men Just Shortened Up Nature” was the offering of Caltech astronomy professor Mike Brown.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/science/20planet_callout/20planet_callout-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 246, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/20/science/20planet_callout/20planet_callout-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 246}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/science/20planet_callout/20planet_callout-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 