s for the new musical tripled over the weekend, after the show’s largely positive reviews came out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s too soon to say if the new Broadway musical “Honeymoon in Vegas” will be able to capitalize on its mostly positive reviews last Thursday and turn around its lackluster ticket sales during recent weeks of preview performances. But ticket sales did almost triple last weekend, a spokesman for the producers said on Tuesday, though the producers declined to provide dollar amounts that would put that box-office jump in context. Meanwhile, according to ticket-sale data released on Tuesday, “Honeymoon in Vegas” – a musical adaptation of the 1992 film comedy of the same name – grossed a modest $440,476 last week, or 43 percent of the maximum possible amount.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/20artsbeat-vegas/20artsbeat-vegas-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/20artsbeat-vegas/20artsbeat-vegas-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/20artsbeat-vegas/20artsbeat-vegas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/20artsbeat-vegas/20artsbeat-vegas-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1528, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/20artsbeat-vegas/20artsbeat-vegas-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'