major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-20T21:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31145147-0346-5881-a69f-5d63f3b94d22', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31145147-0346-5881-a69f-5d63f3b94d22'}, {'abstract': 'There have been enough pops of burnt orange on the runway to inspire otherwise cautious men to take on the autumnal shade.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/fashion-trends-orange-in-london-milan-fall-winter-2015/', 'snippet': 'There have been enough pops of burnt orange on the runway to inspire otherwise cautious men to take on the autumnal shade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to the fall/winter 2015 men’s wear shows, to declare that “orange is the new black” would be to misrepresent most guys’ willingness to experiment with color. So far this season, though, there have been enough pops of burnt orange on the runway to inspire at least somewhat adventurous men to take on the autumnal shade, à la River Phoenix in the film “My Own Private Idaho.” In London at the Margaret Howell show, an orange jumper — worn on a red-headed model for extra oomph — brought new life to the British designer’s usually somber palette. In Milan, where the shows concluded today, the color continued to permeate some of the bigger collections. For Bottega Veneta, Tomas Maier played with a range of hues,\xa0from purple and kelly green to what he called “persimmon,” an orange shade that was deftly implemented in knits, outerwear and accessories like the above scarf. For Jil Sander’s men’s debut under the creative direction of Rodolfo Paglialunga, the designer also deployed accents of retro-inspired colors, including mustard and hunter green as well as a rusty shade seen in a covetable drop-shouldered textured polo. Though the copper-colored teddy-bear coat in No.21’s collection might be a stretch for some men, the matching sweater worn underneath is a much more palatable option to try next fall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/t-magazine/20orange-tudela/20orange-tudela-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/20/t-magazine/20orange-tudela/20orange-tudela-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/t-magazine/20orange-tudela/20orange-tudela-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/t-magazine/20orange-tudela/20orange-tudela-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/t-magazine/20orange-tudela/20orange-tudela-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/20/t-magazine/20orange-tudela/20orange-tudela-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/t-magazine/20orange-tudela/20orange-tudela-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width