r allies lashed out at Alberto Nisman, who was found dead in his home, questioning whether he had allied himself with forces seeking to weaken her government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Facing a public outcry over the mysterious death of Alberto Nisman, the prosecutor leading the investigation into the 1994 bombing of a Jewish community center here, President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner and her allies lashed out at the dead man on Tuesday, questioning whether he had allied himself with forces seeking to weaken her government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentine Leader Criticizes Dead Official ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentine Leader Criticizes Dead Official', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nisman, Alberto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T01:12:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Gilbert and Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilbert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eb06f33-84c7-5951-a316-c51684656c22', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eb06f33-84c7-5951-a316-c51684656c22'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Seidenberg, a civil rights lawyer, is best known for successfully suing McSorley’s Old Ale House in a case in which a judge found that sex discrimination in public accommodations is unconstitutional.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/nyregion/faith-seidenberg-91-dies-took-onmcsorleys-an-all-male-haven.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Seidenberg, a civil rights lawyer, is best known for successfully suing McSorley’s Old Ale House in a case in which a judge found that sex discrimination in public accommodations is unconstitutional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One frigid January night in 1969, Faith Seidenberg vividly recalled a few years later, she and another woman, shivering “as much from fear as from the cold,” boldly swung open the double doors of McSorley’s Old Ale House in Manhattan, which “had withstood for 115 years the entry of female customers.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/nyregion/seidenberg-1-obit/seidenberg-1-obit-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/nyregion/seidenberg-1-obit/seidenberg-1-obit-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/nyregion/seidenberg-1-obit/seidenberg-1-obit-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/nyregion/seidenberg-1-obit/seidenberg-1-obit-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/nyregion/seidenberg-1-obit/seidenberg-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/21/nyregion/seidenberg-1-obit/seidenberg-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/nyregion/seidenberg-1-obit/seidenberg-1-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Faith Seidenberg, 91, Dies; Took On\xa0McSorley’s, an All-Male Haven', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Faith Seidenberg, 91, Dies; Took On All-Male Haven', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McSorley's Old Ale House (Manhattan, NY)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seidenberg, Faith (1923-2015)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T01:20:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3aa8f72-6a39-56c1-89a6-5e1d59f7fca2', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3aa8f72-6a39-56c1-89a6-5e1d59f7fca2'}, {'abstract': 'The United States attorney for New York’s Eastern District signed off on a settlement that would return $447,000 seized from a Long Island business under civil asset forfeiture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/us/447000-seized-by-government-will-be-returned-to-business.html', 'snippet': 'The United States attorney for New York’s Eastern District signed off on a settlement that would return $447,000 seized from a Long Island business under civil asset forfeiture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Loretta E. Lynch, the United States attorney for New York’s Eastern District and President Obama’s nominee for attorney general, signed off on Tuesday to a settlement that would return $447,000 seized from a family-run Long Island business under a controversial area of federal law known as civil asset forfeiture. The business, Bi-County Distributors, was initially targeted because of a pattern of cash deposits under $10,000, but its owners, the Hirsch family, argued that the deposits were legitimate and, though more than two years passed after the money was seized, no criminal charges were filed. Lawyers from the Institute for Justice filed a motion demanding the return of the money. In the resulting settlement, neither side in the case admitted wrongdoing. Last Friday, the outgoing Attorney General, Eric H. Holder Jr., announced a policy change to rein in federal participation in civil asset forfeiture. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$447,000 Seized by Government Will Be Returned to Business', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Courts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$447,000 Seized by Government Will Be Returned to Business', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bi-County Distributors Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dewan, Shaila', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Business', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute for Justice', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Loretta E', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T01:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/69bd6f86-92ea-56b0-b6c9-7fce7a548799', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69bd6f86-92ea-56b0-b6c9-7fce7a548799'}, {'abstract': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration’s new administrator, Mark R. Rosekind, has ordered a review of a 2013 recall of Ford’s biggest pickup trucks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/business/safety-unit-broadens-its-scrutiny-of-a-recall.html', 'snippet': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration’s new administrator, Mark R. Rosekind, has ordered a review of a 2013 recall of Ford’s biggest pickup trucks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A week after the nation’s top auto regulator warned automakers that he would be more vigilant on safety, his agency has taken the unusual move of revisiting the 2013 recall of Ford’s biggest pickup trucks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/business/21RECALL/21RECALL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/2