n November to avoid a no-confidence vote, announced Tuesday that general elections would be held on May 11.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Donald Ramotar, who suspended Parliament in November to avoid a no-confidence vote, announced Tuesday that general elections would be held on May 11. “I expect to win the election and win back a majority in Parliament,” Mr. Ramotar said. His People’s Progressive Party, dominated by Indo-Guyanese, has held power for more than 20 years but fell short of a majority in the assembly in 2011 with the rise of a multiethnic third party as a political force. The two main parties have traditionally hewed to racial lines: one drawing support from the descendants of Africans, the other from the descendants of Indians. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guyana: President Announces Date for Elections', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guyana: President Announces Date for Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Girish', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guyana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramotar, Donald R (1950- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T02:43:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Girish Gupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Girish', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c38db201-0a38-5d05-824a-d2e7139ffc4e', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c38db201-0a38-5d05-824a-d2e7139ffc4e'}, {'abstract': 'The board of the bankrupt opera must name its preferred choice by Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/nyregion/potential-buyers-of-new-york-city-opera-hold-a-bidding-war-in-court.html', 'snippet': 'The board of the bankrupt opera must name its preferred choice by Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City Opera may have run out of money, filed for bankruptcy and sold its costumes and instruments, but two rival groups are so interested in trying to reinvent the company that they held a bidding war in court on Tuesday for its name and remaining assets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Potential Buyers of New York City Opera Hold a Bidding War in Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bidding in Court for Opera’s Assets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dicapo Opera Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NYCO Renaissance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lane, Sean H', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T02:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dadc439-d225-5932-8157-b73cd45eeb08', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dadc439-d225-5932-8157-b73cd45eeb08'}, {'abstract': 'A British man who joined a jihadist group to fight in Syria and then returned to Britain after faking his death has pleaded guilty to four terrorism offenses, the London police said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/world/europe/britain-man-pleads-guilty-to-terrorism-charges.html', 'snippet': 'A British man who joined a jihadist group to fight in Syria and then returned to Britain after faking his death has pleaded guilty to four terrorism offenses, the London police said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A British man who joined a jihadist group to fight in Syria and then returned to Britain after faking his death has pleaded guilty to four terrorism offenses, the London police said Tuesday. The man, Imran Khawaja, 27, of Southall in West London, left last January, joined a group called Rayat al-Tawheed and, with his face concealed, was featured in a grisly video in Syria in which he was described as “British ISIS fighter Abu Daigham al-Britani with government soldier’s head Syria,” the police said. Mr. Khawaja, who is to be sentenced next month, was arrested entering Britain at the port of Dover last June. He pleaded guilty last month to charges including attending a terrorism training camp and preparing terrorist acts, but restrictions on reporting his plea were lifted just Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Man Pleads Guilty to Terrorism Charges', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Man Pleads Guilty to Terrorism Charges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T02:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/06672acf-3f8c-5a40-8ad4-1757d44080a5', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06672acf-3f8c-5a40-8ad4-1757d44080a5'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/nyregion/winning-lottery-numbers-for-jan-20-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan. 20, 2015', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Lottery Numbers for Jan. 20, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T02:48:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/725a77c8-1425-560e-9359-f85991197ec2', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/725a77c8-1425-560e-9359-f85991197ec2'}, {'abstract': 'Experiments confirm a way that politicians can get citizens of the opposing party on their side, even if briefly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/upshot/why-the-guests-because-heartwarming-stories-work.html', 'snippet': 'Experiments confirm a way that politicians can get citizens of the opposing party on their side, even if briefly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the guests who will hear President Obama’s State of the Union speech in person – in the first lady’s box – are a police captain who helped reduce crime in Los Angeles by 50 percent and a college student from Dallas whose undocumented parents are eligible for the administration’s deferred action program for parents of lawful permanent residents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-Stories/21UP-Stories-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-Stories/21UP-Stories-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-Stories/21UP-Stories-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-Stories/21UP-Stories-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-Stories/21UP-Stories-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-Stories/21UP-Stories-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/upshot/21UP-Stories/21UP-Stories-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Guests? Because Heartwarming Stories Work', 'kicker': 'State of the Union', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T02:49:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Vavreck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vavreck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f35d971f-23fb-5fd0-9b6e-97eef0290757', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f35d971f-23fb-5fd0-9b6e-97eef0290757'}, {'abstract': 'Yuta Watanabe, a freshman at George Washington and the first Japanese-born player to earn a Division I basketball scholarship, said he hoped to inspire other Japanese players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/sports/george-washingtons-yuta-watanabe-hopes-to-inspire-players-in-japan.html', 'snippet': 'Yuta Watanabe, a freshman at George Washington and the first Japanese-born player to earn a Division I basketball scholarship, said he hoped to inspire other Japanese players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — After Yuta Watanabe’s first workouts at George Washington University, his teammates recognized that he had the jump shot, the speed and the basketball intelligence to succeed at the Division I level.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/sports/YUTA1/YUTA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/sports/YUTA1/YUTA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidt