4476dc717'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Hilger enjoys left-right symmetry, and gives us a good dose today.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/everyone-pays-their-own-way/', 'snippet': 'Jim Hilger enjoys left-right symmetry, and gives us a good dose today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY PUZZLE — You’ll love this puzzle if you are the type who is vigilant about dotting your i’s and crossing your t’s. We’ll set aside the i’s for today, but Jim Hilger insists that you cross your t’s, and that you do it with the letter T.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Everyone Pays Their Own Way', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T03:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cb339ea-3969-5076-96ec-98aa61f8000c', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cb339ea-3969-5076-96ec-98aa61f8000c'}, {'abstract': '“I’m Gonna Pray for You So Hard” explores the dynamics of the relationship between a playwright and his actress daughter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/theater/im-gonna-pray-for-you-so-hard-with-reed-birney.html', 'snippet': '“I’m Gonna Pray for You So Hard” explores the dynamics of the relationship between a playwright and his actress daughter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like father, like daughter. That sentimental notion, usually cooed to emphasize an endearing trait shared across the generation gap, takes on a bone-chilling dimension in “I’m Gonna Pray for You So Hard,” a potently acted but punishing drama by Halley Feiffer about the destructive relationship between a famous playwright and his daughter, an aspiring actress.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/IMGONNA/IMGONNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/IMGONNA/IMGONNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/IMGONNA/IMGONNA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/IMGONNA/IMGONNA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/IMGONNA/IMGONNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/IMGONNA/IMGONNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/arts/IMGONNA/IMGONNA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Uneasy Rapport', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Uneasy Rapport', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feiffer, Halley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'org