thing they want.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/20/was-joni-ernsts-state-of-the-union-rebuttal-conciliatory-or-just-more-of-the-same/', 'snippet': 'Republicans will be happy to compromise with President Obama, so long as he does everything they want.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year after the State of the Union address, the party in opposition to the president produces a “response” speech from one of its members that, of course, is written long before the president enters Congress for this annual ritual. It’s not a terribly difficult job.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was Joni Ernst’s State of the Union Rebuttal Conciliatory, or Just More of the Same?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ernst, Joni', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T03:38:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a927d29a-76a9-5ee0-8f84-4b3a887bfae8', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a927d29a-76a9-5ee0-8f84-4b3a887bfae8'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Liptak, Supreme Court correspondent for The Times, discussed a case on judicial elections, Williams-Yulee v. The Florida Bar, with the specific issue being whether judges can ask for campaign money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000003338366/on-the-docket-is-a-judge-a-politician.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Liptak, Supreme Court corr