 '_id': 'nyt://article/1fc0359b-49d2-5bd8-8dde-6907d4431110', 'word_count': 1527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fc0359b-49d2-5bd8-8dde-6907d4431110'}, {'abstract': 'Politicians can win hearts on the left with stories about overcoming adversity in childhood, but there’s no evidence it affects their policy positions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/upshot/why-joni-ernst-talked-about-her-tough-upbringing.html', 'snippet': 'Politicians can win hearts on the left with stories about overcoming adversity in childhood, but there’s no evidence it affects their policy positions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As she did in her stump speeches for Senate last fall, Joni Ernst of Iowa mentioned her upbringing in her response to the State of the Union speech Tuesday night. She talked about tough times walking to the school bus and her feelings about being different from the other families in her town. Politicians do this because they think it makes them relatable — it’s a shortcut to many people that says, “I understand you.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/upshot/22UP-Ernst/22UP-Ernst-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/22/upshot/22UP-Ernst/22UP-Ernst-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/upshot/22UP-Ernst/22UP-Ernst-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/upshot/22UP-Ernst/22UP-Ernst-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': 