/article/12c5c246-c1b7-5aab-99bc-96fa8866bd24'}, {'abstract': 'To judge from warnings by Chinese Communist Party officials, the calligraphy racket can be as sordid and ruthless as a rigged wrestling match.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/line-drawn-on-purported-corruption-in-calligraphy/', 'snippet': 'To judge from warnings by Chinese Communist Party officials, the calligraphy racket can be as sordid and ruthless as a rigged wrestling match.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Chinese culture, calligraphy holds a hallowed status. In ancient times, emperors, mandarins and poets prized the skill of using ink and a brush to render words, texts and poems on paper with such vigor and grace that the complex characters of written Chinese become an art form of their own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Line Drawn on Purported Corruption in Calligraphy', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T08:10:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f264a8e-5e56-53c6-93ae-371ff8a15174', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f264a8e-5e56-53c6-93ae-371ff8a15174'}, {'abstract': 'A history of failure has dogged China’s team, and deepened the fans’ gloom. But three wins at the Asian Cup could change all that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/sports/soccer/chinas-national-soccer-team-winning-games-and-fans.html', 'snippet': 'A history of failure has dogged China’s team, and deepened the fans’ gloom. But three wins at the Asian Cup could change all 