k': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T08:27:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3dc7616-a227-53cc-8580-62bcaec1bab6', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3dc7616-a227-53cc-8580-62bcaec1bab6'}, {'abstract': 'The assailant, who attacked a bus driver as well as passengers during the morning rush, was shot and wounded by security forces as he tried to escape. At least three victims had serious injuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/world/middleeast/middle-east-violence.html', 'snippet': 'The assailant, who attacked a bus driver as well as passengers during the morning rush, was shot and wounded by security forces as he tried to escape. At least three victims had serious injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — A Palestinian man stabbed and wounded up to a dozen Israelis on Wednesday as he rampaged through a bus in central Tel Aviv during the morning rush, the police said. He then fled on foot but was shot and wounded by security forces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stabbing on Tel Aviv Bus Breaks a Fragile Calm ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stabbing on Tel Aviv Bus Breaks a Fragile Calm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tel Aviv (Israel)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T09:10:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner and Irit Pazner Garshowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Irit', 'middlename': 'Pazner', 'lastname': 'Garshowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd2e48cd-6c6d-59dc-9840-7f3c55dcd9ef', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd2e48cd-6c6d-59dc-9840-7f3c55dcd9ef'}, {'abstract': 'Here are the first several paragraphs from a Jan. 14 article, “Be the Star of Your Own Snapchat Story.” Can you choose the best word or phrase for each blank?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/test-yourself-snapchat-stories/', 'snippet': 'Here are the first several paragraphs from a Jan. 14 article, “Be the Star of Your Own Snapchat Story.” Can you choose the best word or phrase for each blank?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are the first several paragraphs from a Jan. 14 article, “Be the Star of Your Own Snapchat Story.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Snapchat Stories', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T09:11:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b933c18d-9a75-5c33-b9ce-b88d2960bbc1', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b933c18d-9a75-5c33-b9ce-b88d2960bbc1'}, {'abstract': 'He warned lawmakers in his State of the Union address that failure to take action on trade legislation could be tantamount to ceding America’s leadership role to Beijing.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/obama-urges-congress-not-to-leave-a-trade-vacuum-for-china/', 'snippet': 'He warned lawmakers in his State of the Union address that failure to take action on trade legislation could be tantamount to ceding America’s leadership role to Beijing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama held up China as a formidable rival to the global influence of the United States in his annual State of the Union address on Tuesday, warning lawmakers that failure to take action on trade legislation could be tantamount to ceding America’s leadership role to Beijing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama, Citing China as Rival, Warns Lawmakers Over Inaction on Trade Measure', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hatch, Orrin G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Council', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Finance', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T09:20:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Forsythe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Forsythe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efc29109-0a4d-5839-8afd-4a1dc731d196', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efc29109-0a4d-5839-8afd-4a1dc731d196'}, {'abstract': 'What should colleges and communities do to decrease the amount of binge drinking among young people?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/why-is-binge-drinking-so-common-among-young-people-in-the-united-states/', 'snippet': 'What should colleges and communities do to decrease the amount of binge drinking among young people?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The drinking age in all 50 states is 21 years old, yet under-age drinking is widespread. According to the National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism: “Although youth drink less often than adults do, when they do drink, they drink more. That is because young people consume more than 90 percent of their alcohol by binge drinking.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Is Binge Drinking So Common Among Young People in the United States?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T10:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86fdb23a-fa29-5d37-af49-a22cca1ec6b6', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86fdb23a-fa29-5d37-af49-a22cca1ec6b6'}, {'abstract': 'The anchor has brought Fox News a more unpredictable approach to red-meat politics. Can she draw a more unpredictable audience?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/magazine/the-megyn-kelly-moment.html', 'snippet': 'The anchor has brought Fox News a more unpredictable approach to red-meat politics. Can she draw a more unpredictable audience?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a gray Wednesday in November, the Fox News anchor Megyn Kelly and four producers gathered around a conference table on the 17th floor of the News Corporation building in Manhattan. They were there to plan the 281st episode of “The Kelly File,” which would be shown live in a few hours, at 9 p.m. Kelly’s executive producer, Tom Lowell, a 25-year veteran of TV news, ticked through the program blocks, the between-commercial bits that are the basic unit of television programming. The A Block would contain a Fox News exclusive on the president’s plans to halt millions of deportations. The B and C Blocks would focus on the Obama health care adviser Jonathan Gruber’s declaration, caught on tape, that the Affordable Care Act passed in part because of “the stupidity of the American voter.” Slated for the D block was Jonathan Gilliam, a former Navy SEAL.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25kelly7/25kelly7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25kelly7/25kelly7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25kelly7/25kelly7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25kelly7/25kelly7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 827, 'width': 1241, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25kelly7/25kelly7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25kelly7/25kelly7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25kelly7/25kelly7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Megyn Kelly Moment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Megyn Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rutenberg, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Megyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T10:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71dd83d7-6a3c-59c0-b304-a01d15155a09', 'word_count': 6937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71dd83d7-6a3c-59c0-b304-a01d15155a09'}, {'abstract': 'Going behind the numbers and beyond the political debate, Mark Abramson got close to a young immigrant whose parents took her to California despite not having proper authorization.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/an-immigrants-dream-for-a-better-life/', 'snippet': 'Going behind the numbers and beyond the political debate, Mark Abramson got close to a young immigrant whose parents took her to California despite not having proper authorization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pictures of Blanca’s life in California look ordinary: relaxing with her parents on the banks of a river, dressed up for her quinceañera, studying at school, moving into her first off-campus apartment. Yet to her — and to thousands of other immigrants whose parents brought them to this country without authorization — the pictures represent lives that reach for the future, aware of the obstacles that could one day take it all away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Immigrant’s Dream for a Better Life', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dream Act (Development, Relief and Education for Minors Act)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berkeley (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T10:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ea8c876-7241-526d-aaeb-2659341c2935', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ea8c876-7241-526d-aaeb-2659341c2935'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Manuel Valls of France announced new security measures Wednesday in Paris, including proposals to add about 2,500 new jobs to fight terrorism and monitor potential threats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/world/europe/amedy-coulibaly-paris-gunman-france.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Manuel Valls of France announced new security measures Wednesday in Paris, including proposals to add about 2,500 new jobs to fight terrorism and monitor potential threats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The French government promised a sweeping legislative response on Wednesday to this month’s terrorist attacks, setting out proposals to monitor potential threats more closely and wading deeper into an emerging debate over balancing security and civil liberties.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Vows Forceful Measures Against Terrorism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Vows Forceful Measures Against Terrorism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charl