cases the monetary authorities had accumulated huge reserves. Both found themselves at the mercy of that larger economy’s monetary policies — much obsession here over when the Fed will raise rates, much discussion of how low rates and QE in the US fed housing prices. So is the Hong Kong dollar at risk of a franc-like event?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tale of Two Pegs', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T12:06:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e248f3c3-38c5-5287-8734-a368ecb32d11', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e248f3c3-38c5-5287-8734-a368ecb32d11'}, {'abstract': 'Shareholders are facing a quandary in the battle for Family Dollar. | President Obama sets agenda to help the middle class. | S.&P. is nearing costly settlements with the U.S. | Profit at Morgan Stanley disappoints.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/morning-agenda-dollar-store-predicament/', 'snippet': 'Shareholders are facing a quandary in the battle for Family Dollar. | President Obama sets agenda to help the middle class. | S.&P. is nearing costly settlements with the U.S. | Profit at Morgan Stanley disappoints.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shareholders are facing a predicament in the battle for Family Dollar, Steven Davidoff Solomon writes in the Deal Professor column. On Thursday, Family Dollar shareholders will vote on a proposed $8.5 billion acquisition by Dollar Tree, which is offering about $76 a share. If they vote yes, “it will be the death knell for a competing bid by Dollar General th