t://video/b1138278-9aee-5ff9-9951-ed58db07a833', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/b1138278-9aee-5ff9-9951-ed58db07a833'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Anger at Germany’s Zeppelin raid on Britain in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/1915-murder-from-the-skies/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Anger at Germany’s Zeppelin raid on Britain in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Fierce indignation is the predominant sentiment in this country now that the full results of the cowardly Zeppelin raid on the undefended East Anglian towns are known to the public. For months past the enemy has threatened England with attack by airships, and the very fulfilment of his threat has done more than anything else could have done to dispel the bogey of his creation. Put briefly, all that the Germans have accomplished by their dastardly night attack is the murder of two women, one boy and a man, the injuring of a baby girl and thirty-one adults, nearly all non- combatants, and the destruction of some thousands of pounds’ worth of property. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Jan. 22, 1915 ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/blogs/21iht-old22/21iht-old22-articleLarge.png', 'height': 547, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/blogs/21iht-old22/21iht-old22-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 547}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/blogs/21iht-old22/21iht-old22-jumbo.png', 'height': 697, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/blogs/21iht-ol