f DealBook about his new book and the secret behind the brand known as Tony Robbins.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/video-tony-robbins-reveals-his-secret/', 'snippet': 'The life coach and motivational speaker Tony Robbins spoke with Andrew Ross Sorkin of DealBook about his new book and the secret behind the brand known as Tony Robbins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The life coach and motivational speaker Tony Robbins spoke with Andrew Ross Sorkin of DealBook about his new book and the secret behind the brand known as Tony Robbins.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Tony Robbins Reveals His Secret', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T14:49:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dbbf119-ecb9-5d84-8ecd-1b6390281482', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dbbf119-ecb9-5d84-8ecd-1b6390281482'}, {'abstract': 'In this picture book, a cheerful first grader — who happens to be blind — navigates through her day with her friends at her side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/books/review/cari-bests-my-three-best-friends-and-me-zulay.html', 'snippet': 'In this picture book, a cheerful first grader — who happens to be blind — navigates through her day with her friends at her side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first things we learn about Zulay, a first grader with pigtails like two fluffy pompoms on top of her head and a big, bright smile, are that she likes numbers, she likes symmetry and she likes being connected to her friends. In her classroom, she tells us, “there are 22 chairs and 22 desks,” along with 22 pencils, books, hooks, smocks and people. She in one of “four best friends who help each other, four best friends who help themselves — Maya, Nancy, Zulay, and Chyng.” We soon see this mutuality in action when Maya helps Zulay draw a pyramid, then Zulay helps Maya understand tens and ones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/books/review/21childrens/21childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/books/review/21childrens/21childrens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/books/review/21childrens/21childrens-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/books/review/21childrens/21childrens-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1050, 'width': 1700, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/books/review/21childrens/21childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/21/books/review/21childrens/21childrens-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/books/review/21childrens/21childrens-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ways of Seeing', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Best, Cari', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brantley-Newton, Vanessa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'My Three Best Friends and Me, Zulay (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T15:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Russo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/206679a1-4859-57be-8fa4-28799fa8b7c5', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/206679a1-4859-57be-8fa4-28799fa8b7c5'}, {'abstract': 'The director Pawel Pawlikowski’s family snapshots from his boyhood in Poland were one source of inspiration for the film “Ida.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/have-photo-albums-will-travel/', 'snippet': 'The director Pawel Pawlikowski’s family snapshots from his boyhood in Poland were one source of inspiration for the film “Ida.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' Polish films about the Holocaust have been nominated for Oscars before, notably Agnieszka Holland’s “In Darkness” just three years ago, but strictly speaking, Pawel Pawlikowski’s “Ida,” a nominee this year, is a post-Holocaust movie. It takes place in the early 1960s, when the title character, an 18-year-old novitiate, learns that she is actually Jewish and meets up with her aunt Wanda, a disillusioned Communist prosecutor who guides the naïve teenager through the family’s grim, hidden history.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'su