ad013-a86f-5416-98fc-4460dc1a4ff3', 'word_count': 1268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f50ad013-a86f-5416-98fc-4460dc1a4ff3'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re a Democrat, you probably feel pretty good about the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/tell-me-your-party-and-ill-tell-you-how-you-feel/', 'snippet': 'If you’re a Democrat, you probably feel pretty good about the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re a Democrat, you probably feel pretty good about the economy. If you’re a Republican, you probably don’t. At least that’s the take away from a new Washington Post-ABC News poll.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tell Me Your Party and I’ll Tell You How You Feel', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T16:49:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21f7f18e-96e2-5fed-aa76-e3cfc5e1cebf', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21f7f18e-96e2-5fed-aa76-e3cfc5e1cebf'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The Russian Army struggles in Finland in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/1940-russians-abandon-positions/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The Russian Army struggles in Finland in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH FINLAND’S NORTHERN ARMY — The Russian forces that are still holding on to the village of Markajaervi, on the south Salla road, to which they retreated early in the week, abandoned strong defensive positions without a battle. They were forced out of their fortifications near Joutsijaervi, thirty miles away, by a series of rapier-like flank attacks that made their front line untenable. They picked up their baggage and moved slowly back along the highway that leads to Salla and the Soviet border without taking time to destroy their machine gun nests and dugouts. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 22, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Russians Abandon Positions', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Finland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T16:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b916b36b-ad23-5588-94f7-4454f408ea8b', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b916b36b-ad23-5588-94f7-4454f408ea8b'}, {'abstract': 'The European Central Bank is expected to announce a broad bond-buying program, like the quantitative easing program that largely proved successful in the United States and Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/01/21/business/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying.html', 'snippet': 'The European Central Bank is expected to announce a broad bond-buying program, like the quantitative easing program that largely proved successful in the United States and Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European Central Bank is expected to announce a broad bond-buying program, like the quantitative easing program that largely proved successful in the United States and Britain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/business/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600-articleLarge.png', 'height': 164, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/business/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 164}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/business/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 201, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/business/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 201, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/business/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/21/business/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600/Euro-Style-Bond-Buying-1421799281600-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Style Bond Buying', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T16:54:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/786109e4-bbd8-5f82-9be0-ba8f33bffcff', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/786109e4-bbd8-5f82-9be0-ba8f33bffcff'}, {'abstract': 'The American movie mainstream needs a revolution — and if some women have their way, it just might get one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/movies/on-many-fronts-women-are-fighting-for-better-opportunity-in-hollywood.html', 'snippet': 'The American movie mainstream needs a revolution — and if some women have their way, it just might get one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American movie mainstream needs a revolution — and if some women have their way, it just might get one. It’s time. Not because Ava DuVernay wasn’t tapped as a best director in the recent Academy Award nominations, even though her acclaimed movie “Selma” received a best picture nod. There has been a lot of speculation about the snub, but the reasons are less crucial than the message that the largely white, male directors in the Academy sent: This woman doesn’t deserve credit for her own movie. Women in film are routinely denied jobs, credits, prizes and equal pay, so the rebuke was familiar. That’s because while individual men struggle in the industry, women struggle as a group. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25DARGIS1/25DARGIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25DARGIS1/25DARGIS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit':