n are unexpected highlights in the mile-high city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/travel/what-to-do-in-denver.html', 'snippet': 'Bagels, beignets, a history museum and a botanic garden are unexpected highlights in the mile-high city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The signs of Denver’s economic high times as a pot boomtown and bastion of progressive urban policies are everywhere. There is the B-cycle bike-share program, among the most affordable and best-run systems in the country, and the newly renovated Union Station, which has taken a still-in-use 1881 train station and made it the focal point of the thriving LoDo neighborhood. And there are the inconspicuous marijuana dispensaries that dot nearly every neighborhood, and more stunning public spaces — from Washington Park to the Cherry Creek bike path — than one city has a right to.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Do in Denver', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What to Do in Denver', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moon, Freda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denver (Colo)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Art Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T17:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Freda Moon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Freda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mate