rned in a 22.4 percent return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the years since the dot-com crash of 2000, Silicon Valley’s venture capital firms have generally lagged behind their Wall Street cousins that take companies private in leveraged buyouts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-twitter/dbpix-twitter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-twitter/dbpix-twitter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 307}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-twitter/dbpix-twitter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-twitter/dbpix-twitter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1046, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-twitter/dbpix-twitter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-twitter/dbpix-twitter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-twitter/dbpix-twitter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venture Capital Outpaces Buyouts in Investment Returns', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sequoia Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T17:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f127cdcb-aa4b-514e-95a7-8f96f3d6eb9e', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f127cdcb-aa4b-514e-95a7-8f96f3d6eb9e'}, {'abstract': 'Small, an offshoot of the MAN/WOMAN trade shows, is a 500-square-foot space in the Marais district hosting a rotating cast of soon-to-be-cultish brands.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/new-paris-boutique-small-x-japan/', 'snippet': 'Small, an offshoot of the MAN/WOMAN trade shows, is a 500-square-foot space in the Marais district hosting a rotating cast of soon-to-be-cultish brands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2012, the MAN/WOMAN trade shows, where a tightly edited selection of fashion and lifestyle brands showcase their newest offerings, have been paramount for magazine editors and retail buyers seeking the next big thing. To bring that curatorial point of view to the public, MAN/WOMAN recently opened its first retail location in Paris’s trendy Marais district. The shop, called Small, invites international retailers and brands to install their visions on a monthly basis in a cozy retail venue measuring just under 500 square feet. “Small appears as a good and quite easy option for designers to target a new consumer and market,” says one of its founders, Antoine Floch. Traveling between Paris, New York, Tokyo and sometimes Los Angeles on what seems like a weekly basis, Floch, along with his partners Olivier Migda and Romain Bernardie James, has developed a keen eye for fashion’s soon-to-be-cultish brands. “We are lucky to work with the most creative and most well-produced brands right now, as well as the most beautifully designed and curated stores on the planet,” he says. “Some of them have been friends for a long time.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/t-magazine/21small-tudela/21small-tudela-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/t-magazine/21small-tudela/21small-tudela-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/t-magazine/21small-tudela/21small-tudela-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/t-magazine/21small-tudela/21small-tudela-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/t-magazine/21small-tudela/21small-tudela-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/21/t-magazine/21small-tudela/21small-tudela-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum