rand Budapest Hotel,” discusses his work.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/below-the-line-shooting-the-grand-budapest-hotel/', 'snippet': 'Robert Yeoman, the cinematographer for “The Grand Budapest Hotel,” discusses his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cinematographer Robert Yeoman has long been helping to craft meticulous and precise images for Wes Anderson’s films. He has shot every one of the director’s live-action movies since “Bottle Rocket,” contributing to a motif that is instantly recognizable, frequently praised and sometimes parodied. With “The Grand Budapest Hotel” (Oscar-nominated for best cinematography), Mr. Yeoman and Mr. Anderson took the visuals a level further, shooting in multiple aspect ratios for the different time periods in which the film takes place.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/movies/budapest3/budapest3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 461, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/21/movies/budapest3/budapest3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 461}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/movies/budapest3/budapest3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 787, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/movies/budapest3/budapest3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1574, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/21/movies/budapest3/budapest3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard',