he deal for Hiland Partners comes months after Mr. Hamm, an oil tycoon, was ordered to pay roughly $1 billion to his ex-wife, in one of the most expensive divorce settlements in history.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/kinder-morgan-to-buy-oil-pipeline-company-from-harold-hamm-for-3-billion/', 'snippet': 'The deal for Hiland Partners comes months after Mr. Hamm, an oil tycoon, was ordered to pay roughly $1 billion to his ex-wife, in one of the most expensive divorce settlements in history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kinder Morgan said on Wednesday that it had agreed to buy Hiland Partners, an oil pipeline and gathering company owned by the billionaire Harold Hamm, for about $3 billion, expanding its presence in the oil-rich Bakken rock formation in the northern United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-hamm/dbpix-hamm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-hamm/dbpix-hamm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-hamm/dbpix-hamm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-hamm/dbpix-hamm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1336, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-hamm/dbpix-hamm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-hamm/dbpix-hamm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/business/dbpix-hamm/dbpix-hamm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kinder Morgan to Buy Oil Pipeline Company From Harold Hamm for $3 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamm, Harold', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kinder Morgan Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T22:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d50a8046-2d0f-5d34-b252-e8cd8bcc769e', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d50a8046-2d0f-5d34-b252-e8cd8bcc769e'}, {'abstract': 'David S. Taylor will take over the company’s beauty unit in a move interpreted to put him one step closer to succeeding the chief executive, A.G. Lafley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/business/executive-shake-up-at-procter-gamble-hints-at-next-leader.html', 'snippet': 'David S. Taylor will take over the company’s beauty unit in a move interpreted to put him one step closer to succeeding the chief executive, A.G. Lafley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Procter & Gamble announced a reshuffling of its top ranks on Wednesday in a move that might provide a clue to who will become the next leader of the consumer products giant.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Executive Shake-Up at Procter & Gamble ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Executive Shake-Up at Procter & Gamble', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Procter & Gamble Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, David S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lafley, Alan G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henretta, Deb A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T22:10:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/319e119e-2f69-548e-937b-55f84448791a', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/319e119e-2f69-548e-937b-55f84448791a'}, {'abstract': 'For gluten-free families, the increasing concerns about arsenic and rice are a source of worry and guilt. But how much should parents blame themselves?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/free-of-gluten-but-not-of-arsenic-or-of-guilt/', 'snippet': 'For gluten-free families, the increasing concerns about arsenic and rice are a source of worry and guilt. But how much should parents blame themselves?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until last week, my children ate arsenic daily. Once used to poison royalty, arsenic (among other metals from the soil) is currently tainting rice, and I fed my daughters rice pasta for dinner, rice bread sandwiches for lunch, rice bagels for breakfast and rice cakes for snacks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/06/us/CRAYFISH-1-copy/CRAYFISH-1-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/12/06/us/CRAYFISH-1-copy/CRAYFISH-1-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/06/us/CRAYFISH-1-copy/CRAYFISH-1-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/06/us/CRAYFISH-1-copy/CRAYFISH-1-copy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1237, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/06/us/CRAYFISH-1-copy/CRAYFISH-1-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/06/us/CRAYFISH-1-copy/CRAYFISH-1-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/06/us/CRAYFISH-1-copy/CRAYFISH-1-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Free of Gluten, but Not of Arsenic (or of Guilt)', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celiac Disease', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'majo