te': '2015-01-21T23:47:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandy Keenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db1800d6-42c5-58c2-b301-368ee01871cc', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db1800d6-42c5-58c2-b301-368ee01871cc'}, {'abstract': 'Auction house to sell notebook with writings by Alan Turing, the Enigma codebreaker.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/21/rare-alan-turing-document-outlining-mathematical-thought-to-be-auctioned/', 'snippet': 'Auction house to sell notebook with writings by Alan Turing, the Enigma codebreaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is short, just 56 pages long, and much of it consists of complicated mathematical musings written out in longhand. But it has never been seen before in public, and it provides an exciting insight into how Alan Turing, its author, formulated his theories about mathematical notation and computer science, according to Bonhams auction house. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rare Alan Turing Document, Outlining Mathematical Thought, to be Auctioned', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cryptography, Codes and Ciphers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turing, Alan M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bonhams 1793 Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambridge (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-21T23:51:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a6401b0-6fb2-5d91-a1d8-27c9157c5c7f', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a6401b0-6fb2-5d91-a1d8-27c9157c5c7f'}, {'abstract': 'One admires the chutzpah of party operatives whose platform opposes same-sex marriage hoping the justices will save them from having to choose sides in a fading culture war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/opinion/the-supreme-court-wont-end-the-gay-marriage-debate-for-republicans.html', 'snippet': 'One admires the chutzpah of party operatives whose platform opposes same-sex marriage hoping the justices will save them from having to choose sides in a fading culture war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So the Republican establishment is breathing easy now that the Supreme Court is on the verge of issuing a ruling in favor of same-sex marriage, thus taking the question out of nasty old politics? “I think it’s probably going to be a relief,” a Republican committeeman from California told Jeremy W. Peters and Jonathan Martin of The New York Times, explaining that with such a ruling, “then it’s off the table.” Praise the Lord and thank the court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenh