Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b089a410-f3e5-5dc4-b78f-9d570f1752a3', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b089a410-f3e5-5dc4-b78f-9d570f1752a3'}, {'abstract': 'The police officers were sentenced Wednesday to 10 years in prison for their role in the fatal beating of a university student.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/world/europe/turkey-2-officers-sentenced-in-death.html', 'snippet': 'The police officers were sentenced Wednesday to 10 years in prison for their role in the fatal beating of a university student.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two Turkish police officers were sentenced Wednesday to 10 years in prison\xa0 for their role in the fatal beating of a university student during antigovernment protests in 2013, a case that has become a symbol of police violence. Four other people received lesser sentences in the death of the student, Ali Ismail Korkmaz, 19, who was hit in the head with clubs several times by men in civilian clothing in Eskisehir, a northwestern town. He died more than a month after falling into a coma. On Wednesday the police in Kayseri, a central Anatolian town where the hearing took place, used tear gas to disperse crowds that criticized the terms as too lenient, news reports said. The 2013 protests grew into nationwide riots against the authoritarian tendencies of Prime Minister Recep Tayyip Erdogan, now president, who called the protesters looters and terrorists seeking to overthrow his government. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey: 2 Officers Sentenced in Death', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey: 2 Officers Sentenced in Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arsu, Sebnem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Korkmaz, Ali Ismail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T01:38:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5085f68b-b608-588f-8854-3e408fc3cd86', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5085f68b-b608-588f-8854-3e408fc3cd86'}, {'abstract': 'Jane Helser recently retired after working for nearly 50 years at the Wilson Sporting Goods factory, the source of the N.F.L.’s handmade footballs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/football/100000003463386/a-feel-for-the-game.html', 'snippet': 'Jane Helser recently retired after working for nearly 50 years at the Wilson Sporting Goods factory, the source of the N.F.L.’s handmade footballs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jane Helser recently retired after working for nearly 50 years at the Wilson Sporting Goods factory, the source of the N.F.L.’s handmade footballs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/multimedia/wilson/wilson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/20/multimedia/wilson/wilson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/20/multimed