e number of diagnoses in California reached 59, some schools said students may be barred because they have not been inoculated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — A measles outbreak that began at Disneyland is spreading across California and beyond, prompting health officials to move aggressively to contain it — including by barring unvaccinated students from going to school in Orange County. The outbreak has increased concerns that a longstanding movement against childhood vaccinations has created a surge in a disease that was declared eliminated in the United States in 2000.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Measles Cases Linked to Disneyland Rise, and Debate Over Vaccinations Intensifies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Measles Cases Linked to Disneyland Rise, and Debate Over Vaccinations Intensifies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Measles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Orange County (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Disneyland (Anaheim, Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T01:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney and Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc1c21a1-06ab-5463-85f2-47849cdb366b', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc1c21a1-06ab-5463-85f2-47849cdb366b'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Wojciechowski, whose Marquette team lost to St. John’s at the Garden, is among the many former assistants to Duke Coach Mike Krzyzewski who are now head coaches elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/sports/ncaabasketball/for-duke-players-turned-assistants-moving-up-means-moving-out.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Wojciechowski, whose Marquette team lost to St. John’s at the Garden, is among the many former assistants to Duke Coach Mike Krzyzewski who are now head coaches elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chris Carrawell knew he had to go far away when his time came. That was the way it was with all the former Duke players who had gone on to coaching roles at the university. Life in Durham, N.C., is so nice and cozy for the team’s assistant coaches — top talent, sustained national relevance and consistent job offers — that it is hard to find a reason to leave. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/sports/Y-MARQUETTE/Y-MARQUETTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 457, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/22/sports/Y-MARQUETTE/Y-MARQUETTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 457}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/sports/Y-MARQUETTE/Y-MARQUETTE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/sports/Y-MARQUETTE/Y-MARQUETTE-superJumbo.jpg', 'he