ct Authority fined David Caplin, formerly the firm’s chief executive, and Jeremy Kraft, a former compliance officer, in a case related to manipulation of the London interbank offered rate.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/two-former-rp-martin-executives-fined-banned-over-lack-of-compliance/', 'snippet': 'The Financial Conduct Authority fined David Caplin, formerly the firm’s chief executive, and Jeremy Kraft, a former compliance officer, in a case related to manipulation of the London interbank offered rate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Two former senior executives at RP Martin have been fined and banned from the securities industry for cultural and compliance failings at the small British brokerage firm, which was fined more than $2 million last year for misconduct related to the manipulation of the global benchmark known as the London interbank offered rate, or Libor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain Fines and Bans 2 Former RP Martin Executives Over Compliance Failures', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Conduct Authority (Great Britain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RP Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T12:46:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0139105-c188-544d-9316-33bdf72a4606', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0139105-c188-544d-9316-33bdf72a4606'}, {'abstract': 'In Xavier Dolan’s “Mommy,” a mother and her troubled son confront each other when he returns home after a stint in group living.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/movies/xavier-dolans-mommy-depicts-a-clashing-mother-and-son.html', 'snippet': 'In Xavier Dolan’s “Mommy,” a mother and her troubled son confront each other when he returns home after a stint in group living.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French-Canadian writer, director and actor Xavier Dolan is only 25, but “Mommy,” his fifth feature film in five years, seems like the work of an even younger filmmaker. I mean this, mostly, as a compliment. Stories of adolescence — young adult novels, coming-of-age movies, teenage-targeted television series — are usually the work of adults, and therefore often temper their emotional immediacy with nostalgia, condescension or grown-up wisdom. But “Mommy,” the story of a troubled young man and his mother, seethes and howls with unchecked feeling. Shot in the square, narrow dimensions of a cellphone video, it is a pocket opera of grandiose self-pity, a wild and uncompromising demand for attention, a cri de coeur from the selfie generation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MOMMY/23MOMMY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MOMMY/23MOMMY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MOMMY/23MOMMY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 