, 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9d42107-83b7-575d-8c09-88995259c919', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9d42107-83b7-575d-8c09-88995259c919'}, {'abstract': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2015/01/22/daily-clip-report-107/', 'snippet': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Here is Daily Clip Report, a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Clip Report', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T13:25:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/407bf5e0-d715-5ece-a398-57fbf9474746', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/407bf5e0-d715-5ece-a398-57fbf9474746'}, {'abstract': '“Smog Journeys” follows the lives of two Chinese families: one a mining family in rural Hebei Province and the other a cosmopolitan family in hyper-urban Beijing.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/film-highlights-air-pollutions-broad-reach/', 'snippet': '“Smog Journeys” follows the lives of two Chinese families: one a mining family in rural Hebei Province and the other a cosmopolitan family in hyper-urban Beijing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life in contemporary China as seen through the eyes of the Chinese filmmaker Jia Zhangke is often a gritty, somber affair. At times, the stark realism of Mr. Jia’s films has been too much for China’s censors, as was presumably the case with his last full-length film, the 2013 drama “A Touch of Sin,” which never made it onto Chinese screens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Film Highlights Air Pollution’s Broad Reach', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jia Zhang Ke', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenpeace', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T13:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Qin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78be795c-3d2b-5a39-925e-908e395c3074', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78be795c-3d2b-5a39-925e-908e395c3074'}, {'abstract': 'The president called for a major investment in a federal program, the Child Care and Development Fund, which is on top of the tax credit he announced in his State of the Union address.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/us/obama-economic-agenda-kansas-idaho.html', 'snippet': 'The president called for a major investment in a federal program, the Child Care and Development Fund, which is on top of the tax credit he announced in his State of the Union address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAWRENCE, Kan. — President Obama on Thursday unveiled plans to greatly increase federal assistance to working Americans struggling to afford child care, choosing a Democratic pocket in a solidly Republican state to sharpen the contrast between the two parties’ economic visions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/us/23SUBOBAMA/23OBAMA-1421950110100-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/23/us/23SUBOBAMA/23OBAMA-1421950110100-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/us/23SUBOBAMA/23OBAMA-1421950110100-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/us/23SUBOBAMA/23OBAMA-1421950110100-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1189, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/us/23SUBOBAMA/23OBAMA-1421950110100-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/23/us/23SUBOBAMA/23OBAMA-1421950110100-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'