0', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Adler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/652d0fea-97a4-5d62-a595-f0b7126f8550', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/652d0fea-97a4-5d62-a595-f0b7126f8550'}, {'abstract': 'In recent years, manageable rents in this artsy residential enclave, a short walk from the heart of the city, have encouraged locals to open equally artsy and eclectic shops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/travel/where-cervantes-once-lived-in-madrid-eclectic-boutiques-abound.html', 'snippet': 'In recent years, manageable rents in this artsy residential enclave, a short walk from the heart of the city, have encouraged locals to open equally artsy and eclectic shops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Madrid neighborhood of Barrio de las Letras is famous for the Spanish authors and poets who have lived here since the 14th century, including Cervantes. But, in recent years, the manageable rents in this artsy residential enclave, a short walk from the heart of the city, have encouraged locals to open equally artsy and eclectic shops. These affordable boutiques, selling everything including clothing, furniture, home goods and even guitars, are scattered along the charming crisscrossed streets lined with three- and four-story buildings, some dating back to the 18th century.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/travel/25FORAGING1/25FORAGING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/travel/25FORAGING1/25FORAGING1-articleLarg