le, place and art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although it has come late to contemporary photography, the Met has a few favorites in the field. One of them is the German photographer Thomas Struth, whose midcareer survey in 2003 had the rare distinction of spilling out into the museum’s Great Hall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Humanism on a Grand Scale', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Humanism on a Grand Scale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Struth, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T15:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/97c85672-3470-5eaf-92d1-b1c83dc5630b', 'word_count': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97c85672-3470-5eaf-92d1-b1c83dc5630b'}, {'abstract': 'The idea is similar to what Google did for search more than a decade ago.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/button-a-mobile-start-up-looks-to-link-apps-with-commerce/', 'snippet': 'The idea is similar to what Google did for search more than a decade ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took years for the web to become what it is today: a sprawling, interconnected network of sites endlessly linking back and forth to one another.', 'source': 'The New York