ds': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T17:09:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/447e2528-bd1f-5fa6-8f96-d7ff0752d75c', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447e2528-bd1f-5fa6-8f96-d7ff0752d75c'}, {'abstract': 'Lampedusa’s 1958 international best seller, “The Leopard,” was adapted into a Palme d’Or-winning film of the same name in 1963; a handcrafted letterpress printing pairs the original text with lush color photos from the set of the film.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/the-leopard-novel-film-new-letterpress-edition/', 'snippet': 'Lampedusa’s 1958 international best seller, “The Leopard,” was adapted into a Palme d’Or-winning film of the same name in 1963; a handcrafted letterpress printing pairs the original text with lush color photos from the set of the film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giuseppe Tomasi di Lampedusa’s internationally best-selling 1958 novel, “The Leopard,” is a satirically sad, lush tale of Italy’s lost, decadent aristocratic class. Set during Italian unification after the end of Napoleonic rule, when ancient feudal territories were merged and royal families were ruined, the novel is a meditation on revolutionary change. Luchino Visconti’s 1963 film adaptation of “The Leopard,” which won the Palme d’Or at Cannes, starred Alain Delon and Burt Lancaster and visualized in rich tones that same time period.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Classic Novel of the Italian Aristocracy Returns in a Sumptuous New Edition', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delon, Alain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lampedusa, Giuseppe Tomasi di', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lancaster, Burt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Visconti, Luchino', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Leopard (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T17:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Royal Young', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Royal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Young', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f51291d-b45e-5309-be21-37b3dda55495', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f51291d-b45e-5309-be21-37b3dda55495'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s Dinagyang Festival in Iloilo City in the Philippines will include an exhibition of costumes from across the country.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/costumes-are-in-the-mix-at-philippine-festival/', 'snippet': 'This year’s Dinagyang Festival in Iloilo City in the Philippines will include an exhibition of costumes from across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dinagyang Festival draws an estimated crowd of a million people to the streets of Iloilo City in the Philippines each year, and organizers say they hope the addition of the Philippine Festival Costume Expo will bring even more attention to the event.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im