'Mohammad-Reza Rahimi, who was a first vice president under President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad, is believed to have been involved in insurance fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Signaling new efforts to halt what some officials have called out-of-control corruption, Iran’s judiciary announced this week that it had sentenced a former vice president to five years in jail and fined him the equivalent of $1 million after his recent conviction in a longstanding corruption case.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Iranian Official Gets Jail and $1 Million Fine in Corruption Case', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Corruption Case Snares Ex-Official', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rahimi, Mohammad-Reza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khamenei, Ali', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T17:32:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fac73c48-50ec-5128-b4fe-caa406793b30', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fac73c48-50ec-5128-b4fe-caa406793b30'}, {'abstract': 'Iran’s supreme leader released a letter and posted on Twitter after the attacks in Paris by militants who said they acted in the name of Islam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/world/middleeast/ayatollah-khamenei-appeals-to-western-youth-on-islam-and-prejudice.html', 'snippet': 'Iran’s supreme leader released a letter and posted on Twitter after the attacks in Paris by militants who said they acted in the name of Islam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — In a rare effort to reach out to the West, Iran’s supreme leader released a letter to youngsters in the United States and Europe imploring them to learn about Islam from original sources and not, as he said in a later posting on Twitter, have it “introduced to you by prejudices.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ayatollah Khamenei Appeals to Western Youth on Islam and Prejudice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iranian Ayatollah Beseeches Western Youth on Islam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khamenei, Ali', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T17:47:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a930aa99-2b68-50f8-a77a-91155ebd9960', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a930aa99-2b68-50f8-a77a-91155ebd9960'}, {'abstract': '“Rasheeda Speaking,” by the Chicago playwright Joel Drake Johnson, is a dark comedy about racism both covert and obvious, and stars Tonya Pinkins and Dianne Wiest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/theater/rasheeda-speaking-stars-tonya-pinkins-and-dianne-wiest.html', 'snippet': '“Rasheeda Speaking,” by the Chicago playwright Joel Drake Johnson, is a dark comedy about racism both covert and obvious, and stars Tonya Pinkins and Dianne Wiest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tonya Pinkins and Dianne Wiest sank into chairs at the back of the room after a recent rehearsal of the play “Rasheeda Speaking.” Ms. Pinkins sipped a mug of tea; Ms. Wiest wrapped herself in a gray cardigan. The antagonism of the last scene they’d worked lingered.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25RASHEEDA/25RASHEEDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25RASHEEDA/25RASHEEDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25RASHEEDA/25RASHEEDA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25RASHEEDA/25RASHEEDA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1427, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25RASHEEDA/25RASHEEDA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25RASHEEDA/25RASHEEDA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25RASHEEDA/25RASHEEDA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Racism Can’t Be Ignored', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Racism Can’t Be Ignored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Joel Drake', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiest, Dianne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinkins, Tonya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rasheeda Speaking (Play)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T17:47:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Soloski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soloski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69062784-47c8-5a69-b043-1e24109990f4', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69062784-47c8-5a69-b043-1e24109990f4'}, {'abstract': 'Halley Feiffer’s new play, “I’m Gonna Pray for You So Hard,” focuses on an actress and her better-known father, a situation she knows firsthand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/theater/a-provocative-play-connects-halley-feiffer-and-betty-gilpin.html', 'snippet': 'Halley Feiffer’s new play, “I’m Gonna Pray for You So Hard,” focuses on an actress and her better-known father, a situation she knows firsthand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Betty Gilpin and Halley Feiffer suspect they must have crossed paths as infants, lolling in some green room or other. The actor Reed Birney has told them he remembers them as little girls. Ms. Gilpin, 28, and Ms. Feiffer, 30, grew up belonging to the same hothouse subculture: the children of theater people. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25HALLEY2/25HALLEY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25HALLEY2/25HALLEY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25HALLEY2/25HALLEY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25HALLEY2/25HALLEY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1272, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25HALLEY2/25HALLEY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25HALLEY2/25HALLEY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25HALLEY2/25HALLEY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daughters in the Business', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Daughters in the Business', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feiffer, Halley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilpin, Betty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlantic Theater Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "I'm Gonna Pray for You So Hard (Play)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T17:49:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Collins-Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins-Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc7cc5f6-3086-5361-af81-8e6841d90407', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc7cc5f6-3086-5361-af81-8e6841d90407'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Ford, who rose to become the Democratic whip in the Senate, was best known for defending the tobacco industry and for pushing voter-registration laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/us/politics/wendell-h-ford-kentucky-governor-and-senator-dies-at-90.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Ford, who rose to become the Democratic whip in the Senate, was best known for defending the tobacco industry and for pushing voter-registration laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wendell H. Ford, a political moderate from Kentucky who served as governor and then for four terms as a senator, rising to become the Democratic whip, or assistant leader, in the early 1990s, died on Thursday at his home in Owensboro, Ky. He was 90.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/us/23FORD-obit/23FORD-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/23/