iots-bill-belichick-has-no-explanation-perhaps-tom-brady-will.html', 'snippet': 'Coach Bill Belichick and quarterback Tom Brady both said they were utterly baffled as to how the Patriots came into possession of 11 underinflated footballs for the A.F.C. championship game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOXBOROUGH, Mass. — The monosyllabic New England Patriots coach Bill Belichick and his polysyllabic quarterback Tom Brady claimed to be united in mysterious unknowing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nope. No Idea. Not Me. Next. ', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nope. No Idea. Not Me. Next.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T19:25:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68355827-8036-505e-b98a-42513bd4277b', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68355827-8036-505e-b98a-42513bd4277b'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of a show about the coed and girls’ teams our children have grown up with, Nickelodeon offers “Bella and the Bulldogs,” an ugly throwback to an era when girls who love sports are always odd girl out.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/a-new-nominee-for-worst-tween-sitcom-on-tv/', 'snippet': 'Instead of a show about the coed and girls’ teams our children have grown up with, Nickelodeon offers “Bella and the Bulldogs,” an ugly throwback to an era when girls who love sports are always odd girl out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last weekend, my daughter watched the first episode of Nickelodeon’s “Bella and the Bulldogs.” I was ranting two minutes after I walked into the room. Days later, the thought of it still infuriates me — and fills me with disbelief. In 1976, this would have been a reasonable plot to offer; even a clever take on changing gender expectations. In 2015, it’s an embarrassment to middle school students of both genders, imposing stereotypes more rigid and offensive than even the “Dukes of Hazzard” dreamed of.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/us/motherlode-girl-sports/motherlode-girl-sports-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/22/us/motherlode-girl-sports/motherlode-girl-sports-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/us/motherlode-girl-sports/motherlode-girl-sports-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/us/motherlode-girl-sports/motherlode-girl-sports-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 