hip in the light of the Hebdo tragedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a post last week on the debate around the Charlie Hebdo killings, I explained\xa0why I’m not convinced by the argument that Muslims are facing an unusual (phobic?) level of provocations toward their religion in the West, and why I think a consistent standard of self-censorship around religion\xa0that excluded cartoon treatments of Muhammed would require\xa0a radical change in the way that religion generally, but especially Christianity, is treated in contemporary culture. Now, as promised, I want to take up the question of other cases, particularly around racism and anti-Semitism, where our culture more explicitly self-censors, and where the argument I made immediately\xa0following the killings about speech and violence deserves a qualification. Here’s part of what I originally wrote:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Uses and Abuses of Taboos', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim Americans', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenwald, Glenn', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T20:20:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6376bf66-ece8-532b-8870-5c040cfa9df7', 'word_count': 1867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6376bf66-ece8-532b-8870-5c040cfa9df7'}, {'abstract': 'Three presidential contenders will appear on a panel moderated by Jonathan Karl of ABC News.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/01/22/rubio-cruz-and-paul-to-appear-at-koch-donor-event/', 'snippet': 'Three presidential contenders will appear on a panel moderated by Jonathan Karl of ABC News.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The annual donor event hosted by Charles and David Koch in California is among the most sought-after invitations in Republican politics — and one of the most difficult parties to crash. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rubio, Cruz and Paul to Appear at Koch Donor Event', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T20:21:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas',