otage available online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A prank call from Arnold Schwarzenegger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Footage Released From Romney Documentary', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T20:33:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0441467b-8b0d-5b82-b4e9-21579bf41182', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0441467b-8b0d-5b82-b4e9-21579bf41182'}, {'abstract': 'Performing artists are migrating from dance venues to the contemporary art world, and museums are welcoming the traffic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/arts/design/dance-finds-a-home-in-museums.html', 'snippet': 'Performing artists are migrating from dance venues to the contemporary art world, and museums are welcoming the traffic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Thursday evening at the New Museum in New York, the elevator door opened onto a fifth-floor gallery with a pole-dancing class in action. Some visitors looked confused and headed for the exit, but many more crowded around the edges of the floor watching the dance collaborators Brennan Gerard and Ryan Kelly learn strenuous and hypnotic moves — the kind more often practiced by strippers or teenage subway performers.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25PERFORMANCE1/25PERFORMANCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cr