ns', 'value': 'Walker Art Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MoMA PS1', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T20:41:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilarie M. Sheets', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af554551-26d4-5f69-a021-a4952faf4862', 'word_count': 1519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af554551-26d4-5f69-a021-a4952faf4862'}, {'abstract': 'With its unusual seating plan and variety of tempos, the Budapest Festival Orchestra added excitement to Mozart and Brahms standards at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/arts/music/budapest-festival-orchestra-plays-at-avery-fisher-hall.html', 'snippet': 'With its unusual seating plan and variety of tempos, the Budapest Festival Orchestra added excitement to Mozart and Brahms standards at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ivan Fischer and the Budapest Festival Orchestra stick to the repertoire when they come through New York. In that sense they are like any other ensemble, understandably eager to impress in the core of our music. But Mr. Fischer has a restless, inventive mind, and his players seem game for anything. So even in the ordinary, you can count on them for something extraordinary.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23BUDAPEST/BUDAPEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/2