 tricks culled from years of movie- and party-going.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Scott has made a career out of playing cool, self-deprecating men in television shows like the cult sitcom “Party Down” and the NBC comedy series “Parks and Recreation.” But as the Sundance Film Festival kicks off today in Park City, Utah, the real Adam Scott — a husband, father of two and as of late, film producer — is nervous. Though he’s a festival veteran, the stakes are especially high this year for the 41-year-old actor, who has two films debuting at Sundance: the romantic comedy “Sleeping With Other People,” in which he appears with Jason Sudekis and Alison Brie, and the in-competition comedy “The Overnight,” which he produced with his wife, and which he stars in alongside Taylor Schilling, Jason Schwartzman and Judith Godrèche. Scott took time out from his preparations to share with T his best tips for a successful Sundance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22scott-oloizia/22scott-oloizia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22scott-oloizia/22scott-oloizia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22scott-oloizia/22scott-oloizia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22scott-oloizia/22scott-oloizia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22scott-oloizia/22scott-oloizia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22scott-oloizia/22scott-oloizia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22scott-oloizia/22scott-oloizia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tips for Surviving the Sundance Film Festival, From Adam Scott of “Parks and Recreation”', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Adam (1973- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park City (Utah)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T21:45:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c0218cb-c9e1-5e8a-a55c-f1d0492877a5', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c0218cb-c9e1-5e8a-a55c-f1d0492877a5'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge’s ruling on Thursday reflects the fallout from an appeals court decision in December that narrowed the definition of what constitutes insider trading.