n Holler and Joanna Lumley.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/online-garage-jeff-koons-richard-phillips-miuccia-prada/', 'snippet': 'Other donors to the auction, organized by the hip Russian museum and magazine Garage, include Josephine Meckseper, James Franco, Carsten Holler and Joanna Lumley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leave it to the preternaturally hip Russian museum and magazine Garage to subvert that least glamorous of Sunday-afternoon routines: poking through garage sales. This Sunday, Garage will launch a digital sale (the proceeds of which will be split between CalArts and Garage Museum of Contemporary Art Education) that collects objects culled from the homes of 13 artists and creatives. According to the magazine’s editorial director, Michael Polsinelli, the concept was a natural fit for the organization. “It began as a simple editorial idea — we as readers always want better access to great creative contributors, and it’s pretty great access to know what’s collecting dust in their closets, attics and garages,” he says. “From our side, it’s also a neat callback to our roots: Garage — as a museum and subsequently a magazine – began in the famed bus garage designed by constructivist architect Konstantin Melnikov in Moscow.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22garage-symonds-2/22garage-symonds-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22garage-symonds-2/22garage-symonds-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/22/t-magazine/22garage-symonds-2/22garage-symonds-2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', '