graph': 'King Abdullah of Saudi Arabia, who came to the throne in old age and earned a reputation as a cautious reformer even as the Arab Spring revolts toppled heads of state and Islamic State militants threatened the Muslim establishment that he represented, died on Friday, according to a statement on state television. He was 90.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/23abdullah3/23abdullah3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/23/world/23abdullah3/23abdullah3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/23abdullah3/23abdullah3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/23abdullah3/23abdullah3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/23abdullah3/23abdullah3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/23/world/23abdullah3/23abdullah3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/23abdullah3/23abdullah3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'King Abdullah, a Shrewd Force Who Reshaped Saudi Arabia, Dies at 90', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'King Abdullah, Who Reshaped His Country Amid Arab Revolts, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Douglas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abdullah, King of Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T23:56:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin and Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dce7599-a572-5510-824c-5e3a9bfbf24b', 'word_count': 2150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dce7599-a572-5510-824c-5e3a9bfbf24b'}, {'abstract': 'In “Mortdecai,” Johnny Depp plays a rakish aristocrat who hopes to pay off an enormous tax debt by tracking down and selling a missing Goya painting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/movies/mortdecai-starring-johnny-depp.html', 'snippet': 'In “Mortdecai,” Johnny Depp plays a rakish aristocrat who hopes to pay off an enormous tax debt by tracking down and selling a missing Goya painting.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Mortdecai” might as well be called “The Johnny Depp Movie,” because its preening star, wearing an ascot and a walrus mustache that becomes a tiresome running joke, is the whole show. And what a frantically dull spectacle this vanity project is. “Mortdecai,” directed by David Koepp from a screenplay by Eric Aronson, would never have been made without Mr. Depp’s enthusiasm for the source material, the first of the 1970s trilogy of farcical novels by the British author Kyril Bonfiglioli, in the P. G. Wodehouse tradition of sophisticated silliness. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MORTDECAI-ALT/MORTDECAI-ALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MORTDECAI-ALT/MORTDECAI-ALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MORTDECAI-ALT/MORTDECAI-ALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MORTDECAI-ALT/MORTDECAI-ALT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MORTDECAI-ALT/23MORTDECAI-ALT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MORTDECAI-ALT/23MORTDECAI-ALT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/arts/23MORTDECAI-ALT/23MORTDECAI-ALT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Comes an Aristocrat, Mustache Flaring', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comes an Aristocrat, Mustache Flaring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koepp, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Depp, Johnny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paltrow, Gwyneth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettany, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mortdecai (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-22T23:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d136819-4c76-53c7-afba-c7691de1b0b2', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d136819-4c76-53c7-afba-c7691de1b0b2'}, {'abstract': 'A program has shown that mixing boys and girls together for discussions helps build empathy across the gender divide.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/22/in-egypt-sowing-the-seeds-of-gender-equality/', 'snippet': 'A program has shown that mixing boys and girls together for discussions helps build empathy across the gender divide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Sara was supposed to marry young. She was supposed to get a job teaching at the school a few minutes’ walk from her family’s apartment in Cairo so she’d always be close to home, safe from sexual harassment, keeping her reputation as a virtuous, Muslim woman intact.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opi