nces is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dance Listings for Jan. 23-29', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Dance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T00:45:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/da6cdb38-06f7-5850-9291-eb6b833e2f77', 'word_count': 1800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da6cdb38-06f7-5850-9291-eb6b833e2f77'}, {'abstract': 'A selected, critical guide to the visual arts in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/arts/design/museum-gallery-listings-for-jan-23-29.html', 'snippet': 'A selected, critical guide to the visual arts in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Museums and galleries are in Manhattan unless otherwise noted. Full reviews of recent art shows: nytimes.com/art. A searchable guide to these and many other art shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum & Gallery Listings for Jan. 23-29', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T00:47:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b9c2126-a542-52ab-8433-056b6bbe9950', 'word_count': 4897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b9c2126-a542-52ab-8433-056b6bbe9950'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama proposes to make community college free for two years for qualifying students. Education ideas that Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo endorsed include a tax credit for charitable contributions to public, charter and parochial schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/nyregion/disparate-education-plans-from-obama-and-cuomo.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama proposes to make community college free for two years for qualifying students. Education ideas that Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo endorsed include a tax credit for charitable contributions to public, charter and parochial schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since President Obama announced his proposal this month to make community college free for two years for qualifying students, arguments for and against the plan have been abundant. Some have assailed the initiative as futile, maintaining that federal Pell grants already cover the cost of community college for most poor and working-class students, and that the real obstacle comes not in tuition but in living expenses and the high price of textbooks. In actuality, tuition covered by the new subsidy would free up Pell grants to help alleviate those burdens.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25BIGSUB/25BIGSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25BIGSUB/25BIGSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25BIGSUB/25BIGSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': No