rt! Once again, the Ace Hotel and I will be gently waking up New York City with the Jan. 25 Sunday crossword, and we hope you can join us for trivia, coffee and crossword-solving fun. We invade, sorry, we start at 11 a.m. Sunday, January 25, in the beautifully appointed Ace lobby, located at 20 West 29th Street. See you there!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Measure of a Radio Band', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T03:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27efe33e-ef4a-56e5-9217-ccc9f643c9af', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27efe33e-ef4a-56e5-9217-ccc9f643c9af'}, {'abstract': 'The federal criminal complaint against Sheldon Silver reads like a political thriller, a lurid tale of abuse of power whose main character squeezed a tidy fortune out of lucrative legal niches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/nyregion/complaint-details-how-silver-earned-millions-from-obscure-legal-work.html', 'snippet': 'The federal criminal complaint against Sheldon Silver reads like a political thriller, a lurid tale of abuse of power whose main character squeezed a tidy fortune out of lucrative legal niches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — When federal prosecutors subpoenaed a law firm to learn what exactly Sheldon Silver, the powerful leader of the State Assembly, had done to earn the hundreds of thousands of dollars the firm paid him each year, prosecutors received just one file.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaint Details How Silver Earned Millions From Obscure Legal Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Complaint Paints Picture of a Politician Who Meticulously Hid an Abuse of Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T03:05:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc99d5e5-1a39-584c-8700-2f9255dc6203', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc99d5e5-1a39-584c-8700-2f9255dc6203'}, {'abstract': 'An outbreak of avian flu that began in two states has spread to seven since last week and has infected more than 140,000 birds, Nigeria’s agriculture minister was quoted as saying by Nigerian news media on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/world/africa/nigeria-a-bird-flu-outbreak-spreads.html', 'snippet': 'An outbreak of avian flu that began in two states has spread to seven since last week and has infected more than 140,000 birds, Nigeria’s agriculture minister was quoted as saying by Nigerian news media on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An outbreak of avian flu that began in two states has spread to seven since last week and has infected more than 140,000 birds, Nigeria’s agriculture minister was quoted as saying by Nigerian news media on Thursday. The minister, Akwinumi Adesina, sought to assure the public that the outbreak had not reached a crisis. “There is no cause for alarm,” he said, though at least one strain of the virus that causes the disease, H5N1, can infect humans. He also exhorted Nigerian consumers not to fear poultry consumption because the virus is spread only through contact between live birds and people who directly handle them, and the virus dies when cooked. “So, let Nigerians feel free to eat chicken and eggs,” Mr. Adesina was quoted as saying. Nigeria is Africa’s most populous country and leading poultry producer. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nigeria: A Bird Flu Outbreak Spreads', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nigeria: A Bird Flu Outbreak Spreads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T03:05:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/443ad145-b458-5239-88d0-5ec68d058422', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4