0 poor people through the HealthCare.gov marketplace instead of adding them to traditional Medicaid. The Republican-dominated Legislature has to reauthorize the program with a three-fourths vote every year, and a number of lawmakers, including some elected in November, oppose it. Mr. Hutchinson said he wanted to find a “compassionate, reasonable and cost-effective” way to provide health care for people currently benefiting from the private option. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arkansas: Governor Seeks to Continue an Alternative to Medicaid', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arkansas: Governor Seeks to Continue an Alternative to Medicaid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hutchinson, Asa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T03:42:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4f93b17-cce1-5858-9b4a-7b4da2adbd24', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4f93b17-cce1-5858-9b4a-7b4da2adbd24'}, {'abstract': 'McSorley’s Old Ale House, which opened in 1854, admitted Ms. Shaum as its first female patron, in 1970, after New York City barred discrimination against women in public places.', 'web_u