, 'word_count': 561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a1b1ef3-7a39-5d9d-be50-d800a864bc82'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a rare rupture in the image-conscious world of Broadway and another bump in the road for a highly anticipated musical.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/after-dispute-harvey-weinstein-parts-ways-with-the-press-agent-for-finding-neverland/', 'snippet': 'It’s a rare rupture in the image-conscious world of Broadway and another bump in the road for a highly anticipated musical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The film producer Harvey Weinstein and the veteran Broadway press agent Rick Miramontez have parted ways on Mr. Weinstein’s forthcoming musical “Finding Neverland” after sharp words were said at their weekly planning meeting on Tuesday — a rare rupture in the image-conscious world of Broadway and another bump in the road for a highly anticipated musical.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weinstein Parts Ways With Press Agent for ‘Finding Neverland’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grammer, Kelsey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miramontez, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morrison, Matthew (1978- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulus, Diane', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudin, Scott', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN REPERTORY THEATER', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambridge (NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T05:33:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4db1bb68-eb4c-5ab3-93b8-3ddb75c8ade5', 'word_count': 1281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4db1bb68-eb4c-5ab3-93b8-3ddb75c8ade5'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/arts/television/whats-on-tv-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:30 P.M. (FX Movie Channel) THE GIRL WITH THE DRAGON TATTOO (2011) Daniel Craig stars as a crusading Swedish journalist hired by a wealthy industrialist (Christopher Plummer) to investigate the disappearance of his niece 40 years earlier in this adaptation of the Stieg Larsson novel, directed by David Fincher. Rooney Mara, in an Oscar-nominated performance, is Lisbeth Salander, the vulnerable yet ruthlessly competent computer hacker who helps him solve the mystery. “She is a marvelous pop-culture character, stranger and more complex than the average superhero and more intriguing than the usual boy wizards and vampire brides,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times about Lisbeth, first played by Noomi Rapace in the 2010 Swedish adaptation. “It has been her fate, unfortunately, to make her furious, uninspiring way through a series of plodding and ungainly stories.” And “despite the slick intensity of Mr. Fincher’s style, his movie is not immune to the same lumbering proceduralism,” Mr. Scott said, while acknowledging that “Mr. Fincher’s impressive skill is evident.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T06:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ef6512e-a8c1-5623-926c-fb96a1109b61', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ef6512e-a8c1-5623-926c-fb96a1109b61'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Friday, January 23, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/pageoneplus/corrections-january-23-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Friday, January 23, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 23, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T06:52:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15efab41-cff7-5969-8a66-77a8ec1d3c57', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15efab41-cff7-5969-8a66-77a8ec1d3c57'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, January 23, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, January 23, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“For many years, New Yorkers have asked the question: How could Speaker Silver, one of the most powerful men in all of New York, earn millions of dollars in outside income without deeply compromising his ability to honestly serve his constituents? Today, we provide the answer: He didn’t.”', 'print_section': 'A', '