-view-of-new-york-city/', 'snippet': 'Diego Acosta López wanted to document New York from his son’s perspective: inside a stroller. Thousands of pictures (including little feet and hands) ensued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot has been said about embracing a child’s view of photography. That a child’s vision is innocent. That it is naïve. That above all, it is pure, unburdened by the rules of cynical grown-ups. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Toddler’s View of New York City', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A View From the Bugaboo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Carriages, Strollers and Carriers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'School of Visual Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quito (Ecuador)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ef9a27d-96de-56c3-9753-b5a0b9cb8aea', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ef9a27d-96de-56c3-9753-b5a0b9cb8aea'}, {'abstract': 'Should students have a right to higher education, the way they now have a right to elementary and secondary education?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/should-a-college-education-be-free/', 'snippet': 'Should students have a right to higher education, the way they now have a right to elementary and secondary education?', 'lead_paragraph': 'States offer children a free public school education until they complete 12th grade. After that, they have to pay tuition. President Obama recently announced his proposal to make community college free for many students. Is he onto something? Should students be able to get a free education after high school? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should a College Education Be Free?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T10:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e72148f-c6be-5711-85ef-d84ffc1ae941', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e72148f-c6be-5711-85ef-d84ffc1ae941'}, {'abstract': 'The company said it would delay a quarterly earnings report as a result of disruptions to the computer network at its American film studio, Sony Pictures Entertainment.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/sony-postpones-earnings-announcement-blaming-hacking-attacks/', 'snippet': 'The company said it would delay a quarterly earnings report as a result of disruptions to the computer network at its American film studio, Sony Pictures Entertainment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Sony said Friday that it would delay the report of its earnings for the quarter ended Dec. 31 as a result of the hacking attacks on its American film studio, Sony Pictures Entertainment.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'ca