e': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9a7a1ec-5994-5c09-a281-78dc8deb0213', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9a7a1ec-5994-5c09-a281-78dc8deb0213'}, {'abstract': 'In “Timbuktu,” the filmmaker Abderrahmane Sissako casts the extremists who impose Muslim law on a desert city as contradictory buffoons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/movies/abderrahmane-sissako-on-the-jihadists-in-timbuktu.html', 'snippet': 'In “Timbuktu,” the filmmaker Abderrahmane Sissako casts the extremists who impose Muslim law on a desert city as contradictory buffoons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To mock Adolf Hitler, Charlie Chaplin created Adenoid Hynkel, who sputtered gibberish and danced with a balloon in “The Great Dictator.” Woody Allen lampooned American relations with Cuba in “Bananas” by donning a glue-on beard and impersonating a fulminating Fidel Castro. Skewering Muammar el-Qaddafi in “The Dictator,” Sacha Baron Cohen wore a “Love Boat” cap and wandered cluelessly around Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25TIMBUKTU1/25TIMBUKTU1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25TIMBUKTU1/25TIMBUKTU1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25TIMBUKTU1/25TIMBUKTU1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/arts/25TIMBUKTU1/25TIMBUKTU1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name