e legend. Coincidentally, at the men’s fall/winter shows in Paris, tattered knits of the sort Cobain might have worn have surfaced on the runways. Raf Simons, whose collections always reflect on the rough-and-tumble energies of youth and music, presented a series of looks with pieces in various states of deterioration. There were floor-length vests with frayed edges, coats with ragged hems, trenches with their linings spilling out of the sleeves and the hole-ridden sweater vest seen above. Unraveling ribbed sweaters at Damir Doma were a nice contrast to the tailored suits and pleated high-waisted trousers in the collection. And Yohji Yamamoto showed a Frankenstein of a jumper — two different knits ripped and haphazardly sewn together down the front.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/t-magazine/23trend-ruined-tudela/23trend-ruined-tudela-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/23/t-magazine/23trend-ruined-tudela/23trend-ruined-tudela-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/t-magazine/23trend-ruined-tudela/23trend-ruined-tudela-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/t-magazine/23trend-ruined-tudela/23trend-ruined-tudela-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/t-magazine/23trend-ruined-tudela/23trend-ruined-tudela-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/23/t-magazine/23trend-ruined-tudela/23trend-ruined-tudela-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/t-magazine/23trend-ruined-tudela/23trend-ruined-tudela-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Paris Men’s Fall 2015 Runways, an Appetite for Destruction', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knitting and Knit Goods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cobain, Kurt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simons, Raf', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yamamoto, Yohji', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T14:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd6aa62-2f13-5eeb-baec-753626fdf7a5', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd6aa62-2f13-5eeb-baec-753626fdf7a5'}, {'abstract': 'In the lush, primal jungles of the northern part of the country, where thoughts turn to orchids, not juntas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/travel/in-far-flung-myanmar-a-land-of-contradictions.html', 'snippet': 'In the lush, primal jungles of the northern part of the country, where thoughts turn to orchids, not juntas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is strange how some of the world’s most retrograde authoritarian states end up being such inadvertent conservators of both their country’s architectural heritage and vast tracts of wild, unspoiled nature. Of course, it was not their leaders’ intention to distinguish themselves as environmentalists or conservationists, but by so abjectly failing to develop viable economic engines, they nonetheless had this providential effect.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/travel/25MYANMAR/25MYANMAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/travel/25MYANMAR/25MYANMAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/travel/25MYANMAR/25MYANMAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/travel/25MYANMAR/25MYANMAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/travel/25MYANMAR/25MYANMAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/travel/25MYANMAR/25MYANMAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima