 'Adding feta cheese to a saltwater brine adds punch to a simple roast chicken. (Article plus video.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brining a chicken before roasting it is an age-old technique. An overnight soak in brine seasons the bird through and through, and locks in moisture for tender flesh. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Issue That Feta Can Solve ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feta Adds Punch to Brine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T15:22:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccea0777-326f-5ce4-a534-1e1fe6a6af7c', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccea0777-326f-5ce4-a534-1e1fe6a6af7c'}, {'abstract': 'The more people invest in a market, the more they police it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/magazine/risk-factor.html', 'snippet': 'The more people invest in a market, the more they police it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the N.B.A. commissioner Adam Silver announced in November that he was in favor of legalizing sports betting in the United States, he shattered decades of genteel sporting tradition. For generations, major professional sports leagues in America have done their best to pretend sports gambling does not exist. But, as Silver wrote in an opinion column in The Times, illegal gambling is already everywhere. Urging legislators to contend with the reality that information technology has made it impossible to confine sports betting to Nevada, Silver argued for taking the market, worth an estimated $400 billion a year, into the realm of the licit.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25economy/25mag-25economy.t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25economy/25mag-25economy.t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25economy/25mag-25economy.t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25economy/25mag-25economy.t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1486, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25economy/25mag-25economy.t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25economy/25mag-25economy.t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25economy/25mag-25economy.t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case for Legalized Gambling on Sports', 'kicker': 'It’s the Economy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Risk Factor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGugan, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Adam (1962- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donaghy, Tim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T15:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Mcgugan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mcgugan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0526246-839f-5433-a8e5-d5c1fda3dda3', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0526246-839f-5433-a8e5-d5c1fda3dda3'}, {'abstract': 'Benoît Cœuré, a member of the central bank’s executive board, responded to criticism that the bond-buying plan came too late for the eurozone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/business/international/ecb-quantitative-easing-stimulus.html', 'snippet': 'Benoît Cœuré, a member of the central bank’s executive board, responded to criticism that the bond-buying plan came too late for the eurozone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — A top official with the European Central Bank on Friday defended its long-awaited economic stimulus program, saying it would be more effective than critics say because it coincides with other favorable developments, like the plunge in oil prices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coeuré of E.C.B. Says ‘Stars Are Aligned’ for Stimulus Measures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T15:24:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e488fc5d-4dc0-529a-8dea-3ed8fc8fe7f9', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e488fc5d-4dc0-529a-8dea-3ed8fc8fe7f9'}, {'abstract': 'A dig at an ancient tomb in Greece and a possible link to Alexander the Great have captured the nation’s imagination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/arts/design/alexander-the-greats-legacy-stirred-up-by-excavation.html', 'snippet': 'A dig at an ancient tomb in Greece and a possible link to Alexander the Great have captured the nation’s imagination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Call it “CSI: Alexander.” For months, the excavations at a large ancient tomb in northern Greece have gripped the country. First, a marble slab wall was unearthed. Then, through announcements and leaks from the Greek Culture Ministry meted out with the pacing of a good mystery series, headless sphinxes and other statues were found. Finally, bones! But whose? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/arts/24alexander-1/24alexander-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/24/arts/24alexander-1/24alexander-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/arts/24alexander-1/24alexander-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/arts/24alexander-1/24alexander-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/arts/24alexander-1/24alexander-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/24/arts/24alexander-1/24alexander-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/arts/24alexander-1/24alexander-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whose Tomb? Greece Wonders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whose Tomb? Greece Wonders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donadio, Rachel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3,