ue': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schultz, Debbie Wasserman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic National Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cleveland (Ohio)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Columbus (Ohio)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T17:29:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63ef5ab1-c131-5ea7-a0c3-da55512434c3', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63ef5ab1-c131-5ea7-a0c3-da55512434c3'}, {'abstract': 'Tony Schwartz, in the Life@Work column, asks the wealthiest: Are you comfortable having more than you will ever spend, while those around you barely earn what they need to survive?', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/privilege-is-a-privilege-and-a-responsibility/', 'snippet': 'Tony Schwartz, in the Life@Work column, asks the wealthiest: Are you comfortable having more than you will ever spend, while those around you barely earn what they need to survive?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks ago, I walked into a local delicatessen to get a sandwich for lunch. The man behind the counter looked to be in his early 30s, and we struck up a conversation. I asked how he was feeling about the upcoming year, and the one that just passed. It’s amazing what people will tell you if they sense you are genuinely interested. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/dbpix-minimumwage/dbpix-minimumwage-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/24/business/dbpix-minimumwage/dbpix-minimumwage-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/dbpix-minimumwage/dbpix-minimumwage-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/dbpix-minimumwage/dbpix-minimumwage-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/dbpix-minimumwage/dbpix-minimumwage-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/24/business/dbpix-minimumwage/dbpix-minimumwage-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/dbpix-minimumwage/dbpix-minimumwage-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Privilege Is a Privilege, and a Responsibility', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keltner, Dacher', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tirado, Linda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T17:31:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b05e017-b35b-5efc-a8ba-761494c2b8a2', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b05e017-b35b-5efc-a8ba-761494c2b8a2'}, {'abstract': 'Mourning her father’s death, the author undertakes a pilgrimage to Japan’s great Buddhist temples.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/books/review/where-the-dead-pause-and-the-japanese-say-goodbye-by-marie-mutsuki-mockett.html', 'snippet': 'Mourning her father’s death, the author undertakes a pilgrimage to Japan’s great Buddhist temples.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the many shocking things about tsunamis — along with their suddenness, violence and indiscriminate destruction of life and community — is how little there is to say about them. Man-made catastrophes, like wars or nuclear accidents, provide infinite opportunities for blame, recrimination and lessons learned. But natural disasters have no politics. One can quibble about the height of sea walls, the promptness of warnings and the quality of aid given to survivors. But such events have always occurred in countries like Japan, and always will. When the wave has receded, the dead have been counted and the slow work of recovery has begun, the pundits sheepishly quit the field and abandon it to the theologians, the spiritualists and the priests.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25PARRY/0125-bks-PARRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25PARRY/0125-bks-PARRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25PARRY/0125-bks-PARRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25PARRY/0125-bks-PARRY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2040, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25PARRY/0125-bks-PARRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25PARRY/0125-bks-PARRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25PARRY/0125-bks-PARRY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Where the Dead Pause, and the Japanese Say Goodbye,’ by Marie Mutsuki Mockett', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spiritual Journey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parry, Richard Lloyd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mockett, Marie Mutsuki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T17:31:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Lloyd Parry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'Lloyd', 'lastname': 'Parry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/42e772ba-1a77-5a24-8761-2abddd4b9774', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42e772ba-1a77-5a24-8761-2abddd4b9774'}, {'abstract': 'Marina Warner explores the history and enduring power of fairy tales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/books/review/once-upon-a-time-by-marina-warner.html', 'snippet': 'Marina Warner explores the history and enduring power of fairy tales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her new and vigorous book on fairy tales, “Once Upon a Time,” the scholar Marina Warner explains a crucial stage of story pollination. Discussing early versions of “Puss in Boots” and “Rapunzel,” written by the Italians Straparola and Basile, she notes,“It’s no accident that these two authors created their story cycles in great seaports, where cultures, languages and ideas — and above all travelers — met one another.” ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25bender/25bender-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25bender/25bender-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 802}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25bender/25bender-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25bender/25bender-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1725, 'width': 1291, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25bender/25bender-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25bender/25bender-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/books/review/25bender/25bender-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Once Upon a Time,’ by Marina Warner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Casting Spells', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fairy Tales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warner, Marina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T17:32:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aimee Bender', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aimee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bender', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5ab2bd6-ffd0-545f-9535-b3b3694de4d0', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5ab2bd6-ffd0-545f-9535-b3b3694de4d0'}, {'abstract': 'An Armenian-American moves to Turkey to investigate a history of tense relations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/books/review/there-was-and-there-was-not-by-meline-toumani.html', 'snippet': 'An Armenian-American moves to Turkey to investigate a history of tense relations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2005, Meline Toumani, an Armenian-American, went to live in Turkey — the country that, in its former incarnation as the Ottoman Empire, killed more than one million Armenians beginning in 1915, in mass deportations most historians regard as genocide. Fellow Armenians considered her decision perverse, not least because she, like them, had imbibed stories of Turkish plunder and murder along with her mother’s milk. But Toumani is an idealistic, somewhat contrary soul. Although in no doubt of Turkish culpability, she was convinced of the need for reconciliation on a basic, human level. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘There Was and There Was Not,’ by Meline Toumani', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ties That Blind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toumani, Meline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T17:32:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher De Bellaigue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'De Bellaigue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9270861f-25a5-5c6d-9762-3486e88e7b1e', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9270861f-25a5-5c6d-9762-3486e88e7b1e'}, {'abstract': 'The in-flight catalog’s parent, Xhibit, attributed some of its troubles to changes in in-flight entertainment and retail competition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/business/skymall-parent-xhibit-files-for-bankruptcy-protection.html', 'snippet': 'The in-flight catalog’s parent, Xhibit, attributed some of its troubles to changes in in-flight entertainment and retail competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The parent of the in-flight shopping magazine SkyMall said on Friday that it had filed for bankruptcy protection, citing in-flight Wi-Fi access as one of the factors luring shoppers away from its quirky catalog of travel products, pet toys and garden gnomes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/24skymall-web/24skymall-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/24/business/24skymall-web/24skymall-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/24skymall-web/24skymall-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/24skymall-web/24skymall-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/24skymall-web/24skymall-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/24/business/24skymall-web/24skymall-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/24skymall-web/24skymall-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'SkyMall’s Parent Files for Bankruptcy Protection', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SkyMall’s Parent Files for Bankruptcy Protection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skymall Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T17:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6d448c3-f4ac-521e-a589-a1b6d5b3afad', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6d448c3-f4ac-521e-a589-a1b6d5b3afad'}, {'abstract': 'The life of a suffragist daughter of an exiled maharajah.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/books/review/sophia-princess-suffragette-revolutionary-by-anita-anand.html', 'snippet': 'The life of a suffragist daughter of an exiled maharajah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Part of a biographer’s job is to rescue forgotten figures, and in “Sophia: Princess, Suffragette, Revolutionary” Anita Anand has salvaged an extraordinary one. Sophia Duleep Singh was a Punjabi princess and Queen Victoria’s goddaughter, a bucktoothed “docile little thing” who went on to become a celebrated London fashion plate and then a steely suffragist.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm