ct': 'Times critics review “Black Sea,” “Cake” and “Mommy.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/video-reviews-of-black-sea-cake-and-mommy/', 'snippet': 'Times critics review “Black Sea,” “Cake” and “Mommy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s video, Times critics share their thoughts on “Black Sea,” “Cake” and “Mommy.” See all of this week’s reviews.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Reviews of ‘Black Sea,’ ‘Cake’ and ‘Mommy’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T17:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e03a5328-f869-589b-a086-90d114dd15a8', 'word_count': 21, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e03a5328-f869-589b-a086-90d114dd15a8'}, {'abstract': 'Today, Richard Hofstadter, who wrote “The Paranoid Style in American Politics,” might target not just right-wing radio hosts but also the aggrieved left.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/books/review/somebodys-watching-us.html', 'snippet': 'Today, Richard Hofstadter, who wrote “The Paranoid Style in American Politics,” might target not just right-wing radio hosts but also the aggrieved left.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About fifty years ago, the Pulitzer Prize-winning historian Richard Hofstadter exposed a dark recess of the American psyche with an essay in Harper’s Magazine, “The Paranoid Style in American Politics.” Hofstadter was writing about the peculiar tendency of the political right to indulge in paranoid theories, but he was careful to stipulate that the left could just as easily be infected. “American politics has often been an arena for angry minds,” he wrote.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/books/review/LOWENSTEIN/LOWENSTEIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 854, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/10/books/review/LOWENSTEIN/LOWENSTEIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 854}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/books/review/LOWENSTEIN/LOWENSTEIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/books/review/LOWENSTEIN/LOWENSTEIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/books/review/LOWENSTEIN/LOWENSTEIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/10/books/review/LOWENSTEIN/LOWENSTEIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/10/books/review/LOWENSTEIN/LOWENSTEIN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Somebody’s Watching Us', 'kicker': "Critic's Take", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Somebody’s Watching Us', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowenstein, Roger', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hofstadter, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-23T17:37:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Lowenstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fe8f515-ed4b-557a-a18e-4fea9c179e06', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fe8f515-ed4b-557a-a18e-4fea9c179e06'}, {'abstract': 'In this first novel, a young congressional aide navigates a minefield of graft and corruption in present-day China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/books/review/casey-walkers-last-days-in-shanghai.html', 'snippet': 'In this first novel, a young congressional aide navigates a minefield of graft and corruption in present-day China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the lobby of an apartment building in the Chinese factory city of Dongguan, I once saw this sign: “for the peace of residents, renovation will stop on jan. 1. it will resume on jan. 2.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/25CHANG/25chang-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/25CHANG/25chang-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 626}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/books/review/25CHANG/25chang-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 752, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '