 'nyt://article/78edcacb-3f56-547f-9491-2b1e2eeb08bc', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78edcacb-3f56-547f-9491-2b1e2eeb08bc'}, {'abstract': 'The ‘black-ish’ star on how the Internet built a community around natural hair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/23/magazine/tracee-ellis-ross-is-big-on-big-hair.html', 'snippet': 'The ‘black-ish’ star on how the Internet built a community around natural hair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this month, I interviewed the actress Tracee Ellis Ross about her role on “Black-ish” (her new hit show on ABC), her playful presence on social media and her childhood as a daughter of the legendary singer Diana Ross. You can read an excerpt from our conversation in this week’s Talk column. Throughout the hourlong phone call, however, we kept drifting back to one subject: Ross’s trademark curly cloud of hair and the way Instagram and Pinterest have contributed to the expansion of mainstream beauty standards online and in Hollywood. Much of that discussion didn’t make it into the print version of the interview, but it felt worth sharing — and worth adding to. Jenna Wortham', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/magazine/23mag-23natural/23mag-23natural-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 296, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/23/magazine/23mag-23natural/23mag-23natural-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 296}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/magazine/23mag-23natural/23mag-23natural-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/magazine/23mag-23natural/23mag-23natural-superJumbo.jpg', 'height