suburb-killing-dozens.html', 'snippet': 'The government attack targeted an insurgent-held area, as Lebanon’s army fought militants near the border.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — A Syrian government airstrike on Friday hit a market square in an insurgent-held suburb of Damascus, the capital, killing several dozen people, antigovernment activists in the area said, while five Lebanese soldiers were killed in clashes with militants who crisscross the Syrian border, in one of the worst recent cases of spillover violence.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Airstrike Hits Damascus Suburb, Killing Dozens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Government Airstrike Kills Dozens Near Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Damascus (Syria)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T00:48:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d750389b-7c20-573b-a81f-d7826657b614', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d750389b-7c20-573b-a81f-d7826657b614'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo says New York’s education system “needs dramatic reform.” How bad is New York, really? Relative to others states, experts say, not that bad. But not that good, either.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/nyregion/are-new-york-schools-in-crisis-as-cuomo-asserts-not-quite-experts-say.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo says New York’s education system “needs dramatic reform.” How bad is New York, really? Relative to others states, experts say, not that bad. But not that good, either.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, in his State of the State address this week, exhorted lawmakers to make significant changes to New York State’s education system. He painted a picture of a system in crisis: only a third of students reaching proficiency on state math and English tests, less than 40 percent of high school students prepared for college, hundreds of thousands of mostly minority students condemned to failing schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Cites School Crisis in New York; Data Suggest Otherwise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Cites School Crisis; Data Suggest Otherwise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Assessment of Educational Progress', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T00:52:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/784881d5-e071-5579-afe0-89b61e21439f', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/784881d5-e071-5579-afe0-89b61e21439f'}, {'abstract': 'Ariane Duarte, the chef of Ariane Kitchen & Bar, in Verona, said she opened a less expensive place because she wanted “to make a burger” and “have fun.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/nyregion/a-review-of-ariane-kitchen-bar-in-verona.html', 'snippet': 'Ariane Duarte, the chef of Ariane Kitchen & Bar, in Verona, said she opened a less expensive place because she wanted “to make a burger” and “have fun.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A meal at Ariane Kitchen & Bar begins with croissants. They are everything croissants should be: buttery and flaky; their ends just the slightest bit crisp. But they are small, and shouldn’t stop you from enjoying the rest of the meal, you think, as you reach for a second one.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINENJ2/25DINENJ2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINENJ2/25DINENJ2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINENJ2/25DINENJ2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINENJ2/25DINENJ2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINENJ2/25DINENJ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': '