zation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d1ef092-406b-5df3-84a2-3f14bec10931', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d1ef092-406b-5df3-84a2-3f14bec10931'}, {'abstract': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Friday approved a set of mobile applications that allow people with diabetes to share information with doctors using an iPhone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/us/mobile-monitoring-of-blood-glucose-is-approved.html', 'snippet': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Friday approved a set of mobile applications that allow people with diabetes to share information with doctors using an iPhone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Friday approved a set of mobile medical applications that allow people with diabetes to share information about the level of glucose in their blood with doctors in real time using an iPhone. Such apps have existed but were not in broad use, in part because they had not met regulatory requirements.\xa0Dr. K. M. Venkat Narayan, professor of medicine and epidemiology at Emory University, said that the apps would be useful for certain patients, for example those with extreme fluctuations in glucose levels, but would not fundamentally change diabetes monitoring. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mobile Monitoring of Blood Glucose Is Approved ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mobile Monitoring of Blood Glucose Is Approved', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T01:34:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8fc7b4f-8846-5284-9f56-5f06ffecf0e2', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8fc7b4f-8846-5284-9f56-5f06ffecf0e2'}, {'abstract': 'A group of Egyptian archaeologists said that they planned to file charges against officials at the state-run Egyptian Museum in Cairo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/world/middleeast/archaeologists-want-egyptian-officials-charged-for-damage-to-tutankhamens-burial-mask.html', 'snippet': 'A group of Egyptian archaeologists said that they planned to file charges against officials at the state-run Egyptian Museum in Cairo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Outraged over what appears to be serious damage to one of Egypt’s ancient treasures — scratches and a layer of glue on the golden burial mask of Tutankhamen — a group of Egyptian archaeologists said on Friday that they planned to file charges against officials at the state-run Egyptian Museum in Cairo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/middleeast/23open_tut/23open_tut-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/23/world/middleeast/23open_tut/23open_tut-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 550}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/middleeast/23open_tut/23open_tut-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 939, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/middleeast/23open_tut/23open_tut-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/middleeast/23open_tut/23open_tut-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/23/world/middleeast/23open_tut/23open_tut-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/23/world/middleeast/23open_tut/23open_tut-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Archaeologists Want Egyptian Officials Charged for Damage to Tutankhamen’s Burial Mask', 'kicker': 'Open Source', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Egyptian Civilization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Egyptian Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tutankhamen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanna, Monica', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T01:39:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e80f54e-fd36-5159-a86d-b6a47bb08e18', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e80f54e-fd36-5159-a86d-b6a47bb08e18'}, {'abstract': 'Hopscotch, in Croton-on-Hudson, not for the timid, spoils its patrons with personal touches and fancy footwork in the kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/nyregion/a-review-of-hopscotch-in-croton-on-hudson.html', 'snippet': 'Hopscotch, in Croton-on-Hudson, not for the timid, spoils its patrons with personal touches and fancy footwork in the kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a winter’s night at the four-month-old Hopscotch in Croton-on-Hudson, I asked our waiter to tell me about the quenelle-shaped oval that adorned a dish called oxtail strudel. He blushed a bit and backed up in the direction of the kitchen, saying, “I just need to check my notes.” That the waiters at Hopscotch — who are very quick and personable — rely on crib sheets says a lot about the complexity of the dishes with which Kenyon Hart, the chef de cuisine, is spoiling patrons. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINEWE2/25DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINEWE2/25DINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINEWE2/25DINEWE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINEWE2/25DINEWE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINEWE2/25DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbna