: 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9c3f778-e682-5ecc-9240-89b877cfb7f4', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9c3f778-e682-5ecc-9240-89b877cfb7f4'}, {'abstract': 'Teinei Ya, a Japanese restaurant in Little Neck, Queens, that opened last May, more than holds its own in a neighborhood rife with cheap and interesting international food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/nyregion/a-review-of-teinei-ya-in-little-neck-queens.html', 'snippet': 'Teinei Ya, a Japanese restaurant in Little Neck, Queens, that opened last May, more than holds its own in a neighborhood rife with cheap and interesting international food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To enjoy Teinei Ya (pronounced TAY-nay YA), a Japanese restaurant in Little Neck that opened last May, you have to like your food served with a rather large dollop of kitsch. Diners who can get past this — or better yet, learn to embrace it — are in for a culinary treat. On a stretch of Northern Boulevard on the Queens side of the Nassau County border in a neighborhood that is rife with cheap and interesting international food, this is a restaurant that holds its own, and then some. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINELI2/25DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINELI2/25DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINELI2/25DINELI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/nyregion/25DINELI2/25DINELI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'he