s-spains-leader-knew-of-slush-fund.html', 'snippet': 'The former treasurer at the heart of a slush-fund scandal has accused Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy of knowing “from the beginning” about the party’s illegal payments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — The former treasurer at the heart of a slush-fund scandal that has undermined Spain’s governing Popular Party accused Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy on Friday of knowing “from the beginning” about the party’s illegal payments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Party Official Says Spain’s Leader Knew of Slush Fund', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spain: New Accusation Rekindles Slush-Fund Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajoy, Mariano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barcenas, Luis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Popular Party (Spain)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T02:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70b3696f-edb0-55e5-b0f9-e1e588b2eb83', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70b3696f-edb0-55e5-b0f9-e1e588b2eb83'}, {'abstract': 'The speech was the first offered by Jeb Bush since he announced he was actively exploring a run for the presidency, and it focused on traditional conservative positions and avoided specifics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/us/politics/jeb-bush-backs-pipeline-in-speech-to-auto-dealers.html', 'snippet': 'The speech was the first offered by Jeb Bush since he announced he was actively exploring a run for the presidency, and it focused on traditional conservative positions and avoided specifics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — In a sweeping speech that leaned heavily on economic policy, former Gov. Jeb Bush of Florida on Friday described immigrants as the “engine of economic vitality” before calling for a more welcoming immigration policy that could put him at odds with some in the more conservative wing of his party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/us/24BUSH/24BUSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/24/us/24BUSH/24BUSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/us/24BUSH/24BUSH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/us/24BUSH/24BUSH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/us/24BUSH/24BUSH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/24/us/24BUSH/24BUSH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/us/24BUSH/24BUSH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeb Bush Sounds Sympathetic Note for Immigrants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jeb Bush Sounds Sympathetic Note for Immigrants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corasaniti, Nick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Automobile Dealers Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T02:03:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84624a86-c21c-5bf2-8189-cea45963bdb4', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84624a86-c21c-5bf2-8189-cea45963bdb4'}, {'abstract': 'With its kitsch appeal, SkyMall became a kind of cultural reference point, a one-word inside joke that everyone could share.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/business/it-all-seemed-so-cool-at-six-miles-high.html', 'snippet': 'With its kitsch appeal, SkyMall became a kind of cultural reference point, a one-word inside joke that everyone could share.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, it was something of a ritual. You had made it through airport security, survived the lengthy delays and even crammed your carry-on into an overhead bin. Then you could settle in, buckle up and reach into the seat-back pocket in front of you. There, pressed up against the motion-sickness bag or the laminated emergency instruction card, you would find the latest edition of SkyMall.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/skymall/skymall-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/24/business/skymall/skymall-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 670}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/skymall/skymall-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/skymall/skymall-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/skymall/skymall-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/24/business/skymall/skymall-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/business/skymall/skymall-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For SkyMall, It All Seemed So Cool at Six Miles High', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It All Seemed So Cool at Six Miles High', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skymall Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xhibit Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T02:04:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Mahler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a8329c7-60ac-5ce1-9f19-6015c5590f79', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a8329c7-60ac-5ce1-9f19-6015c5590f79'}, {'abstract': 'The “Deflategate” inquiry involving the Patriots is a reminder that athletes in almost every pursuit cheat or practice its fraternal twin, gamesmanship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/sports/football/the-patriots-scandal-and-sports-ethics-deflated-balls.html', 'snippet': 'The “Deflategate” inquiry involving the Patriots is a reminder that athletes in almost every pursuit cheat or practice its fraternal twin, gamesmanship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the years, Derek Jeter developed a tic at the plate that gave him an advantage. Or was it a trick? Whenever a pitch darted inside, Jeter bent over, stuck out his backside, held back his bat, and watched as the ball went by. It was his way of signaling to the umpire that the pitch was a ball, and often he got the call.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/spor