a-way-some-say-is-misguided.html', 'snippet': 'To show, as she put it, “there is a price to Jewish blood,” Nitsana Darshan-Leitner sues nations, terrorist organizations and others that have harmed Israelis — angering some on the left in Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — She is a crusading lawyer who serially sues rogue nations, terror groups and international banks to show, as she put it, “there is a price to Jewish blood.” She is a mother of six who, while seven months pregnant with triplets, astonished an Israeli court with a motion requesting that a hearing be moved to her home. (It was denied.).', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/world/24PROFILE/24PROFILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/24/world/24PROFILE/24PROFILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/world/24PROFILE/24PROFILE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/world/24PROFILE/24PROFILE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/world/24PROFILE/24PROFILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/24/world/24PROFILE/24PROFILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/world/24PROFILE/24PROFILE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crusading for Israel in a Way Some Say Is Misguided ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crusading for Israel in a Way Some Say Is Misguided', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Darshan-Leitner, Nitsana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T02:50:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Biography', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2689a6e-98a1-5a68-a457-5f7a17628e0a', 'word_count': 1359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2689a6e-98a1-5a68-a457-5f7a17628e0a'}, {'abstract': 'The only surprise in the rise of the left-wing Syriza party is that it has taken so long for an anti-austerity party to come to the fore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/opinion/the-greeks-head-to-the-polls-many-saying-enough.html', 'snippet': 'The only surprise in the rise of the left-wing Syriza party is that it has taken so long for an anti-austerity party to come to the fore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Driving along a broad avenue lined with restaurants, the Greek man at the wheel points to the trash cans. Every night, he says, people rummage through them for scraps of food. His two well-educated daughters cannot find jobs; more than half of Greek youths have no work, and the jobs that do appear are often short-term and lacking in benefits.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/opinion/24greeceWEB/24greeceWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/24/opinion/24greeceWEB/24greeceWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/opinion/24greeceWEB/24greeceWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/opinion/24greeceWEB/24greeceWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1336, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/opinion/24greeceWEB/24greeceWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/24/opinion/24greeceWEB/24greeceWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/24/opinion/24greeceWEB/24greeceWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Greeks Head to the Polls, Many Saying ‘Enough’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Greeks Head to the Polls, Many Saying ‘Enough’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsipras, Alexis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coalition of the Radical Left (Greece)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T02:50:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge Schmemann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmemann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d4531d4-9749-5bd1-9f34-f95b77002f19', 'word_count': 683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d4531d4-9749-5bd1-9f34-f95b77002f19'}, {'abstract': 'Sheldon Silver, who has served as Assembly speaker for more than two decades, has given no indication that he plans to resign. But as Democrats look for a potential heir, they are finding few options.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/24/nyregion/with-arrest-of-silver-assembly-democrats-have-few-choices-for-a-successor.html', 'snippet': 'Sheldon Silver, who has served as Assembly speaker for more than two decades, has given no indication that he plans to resign. But as Democrats look for a potential heir, they are finding few options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — With New York Democrats still reeling on Friday from the arrest of their powerful Assembly leader, Sheldon Silver, on federal graft charges, the state’s political corridors were abuzz with one question: Who could take his place?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Long Led by Silver, Assembly Democrats Face