ord_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/045dc9fc-fbaf-5bfb-a6bf-169bd4f5ae06'}, {'abstract': 'The turmoil in the Middle East will dominate the conversations on the Sunday shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/01/24/what-were-watching-sunday-shows-13/', 'snippet': 'The turmoil in the Middle East will dominate the conversations on the Sunday shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yemeni president, prime minister and cabinet all resigned on Friday, but rebel militia leaders have not made an official claim of power. In Saudi Arabia, King Abdullah died, and was succeeded by his half brother, Salman. This turmoil in the Middle East will dominate conversations on the Sunday shows, when Denis McDonough, the White House chief of staff, will discuss the administration’s foreign policy. He will appear on all five network shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Watching: Sunday Shows', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abdullah, King of Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jindal, Bobby', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonough, Denis R', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-24T19:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elena Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'titl