ed Wilpon, was viewed as the right man for the job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It sounds like a punch line: Fred Wilpon, the majority owner of the Mets, is the new chairman of Major League Baseball’s finance committee. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'M.L.B. Defends Fred Wilpon and His Financial Role', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'M.L.B. Defends Wilpon and His Financial Role', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manfred, Robert D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi and Pyramid Schemes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-25T07:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c362956-0391-564a-9dc7-d74ce8faa752', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c362956-0391-564a-9dc7-d74ce8faa752'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Manfred wants M.L.B. to be more of a presence at the amateur level and also has an interest in reaching out to fans “with information via technology.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/25/sports/baseball/robert-manfred-is-determined-to-steer-young-people-toward-baseball.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Manfred wants M.L.B. to be more of a presence at the amateur level and also has an interest in reaching out to fans “with information via technology.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the foot of the desk of the new baseball commissioner, in a frame waiting to be hung on his office wall, is an original roster from the Rome American Little League in upstate New York, dated April 27, 1969. In the No. 10 slot is a 10-year-old from Van Buren Avenue named Robert Manfred. He never played organized baseball past Little League, but on Sunday he will ascend to the top of the game.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/sports/DOG-kepner/DOG-kepner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/sports/DOG-kepner/DOG-kepner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/sports/DOG-kepner/DOG-kepner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/sports/DOG-kepner/DOG-kepner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/sports/DOG-kepner/DOG-kepner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/sports/DOG-kepner/DOG-kepner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,