e Ideas Festival, organizers said on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/arts/live-arts-aims-high.html', 'snippet': 'The lineup of music, dance, lectures and film screenings is set for the 2015 Live Ideas Festival, organizers said on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lineup of music, dance, lectures and film screenings is set for the 2015 Live Ideas Festival, organizers said on Sunday. This multidisciplinary festival of arts and ideas was founded in 2013 by New York Live Arts, a Chelsea group. Each year has a different theme, with previous festivals focusing on the works of the neurologist Oliver Sacks and the playwright and author James Baldwin. This year’s edition, assembled by the visual artist and performer Laurie Anderson, is themed “S K Y — Force and Wisdom in America Today.” “The sky — a multidimensional symbol of aspiration, vastness, change, threat and now information storage — is a fitting image for this year’s festival,” Bill T. Jones, New York Live Arts’ artistic director, said in a statement. Highlights of the festival, taking place April 15-19, include a new commission by the Bessie Award-winning choreographer Beth Gill and screenings of films by Julian Schnabel. Tickets range from free to $65. Information is at newyorklivearts.org.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Arts Aims High', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Live Arts Aims High', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, LAURIE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gill, Beth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schnabel, Julian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-25T22:57:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/67454eb2-0221-5883-a24e-d2109ca9f5a0', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67454eb2-0221-5883-a24e-d2109ca9f5a0'}, {'abstract': 'A new play about six strangers who leave the city for a silent retreat in the woods will open the 2015 season at the Manhattan nonprofit Ars Nova.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/theater/ars-nova-announces-its-2015-season.html', 'snippet': 'A new play about six strangers who leave the city for a silent retreat in the woods will open the 2015 season at the Manhattan nonprofit Ars Nova.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new play about six strangers who leave the city for a silent retreat in the woods will open the 2015 season at the Manhattan nonprofit Ars Nova, organizers said on Sunday. The production, “Small Mouth Sounds,” by Bess Wohl (“American Hero”), is directed by Rachel Chavkin (“Natasha, Pierre & the Great Comet of 1812”) and developed through Ars Nova’s Play Group. It opens March 10 and runs through April 11. Other season highlights include “Bridget Everett” (the full title is unprintable) ” (April 9), a concert by the alt-cabaret performer Bridget Everett and various Ars Nova emerging artists; and the annual ANT Fest in June. Fall will bring “Futurity,” a new musical with book and lyrics by César Alvarez.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/theater/25chavkin/25chavkin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/25/theater/25chavkin/25chavkin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 693}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/theater/25chavkin/25chavkin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 746, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/theater/25chavkin/25chavkin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 746, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/theater/25chavkin/25chavkin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/theater/25chavkin/25chavkin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/theater/25chavkin/25chavkin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Six Urban Characters in Search of a Retreat', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Six Urban Characters in Search of a Retreat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARS NOVA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wohl, Bess', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavkin, Rachel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-25T22:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', '