8152-c398-5241-b220-052e808a80a4'}, {'abstract': 'People are spending more time on messaging apps, which many say allow for multimedia exchanges and commerce in a more intimate setting than on older social media sites.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/daily-report-why-messaging-apps-are-so-hot/', 'snippet': 'People are spending more time on messaging apps, which many say allow for multimedia exchanges and commerce in a more intimate setting than on older social media sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some publishers, game makers and e-commerce companies are using personal messaging apps like Instagram, WeChat and Snapchat as a new distribution and moneymaking platform, Mike Isaac and Michael J. de la Merced report. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: Why Messaging Apps Are So Hot', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Instant Messaging', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kik Messenger', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Line Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Snapchat Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union Square Ventures', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WeChat (Mobile App)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T12:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91ee4ae5-14e5-5188-9b84-8005b45f1da0', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91ee4ae5-14e5-5188-9b84-8005b45f1da0'}, {'abstract': 'The Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee raised more than $4 million after the party’s big losses in November. The total capped off a record year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/01/26/democrats-set-record-in-2014-in-fund-raising-anyway/', 'snippet': 'The Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee raised more than $4 million after the party’s big losses in November. The total capped off a record year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democrats raised $4.1 million in December after their bruising losses in the midterm elections. That put their 2014 total at a record $131 million and helped them shave their debt to $10 million, the Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee said on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Set Record in 2014, in Fund-Raising Anyway', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Republican Congressional Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T12:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9400adbe-9079-5e25-84e2-1ea5466f9692', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9400adbe-9079-5e25-84e2-1ea5466f9692'}, {'abstract': 'Syriza is more mainstream than Brussels.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/those-radical-vsps/', 'snippet': 'Syriza is more mainstream than Brussels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we head for the big Greek face-off, Francesco Saraceno makes a point I’ve also made on a number of occasions: although many of the press reports describe Syriza as “far-left”, it’s actually preaching fairly conventional economics, while the supposedly responsible officials of Brussels and Berlin have been relying on radical doctrines like expansionary austerity and a growth cliff at 90 percent. The same has to a certain extent been true in the US context.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Those Radical VSPs', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T12:41:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/928e0835-8500-5554-a1c9-1e12a24fa05b', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/928e0835-8500-5554-a1c9-1e12a24fa05b'}, {'abstract': 'Federal prosecutors seek to reverse a crucial insider trading ruling. | Markets shake off Greek election results. | An obscure law has its day. | PartnerRe and Axis Capital Holdings agree to merge.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/morning-agenda-u-s-challenges-insider-trading-ruling/', 'snippet': 'Federal prosecutors seek to reverse a crucial insider trading ruling. | Markets shake off Greek election results. | An obscure law has its day. | PartnerRe and Axis Capital Holdings agree to merge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal prosecutors are seeking to reverse, or at least narrow, a crucial insider trading ruling that overturned the convictions of two hedge fund managers last month, DealBook’s Matthew Goldstein and Ben Protess report. Preet Bharara, the United States attorney in Manhattan, is asking the same three-judge panel that issued the ruling to revisit its decision, according to a filing on Friday. As an alternative, Mr. Bharara’s filing proposes the legal equivalent of a do-over in a process known as en banc.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: U.S. Challenges Insider Trading Ruling', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T12:43:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93bf64ad-98f8-5bff-93cb-b99a4c044c13', 'word_count': 1928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93bf64ad-98f8-5bff-93cb-b99a4c044c13'}, {'abstract': 'It’s immensely costly, but the costs have been paid.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/internal-devaluation-in-greece/', 'snippet': 'It’s immensely costly, but the costs have been paid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One point that seems relevant to talk about Grexit (Greek exit from the euro) and all that: at this point it’s not clear that Greece needs a big boost to competitiveness. “Internal devaluation” via falling wages is incredibly costly — but Greece has been paying incredible costs, and has achieved a sharp fall in relative wages:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Internal Devaluation in Greece', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T12:49:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/199c9d01-470c-5e94-aa52-7051aacd171e', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/199c9d01-470c-5e94-aa52-7051aacd171e'}, {'abstract': 'Former Gov. Rick Perry of Texas wasted no time after leaving office to make a presidential pitch to voters in Iowa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/01/26/perry-finds-an-admiring-audience-on-the-road-in-iowa/', 'snippet': 'Former Gov. Rick Perry of Texas wasted no time after leaving office to make a presidential pitch to voters in Iowa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five days after leaving behind the pomp of the Texas governor’s office, Rick Perry stood before 30 Iowans at a Pizza Ranch in Indianola, Iowa, on Sunday trying to convince them that the humble mortal just inches away was fit to occupy the Oval Office.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/us/politics/26firstdraft-rick-perry/26firstdraft-rick-perry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/26/us/politics/26firstdraft-rick-perry/26firstdraft-rick-perry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/us/politics/26firstdraft-rick-perry/26firstdraft-rick-perry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/us/politics/26firstdraft-rick-perry/26firstdraft-rick-perry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,