is short documentary shows a mother’s efforts to manage her daughter’s daily struggle with a life-threatening condition: Type 1 diabetes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past eight years, the Chamberlain family in Fort Worth, Tex., has been coping with a nightmare all parents fear: In 2006, their daughter, Grace, was given a diagnosis of a life-threatening disease. Grace has Type 1 diabetes, for which there is no cure. Now 15 years old, she has endured approximately 34,000 blood tests, 5,550 shots and 1,660 medical tubing injections to keep her alive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Midnight Three & Six’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T15:17:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Callander', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Callander', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c3c1854-99e5-5c3b-b417-db471374122f', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c3c1854-99e5-5c3b-b417-db471374122f'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Paris Couture Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/01/26/t-magazine/26scene-versace.html', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Paris Couture Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the Paris Couture Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/2