il can create the smell, known as petrichor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A familiar scent fills the air after a dry stretch is broken by a summer rain. There is even a word for this fresh, earthy smell: petrichor. The term was coined in the 1960s when scientists reported that the smell came from chemicals in the surface that the rain landed on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Smell of Rain Bubbles From the Ground', 'kicker': 'ScienceTake', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smells and Odors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Communications (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buie, Cullen R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joung, Young Soo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T15:29:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/912b36a2-b68c-5aa0-a783-6d1566442edf', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/912b36a2-b68c-5aa0-a783-6d1566442edf'}, {'abstract': 'The X Prize Foundation paid more than $5 million to several groups for advances in landing, moving on the lunar surface and imaging.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/science/space/millions-paid-by-x-prize-foundation-for-progress-toward-trip-to-moon.html', 'snippet': 'The X Prize Foundation paid more than $5 million to several groups for advances in landing, moving on the lunar surface and imaging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2004, the X Prize Foundation celebrated the culmination of its first prize competition, awarding $10 million for successful flights of SpaceShipOne, the first privately financed reusable spacecraft to take a pilot to space, defined as 62 miles above the Earth’s surface.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Millions Paid by X Prize Foundation for Progress Toward Trip to Moon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moon Travel Progress Pays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'X Prize Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rocket Science and Propulsion', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T15:33:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e083af6-ad44-5839-b845-e598ed79e6c1', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e083af6-ad44-5839-b845-e598ed79e6c1'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Paris Couture Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/paris-couture-week-versace-spring-summer-2015/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Paris Couture Week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the Paris Couture Week photo diary of