, he said he’d build a fence to keep out crooks, criminals and Islamic terrorists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Freedom Summit in Iowa on Saturday, Donald Trump said that if he runs for president, and is elected president, he will build a border fence to keep out criminals, crooks and Islamic terrorists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Comment Necessary: Donald Trump, Border-Fence Builder', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T16:44:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24940147-896d-5ab4-93bb-29080bda0079', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24940147-896d-5ab4-93bb-29080bda0079'}, {'abstract': 'Many films are selling as indie film’s economics start to make sense again.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/sundance-2015-a-buying-spree-propelled-by-video-on-demand/', 'snippet': 'Many films are selling as indie film’s economics start to make sense again.', 'lead_paragraph': ' PARK CITY, Utah – Distributors are snapping up Sundance movies with a ferocity not seen in years, a reflection of the quality of this year’s lineup and independent film’s improving economics, fueled by video on demand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/arts/earl/earl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 889, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/26/arts/earl/earl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 889}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit'