rsons', 'value': 'Meara, John G (1964- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cleft Palate and Clefts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Boston Children's Hospital", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skull (Body Part)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Face', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Alicia Dawn (1980- )', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T19:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Weintraub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weintraub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/760e64a7-57eb-52f0-a397-88000bec16b3', 'word_count': 1331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/760e64a7-57eb-52f0-a397-88000bec16b3'}, {'abstract': 'The pair star in “Experimenter,” Michael Almereyda’s film about Stanley Milgram’s controversial behavioral experiments in the 1960s.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/sundance-interview-winona-ryder-peter-sarsgaard-experimenter-beetlejuice/', 'snippet': 'The pair star in “Experimenter,” Michael Almereyda’s film about Stanley Milgram’s controversial behavioral experiments in the 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Winona Ryder and Peter Sarsgaard seem ambivalent, if amused, by their roles as elder statespeople of the Sundance Film Festival. The actors, both 43, have become synonymous with the kind of quirky indie fare that has come to epitomize Sundance over the years: Ryder, as the breakout star of “Beetlejuice” and with her roles in the cult films “Heathers” and “Edward Scissorhands” in the late ’80s and early ’90s; and Sarsgaard with celebrated turns in the Sundance films “The Dying Gaul,” “An Education” and “Garden State,” among others. This week, they star alongside one another for the first time in “Experimenter,” the director Michael Almereyda’s drama about the social psychologist Stanley Milgram and his controversial experiments on obedience in the 1960s. It’s a peculiar film — as Milgram, Sarsgaard routinely breaks the fourth wall by speaking directly to the camera; at several points an elephant appears from seemingly nowhere to hint at the deeper meaning behind Milgram’s experiments — and yet it never crumbles under its own weight, thanks to the steady talents of Sarsgaard and Ryder, who plays Milgram’s wife, Sasha. (Ryder is also a jury member at this year’s festival.) T sat down with the actors prior to Sunday’s premiere to discuss ambiguous audience reactions, the allure of television and the rising specter of a “Beetlejuice” sequel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/t-magazine/26symonds-winona/26symonds-winona-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/26/t-magazine/26symonds-winona/26symonds-winona-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 799}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/t-magazine/26symonds-winona/26symonds-winona-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/t-magazine/26symonds-winona/26symonds-winona-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/t-magazine/26symonds-wi