rganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f151fe7-9c8e-5d8b-bce3-1c0e91220323', 'word_count': 23, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f151fe7-9c8e-5d8b-bce3-1c0e91220323'}, {'abstract': 'John Cameron Mitchell returned to the role he created in “Hedwig and the Angry Inch,” sparking strong sales. “Honeymoon in Vegas” saw modest sales after strong reviews.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/26/strong-sales-for-hedwig-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'John Cameron Mitchell returned to the role he created in “Hedwig and the Angry Inch,” sparking strong sales. “Honeymoon in Vegas” saw modest sales after strong reviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of the 1990s downtown musical “Hedwig and the Angry Inch” and its 2001 movie version turned out in strong numbers last week to see the original Hedwig, John Cameron Mitchell, play the role for the first time on Broadway in the hit production there. According to box office data released on Monday, “Hedwig” had one of the highest average ticket prices on Broadway last week — $115.72 — and grossed $609,617 for six performances, or 93 percent of the maximum possible amount. “Hedwig” is the creation of Mr. Mitchell (who wrote the book) and Stephen Trask (who wrote the music and lyrics), and won the Tony Award for best musical revival in June (as well as a best actor Tony for its star at the time, Neil Patrick Harris). Mr. Mitchell is scheduled to play Hedwig on Broadway through March 14.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strong Sales for ‘Hedwig’ on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-26T21:19:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patric