type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3722526d-4bb5-5eb8-8d20-ca96680614e9', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3722526d-4bb5-5eb8-8d20-ca96680614e9'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio announced that city schools would be closed on Tuesday because of the snowstorm, giving some students a reprieve from pending exams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/nyregion/for-students-and-some-adults-canceled-school-in-new-york-comes-as-welcome-news.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio announced that city schools would be closed on Tuesday because of the snowstorm, giving some students a reprieve from pending exams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They are perhaps the three sweetest words to a young person’s ear: School is canceled. And this week, students in New York City were able to savor the cheerful news further in advance than usual.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/nyregion/27SCHOOLSweb/27SCHOOLSweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/27/nyregion/27SCHOOLSweb/27SCHOOLSweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/nyregion/27SCHOOLSweb/27SCHOOLSweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/nyregion/27SCHOOLSweb/27SCHOOLSweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/nyregion/27SCHOOLSweb/27SCHOOLSweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/27/nyregion/27SCHOOLSweb/27SCHOOLSweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/nyregion/27SCHOOLSweb/27SCHOOLSweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Students (and Some Adults), School Cancellation in New York Comes as Welcome News', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Early Notice of Closed Schools, Students (and Adults) Cheer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweber, Nate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T00:40:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris and Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3550d1d-f869-5e0d-9c53-fc8a9d9f3a75', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3550d1d-f869-5e0d-9c53-fc8a9d9f3a75'}, {'abstract': 'Legal officials in Oklahoma are seeking a delay by the United States Supreme Court until it decides whether the state’s combination of lethal drugs used in executions is constitutional.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/us/oklahoma-asks-justices-to-delay-executions.html', 'snippet': 'Legal officials in Oklahoma are seeking a delay by the United States Supreme Court until it decides whether the state’s combination of lethal drugs used in executions is constitutional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oklahoma officials asked the United States Supreme Court on Monday to stay the execution of three inmates on death row until the court rules on the constitutionality of the state’s lethal injection process. The court agreed on Friday to decide a case on the constitutionality of the new combinations of drugs that some states are using to execute prisoners, which critics say cause intense suffering. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/us/27OKLAHOMA/27OKLAHOMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/27/us/27OKLAHOMA/27OKLAHOMA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 778}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/us/27OKLAHOMA/27OKLAHOMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/us/27OKLAHOMA/27OKLAHOMA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1083, 'width': 835, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/us/27OKLAHOMA/27OKLAHOMA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, '