tary on Monday terminated the service of 43 reservists from an elite intelligence unit who in September signed a letter refusing to participate in “actions against Palestinians” for moral reasons. The letter by veterans of the clandestine Unit 8200 claimed that its work harmed innocent people, amounted to “political persecution,” and made it more difficult to resolve the underlying conflict. The military said that the refusal violated its “standards and morals,” and questioned why the complaint was aired publicly rather than through the chain of command. The military “views with great severity any attempt to elude mandatory military service especially when the act is intended to make a political statement,” its statement said. A leader of the reservists’ group, speaking on the condition of anonymity because the military prohibits members of 8200 from being identified publicly, said “the army is trying to make the issues that we were trying to raise go away by making us go away.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Dissident Reservists Dismissed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Dissident Reservists Dismissed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T01:41:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/131b1766-7f10-50b3-999a-bae458027719', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/131b1766-7f10-50b3-999a-bae458027719'}, {'abstract': 'Argentina’s president, Cristina Fernández de Kirchner, accused rogue factions of trying to sabotage a deal with Iran to investigate a 1994 bombing that the prosecutor, Alberto Nisman, was looking into.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/world/americas/argentine-leader-attacks-spy-agency-amid-furor-over-prosecutors-death.html', 'snippet': 'Argentina’s president, Cristina Fernández de Kirchner, accused rogue factions of trying to sabotage a deal with Iran to investigate a 1994 bombing that the prosecutor, Alberto Nisman, was looking into.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — With her government badly shaken over the mysterious death of a prosecutor investigating the 1994 bombing of a Jewish center, President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner said in a televised speech on Monday night that she would immediately send a bill to Congress to dissolve the nation’s premier intelligence agency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentine Leader Attacks Spy Agency Amid Furor Over Prosecutor’s Death ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentine Leader Attacks Spy Agency Amid Furor Over Prosecutor’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nisman, Alberto', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides