ed key rulings from January 2007 and April 2007revealing an internal dispute on the court as the Bush administration struggled to put the program on a firmer legal footing. Congress legalized the program with the Protect America Act in August 2007, ending the efforts to fit it into the existing Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/01/27/us/27-fisc-foia-documents.html', 'snippet': 'In response to a Freedom of Information Act lawsuit, the government has declassified two previously Top Secret rulings from May and August 2007 by Judge Roger Vinson of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court. The disclosure filled in a missin...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In response to a Freedom of Information Act lawsuit, the government has declassified two previously Top Secret rulings from May and August 2007 by Judge Roger Vinson of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court. The disclosure filled in a missing link in the history of the evolving legality of the Bush administration’s warrantless surveillance program. The government previously declassified key rulings from January 2007 and April 2007revealing an internal dispute on the court as the Bush administration struggled to put the program on a firmer legal footing. Congress legalized the program with the Protect America Act in August 2007, ending the efforts to fit it into the existing Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Government Declassifies 2007 Surveillance Court Rulings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Information Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (FISA)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject',