 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Vaping Worse Than Smoking?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is Vaping Worse Than Smoking?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Formaldehyde', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Cigarettes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portland State University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T08:27:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/999133fb-6c9f-5879-8306-1344c5236c53', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/999133fb-6c9f-5879-8306-1344c5236c53'}, {'abstract': 'Impact investing is perhaps the most promising new development tool. Young people just getting started and older business gurus alike should consider it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/opinion/david-brooks-how-to-leave-a-mark.html', 'snippet': 'Impact investing is perhaps the most promising new development tool. Young people just getting started and older business gurus alike should consider it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The big debate during the 20th century was about the relationship between the market and the state. Both those institutions are now tarnished. The market is prone to devastating crashes and seems to be producing widening inequality. Government is gridlocked, sclerotic or captured by special interests. Government is an ever more rigid and ineffective tool to address market failures.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1003, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type