 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a15b1ec1-b50b-5701-be90-e962d369c032', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a15b1ec1-b50b-5701-be90-e962d369c032'}, {'abstract': 'The pro-European reformers desperately need financial aid to survive Russia’s assault.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/opinion/bernard-henri-levi-george-soros-save-the-new-ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'The pro-European reformers desperately need financial aid to survive Russia’s assault.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A NEW Ukraine was born a year ago in the pro-European protests that helped to drive President Viktor F. Yanukovych from power. And today, the spirit that inspired hundreds of thousands to gather in the Maidan, Kiev’s Independence Square, is stronger than ever, even as it is under direct military assault from Russian forces supporting separatists in eastern Ukraine.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/opinion/27Soros/27Soros-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/27/opinion/27Soros/27Soros-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 766}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/opinion/27Soros/27Soros-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/opinion/27Soros/27Soros-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1604, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/opinion/27Soros/27Soros-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/27/opinion/27Soros/27Soros-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/opinion/27Soros/27Soros-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Save the New Ukraine', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Save the New Ukraine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soros, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, Bernard-Henri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T08:27:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bernard-Henri Lévy and George Soros', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bernard-henri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lévy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soros', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a86eea8-d60f-51c3-9412-89cdc458a2cc', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a86eea8-d60f-51c3-9412-89cdc458a2cc'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Tomba, a China expert based in Australia, talks about how the privatization of housing in China appears to be strengthening the grip of the Communist Party.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/q-and-a-luigi-tomba-on-privatized-housing-and-political-legitimacy-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Tomba, a China expert based in Australia, talks about how the privatization of housing in China appears to be strengthening the grip of the Communist Party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Luigi Tomba, 49, is the associate director of the Australian Center on China in the World at the Australian National University in Canberra. In his new book, “The Government Next Door: Neighborhood Politics in Urban China,” Mr. Tomba, a native of Italy who first went to China in 1988, challenges the conventional wisdom that a property-owning middle class is helping to foster civil society in China. Instead, his research leads him to conclude that the privatization of housing has strengthened the grip of the Communist Party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/world/27SINO-TOMBA/27SINO-TOMBA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 578, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/world/27SINO-TOMBA/27SINO-TOMBA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 578, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/world/27SINO-TOMBA/27SINO-TOMBA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/27/world/27SINO-TOMBA/27SINO-TOMBA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/