'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Cochrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cochrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9a23283-a417-57be-ba4d-cd04f33b82ac', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9a23283-a417-57be-ba4d-cd04f33b82ac'}, {'abstract': 'Is the deficit scare coming back? No.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/the-debt-non-spiral/', 'snippet': 'Is the deficit scare coming back? No.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid all the other economic news, the CBO has issued its latest budget projections. According to the projections, the US deficit will soon stop shrinking and begin to rise again. Cue the Very Serious People, who are deeply distressed at the failure of the promised fiscal crisis to materialize; I’m sure we’ll see editorials and op-eds in the next few days warning us that the deficit is still public enemy #1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Debt Non-Spiral', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T13:23:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2f144e6-9842-5153-9d01-76c28b3d67ef', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2f144e6-9842-5153-9d01-76c28b3d67ef'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: 1965 Britain Says Farewell to Churchill', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/1965-u-k-says-farewell-to-churchill/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: 1965 Britain Says Farewell to Churchill', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Britain began its long and sad farewell to Sir Winston Churchill today. Just as Big Ben pealed 11 a.m., the great door of St. Stephen at Westminster hall swung wide. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965 U.K. Says Farewell to Churchill', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Churchill, Winston Leonard Spencer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T13:25:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f42efb35-f503-5e24-af19-9fac73b49177', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f42efb35-f503-5e24-af19-9fac73b49177'}, {'abstract': 'Less than a month after 17 people were killed in terror attacks on France, the government is assuring travelers that the City of Light is safe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/travel/paris-takes-pains-to-reassure-tourists.html', 'snippet': 'Less than a month after 17 people were killed in terror attacks on France, the government is assuring travelers that the City of Light is safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A throng of visitors huddled outside L’As du Fallafel on the Rue des Rosiers, braving the cold for a taste of the legendary restaurant’s takeout shawarma and chickpea fritters. Around them, people jammed onto the narrow cobbled street, dressed in bright scarves, arms loaded with shopping bags and cameras.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/travel/01UPDATE-copy/01UPDATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/01/travel/01UPDATE-copy/01UPDATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/travel/01UPDATE-copy/01UPDATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/travel/01UPDATE-copy/01UPDATE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/travel/01UPDATE-copy/01UPDATE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/01/travel/01UPDATE-copy/01UPDATE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/travel/01UPDATE-copy/01UPDATE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Takes Pains to Reassure Tourists', 'kicker': 'Update', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paris Takes Pains to Reassure Tourists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T13:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f48cb00-e4e9-543e-a46a-a5367fba13c6', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f48cb00-e4e9-543e-a46a-a5367fba13c6'}, {'abstract': 'Contemporary structures, from museums to stadiums to churches, in the city’s outskirts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/travel/roman-architecture-beyond-the-colosseum.html', 'snippet': 'Contemporary structures, from museums to stadiums to churches, in the city’s outskirts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For people who love contemporary architecture, trying to find striking new buildings in the historic center of Rome is about as easy as trying to go gluten-free there. But if you move a little farther out — or a lot — there are stunning treasures to find, from museums to stadiums to churches, not to mention animated new neighborhoods that you probably would have never explored in the first place.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/travel/25ROME1/25ROME1-articleLarge-v2.j