ction_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Lubell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lubell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51fb7049-f47f-5204-bf4e-8f9121fe075d', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51fb7049-f47f-5204-bf4e-8f9121fe075d'}, {'abstract': 'In an effort to catch up to rival services like Facebook, Twitter will now allow people to shoot, edit and post video directly from its mobile apps. Also, private messages on the service can now be sent to as many as 20 people.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/twitter-adds-group-messaging-and-video-recording/', 'snippet': 'In an effort to catch up to rival services like Facebook, Twitter will now allow people to shoot, edit and post video directly from its mobile apps. Also, private messages on the service can now be sent to as many as 20 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Faced with slow growth in new users and usage by existing users, Twitter executives repeatedly promised improvements to make the social network more inviting.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/technology/27bits-twitter/27bits-twitter-jumbo-v3.png', 'height': 406, 'width': 565, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/technology/27bits-twitter/27bits-twitter-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 406, 'width': 565, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/technology/27bits-twitter/27bits-twitter-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/27/technology/27bits-twitter/27bits-twitter-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/27/technology/27bits-twitter/27bits-twitter-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter Adds Group Messaging and Video Recording', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twitter Adds Group Messages and More ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Instant Messaging', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costolo, Dick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T13:35:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vindu Goel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vindu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83f98e2c-aa8f-5f90-917d-aae158ad9e41', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83f98e2c-aa8f-5f90-917d-aae158ad9e41'}, {'abstract': 'Did bad luck produce perverse policy?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/the-tyranny-of-greece-over-germany/', 'snippet': 'Did bad luck produce perverse policy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'No, I haven’t lost my mind. That’s the title of a classic book by Eliza Marian Butler arguing that German culture was warped by an obsession with ancient Greece, which has nothing at all to do with the current problems of macroeconomic policy. But the title came to mind when I read Simon Wren-Lewis’s meditation on two different hypotheses about the disastrous 2010 turn to austerity. One hypothesis, as he says, is that it was just bad luck: Greece blew up at the end of 2009, and false analogies with Greece soon dominated policy debate; you can call this Hellenization of discourse the tyranny of Greece, not so much over Germany, as over the OECD as a whole.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tyranny of Greece Over Germany', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T13:45:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12f6a3c-bf47-52d0-bdf5-28d52261aca3', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12f6a3c-bf47-52d0-bdf5-28d52261aca3'}, {'abstract': 'Have you been following the news? Take our quiz to see what you know and to learn more, and look for a new edition each week on Tuesday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/weekly-news-quiz-jan-20-26-2015/', 'snippet': 'Have you been following the news? Take our quiz to see what you know and to learn more, and look for a new edition each week on Tuesday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you been following the news?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/nyregion/20150127_STORMPREP-slide-JN2F-LN/20150127_S