son': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da267c2d-c08a-5a19-8182-1c8907287411', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da267c2d-c08a-5a19-8182-1c8907287411'}, {'abstract': 'One would think that we’d be more ready for her; after all, we had been waiting for this moment for over three years. But “ready” and “get your car seat” are two very different things.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/totally-prepared-still-freaking-out/', 'snippet': 'One would think that we’d be more ready for her; after all, we had been waiting for this moment for over three years. But “ready” and “get your car seat” are two very different things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my wife, Rachel, got off the phone with the neonatal intensive care unit (NICU) on Jan. 19, after her usual morning check in on how Evy was doing — we visit her in the afternoons to be clear of doctors’ rounds, which would keep us in the hallway and not by Evy’s side — her voice had a mixture of amazement, pride and fear, the verbal equivalent of turning white when scared.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/us/motherlode-evy2/motherlode-evy2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/26/us/motherlode-evy2/motherlode-evy2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/26/us/motherlode-evy2/motherlode-evy2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type