': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/64d3e7b3-65ad-5437-aa6a-0d1bc0377c4f', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64d3e7b3-65ad-5437-aa6a-0d1bc0377c4f'}, {'abstract': 'To open the season, Plácido Domingo will sing the title role in Puccini’s one-act opera “Gianni Schicchi” and then, after the intermission, move down to the orchestra pit to conduct Leoncavallo’s “Pagliacci.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/27/los-angeles-opera-season-to-open-with-domingo-singing-gianni-schicchi/', 'snippet': 'To open the season, Plácido Domingo will sing the title role in Puccini’s one-act opera “Gianni Schicchi” and then, after the intermission, move down to the orchestra pit to conduct Leoncavallo’s “Pagliacci.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Plácido Domingo, the general director of the Los Angeles Opera, plans to open the company’s 30th anniversary season in September with a feat few other impresarios could attempt: He will sing the title role in Puccini’s one-act opera “Gianni Schicchi” and then, after the intermission, move down to the orchestra pit to conduct Leoncavallo’s “Pagliacci.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Los Angeles Opera Season to Open With Domingo Singing ‘Gianni Schicchi’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Singing Conductor: Busy Night for Domingo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Domingo, Placido', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-27T22:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported