ted-footballs.html', 'snippet': 'A law firm hired by the N.F.L. has asked Columbia’s physics department for help in understanding how weather could affect the pressure in footballs, according to a summary of the communication.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A law firm hired by the N.F.L. to investigate footballs used by the New England Patriots has formally asked the Columbia University physics department for help in understanding how weather and temperature could affect the pressure in footballs, according to a summary of the communication obtained by The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/sports/28physics/28physics-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/28/sports/28physics/28physics-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/sports/28physics/28physics-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/sports/28physics/28physics-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/sports/28physics/28physics-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/28/sports/28physics/28physics-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/sports/28physics/28physics-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Investigator Seeks to Consult Columbia Physicist Over Patriots’ Deflated Footballs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reisner, Lorin L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-28T04:54:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Glanz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glanz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ede988b4-27b3-505c-bf81-877ae2358bff', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ede988b4-27b3-505c-bf81-877ae2358bff'}, {'abstract': 'The 26-year-old rapper’s first film, “Dope,” a hip-hop-driven comedy in which he plays a drug dealer named Dom, is an early favorite to win the festival’s audience award.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/28/t-magazine/asap-rocky-sundance-dope-interview.html', 'snippet': 'The 26-year-old rapper’s first film, “Dope,” a hip-hop-driven comedy in which he plays a drug dealer named Dom, is an early favorite to win the festival’s audience award.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been an up-and-down couple of weeks for A$AP Rocky. On Saturday, the 26-year-old rapper attended the world premiere of his new film, “Dope,” a hip-hop-driven comedy in which he plays a drug dealer named Dom. (Also featured are Keith Stanfield, Zoë Kravitz and Rocky’s ex-girlfriend, the model Chanel Iman.) The movie — Rocky’s first — has been a Sundance hit, drawing rave reviews and becoming an early favorite to win the festival’s audience award. But Rocky, né Rakim Mayers, was in little mood to celebrate. Just six days earlier, on Jan. 18, his close friend and collaborator Steven “A$AP Yams” Rodriguez died suddenly of still-undisclosed causes. On Sunday morning, Rocky would have to fly to New York City for the funeral.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28symonds-asap/28symonds-asap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28symonds-asap/28symonds-asap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28symonds-asap/28symonds-asap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28symonds-asap/28symonds-asap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28symonds-asap/28symonds-asap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28symonds-asap/28symonds-asap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28symonds-asap/28symonds-asap-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A$AP Rocky on His Sundance Hit, Mourning A$AP Yams and Why He Rejects Those Tupac Comparisons', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-28T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07ee2460-b3a5-5de4-9525-4d3745c394f2', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07ee2460-b3a5-5de4-9525-4d3745c394f2'}, {'abstract': 'A 20-piece collection of the timeless “clothes for heroes” found at the designer’s fabled London store launches at the boutique Feb. 9.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/28/t-magazine/opening-ceremony-vivienne-westwood-worlds-end.html', 'snippet': 'A 20-piece collection of the timeless “clothes for heroes” found at the designer’s fabled London store launches at the boutique Feb. 9.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opening Ceremony’s latest co-conspirator is Vivienne Westwood, who has designed for the boutique a 20-piece collection based on the timeless “clothes for heroes” found at her fabled Worlds End shop in London. “We’d been wanting to do something with Vivienne for a while,” says Humberto Leon, the store’s cofounder with Carol Lim. “Growing up, I remember being excited about her brand’s messages and its relevancy to culture — and I wanted to share this incredible story that I revere, if people don’t already know about it.” The resulting capsule, priced from $95 for a T-shirt to $1,500 for a bomber jacket, includes reissued garments dating back to the ’70s — and transcends gender. “It plays on this idea of unisex that we’ve been working on for many years,” says Andreas Kronthaler, Westwood’s design partner and creative director (and husband). “We know a woman looks great in a man’s shirt, but can a man look great in a woman’s dress? It could be the case — it’s about pushing boundaries and experimenting.” Asked to select a standout item, Kronthaler mentions the Pirate Trouser, originally from Westwood’s 1981 Pirate collection, for its “muscly, active-looking, dynamic leg shape”; Leon, however, declined to choose just one. “It’s hard to pick specifics because it’s about telling the whole story,” he says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28westwood-moss/28westwood-moss-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28westwood-moss/28westwood-moss-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28westwood-moss/28westwood-moss-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28westwood-moss/28westwood-moss-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28westwood-moss/28westwood-moss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28westwood-moss/28westwood-moss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28westwood-moss/28westwood-moss-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Opening Ceremony Brings Vivienne Westwood’s Worlds End Shop Stateside', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-28T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc8da921-375f-5d1d-a126-abe95883f627', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc8da921-375f-5d1d-a126-abe95883f627'}, {'abstract': 'In December, chef Jean-François Piège opened the restaurant Clover, an instant favorite among the Left Bank gratin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/28/t-magazine/clover-restaurant-paris.html', 'snippet': 'In December, chef Jean-François Piège opened the restaurant Clover, an instant favorite among the Left Bank gratin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charmed by their shape and attracted by their purported powers, the Parisian chef Jean-François Piège has been collecting four-leaf clover objects for many years — but the success of his new restaurant Clover is due to a lot more than just luck.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28clover-lobrano-1/28piege-lobrano-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28clover-lobr