icle/e99a9ce0-ecd0-5785-a600-174476da5cb7'}, {'abstract': 'The new coalition said it is committed to finding a way to change financial incentives, moving the bulk of payments to so-called “value-based” arrangements by 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/28/business/28payment.html', 'snippet': 'The new coalition said it is committed to finding a way to change financial incentives, moving the bulk of payments to so-called “value-based” arrangements by 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A coalition of some of the nation’s largest health care systems and insurers vowed on Wednesday to change the way hospitals and doctors are paid — placing less emphasis on the sheer amount of care being delivered and more on improving quality and lowering costs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/business/28PAYMENTSSUB2/28PAYMENTSSUB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/28/business/28PAYMENTSSUB2/28PAYMENTSSUB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/business/28PAYMENTSSUB2/28PAYMENTSSUB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/business/28PAYMENTSSUB2/28PAYMENTSSUB2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/business/28PAYMENTSSUB2/28PAYMENTSSUB2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/28/business/28PAYMENTSSUB2/28PAYMENTSSUB2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/business/28PAYMENTSSUB2/28PAYMENTSSUB2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Industry Group to Back Results-Focused Care', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Industry Group to Back Results-Focused Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abelson, Reed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burwell, Sylvia Mathews', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-28T05:01:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebe99c19-f878-55b5-a806-426511ad73ba', 'word_count': 950, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebe99c19-f878-55b5-a806-426511ad73ba'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 2,322 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/28/word-of-the-day-missile/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 2,322 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'missile •\\ˈmi-səl, -ˌsil\\• noun ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | missile', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-28T05:02:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7e67ba0-8995-5788-bf06-e0abc6070eeb', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7e67ba0-8995-5788-bf06-e0abc6070eeb'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/28/arts/whats-on-tv-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (13, 49) PENGUIN POST OFFICE Every summer in the Southern Hemisphere, a British post office at Port Lockroy, above, becomes the most popular tourist attraction for cruise ships to the Antarctic Peninsula, as some 3,000 gentoo penguins take up residence alongside the other seasonal inhabitants: volunteers from the United Kingdom Antarctic Heritage Trust, who run the remote outpost. There, each November, after a bout of intensive deep-sea fishing, the gentoos find their mates, build their nests, raise their young — and pose for pictures, as long as the photographer stays 15 feet away. This “Nature” episode ventures to Antarctica to film the four-month ritual. In “Sinkholes — Buried Alive,” at 10, “Nova” investigates what happens when the ground opens up beneath your feet.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-