/db92ece1-3b93-52aa-b3bd-29432141f29c', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db92ece1-3b93-52aa-b3bd-29432141f29c'}, {'abstract': 'This short documentary shows a 24-hour bus line in Silicon Valley, which the region’s homeless use as a shelter at night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/28/opinion/hotel-22.html', 'snippet': 'This short documentary shows a 24-hour bus line in Silicon Valley, which the region’s homeless use as a shelter at night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we think of Silicon Valley, we tend to imagine a world of extreme wealth and limitless opportunity. What we forget are the populations that have been displaced or neglected by the recent tech boom. Rising property prices in the area have created unsustainable living costs, especially for the poor. At the same time, Silicon Valley lacks sufficient affordable housing and homeless shelters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Hotel 22’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-28T15:17:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Lo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/24515ff7-c7ba-562c-9d58-2b22cc61d2ad', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24515ff7-c7ba-562c-9d58-2b22cc61d2ad'}, {'abstract': 'The introduction of 