ww.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/travel/belfast-northern-ireland.html', 'snippet': 'A more sophisticated city has emerged with a sleek new cultural center, a vibrant dining scene and plenty of friendly pubs in which to while away the hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Avoided, underrated or just plain forgotten, Belfast is a city that’s been fighting a bad reputation for half a century. A visit today, however, is an eye-opening experience in the best possible way. Belfast has been coming into its own in the last few years, developing a vibrant restaurant scene, award-winning architecture — the Royal Institute of British Architects gave the MAC, a sleek arts venue, a National Award in 2013 — and a new cosmopolitanism, although fried breakfasts and a heightened awareness of sectarian conflict are still an integral part of most residents’ days. The friendliness of the people is what’s most appealing in this small and very walkable city, from smiling servers to talkative bartenders to helpful strangers on the street. Visit Belfast to soak up good vibes, to eat well and to drink unstintingly. It’s a city that’s at its best when enjoyed from behind a pint glass.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Belfast, Northern Ireland', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wulfhart, Nell McShane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belfast (Northern Ireland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Titanic Belfast', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sands, Bobby', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocation