re made and who makes them', 'lead_paragraph': 'From time to time, I take up questions that have come to me from readers, pose them to Times editors, and publish the questions and answers without providing further commentary. I’ll do a few of those over the next few days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perfectly Reasonable Question: Gender of Letter Writers', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-28T19:14:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40dd166c-064b-5848-abaa-c2b51dc18093', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40dd166c-064b-5848-abaa-c2b51dc18093'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The crew of the Arethusa suffered a terrible fate in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/28/1890-horrible-sufferings-at-sea/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The crew of the Arethusa suffered a terrible fate in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Sufferings at sea have seldom taken a more horrible form than those undergone by the crew of the ship Arethusa of Liverpool. The Arethusa was bound from the Tyne to Valparaiso, and on September 29 her cargo of coal took fire. On October 2, the crew of twenty-three men took to two boats, and at that time they were only twenty six miles from Falkland Islands, when the weather became dirty and during the night the boats parted company. Seven days later the boat, with the captain and ten men, arrived at Port Stanley, the crew being in a pitiable condition. The barque Lady Octavia picked up the other boat. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Jan. 29, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1890: Horrible Sufferings at Sea', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-28T19:17:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c54ff56-5f54-5084-96ba-d62bcf609e0d', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c54ff56-5f54-5084-96ba-d62bcf609e0d'}, {'abstract': 'Loretta E. Lynch, President Obama’s nominee for attorney general, answers questions on immigration and law enforcement from the Senate Judiciary Committee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000003477937/lynch-responds-to-senate-committee.html', 'snippet': 'Loretta E. Lynch, President Obama’s nominee for attorney general, answers questions on immigration and law enforcement from the Senate Judiciary Committee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Loretta E. Lynch, President Obama’s nominee for attorney general, answers questions on immigration and law enforcement from the Senate Judiciary Committee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/us/29LYNCH1/29LYNCH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width':