k-that-works-irl-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'How to wear layers of outerwear and still look chic; long chains make low necklines look ladylike; and other shopping news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Piling on outerwear to stay warm is a street-style trick that works IRL. And there are ways to pull off the stratagem without looking like a coat lady. The stylist Kusum Lynn suggests wearing a leather jacket or puffer under a classic men’s wear coat, adding an oversize scarf for color. For an undone yet still chic ensemble, she likes a relaxed-fit robe coat (preferably with an exaggerated collar) worn atop a chunky cardigan. To counter the proportions of slouchy outerwear, wear tailored trousers. “You can be at work with the worst hangover and feel like you’re still getting cozy in bed under the covers,” Ms. Lynn said.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/fashion/29BROWSING_SPAN/29BROWSING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 306, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/29/fashion/29BROWSING_SPAN/29BROWSING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 306}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/fashion/29BROWSING_SPAN/29BROWSING_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/fashion/29BROWSING_SPAN/29BROWSING_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1045, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/fashion/29BROWSING_SPAN/29BROWSING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/29/fashion/29BROWSING_SPAN/29BROWSING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/fashion/29BROWSING_SPAN/29BROWSING_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Street-Style Trick That Works IRL and More', 'kicker': 'Browsing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Street-Style Trick That Works IRL and More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coats and Jackets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handbags and Purses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brother Vellies (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghisellini, Elena', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Aurora', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-28T22:20:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica M. Blumenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60993390-1858-5ebd-a970-daf73bc0faa5', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60993390-1858-5ebd-a970-daf73bc0faa5'}, {'abstract': 'Four exhibitions in New York and Dallas this winter and spring will showcase the work of Kazuo Shiraga, known as the “foot painter” of the underrepresented Gutai Art Association.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/28/kazuo-shiraga-foot-painter-gutai-art/', 'snippet': 'Four exhibitions in New York and Dallas this winter and spring will showcase the work of Kazuo Shiraga, known as the “foot painter” of the underrepresented Gutai Art Association.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ironically, Kazuo Shiraga’s feet were nearly his feet of clay. The breakout star of the Gutai Art Association, Shiraga became colloquially known as the “foot painter”; the Japanese postwar movement’s founder, Jiro Yoshihara, even dismissed Shiraga as a “nobody, if he didn’t paint with his feet.” After his 1955 performance “Challenging Mud,” in which the artist wrestled a mixture of cement, gravel, clay, plaster, pebbles and twigs into a “formless form,” Shiraga devised an entirely new painting technique. From 1959 onward, he suspended himself from his studio ceiling and manipulated the paint exclusively with his ten toes to create a range of textures from the slinky and supple to the protruding and violent. Almost 60 years later, Shiraga, whose dynamic contributions blend painting and performance, is still a misunderstood radical who is only now receiving the sort of American institutional and gallery attention that properly contextualizes the depth and reach of his practice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28shiraga-baumgardner-2/28shiraga-baumgardner-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28shiraga-baumgardner-2/28shiraga-baumgardner-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28shiraga-baumgardner-2/28shiraga-baumgardner-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28shiraga-baumgardner-2/28shiraga-baumgardner-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1044, 'width': 1333, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28shiraga-baumgardner-2/28shiraga-baumgardner-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28shiraga-baumgardner-2/28shiraga-baumgardner-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/28/t-magazine/28shiraga-baumgardner-2/28shiraga-baumgardner-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Inventive Postwar Japanese Painter Has His Moment', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fontana, Lucio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mnuchin, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vervoordt, Axel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Museum of Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mnuchin Gallery', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of