i': 'nyt://article/07e10a00-937e-51ae-9232-c0497f3fb744'}, {'abstract': 'A bill would throw a wrench into the Federal Communications Commission’s plan to adopt strong Internet rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/29/opinion/republicans-try-to-pre-empt-the-fcc.html', 'snippet': 'A bill would throw a wrench into the Federal Communications Commission’s plan to adopt strong Internet rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many Republicans have no fondness for net neutrality — the idea that cable and phone companies should treat all information equally as it travels over their broadband Internet networks. So it comes as no surprise that some of them are trying to throw a wrench into the Federal Communications Commission’s plan to adopt strong Internet rules.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu3web/29thu3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu3web/29thu3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu3web/29thu3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu3web/29thu3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu3web/29thu3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu3web/29thu3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu3web/29thu3web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Try to Pre-empt the F.C.C.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Try to Pre-empt the F.C.C.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thune, John R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Upton, Fred', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-29T08:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/69311c9e-21a6-577e-8623-1b406d398605', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69311c9e-21a6-577e-8623-1b406d398605'}, {'abstract': 'Americans are entitled to the unvarnished truth about the $107.5 billion the United States has invested in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/29/opinion/inconvenient-truths-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Americans are entitled to the unvarnished truth about the $107.5 billion the United States has invested in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late December, as they do every few months, American military officials in Kabul sent a trove of data to the office of the Special Inspector General for Afghanistan Reconstruction for its quarterly report. Over the years, such figures have told an often dispiriting story about Washington’s enormous investment in the country’s security forces, laying out their size, readiness, attrition level and the state of their infrastructure. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu1web/29thu1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu1web/29thu1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu1web/29thu1web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu1web/29thu1web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1224, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu1web/29thu1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu1web/29thu1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/opinion/29thu1web/29thu1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inconvenient Truths in Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inconvenient Truths in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'val