times.com/2015/01/30/world/asia/north-korea-sought-talks-and-attached-a-hefty-price-tag-souths-ex-leader-says.html', 'snippet': 'In a new memoir, Lee Myung-bak, the South’s president from 2008 to 2013, writes that Kim Jong-il pressed hard for a meeting but demanded, among other things, $10 billion in cash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — North Korea repeatedly but unsuccessfully pushed for a summit meeting with the former South Korean leader Lee Myung-bak, demanding a huge aid package, including $10 billion in cash, as an incentive, Mr. Lee says in a memoir to be published next week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Sought Talks and Attached a Hefty Price Tag, South’s Ex-Leader Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea: Ex-Leader Reveals North’s Cash Request', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee Myung-bak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-29T12:13:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f963c80-b2fb-50be-afef-d79387af4845', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f963c80-b2fb-50be-afef-d79387af4845'}, {'abstract': 'The decision cleared the way for relatives of the 239 passengers and crew members who disappeared to receive compensation, but did nothing to clear up what happened to the plane.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/world/asia/malaysia-declares-loss-of-flight-370-in-march-an-accident.html', 'snippet': 'The decision cleared the way for relatives of the 239 passengers and crew members who disappeared to receive compensation, but did nothing to clear up what happened to the plane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The Malaysian government declared on Thursday that the loss of Malaysia Airlines Flight 370 last March was an accident according to the terms of an international air agreement and that the 239 passengers and crew members aboard the plane were presumed dead.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/world/MALAYSIA/MALAYSIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/30/world/MALAYSIA/MALAYSIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/world/MALAYSIA/MALAYSIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/world/MALAYSIA/MALAYSIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/world/MALAYSIA/MALAYSIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/30/world/MALAYSIA/MALAYSIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/world/MALAYSIA/MALAYSIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Loss of Malaysia Airlines Flight 370 Is Declared an Accident', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Malaysia Declares Loss of Flight 370 in Indian Ocean an Accident', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaysia Airlines Flight 370', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malaysia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-29T12:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d97612a4-f250-58e3-bd02-33c1d494e31c', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d97612a4-f250-58e3-bd02-33c1d494e31c'}, {'abstract': 'Spinning off its stake in Alibaba may make Yahoo a takeover target. |Deutsche Bank swings to profit. | McDonald’s replaces its chief executive. | A push for a greater government role in housing finance.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/01/29/morning-agenda-yahoo-as-takeover-target/', 'snippet': 'Spinning off its stake in Alibaba may make Yahoo a takeover target. |Deutsche Bank swings to profit. | McDonald’s replaces its chief executive. | A push for a greater government role in housing finance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Yahoo completes the spinoff of its $39 billion stake in the Alibaba Group, the Silicon Valley stalwart may not have much time to turn its core Internet businesses around, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced reports. When the spinoff is done, investors and analysts say, Yahoo could become a takeover target.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Yahoo as Takeover Target', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-29T12:38:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cb77902-2d8d-5a7f-a512-bd4964c396b8', 'word_count': 1785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cb77902-2d8d-5a7f-a512-bd4964c396b8'}, {'abstract': 'For a fair immigration policy, end laws favoring one group over the others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/opinion/why-are-cubans-so-special.html', 'snippet': 'For a fair immigration policy, end laws favoring one group over the others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTA BARBARA, Calif. — Every Cuban knows the “wet foot, dry foot” drill: Risk fleeing to the United States and get caught at sea, and you will be sent back to the island; but if you wangle just one toe onto dry land, you’re home free. From there, typically, it’s a fast track to permanent residency, and eligibility for all manner of benefits, from green cards to welfare, then citizenship — all compliments of the Cuban Adjustment Act of 1966. Indeed, for almost a half century, Cubans have been the most privileged immigrants in the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/opinion/30bardach/30bardach-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/30/opinion/30bardach/30bardach-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 933}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/opinion/30bardach/30bardach-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 659, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/opinion/30bardach/30bardach-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1317, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/opinion/30bardach/30bardach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/30/opinion/30bardach/30bardach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/opinion/30bardach/30bardach-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Are Cubans So Special?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Are Cubans So Special?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bardach, Ann Louise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menendez, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cuban-Americans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-29T12:42:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Louise Bardach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': 'Louise', 'lastname': 'Bardach', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7b76cb8-f143-5191-96d0-90d9ea188bb9', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7b76cb8-f143-5191-96d0-90d9ea188bb9'}, {'abstract': 'The city government fears a potential lapse in money being paid into social welfare funds as the high costs of rearing and educating a child may be deterring many from having a second child.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/29/in-shanghai-easing-of-one-child-rule-not-seen-as-cure-for-challenges-ahead/', 'snippet': 'The city government fears a potential lapse in money being paid into social welfare funds as the high costs of rearing and educating a child may be deterring many from having a second child.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirty years ago, People’s Daily, the newspaper of the ruling Communist Party, ran an article with the headline: “It’s good to have just one child; the government will support you in old age.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Shanghai, Easing of One-Child Rule Isn’t Seen as Cure for Challenges Ahead', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'nam