 observe a minute of silence for victims and later defended the men who attacked the satirical newspaper Charlie Hebdo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/world/europe/french-police-questions-schoolboy-said-to-defend-charlie-hebdo-attack.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities said the boy was questioned after he refused to observe a minute of silence for victims and later defended the men who attacked the satirical newspaper Charlie Hebdo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Police officials in the southern French city of Nice questioned an 8-year-old boy who is believed to have made comments in school defending the gunmen who killed 17 people in terrorist attacks in and near Paris this month, a senior regional police official confirmed on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Police Question Boy, 8, After Remarks on Paris Attacks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'French Police Question Boy, 8, After Remarks on Paris Attacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coulibaly, Amedy (1982-2015)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dieudonne (1966- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nice (France)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-29T17:02:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maïa de la Baume and Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f95cea54-30ff-5c1a-b37f-8f1e5c5a4d0c', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f95cea54-30ff-5c1a-b37f-8f1e5c5a4d0c'}, {'abstract': 'From lamps that appear to have burst through the walls to an installation by the Bouroullec brothers, the space is no ordinary luxury flagship.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/29/reed-krakoff-new-soho-boutique/', 'snippet': 'From lamps that appear to have burst through the walls to an installation by the Bouroullec brothers, the space is no ordinary luxury flagship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the moment a customer enters Reed Krakoff’s new SoHo boutique to find lamps that appear to have burst in right through the sheetrock, it’s clear that the store is no ordinary luxury flagship. “It’s surprising,” Krakoff says, referring to both the site-specific lighting installation by Nick Allman and the 2,700-square-foot storefront, his second in New York, which opens Sunday. “The idea was to have a space that combines art and fashion and design in a way that is sort of un-self-conscious and natural.” Krakoff’s well-documented affinity for art and design informed many other elements of the marble-floored interior: Also present are an opalescent table by Mattia Bonetti, which Krakoff says “reads almost like a sculpture”; a custom Ronan and Erwan Bouroullec “Clouds” installation rendered in felt, one of Krakoff’s favorite materials; and a wall installation of chairs created by Krakoff and his wife Delphine that was originally exhibited at Salon 94 and will double as shelving for merchandise. Steven Sebring’s 360-degree photographs of Krakoff’s designs — the same signature technique utilized in the photographer’s recent book featuring Coco Rocha, “Study of Pose” — will also be on prominent display. “The juxtaposition of these things tells a story,” Krakoff says. “It’s different than the typical shopping experience.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29krakoff-hartman/29krakoff-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29krakoff-hartman/29krakoff-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29krakoff-hartman/29krakoff-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29krakoff-hartman/29krakoff-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29krakoff-hartman/29krakoff-hartman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29krakoff-hartman/29krakoff-hartman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29krakoff-hartman/29krakoff-hartman-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Reed Krakoff’s New SoHo Boutique, the Art and Design Are as Compelling as the Fashion', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Store: Shopping in the Clouds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonetti, Mattia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouroullec, Erwan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krakoff, Reed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebring, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-29T17:02:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8894f031-441f-5527-9eac-73af64931d00', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8894f031-441f-5527-9eac-73af64931d00'}, {'abstract': 'T’s men’s fashion editors share their favorites from the latest round of shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29best-paris-ryder.html', 'snippet': 'T’s men’s fashion editors share their favorites from the latest round of shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T’s men’s fashion editors share their favorites from the latest round of shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29best-paris-ryder-slide-27R5/29best-paris-ryder-slide-27R5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/29/t-magazine/29best-paris-ryder-slide