Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e391a3d1-c83e-5bb0-81da-0c7144b05c71', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e391a3d1-c83e-5bb0-81da-0c7144b05c71'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: 1940: Premier Edouard Daladier told civilians that their lives must undergo a complete transformation.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/29/1940-daladier-addresses-civilians/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: 1940: Premier Edouard Daladier told civilians that their lives must undergo a complete transformation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an earnest radio talk to the French nation last night [Jan. 28], Premier Edouard Daladier told civilians that their lives must undergo as complete a transformation as those of the men in the front line if a powerful, destructive and unscrupulous enemy is to be defeated in the ‘‘total war which will not be long now in being let loose. When they left for the frontier, our sons accepted a total transformation of their lives,’’ he said. ‘‘Those who have stayed behind and do not have to put up with the same sufferings and dangers must also agree to transform their lives.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Jan. 30, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/blogs/30iht-retrospective-Daladier/30iht-retrospective-Daladier-articleLarge.png', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/30/blogs/30iht-retrospective-Daladier/30iht-retrospective-Daladier-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo'