r indulges a longtime fancy, and spends a Friday — and a Saturday — at the movies, from “Blackhat” to an Altman festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I try to keep it quiet, but what I really want to do is go to the movies. Not for the same reasons as Binx Bolling in “The Moviegoer” — he wants to escape the sadness of daily life — but because so much is going on that sometimes I need to get out of my head, and I like to do it in a cinema instead of in front of a computer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '12 Theaters, Two Days, One Kick in the Head', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '12 Theaters, Two Days, One Kick in the Head', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyall, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-29T20:49:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8f13488-1080-5990-82f8-39188a2d6b2c', 'word_count': 2898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8f13488-1080-5990-82f8-39188a2d6b2c'}, {'abstract': 'The Bell House in Brooklyn and Posh in Manhattan are offering free football festivities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/nyregion/super-bowl-parties-at-bars-no-cover-required.html', 'snippet': 'The Bell House in Brooklyn and Posh in Manhattan are offering free football festivities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Football isn’t for everyone, but it sure is for a lot of people: It’s America’s most popular sport. Last year’s Super Bowl on Fox averaged 111.5 mi