achingly sincere speeches from filmmakers nobody has ever heard of. But if the shorts are inevitably upstaged by the main show, they also offer a vision of what the Academy Awards should and could be but very rarely are: eclectic, cosmopolitan, scrappy and surprising.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And to the Point ', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'And to the Point', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-29T22:53:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9433c86-6190-5c6e-ac71-9da8dd8088de', 'word_count': 1320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9433c86-6190-5c6e-ac71-9da8dd8088de'}, {'abstract': 'The bombings suggest that Egypt’s campaign of home demolitions, nighttime curfews and geographic isolation has failed to head off the budding insurgency there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/world/middleeast/bombings-of-security-facilities-in-sinai-kill-at-least-26.html', 'snippet': 'The bombings suggest that Egypt’s campaign of home demolitions, nighttime curfews and geographic isolation has failed to head off the budding insurgency there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — A series of simultaneous bombings targeting security facilities in the Sinai killed at least 26 people Thursday night, prompting fears that the Egyptian government’s campaign of home demolitions, curfews and sweeping arrests has failed to choke off a 