_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-30T04:46:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/eef40d7d-f5e8-59ca-aa95-6da4dbf39162', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eef40d7d-f5e8-59ca-aa95-6da4dbf39162'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Derthick’s work on Social Security, federalism, deregulation and welfare was said to vividly bring life to impenetrable subjects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/us/martha-a-derthick-public-policy-decoder-dies-at-81.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Derthick’s work on Social Security, federalism, deregulation and welfare was said to vividly bring life to impenetrable subjects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martha A. Derthick, a political scientist whose trenchant analyses of typically impenetrable subjects like Social Security, federalism, deregulation and tobacco litigation were praised as “masterful” and “definitive,” died on Jan. 12 at a hospital in Charlottesville, Va. She was 81. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/us/DERTHICK-obit/DERTHICK-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 856, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/30/us/DERTHICK-obit/DERTHICK-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 856}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/us/DERTHICK-obit/DERTHICK-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 718, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/us/DERTHICK-obit/DERTHICK-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1435, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/us/DERTHICK-obit/DERTHICK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/30/us/DERTHICK-obit/DERTHICK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/us/DERTHICK-obit/DERTHICK-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Martha A. Derthick, Analyst Who Untangled Public Policy, Dies at 81', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Martha Derthick, 81, Analyst Who Untangled Public Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Derthick, Martha A (1933-2015)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-30T04:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7660fb00-54c9-5dc5-95a1-57f218822f3e', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7660fb00-54c9-5dc5-95a1-57f218822f3e'}, {'abstract': 'Mina Stone, who cooks regularly for Urs Fischer and other big names in the art world, shares dishes from her new cookbook.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/t-magazine/mina-stone-cooking-for-artists-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Mina Stone, who cooks regularly for Urs Fischer and other big names in the art world, shares dishes from her new cookbook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mina Stone just wants to be able to feed everyone. “Every menu is sort of structured around everybody, whether they’re vegetarian or vegan or meat eaters, being able to be satisfied by a dish,” says the Brooklyn-based personal chef who, for the past nine years, has made a name for herself in the New York art scene. She prepares lunch three days a week for the artist Urs Fischer and his staff at his Red Hook studio, serves post-opening dinners for the gallerist Gavin Brown and cooks for the painter Elizabeth Peyton. Fittingly, Stone also admits to developing recipes based on color: “When you look at your plate,” she says, “I feel like all those items should be really beautiful together.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/t-magazine/30mina-beddie-1/30mina-beddie-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/30/t-magazine/30mina-beddie-1/30mina-beddie-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/t-magazine/30mina-beddie-1/30mina-beddie-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/t-magazine/30mina-beddie-1/30mina-beddie-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/