ayed to acclaim under the direction of Jonathan Miller, by delving into the play’s history, pondering how the storm scenes might have been produced at Shakespeare’s own theater and looking at some alternate endings. Ian McKellen and Simon Russell Beale share their insights as well.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-30T06:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd2b5479-8b30-5984-afd1-d5d6f15311b1', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd2b5479-8b30-5984-afd1-d5d6f15311b1'}, {'abstract': 'A spate of suicides last year has raised questions about the effects of the country’s continuing campaign to root out corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/china-to-tally-suicides-by-civil-servants/', 'snippet': 'A spate of suicides last year has raised questions about the effects of the country’s continuing campaign to root out corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China will begin tabulating deaths of officials after a spate of suicides last year raised questions about the effects of the country’s continuing anticorruption campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/world/30sino-suicide/30sino-suicide-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, '