day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Today: Snow Day Fashion', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-30T11:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal and Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/315eb5c3-7974-5c77-b8b5-c430999d6f6e', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/315eb5c3-7974-5c77-b8b5-c430999d6f6e'}, {'abstract': 'Education Minister Yuan Guiren has laid out new rules restricting the use of Western textbooks, part of a drive to ensure that universities emphasize ideological loyalty to the Communist Party, Marxism-Leninism and the ideas of President Xi Jinping.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/china-warns-against-western-values-in-imported-textbooks/', 'snippet': 'Education Minister Yuan Guiren has laid out new rules restricting the use of Western textbooks, part of a drive to ensure that universities emphasize ideological loyalty to the Communist Party, Marxism-Leninism and the ideas of President Xi Jinpin...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In law school at Peking University in the late 1970s, Li Keqiang, now China’s premier, was an avid student of English and helped translate texts that gave his generation its first, exhilarating exposure to Western legal ideals after the death of Mao.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01