sser-Akner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5e40d8a-b87b-5b33-9a07-c2b370574644', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5e40d8a-b87b-5b33-9a07-c2b370574644'}, {'abstract': 'What was treasure and what was trash.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/magazine/dive-nights.html', 'snippet': 'What was treasure and what was trash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One evening in the fall of 1993, when I was 9, my father climbed into a Dumpster. This was in a Connecticut college town — a place totally unlike Chongqing, the sooty, cacophonous Chinese city where I grew up — that was almost as strange to me as my father was. I had known him for only half a year, which was how long my mother and I had been in the United States; he moved here shortly after I was born.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '52', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/magazine/01lives/01mag-01lives.t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 627, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/01/magazine/01lives/01mag-01lives.t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 627}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/magazine/01lives/01mag-01lives.t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 980, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/magazine/01lives/01mag-01lives.t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1789, 'width': 1712, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/magaz