 up for close to an hour to order a burger and some crinkle-cut fries at Shake Shack. On Friday, investors showed an equal amount of enthusiasm for the company’s stock.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shake Shack More Than Doubles Its I.P.O. Price in Market Debut', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Market Debut, Shares of Shake Shack More Than Double', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shake Shack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-30T15:24:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e85e197-5919-52dc-b7a4-78d09c5223a2', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e85e197-5919-52dc-b7a4-78d09c5223a2'}, {'abstract': 'Three states are providing real-life experiments on the impact of paid leave on new parents and employers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/upshot/the-economic-benefits-of-paid-parental-leave.html', 'snippet': 'Three states are providing real-life experiments on the impact of paid leave on new parents and employers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Larisa Casillas gave birth to a boy two years ago, the Bay Area nonprofit organization where she worked gave her only four weeks of paid leave. But she took more than that, including 12 weeks paid by California’s state family leave program, one of