 'By Joseph E. Stiglitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Stiglitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/31854037-86a2-5636-a6b6-e02896e120b3', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31854037-86a2-5636-a6b6-e02896e120b3'}, {'abstract': 'The toymaker, whose chief executive resigned last weekend, said net income fell nearly 60 percent in the fourth quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/31/business/mattel-vows-a-turnaround-as-it-posts-bleak-earnings.html', 'snippet': 'The toymaker, whose chief executive resigned last weekend, said net income fell nearly 60 percent in the fourth quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The toymaker Mattel on Friday promised to take swift action to reverse years of sales declines as it released grim earnings, just days after the abrupt resignation of its chief executive.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bleak Report For Quarter From Mattel ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bleak Report for Quarter From Mattel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mattel Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-30T16:17:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b440716e-6f82-5860-8209-b427dc8f4239', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b440716e-6f82-5860-8209-b427dc8f4239'}, {'abstract': 'On Jonathan Chait, his critics, and the effectiveness of ideological taboos.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/does-political-correctness-work/', 'snippet': 'On Jonathan Chait, his critics, and the effectiveness of ideological taboos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve spent a few days traveling, so I’ve had time to mull over what kind of intervention might be useful in the debate kicked off by Jonathan Chait’s big New York Magazine essay on the alleged return of a speech-policing, debate-squelching, illiberal P.C.\xa0left. The critical response has ranged from the spluttering\xa0to the dismissive, with the latter being seemingly the sophisticated left-wing take: There is no such thing as political correctness, the term is just a tool used by privileged white men to marginalize the legitimate arguments of the less-privileged, Chait’s lament is the latest iteration in a long tradition of internet-era complaints from prominent columnists confronted with tough criticism from outside their comfort zone, except now the criticism making him uncomfortable is\xa0coming from Twitterers instead of netroots types, etc.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Political Correctness Work?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chait, Jonathan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eich, Brendan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank