'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4f0e314-1ca8-5c37-b2a0-6d28d95744c7', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4f0e314-1ca8-5c37-b2a0-6d28d95744c7'}, {'abstract': 'After an unexpected extra day in New York City as a result of a storm, a couple takes some time to be tourists near Central Park, at the Stone Rose Lounge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/nyregion/a-parkside-view-of-winter-white-from-the-stone-rose-lounge.html', 'snippet': 'After an unexpected extra day in New York City as a result of a storm, a couple takes some time to be tourists near Central Park, at the Stone Rose Lounge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many New Yorkers this week, as the blizzard panic lifted from the city, the pressing culinary question on Tuesday was, “Now what do I do with all this Dinty Moore?” One answer was just to walk away, perhaps to find a table someplace where the snow outside maintained its fleeting Currier & Ives majesties. Why not? With Tavern on the Green shuttered because of the weather, scenic duty fell to the slight remove of the restaurants of the Time Warner Center at Columbus Circle, where the trees of Central Park displayed dustings of white thingamajigs suspended perilously above their inevitable future as unloved street slush. Quiet descended on the city, cocktails and Pat LaFrieda beef products descended on the polished black tables of the Stone Rose Lounge, and stranded tourists consoled themselves for having to spend an extra night in the world’s greatest city. Poor babies.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01TABLE/01TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 326, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01TABLE/01TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 326}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01TABLE/01TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 556, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01TABLE/01TABLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1111, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01TABLE/01TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01TABLE/01TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01TABLE/01TABLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Miami Tourists to New York City: Let It Snow', 'kicker': 'At the Table', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Miami Tourists to City: Let It Snow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stone Rose Lounge (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-30T19:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title':