.com/2015/02/01/nyregion/for-manoush-zomorodi-time-for-some-conscious-unplugging.html', 'snippet': 'On Sundays, Ms. Zomorodi, the host and managing editor of WNYC public radio’s New Tech City, spends time outside and with her children, hoping to inspire their minds to drift creatively.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Manoush Zomorodi, the host and managing editor of WNYC public radio’s New Tech City, a podcast that explores how technology affects the way we live, hasn’t been bored in seven years. She traces her condition to 2007, when the iPhone was introduced. Concerned that she’s not alone, and that letting the mind wander spurs creativity, Ms. Zomorodi, 41, is spearheading “Bored and Brilliant,” a seven-day challenge that asks participants to minimize device use and enjoy idle time — with the help of an app. “We’re trying to embrace the ridiculousness of it,” she said. Ms. Zomorodi lives in Carroll Gardens, Brooklyn, with her husband, Josh Robin, 38, a reporter for NY1, and their son, Kai, 7, and daughter, Soraya, 4.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01ROUTINE2/01ROUTINE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01ROUTINE2/01ROUTINE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01ROUTINE2/01ROUTINE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/nyregion/01ROUTINE2/01ROUTINE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub