Met Sally” for jerks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the director Leslye Headland’s “Sleeping With Other People,” which premiered at Sundance last week, Alison Brie plays Lainey, a serial cheater whose longing for a stable relationship is constantly railroaded by an obsession with her college crush (Adam Scott). She meets her match when she strikes up a friendship with Jake (Jason Sudeikis), a good-natured womanizer who just happens to have taken her virginity 12 years earlier. At the premiere, Headland described the film as “When Harry Met Sally” for jerks (though she used a slightly stronger word), which is to say that, like the director’s previous effort, “Bachelorette,” it is more than a little naughty and twisted (and, it follows, a perfect starring vehicle for Brie). The 32-year-old L.A. native has been stealing scenes for the better part of a decade playing type-A characters on “Mad Men” and “Community,” and she viewed Headland’s film — and its many sex scenes — as an opportunity to try out a new direction. T sat down with the actress in Park City to discuss high-school sweethearts, “Sleepless in Seattle” and the highly secretive world of “Mad Men.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/t-magazine/30brie-oloizia/30brie-oloizia-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/30/t-magazine/30brie-oloizia/30brie-oloizia-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/t-magazine/30brie-oloizia/30brie-oloizia-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/t-magazine/30brie-oloi