 statement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/fashion/bill-cunningham-snow-day.html', 'snippet': 'Hoods made a fashion statement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the schools closed, Tuesday was a day in the park for parents, children and dogs. A young mother brought her 10-month-old baby , who looked like an upside-down radish in a green jacket and red hat, and put the child into a plastic bucket for a first sleigh ride. Pedestrians leapt like ballet dancers over slushy curbsides. Tourists ventured into the south end of Central Park. The fountain in Bryant Park was newly frozen, and a group of youngsters had a snow fight using cafeteria trays. A young man built a snowman, chilled wine bottles inside of it, then poured himself a glass. He said it was his birthday.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Snow Day', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Snow Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-30T21:19:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham and Joanna Nikas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': Non