': 'Wines have their Tuscan countryside; cheeses, their hillside caves in southern France. So wouldn’t it make sense that bread, too, might hold a connection to the place where the wheat is grown and the dough kneaded? That’s the goal in Amagansett, where farmers and bakers work the bounty of the land, encouraged by the idea of terroir: that the soil and the elements combine to create a distinct flavor bound to place.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the East End of Long Island, Embracing Local Wheat', 'kicker': 'Dining', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Connecting the Bread to the Wheat to the Land', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wheat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAGANSETT (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bread', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Amber Waves Farm (Amagansett, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Carissa's Breads (Amagansett, NY, Bakery)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Cuevas, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waechter, Carissa E (1979- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merrow, Amanda', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Katie', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T00:08:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily J. Weitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Weitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/781a26d1-ff35-51e0-90b8-cf3895c24adc', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/781a26d1-ff35-51e0-90b8-cf3895c24adc'}, {'abstract': 'The ring of suspected intelligence operatives’ use of journalists tells you everything you need to know about the Kremlin’s paranoia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/30/magazine/spy-vs-nonspy-in-putins-russia.html', 'snippet': 'The ring of suspected intelligence operatives’ use of journalists tells you everything you need to know about the Kremlin’s paranoia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, F.B.I. agents in New York arrested a 39-year-old Russian man named Evgeny Buryakov, whom federal prosecutors accused of participating in a spy ring gathering economic intelligence on the United States. There were three spies in all, according to the criminal complaint federal prosecutors filed on Monday, all agents of the Russian Foreign Intelligence Service (S.V.R.), who had been posing for several years as civilians. Buryakov worked at the New York branch of the Russian state-owned Vnesheconombank; his suspected accomplices worked as a Russian trade representative and diplomatic attaché.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/magazine/30mag-30spies/30mag-30spies-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/30/magazine/30mag-30spies/30mag-30spies-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/magazine/30mag-30spies/30mag-30spies-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/30/magazine/30mag-30spies/30mag-30spies-supe