he airline, clearing a big internal hurdle toward integrating operations from the merger of American Airlines and US Airways.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pilots Union Approves Contract With Airline ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pilots Union Approves Contract With Airline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'US Airways Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T01:25:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2825d19a-1717-5a58-b143-37b7d924bec2', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2825d19a-1717-5a58-b143-37b7d924bec2'}, {'abstract': 'The test, the last in a series ordered by the Federal Highway Administration, appeared to be the first to shed doubt on the widely used barrier system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/31/business/assessment-of-guardrails-hinges-on-final-crash-test.html', 'snippet': 'The test, the last in a series ordered by the Federal Highway Administration, appeared to be the first to shed doubt on the widely used barrier system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a debate swirls over whether a widely used guardrail system is safe, more than 30 states have been waiting for the results of crash tests before deciding whether to continue to use the guardrails or, possibly, have them removed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Assessment of Guardrails May Hinge on Final Crash Test', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Assessment of Guardrails May Hinge on Final Test', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kessler, Aaron M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trinity Industries Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Highway Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T01:28:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ivory and Aaron M. Kessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83a32999-f641-5800-82b4-3711336466b2', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83a32999-f641-5800-82b4-3711336466b2'}, {'abstract': 'Venezuela’s defense minister said Friday that Venezuelan military aircraft had shot down a small plane that crashed a day earlier in the waters near the island of Aruba.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/31/world/americas/venezuela-military-says-it-downed-plane-near-aruba.html', 'snippet': 'Venezuela’s defense minister said Friday that Venezuelan military aircraft had shot down a small plane that crashed a day earlier in the waters near the island of Aruba.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Venezuela’s defense minister said Friday that Venezuelan military aircraft had shot down a small plane that crashed a day earlier in the waters near the island of Aruba. Officials in Aruba said Thursday that the plane had gone down after being pursued by Venezuelan jets, but it was not immediately known if they had fired on it. The Venezuelan defense minister, Vladimir Padrino, said that the plane had taken off from the southern state of Apure, which is a regular loading point for drug flights. “Our aircraft intercepted and it did not follow orders and, well, it was disabled,” he said, adding that the encounter took place over Venezuela’s territorial waters. The Aruban authorities said that the craft crashed in waters belonging to the island, which lies just off Venezuela’s coast. Officials in Aruba said that body parts and about 400 packages that appeared to contain drugs were found in the wreckage. A Justice Ministry official in Aruba said Friday that the plane was registered in the United States. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Military Says It Downed Plane Near Aruba', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Military Says It Downed Plane Near Aruba', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARUBA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T01:33:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World',