rld', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/47088d52-5358-5893-9f86-afdac98f35b3', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47088d52-5358-5893-9f86-afdac98f35b3'}, {'abstract': 'These poems about Monday evening’s storm and its relationship to romance (or the lack thereof) were found in the Missed Connections section of newyork.craigslist.org.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/nyregion/love-the-other-letdown.html', 'snippet': 'These poems about Monday evening’s storm and its relationship to romance (or the lack thereof) were found in the Missed Connections section of newyork.craigslist.org.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blizzards — or feared blizzards, like this week’s storm — tear us from our daily lives. In that, they are like love. They also tend to be fickle, blowing in quickly and dissipating just as fast. These poems about Monday evening’s storm and its relationship to romance (or the lack thereof) were found in the Missed Connections section of newyork.craigslist.org. They are printed verbatim, with only line and stanza breaks added; their titles are the subject headings.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Love, the Other Letdown', 'kicker': 'Poetic Connections | the Snowstorm', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love, the Other Letdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T05:06:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fd9a92a-9ecf-5b36-ac7d-688d4d9e7fb8', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fd9a92a-9ecf-5b36-ac7d-688d4d9e7fb8'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn rapper has spent more than six weeks in jail on gun and drug charges related to allegations of a gang conspiracy.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/01/31/bobby-shmurda-posts-2-million-bond/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn rapper has spent more than six weeks in jail on gun and drug charges related to allegations of a gang conspiracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bobby Shmurda, the spark-plug Brooklyn rapper, has posted $2 million bail after spending more than six weeks in jail on gun and drug charges related to allegations of a gang conspiracy, his lawyer said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bobby Shmurda Posts $2 Million Bail', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Judelson, Ira', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shmurda, Bobby (1994- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Epic Records', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manhattan Dentention Complex', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T05:12:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9c9ebee-389d-5895-84c7-8724e751d56b', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9c9ebee-389d-5895-84c7-8724e751d56b'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/31/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Cinemax) BAD WORDS (2014) Guy Trilby (Jason Bateman, who also directed), a 40-year-old bully who has wormed his way onto the spelling-bee circuit, mows down the small-fry competition with one expletive after another until he reaches the nationals. And then he encounters Chaitanya Chopra (Rohan Chand), a socially awkward 10-year-old sorely in need of a friend. “It would be something to see Mr. Bateman go authentically dark (perhaps not that dark), but it’s also enough just to watch him as he widens his eyes, furrows his brow and shows off his excellent timing,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “It’s a fluid feature-directing debut, and he pulls the ensemble together smoothly,” she added. “The performances are funny, appealing and, in the case of Allison Janney, as a spelling bee official, wonderful. A dowdied-down Kathryn Hahn has it tougher as Jenny, a reporter who’s chasing Guy for his story and occasional sex. It’s a pathetic role, largely because she’s a sad piñata made for the whacking simply because, it seems, the only thing worse than making kids cry is being a journalist.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T06:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd41b2c6-12b5-57a7-8f9f-20de767e7770', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd41b2c6-12b5-57a7-8f9f-20de767e7770'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Saturday, January 31, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/01/31/pageoneplus/corrections-january-31-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Saturday, January 31, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 31, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T06:49:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54db7a49-c411-5a58-b98c-dc05536b2e90', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54db7a49-c411-5a58-b98c-dc05536b2e90'}, {'abstract': 'Williams won her 19th Grand Slam singles title on Saturday, defeating Sharapova, 6-3, 7-6 (5) to become the oldest woman to win the singles title in the Open era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/sports/tennis/serena-williams-beats-maria-sharapova-in-australian-open-final.html', 'snippet': 'Williams won her 19th Grand Slam singles title on Saturday, defeating Sharapova, 6-3, 7-6 (5) to become the oldest woman to win the singles title in the Open era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — The record still shows that Maria Sharapova is a pushover for Serena Williams: her muse, 