cle/280a1dc3-e833-5d92-9942-ec8c26d0a56b', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/280a1dc3-e833-5d92-9942-ec8c26d0a56b'}, {'abstract': 'Pete Wentz and Patrick Stump of Fall Out Boy talk about what went into making their new album.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/arts/music/fall-out-boy-on-the-new-album-american-beauty-american-psycho.html', 'snippet': 'Pete Wentz and Patrick Stump of Fall Out Boy talk about what went into making their new album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With their second act as a band, the members of Fall Out Boy have pulled off what once seemed at least highly unlikely: not only outlasting their emo peers from the early aughts but also transcending them all the way to the top of the Billboard charts — and with real guitars, too, a rare sound on pop radio today. After a five-year hiatus, the band returned in 2013 with “Save Rock and Roll,” a typically irreverent album that made its debut at No. 1; now, its new single, “Centuries,” is hovering in the Top 20 and scoring sporting events on TVs and in stadiums across the country. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01PLAYLIST1/01PLAYLIST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01PLAYLIST1/01PLAYLIST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01PLAYLIST1/01PLAYLIST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01PLAYLIST1/01PLAYLIST1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': '