': 'Weizsacker, Richard von (1920-2015)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitler, Adolf', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T19:13:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wolfgang Saxon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wolfgang', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saxon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/73df38df-77eb-5841-8b46-36dd5b375546', 'word_count': 1248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73df38df-77eb-5841-8b46-36dd5b375546'}, {'abstract': 'An intensive tutoring and mentoring program in Chicago has produced big improvements for kids.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/opinion/sunday/intense-tutoring-can-close-the-math-gap.html', 'snippet': 'An intensive tutoring and mentoring program in Chicago has produced big improvements for kids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a recent afternoon, the banter of boisterous adolescents at Edwin G. Foreman High School, in a poor, racially and ethnically mixed Chicago neighborhood, echoed off the corridor walls. But Room 214 was as silent as a meditation retreat. Inside, 16 ninth- and 10th-grade African-American and Latino boys were working, two-on-one, with a tutor. They’re among 1,326 boys in 12 public schools in this city who are sweating over math for an hour every day.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Kirp-David-circular/Kirp-David-circular-art