 a third bid for the White House on Friday, but other 2016 Republican hopefuls are still gearing up for a long campaign season. Gov. Scott Walker of Wisconsin will appear on ABC’s “This Week,” and Mike Huckabee, the former governor of Arkansas, will be on CNN’s “State of the Union.” Senator Lindsey Graham of South Carolina, who just formed an exploratory committee for the presidency, will talk about this move on CBS’s “Face the Nation.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Watching: Sunday Shows', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayotte, Kelly A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durbin, Richard J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-01-31T19:56:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elena Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e358b2f0-6721-5595-9eb3-c59baf9fb4f8', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e358b2f0-6721-5595-9eb3-c59baf9fb4f8'}, {'abstract': 'The China Minsheng Banking Corporation gave no explanation for the resignation of Mao Xiaofeng and no indication whether he had been questioned or was assisting inves